window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":501,"title":"Chapter 501: Promotion of Quality of Source Sand","paragraphs":["Although its spiritual power was restored by Lin Yuan, the ability of the Insect Queen’s body to produce insect protein could not only rely on the Protein Silkworm Chrysalises.","It also needed nutrients that could be absorbed from meat, blood, and even bones.","Lin Yuan had originally planned to continue channeling more spiritual power into its body.","However, because the Insect Queen’s body greatly lacked the energy that could not be obtained from the Protein Silkworm Chrysalises, it had to stop the continued production of insect-species fey.","These colossal Diamond Giant Cattle, along with a group of high-grade, non-combat-class fey, would let the Insect Queen and the imperial insect swarm enjoy a good meal.","Yet, immediately after, Liu Jie abruptly came to his senses and frowned.","Based on the 400 simplified Hurricane Owlet Moths that he had previously sent, it appeared that the oncoming enemies were some of the weakest feys that he had ever detected.","There was only one possibility when such an enemy appeared, which was that the enemy would attempt to stall for time.","The other party would send these logistics personnel out to fight, which was tantamount to tempting fate.","Such behavior was enough to demonstrate the enemy’s determination to fight to the death.","Lin Yuan saw that Liu Jie’s expression was still changing and quickly asked, “Big Brother Liu, how is the situation?”","Liu Jie hurriedly told Lin Yuan and Zhou Luo about the situation that he had personally witnessed.","Then, Liu Jie proceeded to share his opinion on the matter.","“I plan to treat the enemy’s contracted feys as the Insect Queen’s nutritional base, providing it with the nutrients to continue producing insects.","“If not, as there isn’t enough high-grade fey flesh now, the insects produced by the Insect Queen would not have shells with sufficient strength.”","As he spoke, Liu Jie scratched his head in embarrassment.","He felt that he had been negligent as he had not expected that such a situation would arise upon his arrival in Indigo Azure City.","Under normal circumstances, besides preparing Protein Silkworm Chrysalises that would help the Insect Queen restore insect protein in the Diamond fey storage box, Liu Jie would also prepare some high-grade fey flesh for it.","Although this time was no exception, there was not enough flesh of high-grade dimensional lifeforms to sustain the production of so many insects.","This time, Liu Jie understood that in the future, there had to be at least five times or even ten times more Protein Silkworm Chrysalises and high-grade fey flesh in his Diamond fey storage box.","Only then could various dangerous situations be faced.","There would never again be a situation like the present one,when there was insufficient high-grade fey flesh.","The main reason that such a circumstance had occurred was Liu Jie’s failure to consider that Lin Yuan would have such a powerful ability to restore spiritual power.","Upon hearing Liu Jie’s words, Lin Yuan opened his mouth to speak. “Big Brother Liu, let me face these enemies.","“You need only be responsible for letting the insect swarm consume the feys that have sunk under the sea of sand and allowing the swarm to restore their energy.”","As Lin Yuan spoke, he carefully sensed the spiritual power reserve in his body and found that a third of the Spirit Qi Imprint had not been depleted.","In spite of this, even a third of the spiritual power accumulated over time by the Bronze X/Legend’s Spirit-Drawing Ichthyosaur was a huge amount.","Lin Yuan had firmly decided to face these enemies alone in order to preserve Liu Jie’s strength as much as possible.","At the same time, after absorbing part of the Mountain-Containing Embryo, the Bronze X/Fantasy I Source Sand had already been promoted from Fantasy I to Fantasy II. It had now become a Gold I/Fantasy II elemental source-type item.","Liu Jie immediately put some of the late-stage Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects in the quicksand on standby. These had been produced by the Insect Queen when she had insufficient nutrients.","The insects prepared for a bloody meal.","Given the Lava Dragon Lizard’s immense speed and the fact that the enemy on the opposite side was dashing towards them, Lin Yuan soon saw the oncoming enemies.","Upon closely inspecting the spirit qi professionals on the backs of the approaching Diamond Giant Cattle, Lin Yuan’s pupils immediately constricted.","This was because they closely resembled the spirit qi professionals who had launched surprise attacks on him back in the controlled Class 3 abyss dimensional rift.","One is the product of one’s environment. There were also differences in the appearances of spirit qi professionals from different continents.","Just based on their looks alone, it was obvious that they had come from the Radiance Federation.","It was highly possible that they were from the Dark Continent, just like the spirit qi professionals who had previously attacked him.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’ True Data to scan the approaching feys.","He then closed his eyes and used his spiritual energy to communicate with Source Sand.","Following which, the sound of the boiling sea of sand under the seabed came out of his ears.","At this moment, the spirit qi professionals riding on the backs of the Diamond Giant Cattle also noticed Lin Yuan’s presence.","Even though most of the opposing side’s fey were not natural fighters, fey who had reached the Platinum and even the Diamond rank still possessed a certain killing ability.","Those feys released many long-range attacks toward the Lava Dragon Lizard.","Zhou Luo, who was riding on its back, yelled, “Lava Dragon Lizard, activate Lava Shield!”","Right after, a spherical shield enveloped the Lava Dragon Lizard’s outer body surface, firmly protecting the Lava Dragon Lizard, Zhou Luo, Lin Yuan, and Liu Jie within the shield.","Various attacks were made on the shield, some splashing with ripples, and others disappearing without making even a single splash.","It could have been said that Zhou Luo singlehandedly warded off this flurry of attacks.","The Lava Dragon Lizard had awakened the dragon-species bloodline, so it was unrecognizable after its mutation and the growth of double heads.","The strength level of the Diamond Fantasy Breed was much higher than that of an ordinary Diamond fey.","Zhou Luo’s existence had always been extremely low, but this time, he directly demonstrated his king-class strength.","At the same time, the seabed within the compatibility range of two kilometers instantly turned into a vortex of boiling quicksand.","The oncoming feys from the opposite side were all running on land, and as non-combat terrestrial feys, their mobility was not strong.","This caused many of the Platinum feys to be dragged immediately into the Fantasy Breed Source Sand’s seas of sand, where they continued to sink.","Without Lin Yuan doing anything, Liu Jie’s Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects, which he had instructed to hide and wait within the sand, ate these sunken feys alive. Not even a trace of blood or bone was wasted.","Compared to fey flesh, fey blood and bones contained nutrients that the Insect Queen needed more.","Thus, those few Diamond Giant Cattle struggled violently in the sea of sand."]},{"number":502,"title":"Chapter 502: Gentleness Deserving of Death","paragraphs":["When a fey’s mobility was strong enough, it could run as much as it liked, even in churning quicksand.","It was just that the Giant Cattle were far too heavy, so they could only ensure that their heads did not sink under the quicksand during the struggle.","In the meantime, their entire bodies were submerged in the quicksand, save for a small part of their backs.","Even so, no matter how much Lin Yuan made the Source Sand drag the Giant Cattle downward, they could still move in the quicksand using their own strength.","The only difference was that the speed at which the Giant Cattle moved was really as slow as that of an old cow pulling a cart.","Seeing the situation, Lin Yuan immediately let the Source Sand use its exclusive skill of Gravel Spirit Acceptance, which was equivalent to the combat power of the Platinum III/Elite Heart-Penetrating Ironline, to kill the Diamond Giant Cattle.","However, at that very moment, Lin Yuan somewhat helplessly realized that even if the Source Sand’s Gravel Spirit Acceptance could penetrate the Giant Cattle’s body, it would only penetrate half a meter of flesh.","This was not enough to fatally wound the 15-meter-long Giant Cattle.","After such effort, Lin Yuan finally understood the bitterness of a mosquito in the summer.","Some people with thick hair or rough skin were akin to a nightmarish blow to the hungry mosquito.","After a hard night’s work, not only would it be unable to suck even a drop of blood, its bloodsucking needle would also be blocked by dander.","However, Lin Yuan did not believe in evil and continued to direct the Heart-Penetrating Ironline towards the Giant Cattle’s weakest spot.","Yet, the Giant Cattle actually clamped its tail tightly between its legs, completely protecting its fragile place.","Lin Yuan curled his lips and took a few Heart-Penetrating Ironlines of greater strength than Platinum III/Elite out his leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","After a simple test, he directly replaced the Gravel Spirit Acceptance’s previous Platinum III/Elite Heart-Penetrating Ironline with a Platinum V/Flawless one.","The needle on this mosquito’s mouth was directly upgraded, although only by two small grades.","Nevertheless, the quality was also upgraded by one level.","The Platinum V/Flawless Heart-Penetrating Ironline was already able to completely penetrate the Giant Cattle’s body and wander within it. The Heart-Penetrating Ironline then did its job of piercing the Giant Cattle’s heart.","For a moment, each of the Giant Cattle appeared to be suffering tremendous pain in all four hooves.","They all emitted one last sound before they ceased to struggle, taking the spirit qi professionals on their backs down into the quicksand with them.","This scene only served to inspire horror in Liu Jie and Zhou Luo.","Lin Yuan’s sea of sand was not as simple as it looked on the surface. There was clearly an entire cosmos lying within its depths.","It was as though there was a demon lurking in the dark, holding a scythe, ready to harvest the lifeforms in the sea of sand at any time.","Zhou Luo and Liu Jie had just witnessed how Lin Yuan had thrown the alien insect Heart-Penetrating Ironline into the sea of sand.","Presumably, the demon beneath the deep sea of sand was related to the dead Heart-Penetrating Ironline that Lin Yuan had thrown into the sand.","Only the specific connection between the two remained unknown.","Immediately afterwards, Zhou Luo and Liu Jie saw Lin Yuan taking a large quantity of Bronze ferromanganese and one cubic meter of Day and Night Spirit Silver out of his fey storage box.","Lin Yuan threw both of these spiritual materials into the quicksand vortex formed by the Source Sand.","Since the Source Sand had upgraded from Fantasy I to Fantasy II, its dedicated skills had all been strengthened as well.","Besides the Gravel Spirit Acceptance being able to accept stronger fey, the Metal Consume Manifestation could now also devour more metal.","The shape the Source Sand took during the change also became more refined.","One had to know that the Source Sand had only absorbed around half of the Mountain-Containing Embryo.","The Source Sand’s remaining half was still holding the earth-elemental pearl produced by the Thick Earth Elemental Shellfish, fondling the pearl like an old man.","After the Mountain-Containing Embryo that it had previously absorbed changed its abilities, the Source Sand could also produce Close Guard Sand with three more layers than before.","For Lin Yuan, the increase in Close Guard Sand was tantamount to once again improving his own defense abilities.","Liu Jie was letting the Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects gnaw on the recently deceased Diamond Giant Cattle while urging the Insect Queen to use its Blast Recovery to explode the Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects to recover its energy from the large amounts of fey flesh and bones inside the insects’ bodies.","The churning sea of sand’s interior was akin to a chain of farts, continuously emitting puffing sounds.","Previously, Lin Yuan had always believed that his contracted Red Thorn was not good to the child ramets and ramets that it had bred.","Yet, seeing how Liu Jie’s Insect Queen was using her insects now, Lin Yuan felt that Red Thorn was really a warm and lovely plant.","Of course, the most important thing was the damned gentleness with which Red Thorn treated the child ramets and ramets that it had spawned.","In actual fact, when Lin Yuan launched the quicksand’s large-scale attack this time, he did not deplete much of the spiritual power in his body.","In the seabed, a large amount of gravel had already been created. This large-scale quicksand was, to a large extent, the instinctive behavior of the Source Sand as an elemental source-type item.","The real consumption of spiritual power occurred when he let the Source Sand use its exclusive skill to drive the Heart-Penetrating Ironline into the Diamond Giant Cattle to kill them.","In a short while, a small vortex of quicksand appeared at the Lava Dragon Lizard’s feet.","Several golden discs were directly spat out of the vortex.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up, and he jumped down from the Lava Dragon Lizard’s back.","He picked up these 30 golden discs and inspected them one by one.","Following which, he realized that these golden discs were entirely identical to the ones that he had previously obtained.","The only difference lay in a light discrepancy in the size of the hole within each disc.","Lin Yuan’s eyebrows raised in joy. The happiness he felt after obtaining these golden discs was infinitely greater than that he felt after obtaining some precious spiritual ingredients.","As the number of spirit-qi consumers in his Spirit Lock spatial zone increased, the energy ores originally stored within the golden discs were also consumed more and more quickly.","Especially since there were now a total of seven Bronze/Legend Elemental Shellfish continuously producing elemental pearls, the consumption of spirit qi had increased exponentially.","Hence, Lin Yuan needed to replenish the energy ores in the golden discs at short intervals of time.","Now, with 30 golden discs at hand, this no longer posed an issue.","Lin Yuan’s trivial troubles were finally reduced.","Even if Morbius’ Spirit Lock spatial zone evolved or too many spirit-qi consumers joined, Lin Yuan could handle it completely.","At the same time, he could not help but think that since the suicide squad sent by the enemy possessed golden discs, then others must also have them.","Just as Lin Yuan was ruminating over these golden discs, a violent spatial fluctuation came from the distance."]},{"number":503,"title":"Chapter 503: Await His Return!","paragraphs":["The expressions on Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Zhou Luo’s faces changed in that instant.","The problem that they had all worried would arise had now truly appeared.","The fact that they could feel such a violent spatial fluctuation from so far away proved that the evolving Class 3 water world spatial rift had now, for whatever reason, already reached Class 4.","It had even begun its promotion to Class 5.","The current situation was so severe that it was necessary to race against time to retrieve the source-type items from the dimensional hub.","A typical dimensional rift required around 12 hours to evolve.","Hence, Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Zhou Luo had still had time to plan and prepare.","However, now affected by external factors, the dimensional rift was suddenly undergoing a leap-forward evolution. Moreover, acute spatial fluctuations were still coming from not far away.","This meant that the dimensional rift’s evolution from Class 4 to Class 5 could be completed any time now.","Lin Yuan knew that even after he and others were sucked into the dimensional rift; the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Listen would definitely realize it and be on high alert.","Yet, no matter how much preparation was done, if the Class 5 dimensional rift really opened in the coastal sea so close to Indigo Azure City, then the entire city would be destined to fall into ruins at the seabed.","Just as Lin Yuan and Liu Jie’s expressions grew increasingly heavy, Zhou Luo raised his head and looked into the distance.","He then turned his head back and gazed at Liu Jie before casting a deep look at Lin Yuan.","The faintly determined expression between Zhou Luo’s eyebrows now thickened, as though he was solidifying the decision he had made in his heart at that moment.","Lin Yuan inhaled deeply and did not stop until his lungs were swollen and painful.","Then, Lin Yuan expelled all of this breath again, suppressing the urgency that had arisen in his heart.","Gazing calmly at Liu Jie and Zhou Luo, he said, “We will rush directly towards the dimensional hub’s position. Whatever the cost, we must stop the dimensional rift’s evolution.”","Just after Lin Yuan’s had spoken, before Liu Jie could respond, Zhou Luo shouted, “Alright!”","This one yell seemed to contain all of Zhou Luo’s solitary bravery.","Zhou Luo did not understand why the blood in his heart was surging at this time.","He also could not tell if Lin Yuan’s thoughts caused this surge of blood. As a servant, Zhou Luo had to obey Lin Yuan’s orders in order to repay the latter’s kindness in giving him a new lease of life.","Perhaps, it was simply caused by the sight of the determined light twinkling in Lin Yuan and Liu Jie’s eyes.","Liu Jie did not say anything. He was focused on quickly manipulating the insect swarms in the sand under the seabed into ingesting the dead Diamond Giant Cattle with all their strength.","Liu Jie knew that a tough battle would be fought next.","In this crisis, even replenishing the depleted energy in the Insect Queen’s body was considered a huge luxury.","Liu Jie raised his head and said, “It will take some time for these Diamond Giant Cattle to be completely consumed. I have left around 500 Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects here to finish ingesting the feys under the sea of sand.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan stopped concealing the Source Sand’s large amount of yellow sand under the seabed.","Lin Yuan did not channel his spiritual power into the Source Sand. It was only because the Source Sand sensed his instructions that it drove the entire ocean of sand and gravel by itself.","Looking around, one saw that the surrounding environment was instantly transformed into a world made of gravel.","Before Zhou Luo and Liu Jie could register their shock, everyone had once again mounted the Lava Dragon Lizard.","The billowing sand grains pushed the Lava Dragon Lizard to thrust itself forward. Although not obvious, this truly increased the lizard’s running speed.","At the same time, at the coastal sea close to Indigo Azure City, outside the evolving dimensional rift, a woman dressed in moon-colored long robes was bathing under the blood-tinted moonlight. Murderous intent and worry were written on her face in equal parts. Her body’s imposing manner was exposed without concealment.","This woman was the Moon Empress, who had just arrived an hour ago.","The dense moonlight cast a heavy curtain behind the Moon Empress. Beneath this curtain, there was only the Moon Empress, Mystic Moon, and the blocked entrance to the dimensional rift.","Outside of it stood the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Listen.","The trio’s bodies were also enveloped by rich moonlight, obscuring their figures.","Behind them stood countless experts who had come from areas within and close to Indigo Azure City upon learning of the Moon Empress’ arrival.","A vast majority of these experts were Creation Masters.","Yet, most of them stood with their bodies bowed and their eyes gazing only at the ground.","It was as though even lifting their eyes would be considered overstepping their authority.","Amongst them were the two Guard Envoys, who stood five positions behind the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Listen.","Behind the curtain of moonlight, Mystic Moon looked at the Moon Empress’ expression and understood more deeply how much Lin Yuan weighed in her heart.","In the many years that he had followed the Moon Empress, he rarely saw such worry written on her face.","Moreover, this anxiety had already cast a shadow over her face for many hours.","Mystic Moon lowered his head and glanced at the bright red Ethereal Jellyfish in the Moon Empress’ arms.","He then cast another gaze at the small rabbit at her feet that looked like it had fallen into disfavor, with its drooping ears and lack of energy.","Mystic Moon then understood that the extent of the worry in the Moon Empress’ heart was not at all as simple as that which was revealed on her face.","However, at this time, as one of the Moon Empress’ Moon Envoys, Mystic Moon still had matters to attend to.","Suddenly, he thought of something and asked the Moon Empress softly, “Moon Empress, on Cold Moon’s side, would you like to...”","Before he was finished speaking, the Moon Empress already understood his words.","She raised her brows and thought about it for three seconds before replying, “Yes.”","Naturally, the Moon Empress knew that when Mystic Moon had mentioned Cold Moon, he had actually been referring to Chu Ci.","The Moon Empress was very clear about the sibling bond between Lin Yuan and Chu Ci. At this moment, it could be said that Lin Yuan was in a life-and-death situation. Putting herself in Chu Ci’s shoes, the Moon Empress felt that Chu Ci had to be informed of Lin Yuan’s plight.","After all, as Lin Yuan’s master, she would consider it unacceptable if she was the one who did not know about this matter.","When it came to the ways of the world, it was better to say more rather than less. In the face of true familial relations, these slick and sly ways appeared more like falsehoods and heresies.","Besides Chu Ci, Cold Moon, as one of the Moon Envoys, should also have been standing there, awaiting the return of the Young Lord of Radiant Moon Palace! His return!"]},{"number":504,"title":"Chapter 504: Really Too Short!","paragraphs":["Mystic Moon turned and walked out from behind the curtain of moonlight, thinking about how he should inform Cold Moon about the situation.","It was truly anxiety-inducing to have to relay bad news.","Just after he stepped out, the Mother of Bloodbath, standing cloaked in rich moonlight, immediately came forward and asked urgently, “Lin Yuan—”","Before it could finish its sentence, Mystic Moon raised his eyes to gaze upon it and said, “You did not fulfill your duty as the Path Protector and betrayed the Moon Empress’ trust.”","Mystic Moon’s words cut into the Mother of Bloodblath’s arachnid heart like a knife.","To begin with, worry had been written on its face, but upon hearing Mystic Moon’s words, the Mother of Bloodbath turned pale as a sheet.","Ignoring its reaction, Mystic Moon continued as he walked past the Mother of Bloodbath, “You also betrayed Lin Yuan’s trust.”","If his previous words had been a knife, then what he said now was a hammer, slamming repeatedly into the Mother of Bloodbath’s heart.","Endless Summer quickly extended a hand to hold the Mother of Bloodbath and give her a little strength.","Upon hearing Mystic Moon’s words, Endless Summer’s heart was like the Mother of Bloodbath’s. Such was the empathy it felt towards the Mother of Bloodbath.","Although Endless Summer was not Lin Yuan’s Path Protector, it was still his Protector and had the duty of protecting him.","While Mystic Moon’s words had been spoken to the Mother of Bloodbath, they had also been directed to Endless Summer.","As Mystic Moon’s figure appeared through the rich moonlight, some of the experts in front who had been bowing before now raised their heads slightly.","The two Guard Envoys in the first line hurriedly went up to him and asked, “Mystic Moon, how did the Moon Empress make arrangements here?”","They felt great anxiety in their hearts, as they had come to Indigo Azure City for a mission, but they had been met with many ups and downs.","Initially, they had come to the deserted island to investigate the energy fluctuations in the experts’ battle, but they had then accidentally run into the Moon Empress’ disciple.","Now, the Moon Empress had personally arrived at the deserted island.","In hindsight, the problem had probably arisen with the little ancestor who had been unwilling to even address the two as ‘Seniors’.","If they had known earlier that such a situation would arise, the two would not have left the deserted island so hurriedly. Instead, they would have stayed behind on it.","Now, a controlled Class 3 water world dimensional rift had unexpectedly appeared in the sea region near Indigo Azure City.","Moreover, the main thing was that this dimensional rift was still evolving.","This was a matter of heavenly importance!","Even though the two Guard Envoys were used to witnessing great upheavals and changes, they still did not know how to handle the current situation.","Standing far in the distance behind them, Duan He secretly raised his head.","However, he did not look directly ahead but first glanced left and right.","With this, he sighed deeply in his heart.","There were so many Class 4 Creation Masters surrounding him. It was as though those who could make it had all hurried here!","It was likely that even if Indigo Azure City’s Creation Master Association held a large event, one would not see so many Class 4 Creation Masters gathered together at the same time!","Duan He secretly raised his head and looked ahead.","Yet, with this one glance, he already sensed that the three distant silhouettes bathed in rich moonlight appeared vaguely familiar.","As they were concealed by the moonlight, Duan He could not deduce why this was so at the current moment.","Just then, he heard a cold voice.","It carried with it the iciness of Ethereal Spirits frozen on the ground and an unspeakable severity, as though it was relaying an order that none could disobey.","“Mystic Moon, inform the imperial court that for this dimensional rift, preparations must be made in advance to handle a Class 5 or higher dimensional rift.”","The Moon Empress’ voice made the hearts of everyone present skip a beat. At the same time, faces immediately filled with shock.","Did the Moon Empress really mention that this was a Class 5 or higher dimensional rift?","This kind of dimensional rift had never been heard of in the past!","At that very moment, the two Guard Envoys, with cold sweat dripping down their foreheads and worry in their hearts, did not expect it when the Moon Empress proceeded to call out their names.","“The Guard Envoys of the Spirit Guards, go and request of the Chief Guard,Night Leaning Moon, that she preside over this.”","...","The Lava Dragon Lizard raced across the sea of sand without once stopping.","A minute ago, Lin Yuan had already sensed that something was rushing towards him and the others over the sandy sea of endless gravel.","Lin Yuan faced Liu Jie and said in a deep voice, “Big Brother Liu, don’t hold back in the fight later. We will get the battle over and done with quickly.”","Liu Jie immediately replied, “Okay, I will let the Lightning Gathering Moths use the previously gathered lightning beams to direct long-range strikes.”","Having absorbed the plasma energy from the Plasma Caterpillars, the Lightning Gathering Moths could be seen as the most formidable attack tactic in Liu Jie’s sea of insects.","Originally, Liu Jie and Lin Yuan had planned to use these moths as assassins for sneak attacks.","However, at this critical moment, it would not do to employ such logical battle strategies.","One could only be reckless, continuously reckless, reckless all the way to the dimensional hub!","From the situation on the sea of sand, Lin Yuan had already known that the incoming enemy was a tough guy.","Because even the rushing feys, which were extremely flexible, had been continuously pulled down into the quicksand vortexes in the Source Sand.","These feys could still rely on their extreme mobility to not be greatly hindered in the process of advancing.","The Lava Dragon Lizard did now slow down even at the prospect of facing the enemies.","Soon after seeing the situation on the opposite side, Lin Yuan’s eyes narrowed suddenly.","He had just seen that every one of the feys rushing towards him was huge and had a strange blade-like object inserted into its body.","Lin Yuan immediately used True Data to scan one of the largest of these strange creatures at the very front.","[Fey Name]: Blade Worm (Blade Queen Bee Larva)","[Fey Species]: Paracaridae/Heridae","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (7/10)","[Fey Type]: Metal","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Lin Yuan now knew what these strange lifeforms with blades were.","They turned out to be the larvae hatched from the Blade Queen Bee’s eggs.","But the bodies of these Blade Worm were really too short!","They were just like fat sea cucumbers.","Rather than ‘Blade Worm’, calling them ‘Blade Fat Sea Cucumber’ would have been a little more vivid."]},{"number":505,"title":"Chapter 505: The Art of Explosions","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan dared not to look down on the Blade Worms.","The Blade Queen Bee was a carcinoma fey that the Spirit Guards had documented.","The Blade Queen Bee had the greatest destructive capabilities of all the carcinoma feys documented by the Spirit Guards.","Although it did not have strong fighting abilities of its own, it had a psychotoxin that allowed it to smoothly produce eggs, as well as a stinger that could penetrate almost anything.","Every Blade Worm birthed by the Blade Queen Bee was a lethal weapon. The Blade Worms lived to fight and kill until they were incapacitated. Thus, they had to give this battle their all.","However, the thought of the imminent challenge delighted Lin Yuan.","The situation could only be described as good news.","This was the water world dimensional rift, and the Blade Queen Bee needed enough fresh feys to produce Blade Worms.","After producing the eggs, the psychotoxin the Blade Queen Bee injected into the target would homogenize with the psychotoxins on the Blade Worms’ eggshells.","The psychotoxin would immediately turn into a deadly psychotoxin.","It was a defense mechanism that ensured the Blade Worms’ eggshells would break after the host died.","Because of the two toxins’ effects, the newly hatched Blade Worms would make short work of devouring the target’s brain.","Despite the death of the host, their memory would remain intact. The Blade Worms would steal the host’s fighting experience and skills that were encoded in the brain.","Hence, when the Blade Worms matured, they would automatically turn into capable war machines.","This was also why the support fey that had run to their deaths did not turn into Blade Worms.","After eating brains, the freshly hatched Blade Worms would tunnel upward to the surface of the target’s body to breathe their first breath of air.","Then, they would move on to feast on the host’s organs, flesh, and bones.","When the Blade Worms were done absorbing the energy in the host’s body, they would align their grade and quality to that of the host.","However, high-grade water world dimensional lifeforms decayed swiftly after death.","There was not enough time for the Blade Worms to feed. That’s why there weren’t many Blade Worms initially.","As long as there was a dependable energy source, the Blade Queen Bee would birth a batch of eggs in about 48 hours.","Even if the Blade Queen Bee’s production rate was slow, it would still be at least 10 or even 100 times faster than normal feys.","There did not seem to be enough ingredients available in the area for the Blade Queen Bee to begin producing eggs.","Otherwise, Lin Yuan’s side would lose for sure.","Lin Yuan had already used True Data to check on the Blade Worms’ quantity and grade.","When he was done, he let out a thunderous yell. “25 Diamond Blade Worms and 47 Platinum Blade Worms. Big Brother Liu, don’t send the recharging Lightning Gathering Moths to attack the Diamond Blade Worms. We should kill the 47 Platinum Blade Worms first!”","When Liu Jie heard Lin Yuan mention the 25 Diamond Blade Worms, he immediately disregarded the depletion of the insect army and called out the 300 recharged Lightning Gathering Moths from the swirling quicksand Lin Yuan created.","Liu Jie immediately directed 100 Lightning Gathering Moths to shoot the lightning beams formed from the absorption of the Plasma Caterpillars at the 47 Platinum Blade Worms that were running behind the 25 Diamond Blade Worms.","100 brilliant purplish-blue beams of electricity were released with an ear-splitting crack.","The purplish-blue beams of electricity struck the 47 Platinum Blade Worms, electrocuting the quicksand below them and turning it into a sticky fluid.","Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Zhou Luo held their breaths as they watched the countless darting streaks of electricity.","Unfortunately, when the electricity cleared, it was revealed that the 100 beams of light had only managed to kill one Platinum Blade Worm.","There were also seven or eight Platinum Blade Worms that had also been taken down, and the electricity had also punched large holes in these fainted Blade Worms.","However, thorns rapidly sprouted from the large holes, sealing them up.","Through the use of True Data, Lin Yuan discovered that the recuperated Blade Worms had dropped to Platinum IV.","Although the Blade Worms’ wounds caused their grade to fall, the newly grown thorns looked ferocious.","Liu Jie looked forward, where the Blade Worms were still charging, and said, “I plan to use Battle Strategy 4.”","“Take care of attacking. I’ll use the Source Sand to assist you.”","Lin Yuan injected spiritual power into the Source Sand’s sea of gravel, and 150 Shield Ladybugs tunneled out.","50 Shield Ladybugs formed one group, and the three groups blocked the front of the Lava Dragon Lizard.","Zhou Luo started to apply Lava Shield on each of the Shield Ladybugs in the first group.","Liu Jie did not use the remaining 200 Lightning Gathering Moths to continue shooting lightning at the Platinum Blade Worms.","Instead, he sent the 200 recharged Lightning Gathering Moths and the 100 already spent ones charging toward the remaining 46 Platinum Blade Worms.","When the 200 recharged Lightning Gathering Moths closed in on the Blade Worms, they released the lightning in their bodies.","Before the lightning made contact with the Blade Worms, Liu Jie bellowed, “Insect Queen, use Blast Recovery!”","A deafening clap of thunder and the roar of the exploding Lightning Gathering Moths echoed as the 46 Blade Worms were struck!"]},{"number":506,"title":"Chapter 506: Strange Grunting","paragraphs":["Liu Jie did not falter in the attack. He pressed on and commanded the 200 Plasma Caterpillars to also join in the wreck of self-explosions.","When he was done, Liu Jie put the survival of the 46 Platinum Blade Worms out of his mind.","He shifted his attention to the thousands of Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects crawling out of the quicksand that were charging toward the 25 Diamond Blade Worms.","Liu Jie knew that regardless of the regenerative abilities of the 47 Platinum Blade Worms, it was impossible for them to have survived the previous attack.","Lin Yuan had already activated the Source Sand to coat every Flesh-Mincing Blade Insect with a thin layer of gravel.","The thin layer of gravel enabled Lin Yuan to create extremely durable ferromanganese. The ferromanganese’s strength lowered the Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects’ speed, but it did not affect Liu Jie’s Battle Strategy 4.","Liu Jie’s Battle Strategy 4 was not impacted by the individual insect species, for it treated every insect species produced by the Insect Queen as explosive collateral stock.","Using art was the way to fight using explosives!","Liu Jie totally looked like a terrorist!","But, this fighting style fit the current situation to a tee.","On the battlefield, everything occurred in split seconds.","Now, any and all methods should be used to stop the Diamond Blade Worms’ advance.","If the Diamond Blade Worms closed in on them, Lin Yuan and his team would lose their lives, much less be able to prevent the dimensional rift’s evolution.","A section of the Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects charged at the 25 Diamond Blade Worms from the ground.","The remaining section of the Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects was transported underground by Lin Yuan. These Flesh-Mincing Blade Insects, which were meant to be exploded, were delivered directly under the Blade Worms.","Liu Jie ordered the Hurricane Owlet Moths to call upon hurricanes, so the gale force could impede the Blade Worms’ strength.","The strong winds kicked up sand, which allowed Lin Yuan to control the Hurricane Owlet Moths.","A large number of ferromanganese chain blades appeared amongst the flying sand.","The ferromanganese chain blades sailed toward the Blade Worms, which would have instantly torn them to shreds.","Due to the savage winds, the 250 Blade Worms had already slowed by at least 30%.","Most of the insect species were in position.","Liu Jie glanced at the 150 Shield Ladybugs in front of the Lava Dragon Lizard and gnashed his teeth.","He ordered the Shield Ladybugs to spread the wings under their armor and fly toward the Blade Worms.","Zhou Luo, who had been maintaining the shields, shouted, “Lava Dragon Lizard, use Elemental Release!”","The lava-shielded Shield Ladybugs expanded with energy in an instant, setting the shields alight with raging fires.","The Hurricane Owlet Moths stopped creating hurricanes and instead shot down from the air toward the Blade Worms.","Explosions from above and below erupted in all directions.","A wave of energy was redirected into the Insect Queen’s body, and its body, which had transformed into an insect base, was awash with a glowing green exterior of energy.","This was how the Insect Queen looked when its energy capacity had reached the maximum.","At this point, the insect army created by Liu Jie and Lin Yuan was almost all gone.","Other than Lin Yuan’s Extreme Token, everyone had utilized all the power they had access to without holding anything back.","Lin Yuan suddenly thought about the effects of the exclusive skill the Lava Dragon Lizard used.","The exclusive skill Elemental Release allowed the Lava Dragon Lizard to release fire-elemental energy from its new head. It could significantly increase the damage of explosions.","When Lin Yuan was recruiting the white-clothed followers, he had concentrated on Freezing Cold’s contracted feys at Purchase With No Loss store.","Lin Yuan had only done a brief scan of Zhou Luo’s feys, so he had not noticed their abilities and exclusive skills.","The Iron Bone Tearing Lizard’s abilities and exclusive skills changed considerably when it evolved to the Lava Dragon Lizard.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’ True Data to check on the Lava Dragon Lizard he was riding on.","[Fey Name]: Lava Dragon Lizard","[Fey Species]: Iguanidae/Huge Iguana","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Earth/Fire","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Strong Head Lizard Hit]: Strengthens the head and concentrates all the body’s strength to the head to strike.","[Shield Tail Parry]: Strengthens the skin of the tail to turn it into a shield. Used to parry attacks.","[Lizard Roar]: Uses neighing to increase the body’s blood circulation to direct blood to the lizard skin and raise its defensive ability.","[Thick Shield]: Apply a double layer of thick shields to a select target. The floating double layer of shields can slow oncoming damage.","[Lava Strong Shield]: Combine the body’s earth-elemental and fire-elemental energy into lava and set up a single layer of lava imbued shielding on numerous targets.","[Shield Regeneration]: Broken shields are fixed using the body’s energy. As long as the body still has energy and the shield is not attacked by fire elements, the shield will be immediately recovered.","Exclusive Skill:","[Unbreakable Iron Bones]: Before receiving an attack, the defensive ability is raised before the fighting ability is utilized until the life is ended.","[Elemental Release]: The body’s elemental energy is released onto the surface of any shield so as to increase the shield’s innate elemental properties.","After looking through, if Lin Yuan was going to appraise the Lava Dragon Lizard, he would deem it as barely average.","Its defensive ability was far from being as versatile and comprehensive as Shi Xu’s Silent Thunder Armored Crocodile.","Moreover, Normal, Epic, and Bronze grade abilities would be especially effective on the Lava Dragon Lizard, which greatly depressed the Lava Dragon Lizard’s capabilities as a defense-type fey.","However, Lin Yuan felt Unbreakable Iron Bones was special.","Liu Jie, who was next to Lin Yuan, had already instructed the Insect Queen to change into the insect base and was continuously producing insect armies so as to slow down the depletion during battle.","The smoke from the explosions still had not dissipated.","Surprisingly, at that moment, a strange grunting resounded amid the dulled explosion sounds."]},{"number":507,"title":"Chapter 507: Resolution to Die","paragraphs":["The strange grunting amid the sounds of explosions sounded like a final wail.","But, this final wail was interlaced with undeniable desperation and madness.","The sound immediately gave Lin Yuan a bad feeling.","As the Blade Worms were war machines, the Blade Queen Bee produced, and under normal circumstances, they were purely produced for battle and did not have any emotions of their own.","However, the Blade Worms’ grunting now carried obvious emotions, indicating the Blade Queen Bee’s death.","The suppressed genetics inside of the Blade Worms would only be unlocked after the Blade Queen Bee’s death.","Lin Yuan summoned Genius and removed the mask Hu Quan had created before putting on the mask Genius transformed into.","Lin Yuan carefully scanned the surroundings.","The timing of the Blade Queen Bee’s death was too coincidental, for it coincided with the exact time that the 25 Diamond Blade Worms were struck.","Logic dictated that such an enormous succession of explosions must have killed the 25 Diamond Blade Worms.","Because the concurrence of the Blade Queen Bee’s death unlocked the Blade Worms’ genetics, an unknown number of Blade Worms could have survived the explosions.","After studying the surroundings while wearing the Genius mask, Lin Yuan did not learn anything.","This raised a problem—a carcinoma fey like the Blade Queen Bee that was skilled at hiding would definitely not have died in a random fashion.","This meant someone had murdered the Blade Queen Bee intentionally.","After the smoke dissipated, the Diamond Blade Worms had formed a pile the size of a small mountain.","The outer layer of the Diamond Blade Worms had been burnt to a crisp by the explosions.","At that moment, the small mountain of 25 Diamond Blade Worms started to shake.","Eight thorn-covered Blade Worms that resembled sea urchins emerged from the small mountain.","The thorns protruding from the Blade Worms showed that the explosions had injured those Blade Worms in spite of the protection they received from their comrades in front of them.","Using True Data, it was found that the eight Diamond Blade Worms were now Diamond V at best and Diamond II at worst.","Judging from the skin of thorns that covered the eight Blade Worms that managed to survive, Lin Yuan could see that the originally purplish-gray skin was now purplish-red.","The eight Blade Worms were in no rush to charge toward Lin Yuan’s group.","Instead, they bitterly grunted a distance away.","The Blade Queen Bee’s death doomed the rest of this colony of Blade Worms.","As the wails of despair persisted, the aura around the eight Blade Worms climbed.","Suddenly, a vigorous dimensional fluctuation started up a distance away.","The dimensional fluctuations were moving at high frequencies, which formed a whistle that sounded like a kettle boiling.","The whistle of the dimensional fluctuation resulted in a shift in expression in Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Zhou Luo.","The whistle coming from the dimensional hub meant that the dimensional rift’s evolution would be completed in an hour.","From Lin Yuan’s position, the Lava Dragon Lizard would need 50 minutes to arrive at the dimensional hub at its current speed.","Not to mention they would need to ensure that the journey was clear of obstacles.","Even if Liu Jie’s Insect Queen’s Hurricane Owlet Moths teamed up to manipulate the winds along their journey, they would still need at least 30 minutes to reach the dimensional hub.","Time waited for no man. The dam was on the cusp of breaking.","There were still the eight Diamond Blade Worms blocking their path.","Behind Zhou Luo’s composed expression was an extreme yearning for determination.","Zhou Luo turned to say seriously to Lin Yuan, “Young Master, how does it feel to be a hero?”","Lin Yuan was in the middle of trying to come up with a way to overcome the present issue. He froze when he heard Zhou Luo’s question.","Lin Yuan felt that the question was rather weird, but he replied nonetheless, “I don’t know what it feels like to be a hero.”","Ever since the incident at Millstone Town, Lin Yuan had only brought out the Black identity during the Star Web Star Tower Celestial Stairway match.","Moreover, Lin Yuan was not interested in online forums and platforms, and he did not even participate in Black’s fan clubs.","Thus, it was true that Lin Yuan had never really experienced heroism.","Zhou Luo was stunned when he heard Lin Yuan’s reply. Lin Yuan quickly added, “There are some things that require someone to take responsibility of the frontline. I’m not a real hero and won’t go out of my way to do heroic acts. But, if I happen to encounter such events, I will never shy away.”","The yearning in Zhou Luo’s eyes shone with a special gleam when he heard Lin Yuan’s words.","The glow in Zhou Luo’s eyes steadily grew, adding a hint of austerity to his resolute demeanor.","Lin Yuan was preparing for battle when Zhou Luo spoke. “Young Master, you two should head toward the dimensional hub. Leave these eight gross bugs to my buddy and me.”","Lin Yuan fixed his gaze on Zhou Luo.","While Liu Jie was instructing the Hurricane Owlet Moths, he too noticed the shared sentiment in Zhou Luo’s eyes.","When Zhou Luo had the eyes of both men on him, he beamed charismatically.","“Don’t worry. My buddy has really hard bones. When I’m finished with these eight gross bugs, I’ll regroup with you two. Then, we’ll leave this place together.”","As Zhou Luo spoke, he glanced toward the dimensional hub, and a look of concern was evident on his face.","But when he turned toward the eight Diamond Blade Worms, Zhou Luo only had charm and determination in his eyes.","Lin Yuan took a sharp intake of breath.","If Zhou Luo is standing out to take on these Blade Worms whose genetics have been unlocked, he must be going in with the resolution to die. The Lava Dragon Lizard might be a Diamond/Fantasy Breed, but it’s only a Diamond I defense-type fey."]},{"number":508,"title":"Chapter 508: Blooming Carnage","paragraphs":["Liu Jie had already created eight Hurricane Owlet Moths.","“Big Brother Zhou made the right choice. We should head up first. If we encounter any danger, I’ll take care of it. We have to deliver you to the dimensional hub,” said Liu Jie to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan felt a heavy weight pressing down on his chest. He understood where Liu Jie was coming from, so Lin Yuan agreed with their decision.","Lin Yuan’s resolve to prevent the dimensional rift’s evolution was unwavering. He just felt that he was too weak to prevent such a disaster on his own.","Lin Yuan turned and said to Zhou Luo, “I want to give you something, Big Brother Zhou.”","Zhou Luo felt warmly validated when he heard Liu Jie and Lin Yuan address him in such a manner.","Zhou Luo doubtfully stretched out his hand to Lin Yuan.","What does he have for me?","When he saw what Lin Yuan had taken out, he immediately stretched out his other hand as well.","The heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls from Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone were in a pile.","Lin Yuan placed all the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls produced by the Scorching Elemental Shellfish and the Thick Earth Elemental Shellfish in Zhou Luo’s hands.","Since Lin Yuan had spent away the previous elemental pearls, the ones at hand were just the fruits of two days worth of production, which totaled about 100 pieces.","Most of the elemental pearls were earth-type. The fire-elemental pearls were the Twin Red Pagoda’s leftovers, and there were only a small number of them.","Zhou Luo’s Lava Dragon Lizard was a fire- and earth-type fey. Its exclusive skill, Elemental Release, could imbue shields with elemental power.","These heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls could effectively supplement the Lava Dragon Lizard’s exclusive skill.","Using the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls to replenish elemental energy was a huge waste, but these 100 elemental pearls could significantly raise the Lava Dragon Lizard’s fighting power.","Time was tight. Lin Yuan and Liu Jie continued following the four Hurricane Owlet Moths toward the dimensional hub after giving Zhou Luo the elemental pearls.","Zhou Luo looked at the 100 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in his hands, and he could feel the immense elemental energy they encompassed.","A spark of hope for survival bloomed in spite of Zhou Luo’s resolution for death.","In order for the spark to erupt into a flame, he needed to brush against death and do all he could to finish off the eight Diamond Blade Worms.","Zhou Luo patted the Lava Dragon Lizard’s two necks, an action he had performed countless times in the past to the point that it came as natural to him as breathing.","“Old buddy, it’s time for us to fight alongside one another again. Let us two lazy bums show off what we can do,” he murmured to the Lava Dragon Lizard.","The Lava Dragon Lizard released the ability Lizard Roar.","The bones on the Lava Dragon Lizard’s skin were flushed with blood and strengthened.","The Lava Dragon Lizard covered itself with the ability Thick Shield followed by Lava Strong Shield.","It reared its two heads and used all the strength it could muster to charge the eight Blade Worms, crashing into two of them.","When the shield came in contact with the thorns all over the Blade Worm’s bodies, a spine-chilling sound was produced.","At that moment, carnage bloomed, but fearlessness arose.","Zhou Luo thought back to his childhood.","A very talented young man that came from a modest background was paired with an Iron Bone Iguana that did not have any concept of teamwork in its abilities before it reached Silver grade.","The two experienced more than their fair share of evil and hardship.","The abilities Strong Head Lizard Hit, Shield Tail Parry, Lizard Roar, and Unbreakable Iron Bones, which had been ridiculed, seemed to be part of destiny.","Those abilities and exclusive skills were now at maximum effectiveness.","The sound of the Lizard Roar and the impact noise upon contact with the Blade Worms’ thorns was deafening.","Behind the horrible sound were one man and one lizard who were forming a barrier between the tsunami that was the Class 5 dimensional rift for the sake of Indigo Azure City.","The horrible sound was earth-shattering, and a pandemonium of aggressive bedlam was created in the raging storm of sand.","One after another, the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were shattered in Zhou Luo’s hand. However, he eventually sensed that the Lava Dragon Lizard had absorbed too much elemental energy and was experiencing a lag in its sensitivity to elemental energy.","In light of the remaining three Blade Worms that could still stand, Zhou Luo disabled the Lava Dragon Lizard’s shield.","Bloody holes were punctured into the shieldless Lava Dragon Lizard’s body by the Blade Worms’ thorns.","The Lava Dragon Lizard looked like a mass of blood, and even Zhou Luo’s leg had been stabbed several times as well.","Zhou Luo injected his last ounce of spiritual power into the Lava Dragon Lizard.","Despite his depleted spiritual energy, this seven-foot-tall man stood with perfect posture, his radiant pride shining through.","The impact noise and the sound of the thorns puncturing skin were neverending until the last Diamond Blade Worm collapsed to the ground with only enough strength left to writhe.","The ten-meter-long Lava Dragon Lizard crashed to the ground, and Zhou Luo fell beside it.","Zhou Luo shakily got to his feet and looked at the sprawled-out Lava Dragon Lizard that was barely clinging to life.","“Old buddy, your exclusive skill Unbreakable Iron Bones, let us hold on to the end. We survived thanks to you.”","Zhou Luo summoned the recently contracted Bronze X/Epic Dark Snake Dragon Lizard that he still had not had time to nurture.","The Dark Snake Dragon Lizard immediately started to attack the writhing Blade Worms in a frenzy.","When the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard emptied its body of energy, the Blade Worms were still left with a final breath, but not enough to make even the slightest movement.","Zhou Luo picked up one of the broken thorns from the ground and walked up to the Diamond Blade Worms.","He plunged the thorn into the Blade Worm’s fist-sized, thorn-covered head.","Zhou Luo seemed to understand what it felt like to be a hero at that moment.","The feeling was like a raging storm and swaying plants. It was like leaning on your own shoulder and lifting the growing grass and flying birds.","This feeling was of utter elation, and it filled him with an effulgent sense of having found his calling."]},{"number":509,"title":"Chapter 509: Could It Really Be a Sacred Source Lifeform?","paragraphs":["Zhou Luo raised his head, gazed into the distance, and yelled with all his might in that direction, “Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, everything depends on you now!”","After shouting this, Zhou Luo staggered towards the Lava Dragon Lizard.","He had just taken some ointment made of spiritual ingredients out of the fey storage box and was preparing to rub it on the Lava Dragon Lizard’s body.","However, at that moment, as his tension eased, he immediately felt dizzy due to the excessive blood loss from the wound on his leg.","This sudden dizziness blackened Zhou Luo’s vision. He collapsed beside the Lava Dragon Lizard and fell into a deep sleep.","...","Lin Yuan, carried by four Hurricane Owlet Moths, rushed towards the dimensional hub.","On one hand, he was now concerned about Zhou Luo’s condition.","On the other, his journey had been unexpectedly calm.","The Source Sand’s gravel had long been laid at the dimensional hub’s location.","Lin Yuan continuously urged the Source Sand to produce sand grains beneath the seabed, using the dimensional hub as the center.","Now, these sand grains completely covered a compatibility range of three kilometer surrounding the dimensional hub.","The Source Sand was not sensitive to small vibrations on the seabed’s surface, but it could easily detect violent vibrations.","Lin Yuan had not been notified by the Source Sand of any severe vibrations within this compatibility range.","It seemed that there probably weren’t any huge feys like the Blade Worm moving about in the dimensional hub’s vicinity.","The Hurricane Owlet Moths carried Lin Yuan and Liu Jie in flight for close to five minutes. Lin Yuan immediately saw many well-built strongholds beneath their feet.","Clearly, people had been living there for a prolonged period of time in the past.","Looking at the strongholds before his eyes, Liu Jie said to Lin Yuan in a deep voice, “This place is very close to the dimensional hub. Should we get off here and walk to it on foot or let the Hurricane Owlet Moths fly us there?”","Liu Jie eyed the strongholds on the ground with vigilance.","Although they appeared deathly still from above, Liu Jie was still unable to confirm if there were any remaining spirit qi professionals within them.","If there were, then wouldn’t he and Lin Yuan have become two obvious moving targets in the air?","As they neared the dimensional hub, Lin Yuan did not know why, but he felt an increasing sense of urgency.","The dimensional fluctuations here were really too severe. If they did not stop the dimensional rift’s evolution immediately, Lin Yuan would not be able to feel at ease.","Looking at the dimensional hub in front of them, Lin Yuan turned to Liu Jie and said, “Big Brother Liu, let’s rush into it directly.”","After receiving Lin Yuan’s answer, Liu Jie immediately ordered the Insect Queen to create four Shield Ladybugs.","After the Shield Ladybugs had been produced, they opened up the shells on their back and flapped their wings beneath the carapaces. Like four guards, they prepared to use their bodies as shields to resist attacks coming from all four directions from the ground.","However, the Shield Ladybugs were obviously unable to keep up with the Hurricane Owlet Moths in the air.","Thus, Liu Jie let the Insect Queen use its exclusive skill of Swarm Frenzy on the ladybugs.","At the cost of depleting their vitality, the Shield Ladybugs could now keep up with the Hurricane Owlet Moths’ speed.","Long before they had made their recent decision, Lin Yuan had already come up with a solution to deal with the strongholds beneath their feet.","The Source Sand had not been able to battle the Platinum Blade Worms alone.","However, if one needed houses to be torn down, then the Source Sand would definitely be the first name to come to mind.","Following Lin Yuan’s orders, the three kilometers of land beneath them turned into a world of turbulent yellow sand that instantly swallowed the strongholds built on the seabed.","During the swallowing process, the strongholds were also crushed by the sand grains, becoming a part of the sea of sand.","Liu Jie’s eyelids jumped wildly as he witnessed this scene before him. He could not help but think of the Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants that Wen Yu had found when he had been trying to level the mansion’s land.","When the Earth-Turning Giant Elephants had turned over the land, the scene had not been as spectacular as that of the surging sand of sea beneath their feet.","Liu Jie suddenly felt that it was unsurprising that Lin Yuan had so many resources on hand.","By simply buying sand, one could make a lot of income in a day.","Lin Yuan realized that the Source Sand he had contracted either had treasure-hunting skill or was a money fanatic.","After swallowing the piece of land where the stronghold had stood, the Source Sand even found a lot of supplies.","Among these supplies were numerous golden discs that Lin Yuan especially needed.","Based on the Source Sand’s feedback, the sea of sand had not swallowed any living beings.","Moreover, those golden discs had pretty much all been stacked together.","This was truly evil!","However, at this time, Lin Yuan did not think too much about it, as the dimensional hub of the evolving dimensional rift quickly appeared in his line of sight.","This was still considered Lin Yuan’s first time seeing a dimensional hub.","For some reason, Lin Yuan found the dimensional hub familiar from a distance. No matter how he looked at it, it resembled the interior of his own Spirit Lock spatial zone. Morbius possessed the stone pillar carvings and the stone bowls on them, which had appeared after its Spirit Qi Condensation.","It was just that the container on the dimensional hub was much larger than the stone bowls in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Upon close inspection, Lin Yuan found that there were nine source-type items and one unknown circular seven-colored light within the dimensional hub’s container.","Liu Jie could finally release his breath now that they were closer to the dimensional hub.","“We finally caught up. There are nine source-type items in here, but even so, it is reasonable to say that there shouldn’t be a Class 5 dimensional rift.”","As he spoke, Liu Jie also turned his gaze to the circular seven-colored light.","After looking at it, he immediately said with some uncertainty, “Seven colors? Might this not be a sacred source lifeform?”","Upon hearing Liu Jie bring up sacred source lifeforms, Lin Yuan’s eyes fixed tightly on the circular seven-colored light.","Lin Yuan had already heard the Moon Empress and the Mother of Bloodbath mention sacred source lifeforms more than once.","However, when Liu Jie brought them up now, Lin Yuan did not feel any awe for this circular seven-colored light. On the contrary, he only felt terror.","Sacred source lifeforms were only produced in Class 5 dimensional rifts, and only one such lifeform was produced in each Class 5 dimensional rift.","Now, it was simply an earth-shattering conspiracy that a sacred source lifeform had appeared in a Class 4 dimensional hub that was about to evolve to Class 5.","When the dimensional rift evolved from Class 4 to Class 5, another sacred source lifeform was bound to drop.","In this case, with the energies of the two sacred source lifeforms stacked together, who knew how far this water world dimensional rift that had opened outside Indigo Azure City would develop?","Just as he was about to urge the Extreme Token in the Flowing Cloud pendant hanging at his chest, Lin Yuan thought that he saw a hazy phantom through his Genius mask."]},{"number":510,"title":"Chapter 510: Lin Yuan, I Will Be Absent","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan immediately turned his head and looked intently at the clearing where he had just seen the hazy figure before.","However, when he checked the spot again, he found that the figure had disappeared.","After checking it once over to no avail, Lin Yuan thought that he had been mistaken.","He inhaled deeply and focused all of his attention on the dimensional hub.","For some reason, Liu Jie, who was standing beside Lin Yuan, constantly felt a sense of danger lurking at all four sides.","Liu Jie was very familiar with this feeling. Previously,whenever he had encountered danger when practicing in the wild, this same feeling would arise.","This sense of crisis could be considered the combat intuition that he had developed after countless battles.","And now, Liu Jie only felt this sense of impending crisis grow increasingly intense.","Just then, he suddenly thought about the clearing that Lin Yuan had just turned his head to look at and realized that the latter must have felt the same inexplicable sense of crisis.","Liu Jie also turned his head to gaze at the same clearing.","As he cast this one glance, he felt his hairs stand on end.","He immediately let out a loud bellow.","“Lin Yuan, defense!”","Right after, Liu Jie ordered the four Shield Ladybugs that were on standby beside him to shield Lin Yuan from the front.","Liu Jie had caught sight of a shadowy figure that had suddenly appeared in the clearing.","And this figure had been launching a purplish-gray crystal directly towards them.","Upon hearing Liu Jie’s loud shout, Lin Yuan subconsciously directed the Source Sand to separate a large amount of feathers from the Close Guard Sand at his feet.","These feathers were made of Gold Day and Night Spirit Silver. Because Lin Yuan had changed their appearance, they now looked like Gray’s feathers.","At the same time, because the Source Sand had already been promoted to Fantasy II, Lin Yuan had added an extra cubic meter of Day and Night Spirit Silver into it.","Hence, when the feathers formed his four wings, they were denser, more agile, and more elegant than before.","At that moment, the four Shield Ladybugs hit the purplish-gray crystal that had been flying towards them.","After hitting the ladybugs, the crystal exploded on impact, and a terrifying energy fluctuation rippled outwards.","Seeing the situation, Liu Jie instinctively sent his Insect Queen, which had just recovered its fairy-like form, towards Lin Yuan without hesitation.","Each of Lin Yuan’s four wings, which were nearly three meters long, had already spread.","Lin Yuan also instinctively protected Liu Jie under his four wings of Day and Night Spirit Silver.","Then, Lin Yuan channeled spiritual power into his wings.","Their original ink color, which was so dark that the wings had seemed to be able to absorb light, turned into a shining white in an instant.","At that moment, Liu Jie was facing Lin Yuan.","Seeing Lin Yuan inhale deeply, Liu Jie revealed a smile that came from the bottom of his heart.","He said softly, “Lin Yuan, I made an appointment with you and Wen Yu before. Unfortunately, ten years later, I will be absent on the grass.”","Before Lin Yuan could respond, Liu Jie had already turned away resolutely. He first reached out to stroke the Insect Queen lovingly before shouting firmly at it, “Transform into producing form! Use the exclusive skill of Swarm Frenzy on yourself!” ”","Following Liu Jie’s instructions, the Insect Queen inflated itself.","However, this time, the insect base that the Insect Queen turned into had a height of two meters.","On its body, a layer of energy flame still burned from the energy that it had recovered from exploding its entire insect swarm.","The Insect Queen was also resolutely fulfilling Liu Jie’s order. A red halo immediately appeared on its body after it had performed Swarm Frenzy on itself.","At that moment, Lin Yuan felt the extent of the purplish-gray energy that was bombarding his four wings of Day and Night Spirit Silver.","In a mere instant, even his wings, made of such a sturdy Gold metal, were blown to pieces by this energy.","Immediately after, this ray of purplish-gray energy blasted the insect base’s body.","As his four wings of Day and Night Spirit Silver had already been exploded into pieces by that energy, Lin Yuan was now completely exposed in the open.","Liu Jie, who was shielding Lin Yuan from the front, fiercely pushed Lin Yuan out of the way.","Subsequently, that purplish-gray energy blasted a huge hole in the Insect Queen’s insect base.","At the same time, the spreading purplish-gray energy also mercilessly blasted the Insect Queen from behind and continued towards Liu Jie, who was pushing Lin Yuan away.","Everything happened in the blink of an eye.","Liu Jie did not even have the time to say more to Lin Yuan before he was struck by that ray of purplish-gray energy.","However, Liu Jie’s act had already expressed everything that he had not had the chance to say in words.","Lin Yuan was pushed close to ten meters away by Liu Jie and fell unceremoniously onto the churning sea of sand.","Lin Yuan immediately dashed to Liu Jie’s side after standing up.","Seeing Liu Jie and the Insect Queen’s condition, Lin Yuan felt a rush of blood surging towards his head.","His eyes instantly turned red.","At that moment, the Insect Queen returned to the state that Lin Yuan had first seen it in. It was now a purple flesh cocoon that was roughly the size of a fist.","On this purple flesh cocoon, a hole had broken through the surface, from which a lot of purplish-gray fluid oozed out.","After being bombarded with that purplish-gray energy, all that was left of Liu Jie’s entire body was its torso.","Half of the shoulder on its torso was also mutilated, and like the Insect Queen, a large amount of purplish-gray fluid was streaming out of the wound.","It was clear that the purplish-gray energy’s attack had carried with it a terrifying poison.","At that moment, the gray figure in the distance revealed itself. He was wearing a satisfied expression on his face.","He elegantly strode over as though he had just finished watching a movie.","His gray eyes looked at Lin Yuan and Liu Jie, who were lying on the ground.smacked his lips and chuckled.","“What a heroic show of brotherhood! This time, it should be accompanied by a glass of wine to be savored fully!","“Despite your evident lack of strength, you could still withstand the strength of a Suzerain fey’s attack. I should congratulate you.","“However, you won’t be so lucky any longer, because your end is here.”","With that, the gray-haired, gray-eyed man summoned a giant hound with three ferocious heads with the wave of a hand.","The instant the hound appeared, it let out three terrifying roars.","The gray-haired, gray-eyed man said to himself, “I had initially feared that my own strength would be insufficient. However, now it looks like I, Hunting-Ashes, was destined to be able to complete Lord Seventh Page War’s decree.”","Lin Yuan was not concerned about the gray-haired, gray-eyed man or the giant three-headed hound that he had summoned.","His eyes seemed to seep blood as he summoned Jasmine Lily with a wave of his hand. Then, he removed the Vitality Imprint on his forehead, which contained a tremendous amount of vitality.","Simultaneously, he urged the Extreme Token that the Moon Empress had given him."]},{"number":511,"title":"Chapter 511: A New Hope","paragraphs":["Under the urging of his spiritual power, the Extreme Token plastered to Lin Yuan’s chest seemed to turn into a round moon in an instant, bursting with soft moonlight.","The moonlight was like water, shining on Lin Yuan’s body as if it could permeate his heart.","In the instant that the gray-haired, gray-eyed man saw the gentle moonlight rising from Lin Yuan’s chest, he felt as if everything would melt into this moonlight and never face.","Yet, as this moonlight, carrying light smoke and untainted by fine dust, left Lin Yuan’s chest, it immediately lost its original gentleness.","In an instant, the mountains and rivers changed color!","With Lin Yuan’s entire body as its origin, a stretch of silk composed of shining moonlight appeared to rise from his chest.","The moonlight was like white silk shining in the sky!","It carried itself with unparalleled might and majesty.","The piece of moonlight silk hovered in the sky before condensing into a bright moon in an instant.","This bright moon that radiated brilliant moonlight on the horizon seemed to take over the world within the evolving dimensional rift.","It created layers of ripples, and the brilliance of these ripples condensed into countless threads of moonlight silk.","As cold, satin-like moonlight poured from the bright moon, it did not give the gray-haired, gray-eyes man and his Fantasy Breed three-headed hound more time to react.","The man and his hound were sublimated into nothingness under this moonlight.","Lin Yuan could not help but feel somewhat frightened by the world’s change in color after he had activated his Extreme Token.","Not only was the gray-haired gray-eyed man and the three-headed hound instantly obliterated by the moonlight, but even the sturdy dimensional barrier at the dimensional hub, formed during the dimensional rift’s evolution, thinned rapidly. It was continuously being sublimated under the moonlight.","Moreover, this happened even when the moonlight had not targeted the dimensional barrier, which made Lin Yuan amazed by the Moon Empress’ strength.","He could not help but sigh. It turned out that his master possessed such immense strength!","Just by looking at the appearance of the gray-haired, gray-eyed man who had launched the sneak attack, Lin Yuan knew that he had not belonged to the Radiance Federation.","Moreover, this Seventh Page War he had mentione and his strange name of Hunting-Ashes were details that Lin Yuan engraved in his heart.","Even if Lin Yuan did not know whom ‘Seventh Page War’ and ‘Hunting-Ashes’ referred to exactly, he would inform the Moon Empress of this news if he could get out.","Given her knowledge, she would very likely know what kind of force was planning all of this.","However, at that moment, Lin Yuan had already focused part of his thoughts on the dimensional hub and was waiting for its barrier to disappear beneath the shining moonlight.","His remaining thoughts were all concentrated on Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan continually channeled the vitality in the Vitality Imprint on his forehead into Liu Jie’s body through the Jasmine Lily.","However, during this healing process, Lin Yuan discovered that given his Jasmine Lily’s grade, even if he were to expand all of the vitality in his Vitality Imprint, the most he could do was suspend Liu Jie’s life for a while to prevent his immediate death.","As he was using the Jasmine Lily, Lin Yuan noticed that more and more pus was oozing out of the wound in Liu Jie’s mutilated torso that was soaked in purplish-gray poison.","This poison was now spreading rapidly, such that even Liu Jie’s cheeks were stained purplish-gray.","Lin Yuan walked towards Liu Jie’s front, smelled the scent of pus and blood emanating from the latter’s wound, and suddenly felt a prick within his spirit.","Lin Yuan could not help but hold his breath.","Previously, he had seen pus leaking non-stop from Liu Jie’s wound. At first, he had just assumed that the purplish-gray poison was one that caused extreme damage to flesh and blood.","However, he had not expected that its real effectiveness lay not only in its capacity to cause extreme damage to one’s flesh and blood but also in its ability to severely harm one’s spirit.","Lin Yuan hurriedly turned all of the Jasmine Lily’s flower heads to face Liu Jie’s head and channeled a massive amount of vitality into it as quickly as he could.","He did this in the hopes that this colossal amount of vitality would disperse the purplish-gray poison.","Even if it could not, Lin Yuan still wanted to protect Liu Jie’s brain by suppressing the spread of the poison to it.","Otherwise, even if Liu Jie’s life was suspended, he would become a vegetative person unable to regain consciousness due to the destruction of his spirit.","Immediately afterward, Lin Yuan realized that even as the vitality channeled more quickly by the Jasmine Lily into Liu Jie’s body suppressed the spread of the purplish-gray poison, it also appeared to be nourishing the poison.","The poison became more active in the areas to which it had spread, preventing Liu Jie’s physical recovery.","Originally, after Liu Jie had been injured, and the poison had entered his body; he had been experiencing constant, unbearable torture within his spirit.","This sharp pain in his spirit had completely numbed Liu Jie to his physical pain.","In the process, Liu Jie’s spiritual energy grew progressively weaker, and his thoughts became increasingly chaotic.","He even faintly felt that his spirit had broken its connection with the Insect Queen.","However, thanks to the Jasmine Lily’s 100 flower heads channeling vitality into his body all together, Liu Jie’s initially chaotic spirit seemed to recover a trace of clarity.","He could faintly discern Lin Yuan’s figure standing by his side, healing him.","It was just that the more Liu Jie wished to see the scene before him, the more the sharp pain prevented him from doing so.","When Liu Jie tried to open his mouth to speak, he squirmed his lips but found that his chin seemed to have been dislocated in the explosion. He could not open his teeth to spit out even a single word.","Liu Jie forced his spirit into clarity and finally determined that Lin Yuan was indeed standing beside him.","A relaxed smile instantly replaced the originally pained expression on Liu Jie’s face.","He wanted to reach his hand out and touch the Class 2 Creation Master crest that he always wore on his chest, but he found that his spirit had started to grow chaotic again.","At the last moment, Liu Jie exerted all of his strength but found that he still could not feel the familiar sensation of the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest.","At that moment, perhaps due to the severe pain in his spirit, Liu Jie did not realize that he had already lost his arms and legs.","Upon seeing that the stubborn purplish-gray spirit poison continued to damage Liu Jie’s already invaded body despite the infusion of the Jasmine Lily’s boundless vitality, Lin Yuan was on the verge of despair.","Then, Lin Yuan’s eyes suddenly lit up.","It was as though he had found a new hope amidst his despair."]},{"number":512,"title":"Chapter 512: Evolve, Jasmine Lily!","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan suddenly remembered the large jar of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar that the Moon Empress had given him.","Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar could restore damaged roots and wash away any impurities in the body.","As the purplish-gray poison had already dissolved in Liu Jie’s body, this harmful foreign substance could obviously be regarded as an impurity in his body.","Once he made this connection, Lin Yuan immediately sprang into action, taking the large jar of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar out of his amber-button-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","Following which, he quickly proceeded to take out the big bowl that he had previously used when he had last taken the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Lin Yuan then filled the bowl to the brim with nectar from the jar while looking at the tortured expression on Liu Jie’s face under the effects of the purplish-gray poison.","Lin Yuan’s heart constricted more tightly.","Just as he was preparing to open Liu Jie’s mouth, Lin Yuan noticed that Liu Jie’s jaw had already been dislocated at some point in time.","Lin Yuan pushed up Liu Jie’s jaw forcefully with his hand, and the latter’s dislocated jaw was put back with a ‘click’.","Slowly, Lin Yuan poured the brimming bowl of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar into Liu Jie’s mouth.","After all of the nectar had been poured, Lin Yuan instantly ripped off a piece of cloth from his moon-white spirit qi clothes.","He then rolled the cloth and let Liu Jie bite it in his mouth.","Lin Yuan had experienced the pain caused by Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar before. Moreover, the purplish-gray poison was still wreaking havoc within Liu Jie’s body.","Lin Yuan truly feared that Liu Jie might bite his own tongue off while bearing these two kinds of pain stacked on top of each other.","Soon, the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar performed its function within Liu Jie’s body, although it caused Liu Jie’s expression to grow even more pained.","The nectar replenished his physical strength, giving Liu Jie the strength to fight.","Upon seeing Liu Jie struggle while unconscious, Lin Yuan’s eyes grew increasingly scarlet.","He gnashed his teeth tightly, forcing himself to calm down and check on Liu Jie’s physical condition after the latter had taken the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Lin Yuan quickly realized that the purplish-gray spirit poison did not stand a fighting chance against the nectar.","Following Liu Jie’s violent struggle, the poison drained out of his body as a thick substance.","Simultaneously, many stains were secreted on Liu Jie’s left torso.","Upon seeing this, Lin Yuan was pleasantly surprised!","This proved that the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar had already completely removed the purplish-gray spirit poison from Liu Jie’s body.","After the poison had been cleansed, Liu Jie immediately fainted under the two kinds of immense pain that he had been under.","Lin Yuan could finally let the Jasmine Lily use its exclusive skill to heal Liu Jie’s mutilated body.","It was just that the Jasmine Lily’s strength was still insufficient now.","Given its Silver I/Fantasy I strength, it would not be able to help Liu Jie recover from such grievous injury.","However, this was not an insurmountable problem for Lin Yuan.","Now, Lin Yuan rejoiced that he had previously used Morbius’ exclusive skill, Pure Land of Bliss, to absorb the Cold Snow Pine’s World Grace.","He had not immediately used up the condensed spirit qi crystals but kept them instead.","Lin Yuan let the Jasmine Lily continue giving out vitality to suspend Liu Jie’s life.","Afterwards, under the full moonlight, Lin Yuan entered his Spirit Lock spatial zone directly.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope rapidly sprinted to Lin Yuan’s side.","However, Lin Yuan simply did not have the time to interact with it at this time.","Upon seeing that Lin Yuan had not acknowledged it, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope did not feel lost.","It was just like a little follower that followed closely behind Lin Yuan.","Perhaps because it sensed Lin Yuan’s anxiety and seriousness, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope also slowed down as it walked.","It did not skip or jump while walking on tiptoes, as it usually did.","Lin Yuan walked over to the spirit pool and caught the Sea Burial Lotus Flower within it that was frantically devouring the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s abundance of spirit qi.","Having previously been disciplined by Lin Yuan, the Sea Burial Lotus Flower clearly still remembered him.","However, before it could even sway its flower branches and greet the enemy who had given it such a pleasant living environment, Lin Yuan had already smashed its flowers in his hand and torn off the Sobbing Sea Crystals that had condensed at its roots.","After its Sobbing Sea Crystals had been ripped off, the Sea Burial Lotus Flower’s grade plummeted to Normal I/Normal in an instant.","Lin Yuan continued to raise the Normal I/Normal Sea Burial Lotus Flower in the spirit pool.","With Spirit Lock spatial zone’s pure and rich spirit qi, Lin Yuan knew that his act would not affect the Sea Burial Lotus Flower’s roots.","He then took the spirit qi crystals that he hadn’t had the time to properly count before. After giving 30 of them to Gray, he had roughly 270 crystals left.","Following this, Lin Yuan exited the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He prepared to use the Sobbing Sea Crystals, condensed from the pressing of an area of sea by the Sea Burial Lotus Flower, and the remaining 270 spirit qi crystals to maximally increase the Jasmine Lily’s grade.","Then, he would again use the evolved Jasmine Lily to treat Liu Jie’s mutilated body.","Lin Yuan could not guarantee that this would cure Liu Jie.","After all, with the severity of Liu Jie’s injuries, anyone would be helpless when placed in the same situation as Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie’s 75 kilograms had now been blown up to the point that there was no more than half of it left.","Even with the Jasmine Lily’s exclusive skill of Severed Limbs Growth, Lin Yuan did not dare to guarantee that it could heal this kind of injury.","Nevertheless, with the Sea Burial Lotus Flower, Lin Yuan was confident that the Jasmine Lily could evolve from Fantasy I to Fantasy III.","When a Fantasy Breed fey evolved from Fantasy I to Fantasy III, it would inevitably metamorphose.","Moreover, as the Jasmine Lily’s Silver grade evolved, it was very likely to mutate.","Hence, it was highly probable that the Jasmine Lily’s healing ability would be strengthened.","Lin Yuan did not scramble to give the Sea Burial Lotus Flower to the Jasmine Lily. Instead, he took out nine spirit qi crystals directly and raised the Jasmine Lily’s grade from Silver I to Silver X.","Right after, Lin Yuan took out another ten spirit qi crystals and smashed them without even blinking.","He let the Silver X/Fantasy I Jasmine Lily absorb this abundance of pure spirit qi.","In the process, the Jasmine Lily’s entire body suddenly lit up with a dazzling emerald green luster.","On its previously fasciated petals, emerald green luster of different colors flickered, causing an emerald haze to rise from the entire Jasmine Lily in an instant.","As the fasciated petals flickered, it appeared as though all of these emerald hues were being transported to the Jasmine Lily’s huge, unfasciated head."]},{"number":513,"title":"Chapter 513: Completely Transformed Jasmine Lily","paragraphs":["Suddenly, the Jasmine Lily’s unfasciated main flower lit up with a bright emerald green luster.","Looking at it, Lin Yuan noticed that many fine crystal threads were continuously growing from it.","These fine crystal threads combined together, continuously entangling and merging until they finally seemed to become a complete crystal.","Lin Yuan knew that this was because the Jasmine Lily had evolved from Silver to Gold.","Now, its unfasciated main flower seemed to have transformed into an emerald green crystal with countless layers.","There appeared to be a few dark green flashes within this crystal.","As the crystallized main flower revolved, although the dark green luster had only flashed once for a moment and had not been obvious, it had a more eye-catching color than the main flower.","The Jasmine Lily’s grade had already evolved from its initial Silver X/Fantasy I to Gold I/Fantasy I.","As a healing-type fey for Morbius’ Spirit Lock, it was now the same grade as Lin Yuan’s main fey, the Source Sand.","Lin Yuan sighed as he watched the Jasmine Lily’s evolution to Gold.","It was entirely a miracle that his Jasmine Lily had been able to evolve to its current grade.","As a succulent plant, the typical Jasmine Lily rarely developed bunches or underwent the fasciation that followed.","It happened that only high-grade succulent plants had a small chance of undergoing crystallization.","Lin Yuan did not know whether it had been his own or the Jasmine Lily’s good fortune.","Now, if the Gold/Fantasy Jasmine Lily were to be taken out, no one would believe that it was a Jasmine Lily anymore.","After crystallization, the healing beam released by the Jasmine Lily’s main flower was faintly mottled with a dark green luster.","Lin Yuan could clearly sense that the healing strength in Heal was now more than ten times greater than before.","Under the supply of this kind of healing strength and vitality, even Liu Jie’s broken body began to slowly grow limbs.","However, although his limbs were slowly growing out, Liu Jie’s broken torso did not show any indication that it would be rejuvenated.","Moreover, Liu Jie’s broken torso was not the most difficult problem facing Lin Yuan right now.","For Lin Yuan, the most serious problem was that Liu Jie’s five internal organs had been shattered in the recent purplish-gray energy explosion.","Lin Yuan took a deep breath and began to work on the Jasmine Lily’s next evolution.","Lin Yuan channeled numerous spirit qi crystals into the Gold I Jasmine Lily as though they were not worth so much money.","As the spirit qi crystals poured into it, the Jasmine Lily’s grade also continuously evolved to...","Gold II...","Gold III...","...","All the way to Gold X!","In the process, Lin Yuan used up a total of 90 spirit qi crystals.","The instant that the Jasmine Lily reached Gold X, Lin Yuan directly channeled the Sobbing Sea Crystals in his hand into the Jasmine Lily’s crystallized main flower.","Immediately afterwards, Lin Yuan squeezed hard and crushed 100 spirit qi crystals.","The spirit qi tornado and Sobbing Sea Crystals raised by the shattering of these 100 spirit qi crystals led the Jasmine Lily to evolve once more.","However, as the Jasmine Lily was evolving, Lin Yuan felt anticipation and endless anxiety.","If the Jasmine Lily was still unable to cure Liu Jie after this evolution, Lin Yuan would not have any other means to heal him.","Then, Liu Jie would truly be done for!","Lin Yuan suddenly remembered what Liu Jie had said while blocking the purplish-gray energy that should have hit him.","“Lin Yuan, I made an appointment with you and Wen Yu before. Unfortunately, ten years later, I will be absent from the grass.”","Lin Yuan’s thoughts returned to a time when the mansion had just been built. It had taken place in late autumn, one evening on the mansion’s grass.","At that time, Endless Summer and Hu Quan had not yet joined the mansion, while the Mother of Bloodbath had not yet transformed into its human form.","At that time, he, Liu Jie, and Wen Yu had been barbecuing and drinking on the grass in the evening breeze.","At that time, that glass of beer had been the first drink in Lin Yuan’s life.","Lin Yuan had not drunk much alcohol in his previous life, and his face had always immediately turned red after drinking a little.","In this new life, Lin Yuan realized that this had not changed.","Lin Yuan remembered that he had sighed after becoming slightly drunk.","“I hope that after ten years, we can all sit together on this grass in the evening breeze, raise our glasses, and discuss our ideals.”","Lin Yuan’s originally casual words had been firmly engraved in Liu Jie’s heart.","Lin Yuan looked at the sleeping Liu Jie with red eyes and said softly, “Ten years later, none of us will be allowed to be absent on the grass.”","Suddenly, the emerald green haze that had risen from the steadily evolving Jasmine Lily turned into a magnificent red.","Lin Yuan hurriedly looked over and realized that the disappearance of the magnificent red glow had left the Jasmine Lily yet again completely transformed.","Lin Yuan could not even recognize it.","The Jasmine Lily’s originally small size had been reduced by more than half.","Lin Yuan held the evolved Jasmine Lily in his hand and found that its size was now extremely suitable.","There was no longer the same feeling as before of holding two basketballs.","However, if the current Jasmine Lily were not Lin Yuan’s contracted fey, he would never have believed that this was a Jasmine Lily, even if he were a Creation Master.","The Jasmine Lily’s originally fasciated parts had already turned dark red. It had also been compressed such that it now vaguely resembled a square.","It was comparable to a squarish flower stand carved with many strange flowers.","Above the flower stand, a crimson crystalline flower the size of a bowl bloomed brightly.","However, there was a blood-red luster that looked coquettish to the extreme within this flower.","A long spike of about 15 centimeters with a small emerald green flower bud on it grew on this flower.","A long pistil stuck out of the bud.","No matter how he looked at it, Lin Yuan found that this tiny flower bud and its long, protruding pistil were the main body of the evolved Jasmine Lily.","The verdure carried by this tiny flower bud, smaller than a little finger, far surpassed all the verdant colors on Jasmine Lily’s entire body when it was at Gold X."]},{"number":514,"title":"Chapter 514: Bud of Mountain Jade","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Although the evolved Gold/Fantasy Jasmine Lily had been unrecognizable to ordinary people, some Class 4 and Class 5 Scholars would still be able to uncover its essence upon investigation.","However, after its subsequent evolution, Class 4 Scholars were no longer able to see through to its essence.","It was likely that if the Class 5 Scholars did not hold it in their hands and study it carefully for a few days, they would not have been able to guess that this specimen before them had evolved from a Jasmine Lily.","Lin Yuan quickly used Morbius’ True Data to scan the evolved Jasmine Lily.","[Normal Spirit Lock]:","Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade): Platinum (1/10)/Fantasy III","Ability – [Heal]:","– Fasciated Flower Stand: Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target, absorbing its vitality and letting it experience extreme comfort at the same time.","– Crystallized Main Flower: Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target and absorb a large amount of its vitality.","– Bud of Mountain Jade: Its Heal ability will heal the target and channel rich vitality into it through its Bud of Mountain Jade, restoring the target’s damaged vitality.","Exclusive Skill:","[Recovery Imprint]: It accumulates the healing energy that is released by the Jasmine Lily during normal times. The contractor can activate the imprint to release the accumulated healing energy.","[Severed Limbs Growth]: It comprehends the arcana of plant growth. Even if one’s gene template is damaged, the rich vitality can allow one to continue to grow slowly.","With this scan, Lin Yuan felt that his eyeballs almost fell to the ground.","He hurriedly stopped letting the Jasmine Lily’s dark red Fasciated Flower Stand and its blood-red Crystallized Main Flower continue to heal Liu Jie.","If he let them continue healing Liu Jie, he would be harming the latter.","Lin Yuan could not understand where he had gone wrong!","Was the Sea Burial Lotus Flower’s Sobbing Sea Crystals the reason?","The Sea Burial Lotus Flower only condensed Sobbing Sea Crystals after it had deprived the entire ocean of vitality.","Now, after the Jasmine Lily had used the Sobbing Sea Crystals to evolve, it had also assimilated some of the Sea Burial Lotus Flower’s skills.","Could these skills not have been integrated in the Jasmine Lily’s Heal ability?","This was still the first time that Lin Yuan had heard of reverse-healing.","Had his own Jasmine Lily fey just turned from a big blood bag that could only donate blood into a blood-sucking vampire?","Moreover, it was now an unscrupulous vampire!","Absorbing the vitality in the body of any living being was an extremely cruel means of harming it.","It was still considered normal that the Crystallized Main Flower’s Heal ability directly extracted the target’s vitality.","However, the Fasciated Flower Stand actually allowed the target to retain the extreme pleasure experienced during healing while reverse-healing it.","To suck your blood and still let you feel extremely comfortable in the process was truly something that a considerate being would do!","Damn!","The direction of its affinity was healing and support!","How had a well-behaved fey like the Jasmine Lily even begun to become so reckless?","At that instant, Lin Yuan was too ashamed to even enact the Forge-Sister-into-Iron-Bucket 3.0 plan again.","However, he had to swear solemnly to the sky that he had never intended to make the Jasmine Lily so reckless.","Under True Data’s recent scan, the Jasmine Lily’s name had already been changed to Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade), and its grade had already evolved to Platinum I.","This time, the Jasmine Lily had consumed more than half of the spirit qi crystals that Lin Yuan had preserved by using Morbius’ Pure Land of Bliss to absorb Cold Snow Pine’s World Grace.","In order to evolve to a Platinum I/Fantasy III fey, the Silver I/Fantasy I Jasmine Lily had used up 199 spirit qi crystals and a whole piece of Sea Burial Lotus Flower.","Now, only 71 spirit qi crystals remained in Lin Yuan’s hand.","In order to heal Liu Jie, Lin Yuan had chosen to evolve its only healing-type fey, Jasmine Lily.","This was tantamount to giving up the good opportunity of using so many spirit qi crystals to improve his fighting ability.","Yet, he had not thought that the originally honest Jasmine Lily would suddenly have grown so reckless.","It had transformed from a well-behaved healing-type fey into a large needle that could absorb energy ‘milk’.","If Lin Yuan’s Gold I/Fantasy II Source Sand had previously given him Platinum fighting ability to fight in one Radiance Hundred Sequence battle,","then his Platinum I/Fantasy III Jasmine Lily now gave him the ability to stand firm in countless Radiance Hundred Sequence battles.","It could be said that if there were really to be a fight, the Platinum I/Fantasy III Jasmine Lily would directly surpass the Source Sand to become Lin Yuan’s main fey.","As a healing-type spirit qi professional who now had a Platinum/Fantasy healing-type fey, Lin Yuan was now akin to sweet pastry that everyone wanted to snatch up.","To Lin Yuan, the Platinum I/Fantasy III Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade) was somewhat strange no matter how he looked at it.","Part of it that had originally been vibrant green had turned bloody red, making it give up its healing ability.","However, at the same time as this transformation, an emerald bud had bloomed on its top like a ridge.","This bud had perfectly inherited the Jasmine Lily’s original positive healing ability.","It was equivalent to an attack ability that the Jasmine Lily had drawn out of thin air.","With that in mind, Lin Yuan suddenly saw the good in the Jasmine Lily!Wonderful recklessness! Top-notch recklessness!","So what if it was a healing-type fey? Such fey should be reckless!","Besides, it could still heal!","Taking your blood, returning my blood... I don’t care if you’re upset, because I’m not.","Moreover, with the Fasciated Flower Stand, it would not do for you to be upset.","Pressed for time, Lin Yuan did not closely inspect the recently evolved Platinum I/Fantasy III Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade) in his hand.","He immediately let the Bud of Mountain Jade at the top of its Crystallized Main Flower use its Heal ability to treat Liu Jie.","As Lin Yuan channeled the majestic vitality in his Vitality Imprint into the Jasmine Lily’s Bud of Mountain Jade, the emerald bloods blooming on its blood-red crystallized flowers sprayed a mist of vitality like a cloud.","As this mist of vitality fell on Liu Jie continuously, his broken torso slowly recovered."]},{"number":515,"title":"Chapter 515: Treatment and Rolling Grade","paragraphs":["The sight of Liu Jie’s broken body slowly starting to recover as it basked in the Bud of Mountain Jade’s glowing vitality immediately put a smile on Lin Yuan’s face.","Lin Yuan closed his eyes and focused on sensing Liu Jie’s current physical condition.","After the Bud of Mountain Jade’s vitality scattered, Lin Yuan could sense that it had regenerated Liu Jie’s organs.","When he was done with his inspection, Lin Yuan felt a heavy weight lift from his shoulders.","However, the rate at which Liu Jie was recovering was too slow!","The dimensional hub in the distance that was eroding under the moonlight had been reduced to a thin layer of spatial obstacle.","Lin Yuan knew that time was not on Liu Jie’s side, and he could not continue to recover at such a slow pace.","Lin Yuan attempted to inject all the vitality in the Vitality Imprint on his forehead into the Bud of Mountain Jade at the top of the Jasmine Lily.","The vitality in Lin Yuan’s Vitality Imprint came from the Jasmine Lily’s accumulation when it had been Silver I/Fantasy I, but it was now Platinum/Fantasy III.","The Bud of Mountain Jade received all of the vitality Lin Yuan was directing.","The small Bud of Mountain Jade growing on the tassels started to vibrate intensely after receiving the massive amount of energy.","A dark green pistil sprouting from the Bud of Mountain Jade started to ripple gently.","The gentle ripples brought the dark green waves of concentrated energy with them, which coalesced into one dark green droplet.","When Lin Yuan saw the droplet, a thought entered his mind.","If life can be interpreted in terms of color, vitality has to be represented by this dark green. The dark green droplet must contain all the vitality from my Vitality Imprint. This means the Vitality Imprint on my forehead is now empty.","The dark green droplet landed on Liu Jie, and his body started to pulse with jade-colored ripples.","Shortly after, the jade-colored glow enveloped Liu Jie’s body.","When the jade-colored cocoon broke soon after, Liu Jie fell out onto the ground looking as good as new.","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie was completely drained after the double attack of the purplish-gray poison and the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Unfortunately, Lin Yuan did not possess any feys that could replenish energy.","Lin Yuan grabbed a bunch of Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus from the Spirit Lock spatial zone and crushed the petals before placing them in Liu Jie’s mouth. He helped Liu Jie swallow by pouring water down his throat.","He also instructed Morbius to use Calm Mind on Liu Jie.","With this, Lin Yuan had done all he could to aid Liu Jie.","It could also be said that Lin Yuan had undertaken a major risk as well.","As a C-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan should only be able to control feys that were a maximum of Gold/Fantasy X.","He had decided to gather his courage because his attempt at using the Gold/Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily to heal Liu Jie had proved futile.","He had come up with this plan because he had heard the Moon Empress talk once about how some top factions would use Rolling Grade when nurturing the younger experts. It allowed the younger generation’s contracted feys to be able to break through the spirit qi professional’s supposed maximum grade of fey they could contract.","It was said that this required a rare fey called the Starlight Intelligent Dark Clouds as well as other resources.","The utilization of so many resources would allow a person’s fey to only break through a small grade. It was too much of a waste.","The top factions still went ahead with it because the small breakthrough was enough to greatly raise the younger generation expert’s individual power.","They would be able to attain more glory while still providing the younger generation with more means of protecting themselves.","As long as a young person’s contracted fey exhibited signs of Rolling Grade, it indicated that the young person came from an impressive background.","Naturally, the Moon Empress had not elaborated on the details, and Lin Yuan was none the wiser.","The crux had to do with the level of spiritual energy.","After evolving to Platinum, feys would experience a large increase in wisdom and spiritual energy.","Spirit qi professionals who could not reach B-rank would be a large burden to Platinum feys in terms of spiritual energy.","Their contracted fey would even inhibit the spirit qi professional’s spiritual energy.","If such an event occurred, said spirit qi professional would suffer spiritual collapse and permanent spiritual damage.","Given that the Jasmine Lily was Morbius’ exclusive Spirit Lock fey, its spirit was connected to Morbius.","It would not significantly impact Lin Yuan even if it underwent Rolling Grade.","At the very most, Lin Yuan would be exhausted after commanding the Platinum/Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily.","After communicating with Morbius, Lin Yuan had decided that the Jasmine Lily would undergo Rolling Grade.","This would allow Lin Yuan, as a C-rank spirit qi professional, to be able to command Platinum/Fantasy Breed feys.","Luckily, Lin Yuan’s hard work and risk-taking did not go to waste.","After Lin Yuan treated Liu Jie, he pushed through his ragged breathing and placed the purple flesh cocoon beside Liu Jie.","The purplish-gray liquid leaking out of the purple flesh cocoon was darker.","The purplish-gray poison had spread throughout the Insect Queen’s body, giving the purple flesh cocoon an odd darker hue.","The Insect Queen needed to be attended to immediately.","Being a Creation Master, Lin Yuan could clearly sense the Insect Queen’s situation.","The Insect Queen was a fairy source-type lifeform.","The purplish-gray poison had already started to eat away at the Insect Queen’s spirit, which was extremely detrimental to the Insect Queen.","The Insect Queen was Liu Jie’s only contracted fey. If anything happened to it, even if Liu Jie fully recovered, he would revert to his rudderless mentality before meeting Lin Yuan. He might even deteriorate.","Previously, the Insect Queen might have been at death’s door, but there had still been a ray of hope for its recovery.","But now, death was literally knocking on the Insect Queen’s door.","Lin Yuan scooped a bowl of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar out of the barrel and dripped it into the holes on the Insect Queen’s body."]},{"number":516,"title":"Chapter 516: The Insect Queen’s Metamorphosis and the Two Sacred Source Lifeforms","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar entered the Insect Queen’s body, Lin Yuan took out a spirit qi crystal without hesitation and crushed it in his hand.","What the Insect Queen needed most for its recovery was not vitality but rather an enormous amount of pure spirit qi.","The Insect Queen would start to heal itself after it absorbed the pure spirit qi.","Being a Platinum/Fantasy Breed source-type lifeform, the Insect Queen had strong recovery capabilities.","Moreover, with a treasure like the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, it would be child’s play to expel the purplish-gray poison.","However, Lin Yuan frowned deeply at what happened next.","Instead of the purplish-gray poison being expelled in the form of a thick substance flowing out of the holes, like what had happened to Liu Jie, the Insect Queen absorbed the purplish-gray poison along with the enormous amount of spirit qi.","Before Lin Yuan could react, the Insect Queen’s purple flesh cocoon suddenly squirted out a large volume of gummy insect protein.","After being expelled, the insect protein changed from transparent to creamy white.","The creamy white insect protein started to harden, sealing the Insect Queen inside.","Lin Yuan immediately used Morbius’ True Data to check on the Insect Queen.","He found that the Insect Queen was undergoing metamorphosis.","Lin Yuan sighed. “Could the Insect Queen’s metamorphosis have something to do with the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar?”","The Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar was used to purge impurities and repair damaged roots. It was not supposed to trigger metamorphosis.","Thus, the Insect Queen’s sudden metamorphosis had to be linked to the purplish-gray poison.","Besides being unable to battle on the water, Liu Jie’s mastery over using the Insect Queen’s abilities had grown into a near-perfect fighting combination on land.","Hence, the Insect Queen’s abrupt metamorphosis might not be a positive change.","Who could say how Liu Jie’s fighting style would change after the Insect Queen’s transformation?","Liu Jie was the kind of spirit qi professional that prioritized directing an insect army on the battlefield and adjusted the insect types accordingly.","He had a set fighting style.","Unlike other spirit qi professionals, Liu Jie did not have many feys. He only had the Insect Queen.","The slightest change to the Insect Queen could have untold impacts on Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan could only rely on himself to treat the Insect Queen, and he could not predict what kind of changes would occur as a result of his methods.","Whether this would be a blessing or a curse, it depended on Liu Jie’s fate!","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard something akin to a mirror-shattering sound.","Lin Yuan dashed at the evolving dimensional hub.","Soon, another twist took place as Lin Yuan ran toward the dimensional hub.","The waterfall of moonbeams in the sky could sense Lin Yuan’s aura and did not make a move against Zhou Luo or Liu Jie.","The shell blanketing the mass of rainbow light at the dimensional hub was illuminated by the moonlight and disintegrated.","Without the shell, the mass of rainbow light at the dimensional hub emitted a rainbow glow.","Lin Yuan suddenly realized that the dimensional rift that was supposed to only finish evolving in ten minutes had been torn open.","Another glowing rainbow mass fell from the torn open dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan’s expression changed completely. It struck him what the glowing rainbow mass was.","The glowing rainbow mass, whose identity had Liu Jie been speculating all this time, was the legendary sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan never expected the Extreme Token that the Moon Empress had gifted him would be of aid at such a crucial moment.","The moonlight might have mostly quenched the dimensional hub’s spatial fluctuations, but the dimensional rift was still being torn wider under the rainbow glow of the two sacred source lifeforms.","Lin Yuan seemed to catch a glimpse of a seemingly endless water world through the rift.","Lin Yuan could also feel the intensely powerful aura surging out of the water world.","The boundless ocean water was pouring out of the water world.","At this moment, the majestic moonlight beamed down as though it was headed for a target.","The moonlight and water crashed together, and the moonlight utterly sublimed the water.","The moment the moonlight sublimed the water, Lin Yuan felt the energy in the Extreme Token hanging on his chest deplete.","Lin Yuan finally witnessed his Master’s true power.","The Moon Empress’s moonlight domain was currently combating the entire Class 5 dimensional rift and immediately sublimating any of the powerful energy flowing out of the dimensional rift. Not even one drop of water managed to land on the gravel by Lin Yuan’s feet.","Lin Yuan stuck his arm into the dimensional hub without a second thought.","He was going to stop the dimensional rift’s evolution!","Zhou Luo and Liu Jie risked their lives for me to be here! All I can do now is to stand straight and make use of the window opened for me that is the sublimating waters.","Before the energy in the Extreme Token was completely gone, he needed to remove the two sacred source lifeforms.","Despite the moonlight suppressing the dimensional hub’s energy, Lin Yuan’s hand immediately desiccated when it entered the dimensional hub.","Lin Yuan had anticipated this, but the excruciating pain of his mangled arm had turned to numbness, to the point that Lin Yuan did not immediately feel the pain.","Lin Yuan ground his teeth as he fought through the pain—the grinding of his jaw was so loud that it sounded as though Lin Yuan’s teeth were about to break.","His fingers were connected to his heart, as were his palms, wrist, and forearm.","The spatial energy in the dimensional hub was like sticky mud. Even if Lin Yuan exerted all his strength, his arm could only inch forward.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan shouted, “Bud of Mountain Jade, Heal!”","Lin Yuan pumped the remaining spirit qi in the Spirit Qi Imprint into the Jasmine Lily.","It was not because Lin Yuan was afraid of being seriously hurt and was trying to heal himself. He was afraid that his bones would break and prevent him from retrieving the two sacred source lifeforms.","If that happened, all his effort would go down the drain.","The sand was whipping around!","The moon hung high in the sky!","The torrents of water were surging!","The moonlight was youthful and stained with a blood-red glow.","The youth’s arm started to reveal bone, but his gaze remained steadfast as his arm continued to stretch out toward the two glowing rainbow sacred source lifeforms."]},{"number":517,"title":"Chapter 517: The Terrified Sacred Source Lifeforms","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan stood there. His usually pristinely straight spine was now hunched over and quivering.","Lin Yuan was worried that the energy in his Extreme Token would run out quickly while combating the Class 5 dimensional rift.","However, Lin Yuan never expected that the spirit qi in his Spirit Qi Imprint would run out before the energy in the Extreme Token.","Lin Yuan had been activating the Bud of Mountain Jade to heal his injured arms, but he had underestimated the depletion of the Platinum/Fantasy III Jasmine Lily’s spirit qi, as well as the severity of his injuries.","The dimensional energy in the dimensional hub was like sharp knives that were slicing apart each inch of Lin Yuan’s skin that was in the dimensional hub.","Not even the supple skin between his fingers was spared.","With every dimensional fluctuation, agonizing pain pierced Lin Yuan’s brain.","The dimensional fluctuations took place every second.","Lin Yuan’s brain was dizzy with anguish, and it soon started to feel numb.","To make matters worse, Lin Yuan also needed to withstand the draining feeling that came with having the spirit qi in his body siphoned out.","It was already enough of a struggle for spirit qi professionals to fight through the feeling of having their spirit qi siphoned out, much less when they needed to endure torturous pain as well, like what Lin Yuan was doing.","His determined expression was partially obscured by the sand blowing around in the air.","Even if Lin Yuan’s Source Sand was not particularly intelligent, it could still sense Lin Yuan’s current condition.","The flying sand was the Source Sand’s way of motivating Lin Yuan.","The Genius mask that Lin Yuan was wearing fell from his face, and the silver mask turned into a three-tailed white cat.","When Genius saw Lin Yuan, its blue eyes welled up with tears.","Instead of snuggling into Lin Yuan’s embrace like what it usually did, it jumped onto Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","Genius knew that if it touched Lin Yuan, it could very well be the last strand that caused Lin Yuan to collapse, effectively wasting all his effort.","Although Lin Yuan was dizzy, numb with fatigue and pain, and seemed as though he could fall asleep at any moment, his mind was actually exceptionally clear.","Even if he only had one breath left in him, Lin Yuan was going to retrieve the two sacred source lifeforms—it was the last thing he would do.","Unfortunately, the damage to his hands was too serious.","The Bud of Mountain Jade could not receive Lin Yuan’s spirit qi, and no matter how much it tried to use Heal on Lin Yuan, his hands would not recover as fast as he was worsening.","In a flash, Lin Yuan’s hands had been reduced to a mere slip of flesh.","The helplessness and pain from being drained of spirit qi combined with the blood loss from his hands weakened him severely.","The three centimeters separating his hand from the source-type lifeforms suddenly felt more like miles to the determined Lin Yuan.","Morbius’ voice rang out from beside Lin Yuan’s ear.","“You can do it, Yuan!”","Along with Morbius’ voice that came from Lin Yuan’s spiritual spatial zone, Morbius also used Calm Mind on him.","During the short period of comfort that came from Calm Mind, a stunning magnificence radiated from between his brows, and Lin Yuan mustered all the strength in him for one final stretch.","One hand after the other closed in on the glowing rainbow masses.","As he lurched forward, he grabbed and swiped all the source-type lifeforms out of the dimensional hub.","Lin Yuan crashed onto the gravel.","The flying gravel was like a bed of cotton that gently cushioned his fall.","Utter exhaustion was evident on Lin Yuan’s face, but the magnificent radiance between his brow was dimming but had not disappeared.","He had just experienced a gut-wrenching fight with death.","The dimming radiance was now wider than his shoulders.","The Bud of Mountain Jade’s healing light continued to work on Lin Yuan’s injured hands.","Lin Yuan immediately felt a numbing itch of pain on his hands.","Lin Yuan silently endured as the pain came from the regrowth of new flesh.","This meant his hands were in a state of recovery.","Lin Yuan took a few deep breaths but still could not fully calm himself.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan felt a different kind of pain than the physical one, and he noticed the two glowing rainbow masses in his hand had disappeared.","Once again, Lin Yuan was awash in excruciating anguish.","The pain was similar to the one he had experienced while cleansing his soul of impurities at the Radiant Moon Palace.","After his soul had been cleansed, Lin Yuan never had the chance to see the two human silhouettes in the depths of his soul again.","But now, Lin Yuan’s consciousness returned to the depths of his soul again.","What Lin Yuan found most appalling was that the two glowing rainbow masses were melding with the two human silhouettes in the depths of his soul.","The two glowing rainbow masses were shining brilliantly as they crashed against the human silhouettes like in a fight for dominance.","Lin Yuan remembered that when the Moon Empress had been talking about the sacred source lifeforms, she had mentioned that one needed the help of numerous soul-nourishing spirit ingredients in order to successfully contract the sacred source lifeforms.","One also needed to be at least 20 years old to contract sacred source lifeforms.","If one’s soul was not strong enough, it was highly possible that the sacred source lifeforms would destroy one’s soul.","Lin Yuan had understood from the Moon Empress’s tone how precious sacred source lifeforms were and how dangerous it was to form contracts with them.","Lin Yuan did not know if he was blessed or cursed.","He never expected that the sacred source lifeforms’ method of contraction was forming blood contracts.","Because of the bloodied state of his hands when he had reached out for the sacred source lifeforms, the contract-forming process had immediately begun.","Lin Yuan could not deny how lucky he was.","Normally, people required the help of soul-nourishing spiritual ingredients to form a contract with a sacred source lifeform.","Yet, he started to contract two sacred source lifeforms without any soul-nourishing spirit ingredients. It was a disaster!","Lin Yuan could feel his soul silhouettes repeatedly being smashed under the power of the two sacred source lifeforms.","The agony of having his soul shattered could not even be compared to physical pain.","Just as the two sacred source lifeforms were about to destroy Lin Yuan’s soul, Lin Yuan lost consciousness.","At that moment, Morbius lit up again.","The light coming from Morbius was no longer creamy white, like when it was using Calm Mind, but rather a gold light that shone out of its body.","Initially, both the soul silhouettes and sacred source lifeforms in the depths of Lin Yuan’s soul refused to give in.","They fought ferociously like two lions clashing over territory. All they wanted was to take over Lin Yuan’s soul in order to complete the contract.","However, when the gold light lit up from within Morbius, the two glowing rainbow masses pulsed.","It was as though they had encountered something terrifying and were cowering in fright."]},{"number":518,"title":"Chapter 518: The Rabbit’s Broken Carrot","paragraphs":["In the end, the two sacred source lifeforms could not form a contract in the clash against Lin Yuan’s soul silhouettes.","Yet, they seemed terrified of Morbius’ golden light.","The two sacred source lifeforms seemed to stick together reluctantly.","Every corner of Lin Yuan’s soul silhouette radiated rainbow light.","The movements of the two sources of rainbow light did not attack Lin Yuan’s already broken soul silhouette again.","Instead, they melded into one and entered Lin Yuan’s broken soul silhouette.","When the rainbow light scattered, the sacred source lifeforms’ shape could be seen again.","After Morbius lit up with golden light, it seemed as though all the light from the Morbius bracelet was gone.","Morbius’ weak voice sounded in Lin Yuan’s mind. “Yuan, I need to hibernate for a while.”","Morbius continued after pausing. “I’ll be hibernating longer than usual this time. I might not be able to wake up before evolving to Fantasy Breed. However, with the new sacred source lifeform formed from the two sacred source lifeforms, I can sleep without worries.”","Morbius spoke slowly as it was offering affectionate instructions.","Finally, Morbius fell into a deep slumber.","However, Lin Yuan had no idea what took place after losing consciousness.","Inside Lin Yuan’s broken soul silhouette, the sacred source lifeforms looked as though they had been praised by their betters and were in seventh heaven.","They leaped about vigorously with glee inside of the dimensional rift that had stopped evolving.","Without the support of the source-type items, the space inside the dimensional hub was about to disappear.","The unconscious Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Zhou Luo were spat out like pieces of garbage from the disappearing dimensional hub.","...","The black-masked, black-robed woman looked at the halted dimensional rift’s entrance with a grim expression on her face.","She suddenly realized that the woman next to her, who was wearing moon-colored long robes, had a serene expression.","The eeriness and madness of power were almost tangible.","The woman dressed in black uttered, “Oh no.”","The temper of the woman in moon-colored long robes seemed harder to deal with than the evolving dimensional rift.","“Moon Empress, since you arrived earlier, did you find out which faction is behind this dimensional rift?”","The Moon Empress stared unblinkingly at the dimensional rift, ignoring the woman in black.","She spoke with an odd coldness. “Chief Guard Ye, This Empress has not left Leaning Moon Mountain in a decade! Isn’t it a bit stupid to ask This Empress which faction is behind this?”","The Spirit Guards’ Chief Guard Night Leaning Moon immediately knew that she had misspoken.","How could I have forgotten the Moon Empress’ real temper? She’s basically a ticking time bomb! Her composed expression is nothing but a facade.","The root of the Moon Empress’s murderous intent lay in the thought that her disciple might not return alive. If that happened, ten landmasses could sink, and her rage would not be quelled in the slightest.","When the Moon Empress was done speaking, she realized that she had not received the reaction she wanted. Her brows furrowed, but she still did not turn to look at Night Leaning Moon.","“Night Leaning Moon, as the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards, how could you have only sensed such a monumental incident happening right outside Indigo Azure City after so long?”","The Moon Empress’ voice got stuck in her throat.","Night Leaning Moon stood rooted to the ground. The present situation seemed extremely familiar.","20 years ago, when the Moon Empress and I were part of the Radiance Envoy, it was like the Moon Empress was in front while the other three disgusting men and I were at the back. The three disgusting men and I were constantly punished like we were naughty schoolchildren.","20 years later, the only difference is that the three gross men are now gone. The Moon Empress might have said she wanted me here to preside over the situation, but she might as well have summoned me to vent her anger on. This is torturous!","When she heard the sudden choke in the Moon Empress’ voice, Night Leaning Moon, who knew the Moon Empress very well, lifted her head violently.","She noticed a subtle redness in the Moon Empress’ eyes, but it was a gaze that was empty of murderous intent.","The Moon Empress’ murderous intent would only be exhibited through her powers and would not be present on her face.","Normally, it would be surprising for her face to betray any sort of expression.","Now, the redness that had welled up in her eyes reminded Night Leaning Moon of what the Moon Empress had said at the imperial court council while looking at her hand.","She now knew what the Moon Empress meant by “I’m different from who I was before. I’m soft-hearted now.”","Night Leaning Moon took two steps toward the Moon Empress, but she could not decide on the right words of assurance to say.","At that moment, the Moon Empress realized that the dimensional rift’s entrance had vanished.","This sight stunned the ever-calm Moon Empress.","The diminished entrance of the dimensional rift ejected items in a similar fashion to diarrhea before closing for good.","The Moon Empress instantly spotted the bloodied and feeble Lin Yuan on the ground.","In a flash, the Moon Empress was by Lin Yuan’s side. When she saw Lin Yuan’s hands, her face twisted with heartache and worry.","A moonbeam flowed out of the Moon Empress’s fingers. Her expression changed again and again as she checked up on Lin Yuan’s condition.","When she was done with her assessment, the Moon Empress’ face spread into a smile.","Her smile blossomed like flowers.","Her smile seemed to lay all her worries at rest. She sighed and said, “As long as you’re back. As long as you’re back.”","The Moon Empress turned and looked at the sad-looking rabbit squatting by her leg and lifted it into her arms.","“Give me your carrot, Xixi.”","The rabbit gingerly handed over its carrot to the Moon Empress.","At the same time, it stretched out its long ears toward the carrot skin that was peeling upward.","It seemed reluctant despite its resolve.","The Moon Empress snapped the carrot in half with one strong wrench.","The loud snap floored the rabbit in the Moon Empress’s arms, and it resembled the famous painting ‘The Scream’."]},{"number":519,"title":"Chapter 519: Come, Come Home with Master","paragraphs":["After breaking the carrot, the Moon Empress handed half of it to the suddenly sluggish little rabbit in her arms.","Then, she placed the little rabbit on the ground.","Standing by Lin Yuan’s side, the Moon Empress gently placed the other half of the carrot at the corner of his mouth before immediately beginning to urge spirit qi.","Under the Moon Empress’ urging of spirit qi, the half-carrot dissolved into a liquid and flowed into Lin Yuan’s stomach on its own.","After Lin Yuan’s body absorbed the energy in this half-carrot, it immediately transformed as carrot-colored energy radiated from it.","Lin Yuan’s body and soul had long been broken, while his spirit had also fallen into a deep sleep.","However, upon digesting this half carrot, the broken soul silhouette in the depths of Lin Yuan’s soul, together with his arms that had their bones exposed, rapidly recovered.","Mere moments after the half carrot had entered Lin Yuan’s body, everything in it was restored to its original state.","However, Lin Yuan’s soul and spirit were still deep in slumber, just like how a person who had been awake for three days and three nights needed a long night’s rest to replenish his energy.","Although Lin Yuan’s body had completely recovered, the tragedy of what he had just experienced in the dimensional rift would always be engraved on his tattered moon-white spirit qi clothes and the blood that stained them.","At that moment, the little rabbit’s eyes first looked toward Lin Yuan. Upon finding that he was alright, it appeared to release its breath.","Yet, when it lowered its head and saw that it only had half a carrot left in its paws, the little rabbit’s ears immediately drooped to the ground.","It tenderly rubbed its half carrot. Suddenly, the half carrot regrew the part that had been broken by the Moon Empress and became whole again.","However, the newly-grown carrot looked to be smaller than its previous size by a whole round.","The little rabbit had initially decided to continue gnawing on its carrot. However, upon seeing that the carrot had shrunk by a round, it could not bear to put it in its mouth.","Instead, it put the carrot behind its bottom and hid it there.","Night Leaning Moon’s gaze was currently on the other two people the dimensional rift had spat out.","After giving Zhou Luo and Liu Jie a once-over, Night Leaning Moon turned her gaze on Liu Jie.","If one considered Liu Jie to only be a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, then Night Leaning Moon, as the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards, would not have had such a deep impression of him.","Yet, upon looking at him only once, Night Leaning Moon immediately recognized him.","Unexpectedly, Liu Jie was amongst those who had emerged from the evolving dimensional rift.","Night Leaning Moon could not help but recall when Liu Jie had been outside Cold Frost City blocking the insect swarm to help the Spirit Guards face the insect tide for a full half an hour.","She walked to Liu Jie’s side, extended a hand, and inspected his condition. After which, she found that his present physical condition was unusually good.","Unexpectedly, Liu Jie’s internal vitality was in a state of surplus.","Vitality would ooze out of Liu Jie’s body from time to time.","This was clearly because it had received excessive healing.","However, when Night Leaning Moon glanced toward the Insect Queen by Liu Jie’s side, her eyebrows immediately rose. She held the cocooned Insect Queen in her hands and muttered, “This Insect Queen has absorbed the Blade Queen Bee’s natal poison. What good fortune...","“It’s just that there is too little of the Blade Queen Bee’s poison in the Insect Queen’s body to support the Insect Queen’s complete mutation.","“Since that is the case, why don’t I give you some good fortune—”","The Moon Empress suddenly interrupted Night Leaning Moon.","“Night Leaning Moon, This Empress has indeed underestimated you. Even with your stupidity, you became a Class 4 Creation Master in ten years.”","Upon hearing this, the corner of Night Leaning Moon’s mouth could not help but twitch twice behind her black veil.","She thought to herself, How am I stupid?","Back then, had it not been for my lack of talent as a Creation Master, I thought that it would at least be possible to become a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master or even a Class 5 Creation Master.","However, even if I have not become a Class 5 Creation Master, I am still strong!","How can you not praise me?","When I was a Radiance Envoy with you, I was always the main center in the team!","With that, Night Leaning Moon suddenly recalled how she had always been given the cold shoulder when she had been a Radiance Envoy with the Moon Empress.","The involuntary twitching of the corner of Night Leaning Moon’s mouth grew more severe.","At that moment, the Moon Empress spoke again.","“This evolving dimensional rift is at least Class 5.","“Now, its evolution has already been stopped by the three of them. Giving him a Blade Queen Bee is not considered giving him good fortune.”","Upon hearing this, Night Leaning Moon looked at Liu Jie, who was lying on the ground and said after pondering for a while, “All these years, I have never accepted a disciple. Once he awakens, if he is willing to take me as his Master, I will be willing to teach him with all of my heart.”","The Moon Empress could not help but reveal her shock.","It would really be considered good fortune to be accepted as the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards’ disciple.","Immediately, the Moon Empress thought, if Liu Jie was Lin Yuan’s retainer knight and Night Leaning Moon wanted to teach Liu Jie with all of her heart, would she not be working for Lin Yuan indirectly?","That was not bad at all!","Right after Night Leaning Moon had spoken, she looked wordlessly at Zhou Luo and Lin Yuan beside the Moon Empress. Then, she transferred her gaze to the Moon Empress.","Obviously, she was not done speaking.","Upon noticing Night Leaning Moon’s gaze, the Moon Empress immediately said, “Some people are destined to scale mountains and cross oceans. These people do not care about temporary glory.","“Three years later, the five new Radiance Envoys will be decided.”","Having said this, a trace of recollection flashed in the Moon Empress’ eyes.","Right after, the Moon Empress gently let her next sentence drop.","“The enemy is Dark, I know. You can handle this matter as you see fit.”","With that, she directly bent over and hugged Lin Yuan in her arms before stepping out of the curtain of moonlight.","Then, she said to Mystic Moon, who was standing guard outside, “Mystic Moon, bring the two people inside to Radiant Moon Palace and...”","The Moon Empress stopped here before continuing.","“Bring them to Lin Yuan’s mansion so that they can recuperate well.”","Mystic Moon had already seen Lin Yuan in the Moon Empress’ arms earlier when she came out.","Although Lin Yuan looked to be in a deep sleep, Mystic Moon could tell just by the Moon Empress’ mood that Lin Yuan’s life was not in danger.","Moreover, just before the Moon Empress had come out, the layer of blood coating the bright moon in the sky had grown extremely intense before disappearing entirely.","At that time, the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Listen had all seen Lin Yuan in the Moon Empress’ arms.","In that instant, their tight heartstrings had finally loosened slightly.","The Moon Empress did not acknowledge the trio. She just carried Lin Yuan and walked outside.","Outside, dense moonlight rose from the Moon Empress’ entire body, covering Lin Yuan’s figure.","The Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan and whispered, “Come, come home with Master.”","When the Moon Empress stepped outside, the experts standing guard outside all lowered their heads. Yet, even the expressions they wore while looking at the ground became extremely respectful.","However, just as they lowered their heads, they suddenly sensed that the coldness from the light shining on their bodies had been replaced by warmth.","After a long while, the two Guard Envoys standing in front slowly raised their heads.","Only then did they realize that the bright moon, which had placed itself above everything else in the sky, had disappeared.","Now, the sun was rising high in the sky, exuding a warm light."]},{"number":520,"title":"Chapter 520: Is Someone Chasing You Again?","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan had fallen into a deep sleep. However, he dreamed a long, long dream as he slept.","In his dream, Lin Yuan was gazing upon a world like a bystander.","That world had originally been full of life, with unknown small flowers blossoming in the wilderness.","However, at that moment, two rainbows radiating light in seven colors suddenly appeared in the sky.","These two rainbows fought to invade the deep blue sky, neither willing to give way to the other.","The rainbow light appeared gentle, but it was actually unusually untamed.","As the light spread all over the earth, the earth cracked while the unknown flowers blooming on it withered.","At that moment, a figure suddenly descended from one of the rainbows.","This figure was a girl with closed eyes and a body like a phantom’s.","The girl wore a crown and a long skirt. She carried herself with a kind of inherent nobility.","In the instant that she descended from the rainbow, she seemed to almost invade the entire world as though she was about to become its master.","Just then, a sword without a scabbard fell directly from the other rainbow.","The sword’s hilt was gorgeous, carved with various animal totems. Its slender body contained a sharpness that was enough to slice through anything.","The sharp sword launched an assault on the crown-wearing girl.","The two were locked tightly in a stalemate.","It was precisely this stalemate that made the rainbow light even more unscrupulous. The world that had already fallen apart was about to collapse completely.","In that instant, the entire world was suddenly shrouded in a reddish-gold brilliance that felt unusually familiar and warm to Lin Yuan, who had been watching everything.","As the reddish-gold brilliance descended, the girl and the sword that were locked in a stalemate became unusually fearful.","This brilliance appeared to be imposing its will on the crown-wearing girl and the sword without a scabbard.","In the end, the girl reluctantly walked toward the sword.","She opened her arms and hugged it.","At that moment, the two became one. From two single entities, they combined to become a new whole.","The world was on the verge of collapse when the crown-wearing girl curled her legs up as her skirt fluttered in mid-air.","She was holding the sword with an unusually gorgeous hilt tightly in her arms.","At that moment, the sword’s ornate carvings seemed to hold the girl’s power.","With this power added, its desire grew exceedingly great!","Just then, the two initially feuding rainbows also fused into one.","The previously unruly rainbow light also became beautiful and gentle, spreading all over the earth again.","This time, the light did not destroy the world on the verge of coming apart but melted perfectly into it.","After the rainbow light completely melted into it, the girl hugging the sword surrendered to the broken world and became a part of it.","In other words, she became like a guardian, protecting this world that was on the brink of collapse.","Like a bystander, Lin Yuan had witnessed everything that had happened.","At that moment, he seemed to suddenly smell the aroma of radishes. Immediately after, the dry, fragmented land of the world on the verge of collapse was covered with endless fields of radishes.","These radishes grew, flowered, bore fruit, grew old, and rotted.","In this way, crop after crop of radishes continued to provide energy for this world on the verge of breaking apart.","Slowly, the broken soil became fertile, and unknown wildflowers bloomed all over the land again.","This world’s savior, the radishes that had healed the world on the verge of collapse, had disappeared.","Yet, the fragrance of radishes still permeated the air.","Lin Yuan witnessed this strange scene in his dream.","...","“Moon Empress, you don’t have to beat so much jujube, do you?","“Even if you’re right about the Young Lord waking soon, he will also not be able to finish so much jujube!”","Cold Moon looked at the Moon Empress as she continuously removed the pits from the Diamond Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes that she had picked from the inner palace jujube garden.","Then, she used a pestle completely made of jade-textured osmanthus wood to continuously pound the jujubes.","Cold Moon thought that this was all far too exaggerated.","The Moon Empress might have picked all of the Diamond Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes on the only three jujube trees that grew them in Leaning Moon Mountain’s jujube garden.","Cold Moon had long been aware that the Moon Empress was unusually doting toward Lin Yuan.","However, the extent of her doting seemed to be a bit better than before.","Ordinarily, after the lotus flower feys in the lotus pond had reached the Suzerain grade, the light that they spurted forth could envelop the inner palace entirely.","However, it now only shrouded a five-meter radius surrounding the lotus pond.","Who knew how many lotus roots the Moon Empress had cut from the Suzerain lotus flower feys in the pond?","The Moon Empress peeled the jujubes in her hand somewhat anxiously. Hearing that Cold Moon still had time to speak, she said quickly, “Cold Moon, help This Empress to pound these jujubes. This Empress’ disciple suffered serious injuries to his hands when he came out of the dimensional rift. What will happen to him if he doesn’t take supplements?","“This Empress plans to make this jujube paste into jujube powder. Even if This Empress’ disciple takes it every day, it should be enough to last three months.”","Cold Moon could not help cupping her forehead in her hand. She had only left Radiant Moon Palace for a short while. Why did the Moon Empress seem like a completely different person?","If the Young Lord were to take the jujube powder every day, he would likely become a humanoid blood-dripping cart that could water all of the plants on Leaning Moon Mountain with his nosebleeds.","Moreover, hadn’t the Moon Empress already let the Young Lord eat half of the Rabbit Emperor’s sacred source lifeform?","Even if he were a Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujube that was made into a paste, then powder, the Young Lord would still not be as healthy as he was right then!","With that thought in mind, Cold Moon glanced surreptitiously at the front of the small flowerpot containing crystal soil.","The listless Rabbit Emperor was currently using its ear to plant its carrot in the crystal soil.","To Cold Moon, the Moon Empress doted on the Young Lord to a truly terrifying degree!","Nevertheless, once she thought about the gains that she had made at Redbud City after leaving the Radiant Moon Palace, Cold Moon could not help but smile faintly.","Upon seeing Cold Moon’s smile, the Moon Empress immediately stopped pounding on the Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes. Looking at her with suspicion, the Moon Empress asked, “After ten years, are people still chasing you?”","She had suddenly recalled how Marquis Jing Shi had directly expressed his love and publicly shown his fondness for Cold Moon...","...only to have Cold Moon break both of his legs, to the point that he was confined to a wheelchair for ten years.","Although Marquis Jing Shi had indeed gone overboard in the expression of his love, Cold Moon’s methods were truly unladylike.","Upon hearing the Moon Empress’ words, Cold Moon froze immediately.","Right after, Cold Moon knew that the Moon Empress had misunderstood her.","She cast a glance toward the room within the inner palace and said, “Moon Empress, the Young Lord’s sister, Chu Ci, is now already my disciple.”"]},{"number":521,"title":"Chapter 521: Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet","paragraphs":["Upon hearing Cold Moon’s words, the Moon Empress did not appear particularly surprised.","Over the week that Lin Yuan had been sleeping, the Moon Empress had long noticed Cold Moon’s closeness to Chu Ci.","However, she did not expect Cold Moon, whose personality had always been cold, to voluntarily accept a disciple.","With that thought in mind, the Moon Empress was certain that Cold Moon had only gotten the idea of accepting a disciple after seeing her accept Lin Yuan as her disciple.","Since Cold Moon had learned from her, the Moon Empress felt the need to teach the former how to be a good Master.","From the Moon Empress’ point of view, a Master who did not know how to dote on their disciple could not be considered a good one.","“Cold Moon, you must smile more in Chu Ci’s presence in the future. It is not good to be too serious.”","Having said this, the Moon Empress thought for a while before changing the subject.","“Since you just accepted Chu Ci as a disciple, why don’t you find her a Path Protector? This would also guarantee her safety.”","The Moon Empress’ expression was extremely earnest as she said this. After all, the Moon Empress had just been anxious and frightened because of Lin Yuan’s recent incident.","Upon hearing the Moon Empress’ words, Cold Moon hurriedly replied, “Moon Empress, I see that Chu Ci gets along well with my Icy King Dragon. I plan to name it Chu Ci’s Path Protector.”","The Moon Empress felt that Cold Moon was ready to be a Master.","Suddenly, she turned her gaze to the pitiful little rabbit lying on the table that was looking at the carrot growing in the soil.","The little rabbit sensed someone’s eyes on its body and instantly raised its ears vigilantly.","After it saw that the Moon Empress was looking at it, the rabbit quickly turned around, stood up, and fiercely blocked the flowerpot where it had planted its carrot.","The Moon Empress shifted her gaze somewhat reluctantly. This rabbit was so close to falling into the carrot’s eyes!","At that moment, a clear voice rang from the entrance of the inner palace.","“Moon Empress, the Young Lord’s Path Protector, the Mother of Bloodbath, requests to see you.”","Turning her head to look toward the room within the inner palace, the Moon Empress said, “Let it in.”","With that, she placed one of the Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes that she had just peeled on the table.","Cold Moon sharply realized that the Moon Empress’ expression had become more somber.","Right after, Cold Moon saw a red-haired, red-eyed woman dressed in red enter through the inner palace’s entrance.","Cold Moon’s entire body sent out a terrifying force.","Under Cold Moon’s guidance, this force did not affect the plants in the inner palace.","However, when it handed on the Mother of Bloodbath’s body, it made the fey feel as though it was trapped in a glacier.","The Mother of Bloodbath gnashed its teeth and walked forward, against this force, until it stood before the Moon Empress.","At that moment, Cold Moon’s icy voice sounded. “Myth II? Your strength has improved significantly since the last time I saw you, but your alertness is too weak.”","The Mother of Bloodbath had already been extremely worried the past few days. Even though it knew that Lin Yuan was not likely to be in any mortal danger, it still did not know his exact condition. Hence, it still felt uneasy in its heart.","When the evolving dimensional entrance had suddenly swallowed Lin Yuan, the Mother of Bloodbath may not have been the most worried compared to the Moon Empress or Chu Ci.","However, as Lin Yuan’s Path Protector, it had undoubtedly blamed itself the most.","Upon confirming that Liu Jie and Zhou Luo had not been in danger, the Mother of Bloodbath had turned into a fist-sized spider like in the past before landing on the room’s beam.","From there, it had been looking in the direction of Leaning Moon Mountain.","Even when Liu Jie had cooked after waking up, the Mother of Bloodbath had not eaten a mouthful.","Now, it looked at the Moon Empress, someone who had previously saved her life and felt even more remorseful.","Just like what Mystic Moon had said, it had not been by Lin Yuan’s side to ensure his safety.","It had betrayed not only Lin Yuan’s trust but also the Moon Empress’ at the same time.","Even as the Mother of Bloodbath stood before the Moon Empress, it did not know what to say.","Nevertheless, after only two seconds, it broke the silence by asking softly, “Moon Empress, is Lin Yuan doing well now?”","The Moon Empress had originally harbored anger in her heart, but she sighed upon seeing the Mother of Bloodbath’s expression.","“Lin Yuan is no longer in danger now. He will be able to recover fully once he awakes.”","In the past, given the Moon Empress’ temper, it was highly possible that the Mother of Bloodbath would have been sublimated into nothingness the moment the Moon Empress had arrived.","It could be said that the Mother of Bloodbath had not protected Lin Yuan entirely because it had lost her sense of vigilance.","If not, given its Myth II power, the Mother of Bloodbath would never have let Lin Yuan be sucked into the dimensional rift.","However, the present Moon Empress knew that she could not do anything to the Mother of Bloodbath.","When the Moon Empress had been helping Lin Yuan to find a Path Protector, she had been helping him to establish a connection.","This had been comparable to giving Lin Yuan the Extreme Token.","After the Extreme Token had been used, the Moon Empress could replenish its strength by sealing another moonlight domain within it.","Even if a source-type item like the Extreme Token were to be damaged, the Moon Empress could still put some thought into finding a replacement.","Given that Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple, she naturally understood his temperament.","With the Mother of Bloodbath’s role of Path Protector as a fetter, it shared a strong bond with Lin Yuan.","Hence, even the Moon Empress, who had never sighed upon encountering a difficult problem, now sighed for the first time as she faced the Mother of Bloodbath.","The Moon Empress sent a brown flowing light flying toward the Mother of Bloodbath with the wave of a hand.","The Mother of Bloodbath quickly grabbed the brown flowing light and found that it was a simple wooden tablet with a first-quarter and a third-quarter crescent moon carved on it.","The wooden tablet’s surface was faintly tinged with a halo of moonlight, making the crescent moons engraved on it appear somewhat hazy.","The Mother of Bloodbath held the wooden tablet somewhat perplexedly. At that moment, it heard the Moon Empress say, “Back then, I chose you as Lin Yuan’s Path Protector because your exclusive skill and abilities would have allowed you to increase your capital strength. That was why This Empress valued you.”","The Mother of Bloodbath quickly responded, “It was I who betrayed the Moon Empress’ trust.”","It spoke very calmly but with unspeakable firmness. It was as though it had committed a previously committed error to memory and would remember it for life.","Looking directly at the Mother of Bloodbath, the Moon Empress said coldly, “You did nothing to disappoint This Empress. It is This Empress’ only hope that you do not betray Lin Yuan’s trust in the future.","“You already repaid your debt to This Empress when you became Lin Yuan’s Path Protector.”","Upon hearing the Moon Empress’ words, the image of Lin Yuan’s determined gaze upon seeing it evolve to Myth II surfaced in the Mother of Bloodbath’s mind...","Along with all the bits and pieces of the times that it had spent with Lin Yuan."]},{"number":522,"title":"Chapter 522: Smile and Smile Until Tears Fall","paragraphs":["The Mother of Bloodbath bowed to the Moon Empress and said, “Moon Empress, since Lin Yuan is no longer in any danger, I will return to the mansion to await his return.”","After speaking, it prepared to place the wooden tablet that the Moon Empress had just thrown to it on the table before her.","At that moment, the Mother of Bloodbath heard the Moon Empress speak again.","“Am I right to say that your strength is insufficient against a veteran faction like the Zheng family?","“Before the veteran factions, the Myth Breed’s emperor-class combat power will eventually become a shield that does not let a trace of frost pass through.","“However, it’s another matter if you can attain Creation Breed combat power.","“This Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet will protect you through the Trial of World Creation, such that you will not fall when you evolve to the Creation Breed. The rest is up to you.”","The Mother of Bloodbath froze with the wooden tablet in its hands. It had a complicated expression on its face.","However, it regained its original composure in an instant.","The Mother of Bloodbath thanked the Moon Empress again. Then, it gripped the Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet tightly in its hand and left the Radiant Moon Palace to return to the mansion.","After the Mother of Bloodbath left, Cold Moon looked at the Moon Empress as though she was meeting her for the first time. She asked, perplexed, “You could have directly awarded the Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet to the Mother of Bloodbath. Why did you put so much thought into it?”","Cold Moon knew that the Moon Empress had never been a woman of many words.","However, she had unexpectedly disclosed the Zheng family’s might when giving the Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet to the Mother of Bloodbath.","Although the Moon Empress had only said one more sentence, it had completely transformed Cold Moon’s impression of her.","At that moment, the Moon Empress picked up the Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes that she had just put down and began using the jade-textured osmanthus wood pestle to continue pounding them.","Upon hearing Cold Moon’s question, she replied, “This small spider’s self-respect is very great. If This Empress did not mention Lin Yuan and the Zheng family, even if this Crescent Moon Radiant Sunlight Tablet could help it weather the Trial of World Creation, it would not have accepted it.”","Having said this, the Moon Empress glanced at Cold Moon before continuing. “Once you’ve become a Master, you will realize that martial force cannot solve every problem. In This Empress’ view, the wisdom required to be a Master far outweighs that required to be a Class 5 Creation Master.”","Upon hearing this, the corner of Cold Moon’s mouth could not help but twitch.","She did not understand why the Moon Empress had said this.","In Cold Moon’s opinion, it was very easy to be a Master.","In the future, as long as Chu Ci needed it, she would give Chu Ci everything that she could and create the conditions to give everything that she could not. Wasn’t that all there was to it?","It was this simple!","Just then, Mystic Moon’s clear voice rang from the inner palace’s entrance again.","After entering, he immediately reported, “Moon Empress, about the Spirit Savory Pigs that you asked me to get from Chef Supreme... Chef Supreme said that only the last three pigs were left, and I only managed to get one after much struggle.”","Upon hearing this, the Moon Empress’s brows knitted together.","“How can there only be three left this year? Hasn’t old Chef Supreme been studying the Spirit Savory Pigs’ breeding process and the postpartum care of sows in Kitchen Fragrant House these few years?”","Mystic Moon’s face revealed an indescribable expression. After organizing his messy thoughts, he responded, “According to Chef Supreme’s first disciple, his second disciple has been studying how to make braised pork more delicious since the latter’s return.","“Because Chef Supreme hadn’t seen his daughter in a long while, he let his second disciple and his daughter live in Kitchen Fragrant House for half a month.","“However, during this half a month, Chef Supreme’s second disciple had his eyes on those Spirit Savory Pigs. His second disciple slaughtered even the three old sows that had been responsible for producing piglets.","“In my view, it might not only be this year that there are only three Spirit Savory Pigs but every year from now on.”","The Moon Empress and Cold Moon were silent for a long while before responding in unison.","“Lin Yuan is still the best.”","“Chu Ci is still the best.”","Blinking his eyes, Mystic Moon reached out and touched the back of his head.","It looked like he was now the only one without a disciple in the Radiant Moon Palace.","Why did he suddenly feel as though he was being isolated?","...","Lin Yuan had originally been fully immersed in his strange dream.","After an indeterminate period of time, he felt his thoughts return to his body. He could even faintly perceive everything around him through the faint spiritual energy in his mind.","He could feel the soft bed beneath his body, Morbius on his wrist, and the Flowing Cloud Beeswax pendant on his neck.","Although he could sense everything, he could not lift his heavy eyelids no matter how hard he tried.","However, Lin Yuan could already begin interacting with his feys in his mind.","Apart from the sleeping Chimey, Genius, Red Thorn, the Source Sand, and the Ethereal Jellyfish that had returned to his spiritual spatial zone at some unknown time were all interacting with Lin Yuan now.","Especially when communicating with Lin Yuan, Genius had an unusually obvious tearful note in its child-like voice.","After Lin Yuan comforted it for a while, Genius finally calmed down.","However, Lin Yuan found that no matter how he called for Morbius, he was unable to establish a connection with it.","He was extremely familiar with Morbius’ current state.","Morbius was now in the state of deep sleep that it had been in when he had just contracted it.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan inexplicably thought about the reddish-gold light in his dream.","Just at that moment, an ethereal voice sounded from the deepest depths of his soul.","“My Lord.”","Upon hearing this voice, Lin Yuan initially thought of responding. Unfortunately, he fell once again into a deep sleep in his fatigued state.","When he awoke, he found that he could open his eyes.","In the instant that Lin Yuan opened his eyes, he immediately saw Chu Ci standing guard by his bedside.","It was obvious that Chu Ci had been sitting there for a long time. Her hair was rather unkempt, its dull ends sticking up.","Lin Yuan did not know what the dozing Chu Ci had been dreaming about, but there were obviously traces of undried tears in the corners of her eyes.","Lin Yuan subconsciously reached out to help her wipe the corners of her eyes.","Yet, immediately after stretching his hands out, he found that they had returned to their initial positions.","Still, Lin Yuan could not help but recall the pain in his hands at that time, the pain of countless blooming blades.","After experiencing that kind of pain once, one would never wish to experience it again.","When he reached out to wipe the corners of Chu Ci’s eyes, Lin Yuan’s slight movement woke her up in a moment.","In that instant, Chu Ci appeared as though she had not returned from her shallow dream. Panic was still written plainly on her face.","However, upon seeing that Lin Yuan had awakened, a bright smile broke out on Chu Ci’s face.","It was comparable to the bright and beautiful spring sun in April.","Yet, as she smiled and smiled, large teardrops fell from her eyes onto Lin Yuan’s arms, which still carried the warmth of Chu Ci’s body temperature."]},{"number":523,"title":"Chapter 523: Vajra Butterfly’s Willpower Rune","paragraphs":["Upon seeing Chu Ci cry, Lin Yuan’s heart instantly tightened.","From Lin Yuan’s recollection, Chu Ci had never cried more than a few times since childhood. However difficult a problem they encountered, she would always wear a smile while standing by Lin Yuan’s side.","Now, Lin Yuan immediately felt a little numb.","He did not know how to make her feel better so that her tears would stop falling.","Just as he was mulling over this in his head, Chu Ci suddenly threw herself in his arms and said, hiccuping, “Brother, don’t worry. I only cried because I was overjoyed.”","Lin Yuan extended his arms to wrap them around Chu Ci and lightly patted her on the shoulder.","Lin Yuan and Chu Ci were both inept at expressing their innermost emotions.","Hence, the only other time they had both revealed their true emotions like this had occurred during their first year of seeking survival together.","It was when Chu Ci had been so sick that she almost hadn’t made it—such a scene had taken place, but it had never happened again.","As Lin Yuan lightly patted Chu Ci’s shoulder, he sighed in his heart.","Lin Yuan was extremely sensitive to Chu Ci’s moods. She had definitely not been weeping with joy but getting her worry off her chest.","Moreover, Chu Ci had called him ‘Brother’ instead of ‘Lin Yuan’.","Obviously, she had also known the whole story behind his injuries, so she must have been worried sick during this period.","Lin Yuan only came up with something to say to Chu Ci to comfort her after a long time.","Chu Ci asked softly with her face buried in his shoulder, “Brother, do you feel discomfort anywhere on your body?”","As she spoke, Chu Ci raised her head off Lin Yuan’s shoulder, extended her hand, and wiped off a tear from the corner of her eye.","After which, only a smile remained on Chu Ci’s face. Large teardrops would no longer fall from the corners of her eyes.","Upon hearing Chu Ci’s question, Lin Yuan tried to open his mouth to speak, but he found that his throat was dry and rough from having slept for so long.","Before he could utter a single word, he began coughing.","Chu Ci hurried to the jade porcelain tea table beside her and poured Lin Yuan a cup of spirit tea from the teapot.","When he took the cup from Chu Ci’s hands, Lin Yuan smiled sheepishly.","After drinking two mouthfuls of tea and his throat no longer felt dry, Lin Yuan immediately said, “I feel extremely well now! I don’t feel a hint of discomfort!”","When Lin Yuan had been inside the dimensional rift struggling to stop its evolution, he had been the most worried about Chu Ci.","He would never have expected that the first person he would see when he awoke would be his sister, who he had not seen for so many days.","Chu Ci studied the sincere expression on Lin Yuan’s face. It seemed like he really wasn’t experiencing any discomfort.","After another round of scrutiny, she finally felt at ease when she saw that Lin Yuan was in radiant spirits.","At that moment, Chu Ci’s expression grew earnest and severe. She reached her hand out and tidied the corner of Lin Yuan’s blanket before saying, “Lin Yuan, I need to tell you something in earnest.”","Upon hearing how Chu Ci had addressed him, Lin Yuan could not help but stop smiling.","This change had happened too quickly!","Once he had said that he was fine, she had gone back to addressing him as ‘Lin Yuan’.","Nevertheless, upon seeing her serious expression, Lin Yuan also immediately grew serious.","Having grown up with Chu Ci, Lin Yuan understood her extremely well. He knew that she was about to tell him something that was very important to her.","He said very earnestly while leaning against the bed, “Why did you suddenly become so serious? Tell me. I’m all ears.”","Suddenly, Lin Yuan saw a trace of grievance flash in Chu Ci’s eyes.","Immediately after, her eyes reddened once more. Just as Lin Yuan became confused again, Chu Ci’s words stunned him.","“Lin Yuan, can you feel what I felt when I heard that you had been sucked into the dimensional rift, and you were hanging between life and death?","“You can’t understand because I have a brother, but you don’t.”","This sentence, which sounded almost like bragging to Lin Yuan’s ears, caused his heart to tremble fiercely.","Lin Yuan was very good at putting himself in others’ shoes. Whenever he faced problems, he would try his best to consider them from another person’s standpoint.","While he could not accept what some people did, he could at least understand their choices as long as they did not violate moral principles.","However, Lin Yuan realized that he had forgotten to put himself in the shoes of those whom he was closest to.","Lin Yuan’s thoughts suddenly returned to a time when he had been eight years old, and it had been raining overnight in the Xia Region.","Then, Chu Ci’s high fever had not been receding, but he had not had enough money to pay a healer to heal her.","In the end, it happened that Auntie Zhang had just brought Uncle Li, who had been suppressing his leg, back and had found out about Chu Ci’s condition.","Auntie Zhang had hurried to find a healer to heal Chu Ci. Only then had Chu Ci survived the ordeal.","The despair that he had felt at being weak and the belief that the only companion in his bitter life would disappear were deeply engraved in Lin Yuan’s heart.","His eyes reddened involuntarily.","He moved the corners of his lips, meaning to say something.","However, he did not end up speaking his intended words out loud.","Still, he said them softly in his heart.","“I have a sister, but you don’t.","“So I know!”","Chu Ci froze when she looked at Lin Yuan. His eyes had unexpectedly reddened.","Chu Ci immediately became flustered.","Just then, she collected herself and changed the topic.","“Brother, I have comprehended another Willpower Rune.”","In the next instant, Chu Ci’s spiritual energy directly shot forth a Willpower Rune that had an unusually heavy feeling.","This heaviness was like a sturdy shield, but an indomitable might seemed to be hidden behind it.","It was just that this might was hidden behind the heaviness as if only after the latter were shaved off would one be able to see the former.","Lin Yuan could not believe that Chu Ci had comprehended yet another Willpower Rune in such a short period.","However, this Willpower Rune looked somewhat special. Lin Yuan was also rather puzzled by what the will in this rune actually represented.","Lin Yuan could not help but ask, “Chu Ci, under what conditions did you comprehend this Willpower Rune?”","After thinking for a while, Chu Ci responded, “I comprehended this Willpower Rune when I saw the patterns on the wings of the Vajra Butterfly.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan felt as though he was receiving a blow for the first time.","He had always believed that his comprehension of Willpower Runes was already very impressive. Unexpectedly, it was nothing compared to Chu Ci’s.","After all, Lin Yuan had been looking at Genius every day, but he had never comprehended the Willpower Rune that he should have comprehended from doing so.","Still, since the Willpower Rune that Chu Ci had comprehended was from the Vajra Butterfly, then it must have been one that the butterfly could use when it became a Fantasy Breed.","In the room, as Lin Yuan studied Chu Ci’s Willpower Rune, Chu Ci also answered his questions fully.","It was as though they had both forgotten how their eyes had been red just a minute ago.","Steam curled from the tea in the porcelain cup, and the room was stained with the fragrance of matcha.","A jade safety pendant hung on the head of the bed, witnessing the peacefulness through the years under the curl of the steam."]},{"number":524,"title":"Chapter 524: Chu Ci’s Growth","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan looked at the new Willpower Rune Chu Ci had comprehended. He was surprised by how fast she was growing.","Lin Yuan had been working hard the past six months on increasing his own power and had gone through changes multiple times.","Chu Ci had not fallen behind either.","She already had the Fantasy Obsidian Iron Wild Bull, but now she also had the new Willpower Rune, which was the equivalent of possessing another Fantasy Breed fey.","To other spirit qi professionals who comprehended Willpower Runes, the hardest part of evolving Fantasy Breed feys was increasing their quality.","But with Lin Yuan around, it would be easy to evolve the Vajra Butterfly’s quality to Legend.","The recently-turned 16-year-old Chu Ci essentially had two Fantasy Breed feys.","The thought frightened Lin Yuan.","At 16 years old, one was supposed to be in Year 1 at Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy, but Chu Ci already had two Fantasy Breed feys.","As long as Chu Ci’s Fantasy Breed feys both evolved to Silver, she would distinguish herself if she attended Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy.","Moreover, both of Chu Ci’s contracted feys had amazing foundations.","Although Lin Yuan had been hoping that Chu Ci’s fighting style would not be too aggressive, he had to admit that the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull perfectly demonstrated how offense was the best defense.","The Vajra Butterfly was also an exceptional defense-type fey.","Lin Yuan had picked out the Vajra Butterfly for Chu Ci after sorting through numerous defense-type feys.","The Vajra Butterfly’s defensive abilities were considered impressive amongst Bronze-grade feys.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, the Vajra Butterfly’s true strength did not lie in its innate power but in its outstanding potential for evolution.","If the Vajra Butterfly could evolve to the Jadeite Butterfly, Chu Ci’s defensive abilities would rocket up another level.","The Vajra Butterfly would need to absorb a large amount of pollen from plant-type feys to evolve into the Jadeite Butterfly, after which the plant-type feys’ wood-type attribute would start to slowly change the Vajra Butterfly’s aura.","During this process, pure spirit qi would need to be showered over the Vajra Butterfly in order for it to successfully evolve into the Jadeite Butterfly.","The key ingredient was the pollen from the plant-type feys that it needed to absorb.","The Vajra Butterfly was metal-type, and it would struggle to absorb the pollen from plant-type feys.","Thus, the best way for the Vajra Butterfly to evolve into the Jadeite Butterfly was for it to absorb the pollen from metal- and plant-type feys.","Previously, Lin Yuan had been worried about needing metal- and plant-type feys when he was trying to help Chu Ci contract the Vajra Butterfly. However, now he was not troubled at all over the need to procure the pollen from metal- and plant-type feys.","Jiao Hanzhong’s garden-like Diamond fey storage box already had a few Golden Curtain Peonies, a metal- and plant-type fey.","The Golden Curtain Peony was an admire-type fey that blossomed at the end of the year. Its flowers were larger than bowls and glowed brightly with a metallic luster. It looked like a stack of thin metal pieces.","As an admire-type fey, the Golden Curtain Peony did not have any special uses other than highlighting one’s presence.","However, it was suitable for the Vajra Butterfly to absorb its pollen.","Lin Yuan was now extremely confident of being able to evolve the Vajra Butterfly into the Jadeite Butterfly.","Lin Yuan pondered for a while before seriously saying to Chu Ci, “Since you’re on holiday, you shouldn’t need the Vajra Butterfly to enter battles, right?”","Chu Ci nodded and said, “I don’t think I’ll need the Vajra Butterfly for battle before school starts. I’m going to use the holiday to go on Star Web and watch the Radiance Hundred’s members’ fights.”","Chu Ci’s voice was full of enthusiasm.","Ever since Chu Ci had decided to become a part of the Redbud Hundred, she had set her sights on the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Chu Ci could gauge how far her abilities were lacking by watching the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s fights.","Knowing her weak points encouraged Chu Ci and motivated her to increase her power.","Lin Yuan was surprised to discover Chu Ci’s ambition. She was aiming for the Radiance Hundred Sequence after such a short time.","However, the Radiance Hundred Sequence members were all devious, and each of them kept their true powers tightly locked away.","They only demonstrated the powers they possessed when they first entered the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Lin Yuan decided against telling Chu Ci about the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s true power for fear of killing her passion.","Lin Yuan wanted to cultivate her ambition.","“Leave this Vajra Butterfly with me. Let me see if I can nurture it into the Jadeite Butterfly. If I’m successful, you’ll be able to increase your power again when it becomes a Fantasy Breed.”","Chu Ci activated her spiritual energy to summon the Vajra Butterfly.","Chu Ci would never reject Lin Yuan’s suggestion and his willingness to put in effort for her.","Chu Ci was no longer the naive girl who did not have any contracted feys. She now understood the difficulty behind evolving a fey’s quality and transforming a fey.","Chu Ci knew how hard Lin Yuan had to have worked in order to secure her first fey.","She knew he had probably used up all his resources.","Lin Yuan was not one to openly express his feelings, but Chu Ci had grown up with him and knew how kind he really was.","The Vajra Butterfly was not just a fey that Lin Yuan had strengthened—the first face it had seen when it hatched belonged to Lin Yuan.","When it saw Lin Yuan leaning against the bed, the Vajra Butterfly immediately flew over to rest on his nose.","The Vajra Butterfly fluttered its wings, its wingspan covering half of Lin Yuan’s face.","The dust that fell from the Vajra Butterfly’s fluttering wings made Lin Yuan sneeze five times in succession.","After sneezing, Lin Yuan felt unusually relaxed.","Lin Yuan kept the Vajra Butterfly into his Spirit Lock spatial zone and prepared to find the right time to nurture it.","Before nurturing the Vajra Butterfly, Lin Yuan first needed to nurture the Golden Curtain Peonies."]},{"number":525,"title":"Chapter 525: Plan to Forge Iron Bucket Sister Can’t Fail!","paragraphs":["Chu Ci suddenly thought about her evolved Silver Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","Chu Ci was still uncertain when it came to instructing the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","“Lin Yuan, my Obsidian Iron Wild Bull has evolved from Bronze to Silver. Master said that the Silver Obsidian Iron Wild Bull has decent abilities. But my senior in dueling class is always saying that its abilities are nothing special.”","Lin Yuan immediately caught the keyword in Chu Ci’s speech—Master.","The word Master and Teacher was extremely meaningful.","Chu Ci called everyone who taught at Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy as Teacher, but the word Master carried with it the intention of legacy. A Master could have many disciples, but a disciple could only have one Master in their lifetime.","Instead of answering Chu Ci’s question, Lin Yuan asked, “Chu Ci, when did you acquire a Master? Why haven’t you mentioned it to me?”","Although Chu Ci had grown up and was capable of making decisions like becoming someone’s disciple, it worried Lin Yuan that Chu Ci had completely failed to bring up this important development in her life to him.","Lin Yuan’s mind immediately went to her young age.","Could she have been cheated due to her lack of experience?","Chu Ci stuck her tongue out at Lin Yuan and said sheepishly, “My Master is Auntie Cold Moon! She said she wanted me to become her disciple. I feel that she looks at me the same way you do, and she feels like family too. I was planning on telling you over the phone the other night, but by the afternoon, I heard that you were sucked into the dimensional rift.”","When Lin Yuan heard that it was Cold Moon, his worries vanished.","It seemed that Cold Moon and Chu Ci had been getting along very well in those few months since Cold Moon had taken Chu Ci in as a disciple.","Lin Yuan did not ask for details and changed the topic because Chu Ci had brought up the dimensional rift. He did not want her to cry again.","Lin Yuan quickly replied, “Chu Ci, summon the Obsidian Wild Bull. Let me see what’s wrong with its abilities.”","If Cold Moon was willing to compliment the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s abilities, it was definitely not weak.","But Chu Ci’s senior had said during dueling class that its abilities were not special, which told Lin Yuan that there was an issue with ability combination.","Some feys needed some conditions to be met when they used their abilities.","Currently, Chu Ci was unable to fulfill those conditions during battle, and her opponents were of no help either.","This could be why Chu Ci was unable to use the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Silver abilities during battle.","Chu Ci lifted her arm and summoned the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","Lin Yuan carefully used True Data to scan the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","[Fey Name]: Obsidian Iron Wild Bull","[Fey Species]: Horned species/Bull species","[Fey Grade]: Silver (5/10)","[Fey Type]: Metal","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy II","Abilities:","[Iron Horn]: Enhance the metallic properties of the nose horn. Disregard injuries and smash into the enemy with full strength.","[Sacrifice]: When the contractor is injured, automatically split the damage with the contractor. If the contractor is injured, it will feed the contractor with its vitality.","[Pain Buffer]: When damaged by elemental energy, form a shield of elemental energy on the surface of the body that will slow the elemental energy damage for a certain period. Further damage will only be incurred after the shield breaks.","Exclusive Skill:","[Pain Absorption]: When receiving damage, absorb a portion of the damage and turn it into vitality.","[Annihilation Gaze]: Domineering battle consciousness and war fervor drive its instinctive footsteps. The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull instantly transforms all the damage taken in a battle into a mental impact on the opponent.","Lin Yuan was stunned as he stared at the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s data. The spirit tea in his hand splattered all over the blanket.","The silk blanket absorbed the spirit tea, and the patch formed made it look as though Lin Yuan had wet the bed.","Lin Yuan’s eyes were as wide as saucers. He stared incredulously at the metal block that was the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s grade was now Silver V, and its quality had improved from Fantasy I to Fantasy II.","It was difficult for Lin Yuan to evolve the quality of Fantasy Breeds.","Cold Moon definitely had something to do with Chu Ci’s Obsidian Iron Wild Bull evolving to Fantasy II.","Despite this, Lin Yuan sighed heavily again.","Chu Ci’s growth was too fast!","It was possible for Chu Ci to only use the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s power to take on Listen, as the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull was Fantasy II while Listen’s Pain Illusory Fox and Three-Tailed Crimson Fox were both Fantasy I.","If a fight ensued, it would be hard to say who would win.","Chu Ci had been watching Lin Yuan’s expression. When she saw a strange look cloud over Lin Yuan’s face, she anxiously asked, “Lin Yuan, do you also think that the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Silver abilities are lacking?”","Lin Yuan shook his head vigorously. He was pleasantly surprised by the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Silver abilities.","When it came to raising Chu Ci’s overall fighting ability, the Silver-grade Pain Buffer was more effective than the Elite-grade Sacrifice.","As a defense-type fey, the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Sacrifice’s main appeal was that it could protect its contractor, Chu Ci.","However, once the Vajra Butterfly became a Fantasy Breed, its shield could already provide Chu Ci with full protection.","Thus, Sacrifice could only be used as Chu Ci’s last resort for defense.","Pain Buffer was more flexible, and it provided the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull with a temporary impenetrable shield against elemental energy.","Even if Lin Yuan was unaware of how long the Pain Buffer’s shield would last, it still defended the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull against elemental energy.","The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull was already naturally resilient. Given this added temporary defensive ability, its seat as the main fey Chu Ci—a defense-type spirit qi professional—was secured for a long time.","For the first time, the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull did not look as reckless and dense to Lin Yuan.","Chu Ci sighed and said, “If only I could meet more feys on Star Web that attack with elemental energy! When those attacks hit the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull, its metal horns which can release elemental energy will look so much cooler!”","Chu Ci’s lament made Lin Yuan feel that he had misjudged the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull was not the one that was hot-headed... Chu Ci was actually the hot-headed one!","How hot-headed is Chu Ci? How can she already want to show off her power right after acquiring a good defensive ability?","Lin Yuan thought back to the fairy source-type lifeform, the Burning Sunflower, which he had traded for at the Indigo Azure Sea Market.","His confidence spiked.","No matter how impulsive Chu Ci was, the plan to forge his sister into an iron could not fail as long as there was the Burning Sunflower!"]},{"number":526,"title":"Chapter 526: Am I About to Have a Sister-in-law?","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan felt that the present situation was too much of a coincidence.","The Burning Sunflower that Lin Yuan had prepared for Chu Ci was a source-type lifeform that would have a burning effect on everyone other than its contractor.","After the Burning Sunflower was contracted, the Burning Sunflower Spirit would bloom out of its flower buds.","Fairy source-type lifeforms like the Burning Sunflower had high intelligence. As a fire-type, the Burning Sunflower Spirit had a temper like raging flames.","The Burning Sunflower would attach itself onto one target in battle while its flames razed all the opponents present.","If it attached itself onto one of its teammates, said teammate would be covered with a shield that was impervious to fire-elemental energy.","If it attached itself to an opponent, the opponent would suffer excessive damage from fire-elemental energy and burn continuously from the Burning Sunflower’s nearby flames.","The Burning Sunflower also had fairy-elemental energy and could morph its body.","This meant that the feys that the Burning Sunflower Spirit attached itself to would be unable to escape the attachment through physical attacks.","The Burning Sunflower Spirit’s attachment could be either a blessing or a curse depending on which side it chose.","However, the Burning Sunflower Spirit was not without weakness, as it was not as effective against feys with dispersal abilities.","Although the Burning Sunflower Spirit would only show its true might on the battlefield, Lin Yuan did not insist on giving it to Chu Ci because of the damage it could inflict on its enemies.","It was because its imperviousness against fire could provide Chu Ci with an additional level of protection.","The moment Lin Yuan had set his eyes on the Burning Sunflower, he felt that it was exceptionally compatible with the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s exclusive skill, Pain Absorption.","It would help the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull to fulfill the conditions needed for Annihilation Gaze when the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull was not being attacked.","Chu Ci’s enemies would face more than just spirit qi professionals that had attacking abilities from now on.","The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Annihilation Gaze needed it to be injured so as to transform the damage into mental attacks that could be used against the enemy.","Once the conditions for Annihilation Gaze were met, even if Chu Ci was faced with spirit qi professionals that were skilled at using support-type feys, regular defense-type spirit qi professionals, or even healing-type spirit qi professionals, she would be fine.","After seeing the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s Silver abilities, Lin Yuan felt that the Burning Sunflower was complementary to the Pain Buffer ability.","Chu Ci had not formed a contract with the Burning Sunflower, and its abilities had not yet been ascertained.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was already extremely happy with the fairy source-type lifeform’s original abilities.","Lin Yuan could not help but internally whistle his approval.","Many source-type lifeforms might look average, but they will become unexpectedly powerful with the right contractor that can tap into their real power.","For example, the Burning Sunflower, whose flames could not be contained, was considered a burden to most people’s fey teams.","Chu Ci was a defense-type spirit qi professional, and she had the Vajra Butterfly.","The Vajra Butterfly’s shield and the Burning Sunflower Spirit’s protection over its own teammates against fire-elemental energy could protect Chu Ci’s feys from being burned.","Besides hoping that they had an impressive fey, spirit qi professionals also wanted their contracted feys to complement each other so as to form a well-rounded combat system.","The addition of the Burning Sunflower to Chu Ci’s combat system would change the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s originally man-powered strength into nuclear-powered.","Lin Yuan only hoped that Chu Ci’s process of forming a contract with the Burning Sunflower would go smoothly and that the Burning Sunflower was not hiding any strange abilities.","Although Chu Ci had formed a contract with the Burning Sunflower, Lin Yuan felt that his plan to nurture his sister into an iron bucket had completed its beginning stage.","Lin Yuan did not use to be a shut-in, but he did often get dragged off by classmates to play League of Legends.","No matter which hero Lin Yuan chose, he would lose whenever he encountered Demacia powerhouses.","Regardless of how hard Lin Yuan worked, he could not break out of the 0-8 where he died multiple times.","As such, since the Lin Yuan of today was set on turning Chu Ci into an iron bucket, he was determined to help Chu Ci attain power akin to a Demacia powerhouse’s.","The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s exclusive skill, Pain Absorption, was the equivalent of Chu Ci wearing Warmog’s Armor.","The Vajra Butterfly’s exclusive skill Counterattack Tremor was the equivalent of Chu Ci wearing Thornmail.","Once Chu Ci formed a contract with the Burning Sunflower, she would also be wearing the equivalent of Sunfire Cape.","With all these armors, how could she lose? I’m going to nurture her into Demacia itself! This is what a good brother should do.","When Chu Ci saw that Lin Yuan was suddenly stunned, she anxiously waved her hands in front of his face. Lin Yuan did not react, and she had no idea what was going through his mind.","She stared warily at Lin Yuan as she blinked.","Chu Ci considered sending out a message for help on Star Web’s gossip column.","Her post would be—’My brother is suddenly spacing out. Am I about to have a sister-in-law?’","Chu Ci cleared her throat and decided to test Lin Yuan.","“Big Brother, it’s two days until New Year’s. Who are you going to spend it with?”","When Lin Yuan heard Chu Ci’s words, his brain was split between thinking about the next step in his plan to turn his sister into a Demacia powerhouse and the Burning Sunflower’s potential.","The gears in Lin Yuan’s mind were turning rapidly.","Lin Yuan hoped that after the Vajra Butterfly became a Fantasy Breed, it would form a connection with the Burning Sunflower.","This would allow Chu Ci to form a fighting formation with the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull at the center, and the three feys would be working with perfect cohesion.","Since his mind was preoccupied, Lin Yuan unconsciously said, “I’ll be spending it with you, of course!”","Before Chu Ci could react to Lin Yuan’s response, she saw him splutter and turn toward her to ask in surprise, “What? How is it only two days until New Year’s?”","Chu Ci nodded.","Lin Yuan remembered that when he had been sucked into the dimensional rift, there were still ten days until New Year’s.","Lin Yuan was certain that he had only used half a day to stop the dimensional rift from evolving.","This meant he had been in a coma for seven days!"]},{"number":527,"title":"Chapter 527: The Warmth in the Years","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan instinctively touched his pocket.","This was when he realized that his clothes had been changed an unknown amount of time ago.","Instead of his original moon-white spirit qi clothes, he was now wearing moon-white lounge clothes similar to what he and the Moon Empress wore on a daily basis.","Lin Yuan was about to look for his phone when he suddenly remembered the Mother of Bloodbath had taken his phone before he was sucked into the dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan hurriedly turned to Chu Ci and asked, “Chu Ci, lend me your phone. I need to make a call.”","When Chu Ci saw the look of worry on Lin Yuan’s face, she quickly handed him her phone.","Seeing how worried he is, could something urgent have happened?","Before he had lost consciousness, Lin Yuan had treated Liu Jie’s injuries, but Lin Yuan was unsure if Liu Jie’s mental state had been affected by the purplish-gray poison.","During the seven days that he had been in a coma, the Insect Queen’s transformation must be almost completed.","Lin Yuan was also rather concerned about Zhou Luo.","However, Zhou Luo’s life was not in danger.","Since Zhou Luo had taken an oath to Lin Yuan under the Willpower Rune, Lin Yuan was certain that Zhou Luo was still alive.","Lin Yuan received Chu Ci’s phone and was about to call when he realized that Chu Ci did not have Liu Jie’s number.","Lin Yuan did not have the habit of memorizing phone numbers, so he circulated his spiritual energy to summon Genius.","Lin Yuan asked Genius, “Genius, what’s Big Brother Liu’s phone number?”","Genius had evolved into the Thousand Questions Beast and was not what it used to be.","Not only had it retained all its abilities as a housekeeping beast, but it was also even stronger now.","Genius answered in a child-like voice, “1...”","Genius hopped into Lin Yuan’s embrace, its tiny claws digging into Lin Yuan’s neck.","Genius had turned into a mask for Lin Yuan when they were in the dimensional rift.","Thus, Genius and Lin Yuan had shared the same view of everything in the dimensional rift.","Genius had watched with fright as the flesh of Lin Yuan’s hands was stripped by the dimensional fluctuations.","However, Genius had been unable to do anything other than watch.","Lin Yuan had comforted Genius in the spiritual world, but it was still anxious over Lin Yuan after being summoned.","When Lin Yuan saw how worried Genius was, he stroked Genius’ three tails and was about to massage Genius’ furry neck when he saw Genius raise its head to look at him.","Tears were welling up in Genius’s eyes, but it spoke with utter solemnity. “I want to be stronger, Yuan! I want to help you!”","Lin Yuan smiled and stroked Genius’ head.","“Genius has always been helping me. Knowledge is power. You’re amazing!”","Genius swiped its claws at the air before replying, “Genius is as powerful as a plate of roasted meat. I’ll do my best to become as powerful as 100 plates of roasted meat!”","Genius stretched out its claws and waved it in front of Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan pinched Genius’ claws that were moving about in the air and touched the soft pads underneath its claws. He shook the claws twice before hooking his finger around Genius’s claws.","“Then we have a deal. I can’t wait till Genius becomes as powerful as 100 plates of roasted meat!”","Genius’ brilliant blue eyes shone, and the corners of its eyes were still damp.","Genius’ small face spread into a human-like grin.","Before Genius could respond, Chu Ci dashed in.","Chu Ci scooped Genius into her arms and started to stroke Genius’ fur with practiced ease.","Chu Ci’s actions immediately had Genius purring contentedly.","“Did you miss me, Little Genius?”","Chu Ci took a few pieces of meat out of the fey storage box Lin Yuan had gifted her and held the fragrant morsels up to Genius’ mouth.","In the time that Lin Yuan had been in a coma, Genius had not had any appetite for food.","Most of the Cane Luffa in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had ripened and fallen to the ground during the seven days.","Genius had been so worried about Lin Yuan that it had not thought about food at all.","But now that it took a whiff of the meat in Chu Ci’s hand, Genius’ stomach immediately started to gurgle.","Genius said in a child-like voice instead of eating the meat, “Genius missed Chu Ci so much! I missed you as much as 1,000 pieces of roasted meat!”","Lin Yuan raised his eyebrow at Genius’ words.","Genius had always been beloved everywhere it went. Even a middle-aged uncle like Hu Quan enjoyed hugging Genius at every opportunity.","Lin Yuan finally understood why.","At that moment, Lin Yuan’s call to Liu Jie went through.","Lin Yuan rushed to ask, “How are you recovering, Big Brother Liu?”","Liu Jie did not answer Lin Yuan’s question. He could not help but take over the conversation and ask, “How are you, Lin Yuan?”","Liu Jie still had more to say, but Lin Yuan heard Wen Yu’s voice on the other end say, “Big Brother Liu, is the call from Young Master? Why didn’t you say anything? Has his body recovered?”","Lin Yuan heard Wen Yu’s voice increase in volume by several times.","“All of you come here! Young Master is calling!”","Less than half a minute later, Lin Yuan heard Endless Summer, Hu Quan, the Mother of Bloodbath, Listen, and Zhou Luo’s voices.","Their tones were urgent as they anxiously questioned his condition.","A tinge of warmth crept over Lin Yuan’s heart.","When the cacophony of voices died down, and after some idle chatter, Lin Yuan said, “I’ll be going back tomorrow. It’s going to be New Year’s in two days. We should make preparations together!”","Lin Yuan was really looking forward to this year’s New Year’s celebrations.","Last year, Lin Yuan had spent New Year’s with Chu Ci in the Xia Region.","This year, both Lin Yuan and Chu Ci had embarked on a new chapter of their lives and had amassed many caring companions.","After saying that, Lin Yuan was about to ask if Liu Jie’s Insect Queen had finished transforming.","Liu Jie said, “Lin Yuan, I just received word from the Radiance Sacred Hall that the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards wants to see me!”","Now that he knew Liu Jie was busy, Lin Yuan did not ask about the Insect Queen’s transformation.","Lin Yuan was going to return to the mansion tomorrow anyway. If there were any issues with the Insect Queen, Lin Yuan could use True Data then to check.","The moment he hung up, an ethereal and strangely crisp spiritual voice called out once again from the depths of Lin Yuan’s soul.","“My Lord.”"]},{"number":528,"title":"Chapter 528: The Grace Queen and the Sword of Punishment","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was immediately startled upon hearing that voice.","He had already found its source—it had come from the depths of his soul.","He subconsciously pushed his thoughts into the depths of his soul. He discovered that he could touch it unimpeded this time, although he had failed to do so before.","There, Lin Yuan immediately found that within one of the two humanoid shadows was a girl with her eyes closed, a crown on her head, and a sharp sword in her hand.","He used True Data to scan the girl floating in the air within the shadow.","Upon analyzing True Data’s information, Lin Yuan was suddenly at a loss for words!","Could sacred source lifeforms merge?","The girl whom he had scanned was not one sacred source lifeform but two that were merging together.","These two sacred source lifeforms were presently merging together slowly into one.","This led Lin Yuan to think about the scene in his dream where the reddish-gold light had coerced the crown-wearing girl into embracing that sharp sword.","According to True Data, this girl was a sacred source lifeform with the name ‘Grace Queen’.","And the sword with the gorgeous patterns engraved on its hilt was also a sacred source lifeform with the name ‘Sword of Punishment’.","These two sacred source lifeforms had already been 70% fused.","After the remaining 30% fused together, the two would become a new sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan made a rough calculation based on the time that he had spent in a coma. He would know what kind of sacred source lifeform would come about from the fusion of the Grace Queen and the Sword of Punishment in about three days.","In the process, the two’s abilities would be sealed off as they fused together.","As they had already been around 70% fused, Lin Yuan could not understand their individual abilities from the information he had obtained from True Data.","Nevertheless, just by looking at her name, the Grace Queen was a sacred source lifeform with support abilities, while the Sword of Punishment was one with attack abilities.","Lin Yuan was not at all worried about what the two would fuse to become—he was filled only with intense anticipation.","The Moon Empress and the Mother of Bloodbath had both previously mentioned that every sacred source lifeform had irreplaceable abilities.","This also meant that sacred source lifeforms did not have a weak existence.","Moreover, even if Lin Yuan did not know why these two perfectly good sacred source lifeforms would fuse together in his soul, he knew that the new lifeform birthed from their fusion would be stronger than their original forms!","If not, why would they even fuse?","In the depths of his soul, Lin Yuan could hear the crowned girl with her eyes closed calling him “My Lord” continuously, even when he was deep in sleep.","He felt a throb originating from his bloodline.","This throb connected him and the girl tightly.","Back then, in order to prevent the dimensional rift’s evolution, the two sacred source lifeforms in Lin Yuan’s hands had absorbed a lot of his blood.","They had even absorbed some of Lin Yuan’s bone marrow from his broken bones.","If not for the fact that this crowned girl with her eyes closed was an illusory spiritual body, just the feeling of his bloodline’s connection to her would have made Lin Yuan feel as though he were raising a daughter.","At present, Lin Yuan did not think too much. He just needed to wait three days.","Then, he could use True Data to completely understand the new sacred source lifeform’s abilities.","After coming back to his senses, Lin Yuan found that Genius had turned into a cat pancake in Chu Ci’s arms.","Its three small tails wagged continuously as it wore a satisfied look on its face.","Actually, when Lin Yuan had hung up the phone earlier on, he had already noticed that Chu Ci had been looking at him hopefully.","At the same time, her expression carried a hint of shyness.","Lin Yuan could immediately tell what Chu Ci was thinking about.","Lin Yuan stretched his hand out and stroked her hair as she hugged Genius in her arms.","After pressing down the stray hair on her head, he said, “Buy whatever you want when you go shopping for New Year’s goods. This time, the Black Back Mountain Boar and Bighead Carp Soup will be enough!”","Chu Ci chuckled upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words.","Although she still didn’t know how many resources Lin Yuan had on hand, just the pocket money she received from him on her Star Web Card every once in a while would be enough to buy several Black Back Mountain Boar and Bighead Carp breeding farms.","Moreover, Chu Ci always ate the nutritional set meal that Lin Yuan had customized at the Spirit Food Pavilion. She could always eat food that was two times more delicious than Black Back Mountain Boar and Bighead Carp Soup.","However, when Lin Yuan mentioned these two dishes, Chu Ci still felt unrestrained warmth surging in her heart.","No matter what happened in the future, the taste of Black Back Mountain Boar and Bighead Carp Soup had long been engraved in Chu Ci’s memory.","In her 16 years, this taste was equivalent to the memory of celebrating New Year’s with Lin Yuan.","“Brother, don’t be reluctant to eat the carp in the Bighead Carp Soup this New Year’s.”","Lin Yuan rubbed his nose upon hearing this.","Chu Ci had really misunderstood his intentions!","During every New Year’s meal, Lin Yuan would indeed always save the Black Back Mountain Boar’s lean meat for Chu Ci, while he would eat some of the boar skin or vegetable soup that she did not like.","However, he did not eat the carp in the Bighead Carp Soup just because Chu Ci liked eating it... He didn’t like eating foods with strong smells at all.","When it came to this, Genius had the same preferences as Lin Yuan.","After Chu Ci had spoken, the hope in her expression disappeared.","Every year, she and Lin Yuan would hold a few hundred Federation dollars to buy New Year’s goods.","This had been her childhood dream.","Now that she had grown up, even if buying New Year’s goods was no longer her dream, the thought of eating New Year’s delicacies still filled her with delight.","Perhaps what delighted her even more was the fact that she could spend time with Lin Yuan, just like when they had been children.","As the hope on Chu Ci’s face disappeared, her shy and restrained expression grew increasingly intense.","Upon seeing her expression, Lin Yuan revealed his white teeth with a bright smile and said..."]},{"number":529,"title":"Chapter 529: Skipping a Grade and the Woman in Black on the Rope Bridge","paragraphs":["“Haven’t you already met Liu Jie and Wen Yu?","“Previously, you also saw all those people when we were on that video call.","“They all hope that you can come over. Wen Yu already set up a room for you when the mansion was built.","“Uncle Hu knows that you like Black Back Mountain Boars, so he even made some wooden carvings of them that he left in your room.”","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, Chu Ci wondered if she still wanted to defend herself at this time.","She could not remember how many times she had already told Lin Yuan that she only liked eating Black Back Mountain Boars—she didn’t like the boars themselves.","However, every time she explained this, Lin Yuan would always be afraid that she was oversensitive and would hint to her that she was free to like any fey.","Not being too concerned about this, Chu Ci decided to give up on correcting him.","The shyness on her face also vanished.","After she had grown a bit older, Chu Ci had also begun helping Lin Yuan greet the guests at his fey store.","Although she was not good with words, she was also not a coy person.","It was just that, meeting so many of Lin Yuan’s friends at once still made a 16-year-old girl like Chu Ci feel a little nervous.","After all, even if she did know some of the mansion’s inhabitants, she had only met them through a video call and not in real life.","Suddenly, Chu Ci recalled Cold Moon’s suggestion for her before the latter had become her master and said, “Brother, Master said that if I qualify for the Redbud Hundred this year, I can represent them to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s selection next year.","“I will also get the chance to qualify for the ten Radiance Hundred seats.","“If I do qualify for the ten seats, Master suggested that I should directly skip a grade and take the entrance examination for Royal Capital Advanced Spirit Qi University.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan did not immediately help Chu Ci make a decision as he would have done so before.","Instead, he smiled slightly and replied, “You’re all grown up now. You can make your own decisions about these matters.”","In this world, the person who most understood Lin Yuan may not have been Chu Ci, but the person who most understood Chu Ci was definitely Lin Yuan.","Although Chu Ci was usually rather reserved, she was someone with her own ideas.","Since Chu Ci had brought this matter up with him, it proved that she was already planning to skip a grade and enter Royal Capital Advanced Spirit Qi University.","Previously, Lin Yuan had gritted his teeth and chosen to let Chu Ci continue her education under such difficult conditions because he had wanted her to experience a complete childhood and feel that she could gain the same knowledge as other children with parents.","However, Chu Ci now chose to embark on a path for prodigies through her talent and hard work.","After the holidays were over and she returned to school, Chu Ci would possess two Fantasy Breed feys and one fairy source-type lifeform, the Burning Sunflower.","It was very likely that few of the seniors who used to participate in training competitions with Chu Ci were now worthy of being her opponents.","This was, for someone like Chu Ci, who was good at finding problems in actual combat and making progress, tantamount to missing out on many opportunities for hard practice.","Hence, for Chu Ci to maximize her growth, her best option was to attend Royal Capital Advanced Spirit Qi University.","By that time, she would also be able to live in the mansion and return to it directly every day after school.","The siblings could also live together every day.","Chu Ci smiled upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words.","“Then I will do as Master says and aim to skip a grade next year to attend Royal Capital Advanced Spirit Qi University.”","Lin Yuan scratched Chu Ci’s nose, thinking to himself that her heart’s ambition was not small.","Nevertheless, thinking about her Obsidian Iron Wild Bull that had evolved from Silver to Fantasy II and how she now had an expert like Cold Moon as her Master, Lin Yuan suddenly had the feeling that Chu Ci could even get a seat in the Radiance Hundred Sequence the next day if she wanted to.","Having been awake for a while now, Lin Yuan said as he lifted the covers and got out of bed, “Chu Ci, let’s go out! Our Masters must be worried sick!”","As he spoke, Lin Yuan’s expression grew slightly cold.","At that time, he was thinking about Hunting-Ashes, the gray-haired, gray-eyed man whom he had encountered in the dimensional rift.","He also recalled how the man had said the name ‘Seventh Page War’ after injuring Liu Jie and thinking that Lin Yuan and Liu Jie would definitely die.","It could be said that these two pieces of information were all the information about the enemy that Lin Yuan could grasp while he had been in the evolving dimensional rift.","Now that he was back at the Radiant Moon Palace, Lin Yuan could relay this information to the Moon Empress. He could also see if the Moon Empress knew who this opponent was and how much power they had.","...","Liu Jie only felt confused at that moment.","Even if he was ranked Radiance Hundred Sequence #30, he was still unworthy of being personally received by the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards.","Moreover, the Chief Guard herself had personally informed the Radiance Sacred Hall about this matter before they had relayed the news to him. This could be said to be extremely formal.","Yet, the more formal it was, the more Liu Jie felt that it was unusual.","He also had a faint guess. The reason the Chief Guard had summoned him likely had something to do with the dimensional rift that had appeared at the coastal sea near Indigo Azure City.","It was just that, although this was an important matter, the Spirit Guards’ Guard Envoys could have been fully responsible for receiving him.","Besides the Guard Envoys, even the left and right heads could have taken care of this.","It did not require the Chief Guard at all.","While Liu Jie puzzled over this, he arrived at the lakeside of Spirit Guard Lake, where the Spirit Guards’ headquarters was located.","As long as he walked across the rope bridge that led to the center of the lake, Liu Jie would arrive at the Spirit Guards’ headquarters.","When he arrived at the lakeside and was preparing to step onto the rope bridge, Liu Jie saw a black-robed, black-veiled woman in the distance.","She was standing in the middle of the bridge with her hands behind her back.","She did not reveal the slightest spirit qi fluctuation, as though she was an ordinary person.","Even when the east wind caused the rope bridge to sway, the woman’s figure was like the unmoving bronze beast guarding the ends of the bridge.","As a Radiance Hundred Sequence member, Liu Jie had seen the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards before.","Just by looking at the way she was dressed and her appearance on the rope bridge near the Spirit Guards’ headquarters, Liu Jie could immediately confirm her identity."]},{"number":530,"title":"Chapter 530: Greetings, Chief Guard; What a Coincidence","paragraphs":["At that moment, an idea suddenly sprang into Liu Jie’s head.","“Can it be that the Chief Guard is waiting for me here?”","However, he cast this idea aside as soon as he thought of it.","Given the current active period of this dimensional rift, the Chief Guard would have to deal with many things every day. How would she have been able to make time to wait for him?","Just as Liu Jie looked at the black-robed, black-veiled Chief Guard, she seemed to sense his gaze and turned her head to look toward him.","Despite the vast distance between them, Liu Jie still saw the Chief Guard’s pitch-black eyes the moment she turned around.","Under the gaze of that pair of pitch-black eyes, Liu Jie suddenly felt a trace of indescribable pressure.","He was like a fish leaving the water under a final endless, starless night that felt like it would be sealed off by the endless night, doomed to sink forever.","At that moment, Liu Jie stepped onto the rope bridge and walked across it to the other side.","The Chief Guard stared at him unyieldingly, which filled him with a strange feeling.","However, he also had no idea what to do. He had no choice but to move forward one step at a time.","The more he walked, the more misgivings surfaced in his heart.","There was no one on the bridge but Liu Jie, and the Chief Guard kept looking in his direction without shifting from her position.","It really looked like she was specifically there to wait for him.","Liu Jie quickened his pace and walked until he was beside the Chief Guard.","After thinking for so long, he still did not know what to say to her.","Finally, he only said respectfully, “Greetings, Chief Guard. What a coincidence.”","Upon hearing Liu Jie’s words, Night Leaning Moon turned her body to make room for him.","She signaled for him to come forward and walk shoulder to shoulder with her.","Immediately after, Liu Jie heard an unusual sound that was steady yet sweet as a singing yellow oriole.","Upon hearing this sound, he inexplicably thought of the sound that Chimey made when it was calling out.","Because of Bai Hao, Liu Jie had also heard Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess, Star Web’s beautiful host, sing a few times before.","Previously, Liu Jie had only sighed at how Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ singing voice was so pleasant that it could actually be compared to that of an avian fey.","However, Liu Jie suddenly had an idea. What if the beautiful Star Web live streamer was the Spirit Guards’ Chief Guard?","He immediately cast this idea aside as soon as he came up with it.","Liu Jie thought in his heart about the absurdity of this notion. Could the influence of the mental poison in the dimensional rift have messed with his head?","Nevertheless, upon hearing the Chief Guard’s words, Liu Jie’s expression transformed immediately.","He looked both shocked and solemn.","“It was not a coincidence. I intended to come here to wait for you.","“Am I right to say that your Insect Queen has not woken up from its state of mutation?","“The Insect Queen’s body should have absorbed most of the Blade Queen Bee’s natal poison within the natal poison core.”","Back in the evolving dimensional rift, Liu Jie had been tortured by the purplish-gray mental poison.","Even after receiving Lin Yuan’s healing and the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia’s baptism, only his physical body had been healed.","If not for the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus flower paste that Lin Yuan had given him, it was very likely that Liu Jie would have woken up a few days later.","Moreover, Liu Jie had still slept for a full five days and had woken up only two days earlier than Lin Yuan.","Upon awakening, Liu Jie had found himself lying in his own room in the mansion.","According to Wen Yu, it had been Uncle Mystic who had brought him there.","Now, the Chief Guard not only knew about his Insect Queen’s condition, but it was also in such great detail.","This meant that when he had been in a coma after being spat out of the dimensional rift, the Chief Guard must have been there to have personally checked the Insect Queen’s condition.","Upon hearing the Chief Guard mention the Insect Queen, Liu Jie thought about when he had sensed the Insect Queen’s condition himself.","In the process of evolutionary mutation, the Insect Queen had been in an awkward state where it could neither advance nor retreat.","Now that the Chief Guard had mentioned the Blade Queen Bee’s natal poison, Liu Jie finally knew what the gray-haired, gray-eyed man had launched at him in the dimensional rift.","The Insect Queen had absorbed this poison in order to mutate.","However, because there had not been enough poison in the natal poison core, the Insect Queen had been unable to absorb the amount needed to complete its mutation.","The poison had also fused into the Insect Queen’s genetic model during the mutation process.","Now, as the Insect Queen had been suspended in the mutation process for a long time, it was very possible that the absorbed natal poison would attack the Insect Queen’s body.","If that happened, the poison engraved in the Insect Queen’s genetic model would explode in its body.","The Insect Queen’s spiritual energy would be severely damaged by the Blade Queen Bee’s mental poison.","It might even die under the poison’s attack.","Most people would not easily discuss private issues like the condition of their feys with others.","However, since the Chief Guard had asked, Liu Jie did not hold back when he told her about the Insect Queen’s current condition.","As he spoke, his feet traversed the rope bridge and stepped onto the Spirit Guards’ land.","They continued walking toward the study where Night Leaning Moon always stayed.","After understanding the Insect Queen’s condition, Night Leaning Moon said, “The Insect Queen only needs to absorb more of the Blade Queen Bee’s natal poison from its poison core in order to complete its mutation.”","Upon hearing this, a bitter smile revealed itself on Liu Jie’s face.","Carcinoma feys were rare on this continent. Moreover, he needed to find a particular carcinoma fey.","This was simply an impossible task.","At that moment, Night Leaning Moon added unhurriedly, “When you said ‘what a coincidence’ just now, you weren’t wrong.","“Amongst the carcinoma feys kept in the Spirit Guards’ headquarters, there happens to be one Blade Queen Bee.”","As she spoke, Night Leaning Moon was already sitting at the desk in her study where she usually read the secret letters sent by her Guard Envoys.","Liu Jie was pleasantly surprised by her words.","Deeply concerned about the Insect Queen, Liu Jie had forgotten that the Spirit Guards and Guard Envoys took in carcinoma feys found throughout the Radiance Federation and high-grade feys that had committed evil, keeping them on this land.","The Spirit Guards were in charge of the world’s feys.","Based on the Chief Guard’s words, it seemed that he could extract the natal poison core from the Blade Queen Bee’s body and give it to the Insect Queen."]},{"number":531,"title":"Chapter 531: Two Choices","paragraphs":["Liu Jie quickly thanked her.","“Thank you, Chief Guard.”","Upon hearing this, the brush in Night Leaning Moon’s hand stopped. She immediately placed it on the table and said, “Don’t thank me yet. This is your reward for everything you sacrificed in the evolving dimensional rift.","“However, I will still give you two choices...","“The first is to obtain the natal poison core from the Blade Queen Bee’s body and allow the Insect Queen to complete its mutation.","“Following which, if you can obtain one of the top ten seats of the Radiance Hundred Sequence and qualify to compete for a position in the Radiance Envoy, the Spirit Guards will give you a sacred source lifeform.”","Liu Jie was immediately shocked by the Chief Guard’s words.","This first choice actually had a reward in the form of a sacred source lifeform!","It was just that it would not be easy to obtain the sacred source lifeform.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence members all concealed their strength. Everyone was holding in their breaths.","By making it such that he had to get into the top ten of the Radiance Hundred Sequence in two years and qualify to compete for a position in the Radiance Envoy, the Spirit Guards would be making a huge investment in him.","However, Liu Jie would need to prove himself before he could attain this investment.","A sacred source lifeform was at stake!","Within each Class 5 dimensional rift that so many experts had to combine forces to resist, only a single sacred source lifeform could be produced.","This was something that Liu Jie did not even dare to think about.","However, his desire for a sacred source lifeform was no less intense than others’.","After all, Liu Jie had only been able to contract one source-type lifeform—the Insect Queen. He did not have as many choices as others.","Nevertheless, Liu Jie did not immediately agree after hearing about this generous first choice. Instead, he asked, “Chief Guard, what about the second choice?”","Night Leaning Moon proceeded to say cleanly, “The second choice is for you to become my disciple.”","While Liu Jie had been shocked deep down by the mention of a sacred source lifeform previously, he now felt his heart almost leap out of his chest upon hearing this.","This was simply too much excitement for one day!","Did one really need to choose if one were presented with the option of being the Chief Guard’s disciple?","Even someone who was not a fool would choose the second option without hesitation.","Although Liu Jie was no fool, he did not immediately make a choice.","Experts always strove to accept many disciples. Few could tolerate it if their own disciple had already sworn a rune oath to another with a Willpower Rune.","A rune oath made with a Willpower Rune represented a constraint that could never be resisted.","Liu Jie had already sworn to Lin Yuan with a Willpower Rune to become the latter’s retainer knight.","To Liu Jie, becoming the Chief Guard’s disciple could completely be considered an undeniably good thing.","Had it been in the past, he would have definitely fought tooth and nail for such an opportunity.","Yet, this was no longer his first priority.","He extended his hand to touch the Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest on his chest and could not help but feel a twinge of pain in his heart.","Perhaps it was because a small corner of the crest, which Lin Yuan had given him, had been blown up in the explosion within the evolving dimensional rift, but this crest filled Liu Jie with a new hope.","After Liu Jie had returned to the Radiance Hundred Sequence, because he had never hidden his identity as a Class 2 Creation Master retainer, he would always wear the crest on his chest every time he went out, regardless of what he was wearing.","In the Radiance Hundred Sequence, it had not caused a major disturbance that Liu Jie wore his Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest.","However, this had only been the case in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","After becoming #30 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, when the news of wearing of the crest spread outside, it had exploded on the Star Web’s forums.","Perhaps many people believed that becoming a Class 2 Creation Master retainer was not something to be proud of for someone like Liu Jie.","However, this Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest, which was not glorious in others’ eyes, was Liu Jie’s life!","Liu Jie was now already thinking of leaving the Spirit Guards’ land that night if the Chief Guard had nothing else to discuss with him.","He would first go to the Creation Master Association in the Royal Capital to fix his Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest.","If he did not have time, he would buy food first.","Then, when Lin Yuan returned to the mansion, he could cook a hearty meal for the both of them to eat.","Even though Night Leaning Moon was a top-notch Radiance Federation expert, who held one of 13 seats in the imperial court and was the Moon Empress’ equal, she had still felt somewhat nervous after presenting Liu Jie with the second choice of being her disciple.","The stronger one was, the more attention they paid to one’s fetters.","Night Leaning Moon had never accepted a disciple. She had only considered accepting one after seeing how it had changed the Moon Empress.","It was also time for her to find a successor.","However, after Night Leaning Moon had spoken about the second choice, she still did not receive a response after a long while.","Because of the shadow of her childhood, Night Leaning Moon detested waiting for others to make a decision.","What kind of human suffering was this!?","Night Leaning Moon made a few successive strokes with the brush in her hand while waiting for Liu Jie to make his decision.","Just then, Liu Jie raised his head firmly and said with great honesty, “Chief Guard, I... already made an oath with a Willpower Rune to become someone else’s retainer knight.","“Without him, I wouldn’t be who I am today. If you mind that I have become someone else’s retainer, I will choose the first option.”","Upon hearing this, Night Leaning Moon immediately placed the brush on the table.","She tapped her fingers lightly on the tabletop and only felt that the disciple she was about to accept seemed a little dense.","Since she had already decided to accept a disciple, would she not have already investigated clearly all that should have been investigated before?","As she thought about the relationship between Liu Jie and the Moon Empress’ disciple, Night Leaning Moon could not help but recall her and the Moon Empress’ youth.","Back then, she had almost become the Moon Empress’ retainer knight.","However, the Moon Empress had scoffed at her for not being capable of providing for herself and for singing out of tune.","Hence, she had not become the Moon Empress’ retainer knight.","That despicable, unsmiling Cold Moon and that horrid fey Mystic Moon had stolen the position first.","Time always turned tens of thousands of times. The distant years that had never seemed imminent now suddenly appeared before her eyes.","If she accepted Liu Jie as her disciple, everything would seem to form a cycle.","Night Leaning Moon was even more appreciative of Liu Jie’s honesty.","While her disciple was a little foolish, he was unexpectedly honest!","“I am Night Leaning Moon. From now on, I will be your Master.”"]},{"number":532,"title":"Chapter 532: Liu Jie’s Fate","paragraphs":["Night Leaning Moon waved her hand and tossed a box carved out of white jade to Liu Jie.","Liu Jie looked through the white jade box and saw a subtle layer of rainbow light on the interior.","When he saw the rainbow light, Liu Jie felt a strange sense of familiarity. It was as though he had seen it not long ago.","Liu Jie made a guess to himself.","Liu Jie opened the white jade box to see a glowing rainbow mass nestled inside.","The glowing rainbow mass was the legendary sacred source lifeform.","He was shocked and slightly frightened to receive this from his new Master.","Liu Jie did not accept the white jade box with the sacred source lifeform inside.","Instead, he placed it on Night Leaning Moon’s table and said, “Master, I haven’t fulfilled the first condition of reaching the top ten in the Radiance Hundred Sequence and gaining the right to be a Radiance Envoy.”","Night Leaning Moon waved her hand again.","A few petals immersed in soft blue light appeared on the table.","The underside of the petals was as blue as the sea and was dotted with glistening flower sap. They carried a refreshing comfort that could soothe souls, and it seemed like they had only just recently fallen.","“Since you address me as Master, I need to carry out the responsibilities that come with the title. How can my disciple be without a sacred source lifeform? You’re already past 20 years old, which makes you more than capable of contracting sacred source lifeforms. The flower sap of these Blue Snow Soul Fragrance petals can protect your soul and allow you to contract the sacred source lifeform without a problem. You won’t have to suffer soul damage. Why don’t I protect you now while you contract the sacred source lifeform?”","While Liu Jie had spoken with courtesy and honesty, Night Leaning Moon had spoken with utter nonchalance.","For some reason, when Night Leaning Moon heard Liu Jie address her as Master, she experienced a new feeling. It was the feeling of having a sense of responsibility.","This feeling of responsibility was surreal to Night Leaning Moon. It was different from the overwhelming sense of responsibility she felt as the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards. The responsibility of being a Master was more exquisite.","In the past, Night Leaning Moon had never had a legacy, but now with Liu Jie as her disciple, she did.","He was someone to whom she could directly pass down her legacy.","Night Leaning Moon used to think that the Moon Empress was overly doting of her disciple.","Once she became a Master, Night Leaning Moon understood why the Moon Empress did what she did.","It was why she naturally retrieved the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance’s petals.","Liu Jie was floored by the situation. He stared at the blue petals on the table and smiled dazedly when he heard the name Blue Snow Soul Fragrance.","He was unfamiliar with the term.","Liu Jie had never heard of the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance, but it had to be special if it could aid in forming a contract with sacred source lifeforms.","Liu Jie could tell from the way that his Master gently held the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance that it was rather valuable.","“Master, the first choice...”","Before he was done speaking, Liu Jie heard Night Leaning Moon casually say, “If you weren’t my disciple, I would be more discerning about what I gifted you. But now that you’re my disciple, there will no longer be any holds barred.”","Night Leaning Moon rose to her feet, grabbed the sacred source lifeform inside the white jade box, and thrust it into Liu Jie’s hands.","“Forming a contract with sacred source lifeforms is a detailed process. A blood contract will not be enough. Blood contracts allow you and the sacred source lifeform to form a blood bond, but the blood bond does not have contractual obligations. It only establishes an equal connection.” she said solemnly.","Sacred source lifeforms were outrageously wise and had their own sense of morality. Hence, using blood to seal the deal on such a level of blood contract would not be ideal.","Liu Jie reached out his hand and rubbed the back of his head with a wry smile. He only knew of sacred source lifeforms, but his knowledge about them was limited.","For example, he did not know about the contract process. To someone like Liu Jie, who never dared to hope to possess a sacred source lifeform, it was natural that he was ignorant.","When Night Leaning Moon saw the look on Liu Jie’s face, she picked up the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance petals and said, “The best way to contract sacred source lifeforms is to use your own bone marrow to form what is known as a marrow contract.","“Marrow contracts can tame sacred source lifeforms, but your soul will feel pushback from the sacred source lifeforms. Every sacred source lifeform possesses fragments from the other world across the dimensional hub and carries a kind of complete law. The law has a similar ability to the truth.","“Although most people’s souls are fully matured by the time they reach 20 years old, they are still unable to sustain the clash against sacred source lifeforms.","“However, with these monarch-class Creation Blue Snow Soul Fragrance petals, you’ll be able to use your marrow to form the blood contract with the sacred source lifeform without worries.","“During the contract process with the sacred source lifeform, you will need to allow it to be subsumed into your soul in order to forcefully tame it. This will require some time. But with these three Blue Snow Soul Fragrance petals, you should be able to form the contract in a few hours.”","Night Leaning Moon’s voice was as lyrical as an oriole’s. She patiently and seriously cleared all of Liu Jie’s doubts. He might not have asked any verbal questions, but she could decipher his queries from his expressions.","With Night Leaning Moon’s elucidation, Liu Jie now understood how to form a contract with the sacred source lifeform.","He also became aware of why the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance was precious.","Not only was the Blue Snow Soul Fragrance a spiritual ingredient from a Creation Breed fey, but its ability to protect souls already made it invaluable.","The soul had always been shrouded in mystery. Spiritual ingredients that could protect souls were far and few.","They were one of the most sought-after items by top-level spirit qi professionals.","Since he had become Night Leaning Moon’s disciple, Liu Jie mulled for a while before saying, “Thank you, Master.”","After the battle surrounding the evolving dimensional rift, Liu Jie had become acutely aware of where he was lacking."]},{"number":533,"title":"Chapter 533: Ultimate Transformation","paragraphs":["Since Lin Yuan had helped Liu Jie to replenish his spiritual power, the explosive impact of his insect army during the battle was at least three times more powerful than Liu Jie’s original power.","Even if he could raise his power by at least three times, if he could not stand out in battle to blast away the obstacles in Lin Yuan’s way, he would only be able to rely on his body after the Insect Queen’s army had depleted. It would not matter how much he wanted to fulfill his duty; he would still be dead weight.","Liu Jie was unbelievably anguished by his helplessness.","He might currently be #30 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, and the Cocoon of Evolution had started hatching inside the Insect Queen, but watching Lin Yuan improve put immense pressure on him. The Insect Queen’s huge boost in power was not enough.","Liu Jie knew that as long as Lin Yuan continued on this trajectory, he would soon surpass Liu Jie.","When that time came, the sword and shield he could become would be dull and useless in the face of his faith.","With a Master and the chance to reach for the heavens, the ever-insecure Liu Jie had a golden opportunity before him.","Night Leaning Moon needed to understand Liu Jie before she accepted him as a disciple, and Liu Jie also needed to think things through deeply.","To a loyal person like Liu Jie, the moment he addressed Night Leaning Moon as Master, he would hold her in that esteem for the rest of his life.","Night Leaning Moon frowned when she heard Liu Jie’s thanks.","“What are you thanking me for? I’m your Master. Let’s begin. I obtained this sacred source lifeform from within a Class 5 marsh dimensional rift. I hope its powers will be compatible with your Insect Queen,” said Night Leaning Moon.","No one knew what powers a sacred source lifeform contained before it was contracted.","Even an amazing expert like Night Leaning Moon could not know what the rainbow-glowing sacred source lifeform looked like.","It could be said that contracting a sacred source lifeform was just like opening a blind box, for each item in the box had its own use.","Yet, one had no clue if the item in the box would be a good fit with what one already possessed.","Night Leaning Moon’s words, and because she was Liu Jie’s Master, felt like a blessing to Liu Jie.","It did not matter even if the sacred source lifeform was of no use to the Insect Queen.","One contracted sacred source lifeform was akin to Liu Jie owning a technique that defied the laws of reality.","A few hours later, a pillar of energy shot into the sky.","All of the experts in the Spirit Guards’ headquarters looked as though they had been plunged into eternal and all-consuming darkness.","In an instant, the terrifying pressure vanished.","Several Spirit Guard experts looked in the direction of the Chief Guard’s study.","They all began guessing what could have happened to the Chief Guard for her to have released her energy all of a sudden.","At that moment, Night Leaning Moon’s lyrical voice rang out in laughter from inside the room.","She was standing beside the table, and the majestic spirit qi in her hand had formed a spirit qi vortex that was shielding the secret letter from the Guard Envoy.","A mysterious green glow shrouded Liu Jie as his eyes flew open. He looked at Night Leaning Moon rather bashfully and said, “Master, I wasn’t aware that when the sacred source lifeform formed the contract and combined with my soul that it would automatically launch an attack.”","Liu Jie might have apologized, but his gaze shone with surprise and glee.","Night Leaning Moon was wearing a black shawl over her face that hid her facial expression.","However, it was clear from the angle of her eyes that she had to be smiling.","“When one’s soul fully tames a sacred source lifeform, they will launch an attack known as Sacred Source First Cry. It’s as though it heralds the birth of a true ability, and the first cry is the sacred source lifeform’s way of declaring its existence to the world.”","Night Leaning Moon nodded with satisfaction and continued. “Judging from your contracted sacred source lifeform’s attack, I can confirm that it is a sacred source lifeform that specializes in attacking. Not bad! You’re truly my disciple! We have the same inclination.”","At long last, Liu Jie had a sacred source lifeform to call his own.","With this sacred source lifeform, Liu Jie finally understood why sacred source lifeforms were so powerful.","Besides the sacred source lifeform’s innate abilities, Liu Jie was happier to know that his contracted sacred source lifeform had some compatible abilities with the Insect Queen.","The flames of confidence erupted in Liu Jie’s eyes.","He extended his hand and touched the Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest on his chest that was lacking one corner, clutching it tightly in his hand.","Liu Jie was only using the strength in his fingers.","Liu Jie’s palm was gently closed over this damaged retainer crest as though he was afraid of squeezing and breaking it.","He was about to present his contracted sacred source lifeform to Night Leaning Moon when she interrupted him.","Night Leaning Moon’s expression was exceptionally austere and serious.","“You should never speak of the sacred source lifeform’s abilities. You can’t tell anyone, even the people closest to you!”","Night Leaning Moon only continued after she ascertained that Liu Jie was really paying attention.","“I asked someone to retrieve the Blade Queen Bee in the containment item before you came. The natal poison in the Blade Queen Bee could only be condensed after it cleared its body of insect eggs and devoured a large number of feys. This took some time. The natal poison should have condensed by now.”","Liu Jie trailed behind Night Leaning Moon as they left the study room.","Liu Jie was completely different from the person he was before he had entered the study.","Liu Jie used to be a piece of silver. Now, he only appeared to still be a piece of silver, but his interior had already become gold.","Once Liu Jie’s Insect Queen completed its evolution, the silver on Liu Jie’s surface would also change into gold to match his interior.","When Liu Jie walked out of the study, he recalled that there were high winds when he had arrived, but now the sun was hanging high in the sky. The searing light beat down upon him.","Liu Jie’s entire body was flooded with warmth. It felt lovely and comfortable.","...","Mystic Moon looked at the roasted Spirit Savory Pig on the whalebone table. Its skin was golden and crispy, and he was silently stunned for three seconds.","I wonder what became of the two Spirit Savory Pigs left in the Kitchen Fragrance Pavilion. Those are the only two Spirit Savory Pigs left in the world, and they’re both males! It looks like Chef Supreme will never have a chance to use the postnatal care for sows he picked up."]},{"number":534,"title":"Chapter 534: The Definition of Adoration","paragraphs":["The Moon Empress cut up the Spirit Savory Pig into small pieces and added some sauce made from Diamond Plums.","She set the dish down in front of Lin Yuan and said, “The Supreme Chef fattened up this Spirit Savory Pig with many good things. It’s slightly cloying even though it was roasted with the strange Fiery Meteor from the dimensional rift. The Heart Plum sauce is perfect for offsetting the sickening taste, and they taste pretty good together.”","Cold Moon already thought that the Moon Empress was going a bit too far when she used the Diamond Smooth Crystal-Thread Jujubes, but now she thought that the Moon Empress had gone right off the edge.","The Heart Plum was a medicine that could cure damaged sources.","Although healing-type spirit qi professionals could treat all sorts of injuries, if other spirit qi professionals’ feys did not have special exclusive skills, they would still be susceptible to damage from source-type lifeforms.","Injuries related to the heart were not only considered to be external injuries, but they were also under the umbrella of damaged sources.","In order to fully recover, they needed a Creation Master to treat them with a concoction made of spiritual ingredients.","The plant-type Heart Plum’s plums were effective against healing heart-related injuries.","Low-grade Heart Plums were not only sold all over Star Web’s Rare Lifeform Pavilion but they were also sold at large markets. They were not considered precious goods.","On the other hand, a Diamond Heart Plum was another matter.","The Heart Plum was a type of fey that was virtually impossible to nurture to evolve.","Most feys, including the Spirit-Siphon Goldfish, which needed to absorb many more times of spirit qi than other feys, would be able to evolve once they absorbed enough spirit qi.","However, the Heart Plum would be stuck once it reached Gold grade.","It would only be able to evolve if it absorbed the tree cores of ten other Heart Plums of the same grade.","An immeasurable quantity of low-grade Heart Plums’ tree cores would be needed to nurture a high-grade Heart Plum.","In the hands of a Creation Master, a Silver Heart Plum could soothe traumatized hearts.","Creation Masters could use Platinum Heart Plums to heal cracked hearts.","Creation Masters could use Heart Plums to heal shattered hearts, essentially saving a life.","The unique attribute of the Heart Plum was that it tasted delicious.","As a spiritual ingredient that could heal source injuries, the Heart Plum tasted much better than even the most premium food ingredients.","A few prestigious, affluent families made a habit of eating Heart Plums and even added a few dried ones into their cooking to enhance the flavor.","However, even the most elite of affluent families did not consume Heart Plums that were higher than Gold grade.","Cold Moon knew that the Moon Empress was not a wasteful person, and she only made the Diamond Heart Plum sauce because she wanted to nourish Lin Yuan’s body.","The heart circulated blood all over the body. After losing so much blood, Lin Yuan’s heart would not be able to circulate blood as well for some time.","Lin Yuan had already consumed a large portion of the Rabbit Emperor’s carrot, and regardless of how severe his injuries were, he was as strong as an ox now.","The Leaning Moon Mountain’s fruit orchard had seven or eight Diamond Heart Plum trees, and they produced a bountiful harvest each year.","However, Lin Yuan did not need the Diamond Heart Plum to treat his heart anymore!","Every time the Moon Empress and Lin Yuan interacted, Mystic Moon’s definition of adoration a Master could shower on her disciple was redefined.","Using the strange Fiery Meteor to roast the pig was not considered a waste. There would be no negative externalities, but the Moon Empress was probably the only person who would do so other than Chef Supreme.","The Moon Empress wanted to use the Fiery Meteor’s vibrations to induce the oil out of the pig.","Mystic Moon watched as the Moon Empress served Lin Yuan a plate of cut ribs, while the ever-solemn Cold Moon carefully held the Spirit Savory Pig’s ribs.","She sliced the meat off the most roasted parts and placed it on a plate.","Mystic Moon was puzzled.","Cold Moon doesn’t usually eat meat. Why does she look like she’s going to eat the Spirit Savory Pig’s rib meat?","After Cold Moon was done slicing the meat, she went on to slice a crispy golden piece of pigskin and ladled a spoonful of sauce all over the plate.","The tartness of the plums and the fragrance of the pigskin formed a perfect symphony.","Once eaten, one would taste two completely different flavors and textures. Mixing sweet and sour was the best way of eating the Spirit Savory Pig.","Mystic Moon was surprised to see that the normally vegetarian Cold Moon knew how to feast on the meat like a gourmet!","At that moment, Cold Moon placed the plate in front of Chu Ci, just like the Moon Empress did for Lin Yuan.","Mystic Moon noticed Cold Moon looking at him, her eyes shining.","It was as though she was saying, “Hehe, how useless. You can’t even get yourself a disciple after walking the earth for such a long time.”","Mystic Moon immediately lost his appetite.","These two sets of Masters and their sibling disciples looked like they were throwing him scraps that he chose to pathetically gobble up.","Mystic Moon could not help but want a disciple of his own.","Lin Yuan shoveled the pork ribs the Moon Empress had prepared for him and basked in her affection for him.","He took the opportunity to ask about the sacred source lifeform in the depths of his soul.","When the Moon Empress had mentioned sacred source lifeforms to Lin Yuan, she had told him not to tell anyone about his sacred source lifeform’s abilities.","Lin Yuan was not going to ask about his contracted sacred source lifeforms’ abilities because he had no idea what they were.","“Master, can sacred source lifeforms fuse?”","The Moon Empress was momentarily stunned before she quickly replied, “If a person’s soul is strong enough, they can contract two sacred source lifeforms. However, I’ve never heard of sacred source lifeforms fusing.”","The Moon Empress did not know what brought on Lin Yuan’s question, but she knew that he had contracted a sacred source lifeform from the dimensional rift.","Hence, she was troubled about his query regarding sacred source lifeforms."]},{"number":535,"title":"Chapter 535: Make Your Own Decision","paragraphs":["The Moon Empress knew that she needed to share more information about sacred source lifeforms with Lin Yuan during their question-and-answer session.","Could it be that after he contracted a sacred source lifeform, he’s trying to find another so that he can fuse them? Is he trying to form a completely new sacred source lifeform? What a strange way of thinking.","When Mystic Moon heard what Lin Yuan said, he almost choked on the roast meat in his mouth.","He admired Lin Yuan’s weird thought process.","What kind of weird brain would come up with such a way to maximize their advantage? If what he said was true, then sacred source lifeforms would be able to enhance their abilities by absorbing other sacred source lifeforms!","The Moon Empress noticed that Lin Yuan had almost finished his pork. Thus, she picked up a white Dehua porcelain bowl and filled it up with jujubes as dessert for Lin Yuan.","It was one thing for the Moon Empress to adore Lin Yuan, but this treatment was not giving Lin Yuan a secretive lifestyle.","The Moon Empress was anxious over Lin Yuan’s health now because she had been scared silly when he had exited the dimensional rift.","The fright did not stem from the sight of Lin Yuan’s desiccated hands, but because the barely 20-year-old Lin Yuan had undergone a marrow contract with sacred source lifeforms. He had allowed sacred source lifeforms to enter his soul.","This was also why the Moon Empress had snapped the rabbit’s carrot in half without hesitation and given it to Lin Yuan.","Nevertheless, the Moon Empress was thankful that Lin Yuan had formed a marrow contract with the sacred source lifeforms.","It was a milestone in a spirit qi professional’s life when they managed to contract a sacred source lifeform.","There was no way to regret or redo the act.","If Lin Yuan had only formed a blood contract with the sacred source lifeform, then it was likely that he would not be able to utilize it with the same ease as if he formed a marrow contract.","At his age and level of power, Lin Yuan did not understand the difference between a blood contract and a marrow contract.","However, once he became a top expert, the difference would be much more evident.","The Moon Empress saw this coincidence of Lin Yuan contracting a sacred source lifeform as a lucky blessing for him.","When Lin Yuan heard the Moon Empress’s reply, he understood that the fusion process of his sacred source lifeforms was out of the ordinary.","Even someone as powerful as the Moon Empress had never heard of something like that.","After waking up, Lin Yuan had noticed there was really a young crowned girl with her eyes closed and a sword in her hands in the depths of his soul.","This was when he knew that the dream he had been having, while he was comatose, had actually taken place in the depths of his soul.","Lin Yuan thought back to the golden light that had enveloped him in the depths of his soul. The light was the exact same color as Morbius’ bracelet.","Lin Yuan was not stupid.","After finding Morbius deep asleep, it became clear to him that the golden light, which had enveloped him and caused the two sacred source lifeforms in the depths of his soul to fuse, had belonged to Morbius.","From the moment that Lin Yuan had contracted Morbius, he had felt as though this partner of his was no regular fey.","Before Lin Yuan had any concept of what source-type items were, he had just assumed Morbius was one.","After coming into contact with source-type items, Lin Yuan had discovered that Morbius did not possess the same kind of abilities as source-type items.","Soon after, Lin Yuan had also come to know about sacred source lifeforms.","Lin Yuan could not help but wonder if his Morbius could also be a sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan recalled the wild sacred source lifeforms’ terror as they were flooded by the golden light in the depths of his soul, and he made a crazy hypothesis—could there be a level higher than the sacred source lifeform?","Lin Yuan didn’t continue asking the Moon Empress about his sacred source lifeforms’ fusion process.","Since she had never heard of such a thing, talking about it with her would only cause her to worry.","It was unlikely that the fused sacred source lifeforms would be weak.","Once he was done asking his question about sacred source lifeforms, Lin Yuan raised his head and set down his spoon.","“Master, I met someone called Hunting-Ashes in the dimensional rift. He mentioned someone called Seventh Page War,” said Lin Yuan with utmost seriousness.","The Moon Empress had been serving Lin Yuan jujubes with a smile on her face, but her expression flattened when she heard Lin Yuan’s most recent statement.","Cold Moon’s features tensed as well.","Mystic Moon’s silver eyes narrowed.","The Moon Empress’s expression was also solemn for a second, and her original smile quickly replaced it.","She placed the jujubes in front of Lin Yuan and said, “Eat up. These jujubes are great for blood circulation. See if my technique has improved.”","Lin Yuan took note of his Master, Cold Moon, and Mystic Moon’s expressions. He knew that they were aware of his intention, and he now also had a general idea of how powerful this Seventh Page War person was.","The fact that the Moon Empress changed the topic the moment the name was mentioned meant that she did not want to divulge too much to him at the moment.","Lin Yuan did not pursue the matter.","Lin Yuan had used all the strength he could muster and even staked his life in order to stop the dimensional rift’s evolution. He had done what he thought was right.","Lin Yuan was aware that his powers might be improving, but they still lacked when it came to such events.","Only someone as strong as his Master would be able to handle such events.","Lin Yuan dipped his head and took a mouthful of jujubes. He was surprised to find that they were not as sweet as he imagined.","The pure jujube fragrance seemed to engulf Lin Yuan.","The Moon Empress lifted her hand, and a glowing rainbow mass appeared in her palm.","“This is your reward from the Spirit Guards for stopping the dimensional rift’s evolution. You have already contracted a sacred source lifeform. Your soul needs at least three years to recover before you should try contracting another sacred source lifeform. I arranged this sacred source lifeform for you ages ago. So, you can decide for yourself what you want to do with this sacred source lifeform.”","The Moon Empress handed the sacred source lifeform to Lin Yuan as she spoke."]},{"number":536,"title":"Chapter 536: The Brother Who Was Taught a Lesson by His Sister","paragraphs":["When the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan take hold of the sacred source lifeform, she said earnestly to him, “Three years later, I need to be by your side to protect you if you plan on attempting to allow your soul to contract a sacred source lifeform again.”","The Moon Empress thought back to when the dimensional rift had just spat out Lin Yuan and how the sacred source lifeform had cataclysmically shattered his soul.","The Moon Empress had made a point of saying that she needed to be by Lin Yuan’s side the next time he wanted to contract a sacred source lifeform. Still, she was essentially saying that she needed to be there to protect him in order to increase his chances of contracting his second sacred source lifeform.","Souls were different from fate.","A person could lack talent, but as long as they worked hard, they could very well achieve the same results as a more talented person.","However, the difference in souls was decided upon the moment a person was born. Nothing could be done to close the gap.","Even if a spirit qi professional used the most valuable spiritual ingredients in their attempt to contract a second sacred source lifeform, they would only be able to protect their soul from being damaged by the sacred source lifeform’s attacks. His chances of being able to successfully contract the sacred source lifeform would not rise.","The Moon Empress said what she said because she did not want Lin Yuan to suffer the pain of having his soul shattered again.","The Moon Empress’s words of concern brought a bright, toothy smile to Lin Yuan’s face.","“Don’t worry, Master. I’ll make sure to be by your side the next time I want to try contracting a sacred source lifeform,” Lin Yuan promised her.","Lin Yuan’s innocent beam and the promise he gave her were music to the Moon Empress’ ears.","The Moon Empress could not help but smile internally.","The Moon Empress had always felt that Lin Yuan was wise beyond his years. Although he was only 18-years-old, both the way he spoke and the manner in which he acted was that of a fully matured adult.","This had always saddened the Moon Empress.","If Lin Yuan was someone else’s disciple, the Moon Empress might have been impressed at the way that Lin Yuan carried himself.","But since he was her disciple, Lin Yuan hoped that he would not carry so many burdens on himself.","As his Master, the Moon Empress hoped that Lin Yuan could live a carefree life like a regular 18-year-old.","The way that Lin Yuan currently appeared like the young man he was warmed the cockles of the Moon Empress’s heart.","Lin Yuan kept the sacred source lifeform into the amber-button-shaped fey storage box and devoured the fragrant jujubes.","Lin Yuan could not help but start to think about how he could use the sacred source lifeform. He lifted his head and looked at Chu Ci, who was currently scooping jujubes into a bowl for Cold Moon.","Chu Ci’s action reminded Lin Yuan of himself.","As the Moon Empress’ disciple, all he did was sit and receive her generous affection.","Lin Yuan had also taken numerous precious goods from the Radiant Moon Palace.","Every time he tried to bring precious goods back to the Radiant Moon Palace, the Moon Empress would say, “You don’t need to bring anything home. I have everything.” She would insist that he kept it all for himself.","As time went on, Lin Yuan no longer tried to bring anything back to the Radiant Moon Palace.","But now, Lin Yuan felt as though he had been making a mistake. He never imagined that his younger sister would teach him a lesson.","Something small like Chu Ci preparing a bowl of jujubes for Cold Moon, Lin Yuan realized that he had never done anything like that.","When Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci, Cold Moon’s gaze became odd as it landed on Lin Yuan.","After a few seconds of internal conflict, Cold Moon said, “Young Lord, Chu Ci is only 16 years old. She’s still far off from 20 years old. There’s no rush for her to contract a sacred source lifeform. When the time is right, I’ll also prepare a sacred source lifeform for her.”","Lin Yuan felt that Cold Moon was acting like a lioness protecting her cubs on the grassland. She might not have said it explicitly, but Lin Yuan could tell from her expression and tone that she was possessive over Chu Ci.","Lin Yuan chuckled awkwardly.","Ever since Chu Ci got herself a Master, it has even become difficult for me to give her anything.","However, Lin Yuan could sense Cold Moon’s concern for Chu Ci.","“Auntie Cold, I’ll be leaving Chu Ci in your hands!”","Once Cold Moon heard what Lin Yuan said, the aloofness that was written all over her face from the mention of Seventh Page War melted away.","Her usually inexpressive countenance spread into a rare smile.","“Don’t worry, Lin Yuan,” said Cold Moon.","Instead of addressing Lin Yuan as Young Lord, she used his given name.","At that moment, Cold Moon did not regard Lin Yuan as the Young Lord of the Radiant Moon Palace but rather the older brother of her disciple.","Chu Ci telling Lin Yuan not to worry was her way of responding to Lin Yuan entrusting Chu Ci to her.","Lin Yuan was not only delighted that Chu Ci had found a Master in Cold Moon but was also exceptionally comforted.","When Cheng Wu had been chasing Lin Yuan in the Royal Capital’s outskirts, and his life had been hanging by a thread, his brain had unconsciously drifted to: What if I really die? What will happen to Chu Ci?","Now that Chu Ci had Cold Moon as her Master, Lin Yuan would not have to worry about her even if he was about to die.","Lin Yuan had looked at Chu Ci because he had thought about his younger sister the moment that he received another sacred source lifeform.","He did not think about the fact Chu Ci would be contracting a sacred source lifeform before she reached 20 years old.","The Moon Empress had reminded him several times that a spirit qi professional needed to be 20 years old before they could contract a sacred source lifeform.","Otherwise, the spirit qi professional’s soul would be in great danger.","Lin Yuan had his partner Morbius, which had helped him survive the crisis by protecting his soul with its golden light.","However, Morbius was an anomaly that only Lin Yuan possessed.","Lin Yuan could guarantee that from the moment Chu Ci was born, she had remained clean and did not have a partner fey like Morbius.","Since Lin Yuan did not need to worry about Chu Ci, Lin Yuan decided that the most suitable candidates in his faction were Liu Jie and the Mother of Bloodbath.","Lin Yuan was leaning toward allowing Liu Jie to contract the sacred source lifeform between the two of them."]},{"number":537,"title":"Chapter 537: You Eat More Than a Black Back Mountain Boar","paragraphs":["Liu Jie was already 25 years old, at a suitable age to contract a sacred source lifeform.","On the other hand, it was anyone’s guess how much more time the Mother of Bloodbath needed before it reached Creation Breed.","Lin Yuan did not know how much the Mother of Bloodbath could improve by consuming a stick of the Blood Brew Grapevine’s Blood Brew Grapes.","Even if he ordered Red Thorn to maximize its efforts in allowing the Mouth of Relinquish to absorb flesh energy and produce Eyes of Relinquish and nurtured Blood Brew Grapevines to quickly grow Blood Brew Grapes, he had encountered a true glutton.","Compared to the unpredictable state of the Mother of Bloodbath, it was a better choice to allow Liu Jie to contract the sacred source lifeform.","As for Zhou Luo, who had gone through hell and back with him in the dimensional rift, Lin Yuan did not plan on giving him the sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan no longer saw Zhou Luo as merely one of his white-clothed followers from Sky City.","He was now one of Lin Yuan’s true confidants.","Lin Yuan nurtured them so he could exchange Bronze spiritual resources in return for their loyalty.","It would be completely up to the white-clothed followers if they wanted to nurture the Bronze spiritual resources.","However, Lin Yuan wanted to invest a large amount of his own resources into Zhou Luo. He intended on helping Zhou Luo’s Lava Dragon Lizard and his newly contracted Bronze/Epic Dark Snake Dragon Lizard to evolve swiftly.","Lin Yuan planned on raising the Bronze/Epic Dark Snake Dragon Lizard’s quality to Legend before Zhou Luo evolved it to Silver.","Being a member of the white-clothed followers, Zhou Luo had taken the allegiance oath and sworn his loyalty to Lin Yuan. He was a member of Sky City.","Ever since Zhou Luo had volunteered to take on a fight that could have cost him his life, Lin Yuan had validated Zhou Luo.","During this trip back from Indigo Azure City, they had experienced many trials and accumulated numerous advantages.","Even if the advantages from the Indigo Azure Sea Market were not counted, just contracting the sacred source lifeform was enough for Lin Yuan to see this experience as worthwhile.","It was almost New Year’s, after which came the S Tournament season.","The S Tournament season came before the S Tournament finals.","There would also be a duel between the Radiance Hundred Sequence. It was sure to be a highlight.","During the Radiance Hundred Sequence duel, Lin Yuan planned to focus on training his faction in the Royal Capital.","Ever since Lin Yuan had obtained his dedicated territory on Star Web, he had not executed those three rights and announced his private faction’s management to the rest of the people on Star Web who also owned factions with dedicated territories.","Lin Yuan planned on using the new season to properly manage his private faction and spread its impressive reputation.","If Lin Yuan wanted to stand toe to toe with the veterans, he needed to act like a lovable businessman in order to attract people with the message: I have the best goods, come to me.","After the meal, Lin Yuan and Chu Ci started to learn from their individual Masters.","When Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress conducted the question-and-answer session, he took the opportunity to throw out all the questions he had amassed.","Naturally, the biggest problem Lin Yuan threw out was about sacred source lifeforms.","Although he already possessed a sacred source lifeform, Lin Yuan was still completely ignorant about their characteristics.","From the Moon Empress’s answers, Lin Yuan found out that the formation of a contract with sacred source lifeforms was differentiated between blood contracts and marrow contracts.","Lin Yuan remembered the injuries he had sustained while grabbing the sacred source lifeforms, and he knew that he had to have formed marrow contracts with the two sacred source lifeforms.","As he listened to the Moon Empress explain the process of marrow contracts, fear crept into Lin Yuan.","At the same time, he was also curious to know exactly what Morbius was.","How had Morbius protected his soul from shattering in such a perilous situation?","As the question-and-answer session went on, Lin Yuan garnered a basic understanding of sacred source lifeforms.","The Moon Empress realized that a large portion of Lin Yuan’s questions were about the origins of lifeforms.","From this, the Moon Empress’ could sense the exponential rate at which Lin Yuan was improving, and she felt slightly stunned as she answered his questions.","It had barely been half a year since he became her disciple.","But, Lin Yuan’s growth during the past six months was the equivalent of other geniuses’ five years of hard work.","The Moon Empress was also certain that Lin Yuan was hiding some secret techniques that he did not usually employ.","At least, his identity as Black, who was a healing-type spirit qi professional, was the real deal.","Otherwise, such concentrated vitality would not have flowed out of his body when he was comatose after being spit out by the dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan had not reached A-rank and could not circulate the spiritual power in his body to form a spirit qi vortex.","Without the protection of the spiritual power vortex, what kind of healing abilities did Lin Yuan have which allowed him to remove the sacred source lifeform from the evolving dimensional rift?","In order to remove the sacred source lifeform from the dimensional fluctuations in the dimensional hub, one could only rely on the innate strength in their body.","If one utilized a fey to go against the overwhelming power, the energy in the attacks would be transported to the other world through the dimensional hub.","The Moon Empress was not against Lin Yuan hiding his abilities. In fact, she endorsed it.","Thoughts of approval surfaced in her mind.","He really is my disciple. Both of us prefer to hide our power.","The question-and-answer session lasted the entire afternoon.","After the question-and-answer session, Mystic Moon, who was notorious for not having a disciple, prepared a scrumptious feast for dinner.","After dinner, the sun started to disappear below the horizon.","The burnt orange glow of the sunset was exceptionally warm. As Lin Yuan and Chu Ci strolled along Leaning Moon Mountain, their shadows slowly grew longer.","Lin Yuan handed Chu Ci some dried fruit he had picked from Leaning Moon Mountain.","The plants that grew on Leaning Moon Mountain were plentiful, and the feys that lived there would never be able to finish all the ripe fruits that fell.","Lin Yuan peeled the pine nut in his palm and gave it to Chu Ci.","“This fresh nut has not been roasted. It might lack some fragrance, but the freshness is more evident than ever. Are you really okay with eating so many fruits and nuts after such a large dinner?” asked Lin Yuan.","Chu Ci looked at the palm-sized pine nut. As she skipped along, she giggled and said, “Please, these fruits and nuts don’t take up any room in my stomach, Lin Yuan.”","Despite her words, Chu Ci patted her satisfied belly as she chewed on the pine nut.","It was spring all year round at Leaning Moon Mountain.","The young girl walked in step with the young man. They were surrounded by lush greenery, and every expression that lit up their faces was flooded with the beautiful sentiment of sibling love.","The young girl skipped along the path and handed Lin Yuan the half-eaten pine nut.","“I can’t eat anymore, big brother,” said Chu Ci.","The young man turned to look at the young girl. He reached out his hand and swiped at the corner of Chu Ci’s lips with mock frustration, wiping off the pine nut scraps lodged there.","Lin Yuan glanced at the half-eaten pine nut in his hand and said with a half-vexed and half-affectionate voice, “It’s about time you were full. You eat more than a Black Back Mountain Bear.”"]},{"number":538,"title":"Chapter 538: Lin Pigeon Who Chirped for Two Days","paragraphs":["After dinner, Cold Moon immediately led several spirit attendants to organize Chu Ci’s accommodations at Leaning Moon Mountain.","Chu Ci was Cold Moon’s only disciple.","Besides Lin Yuan, Chu Ci was now a true core member of the Radiant Moon Palace.","Chu Ci carefully selected a loft that faced the stream that ran along the Radiant Moon Palace.","The loft had a traditional design. As it was situated next to the stream, the aroma of nature permeated the air.","This loft was not far from where Lin Yuan was staying.","As the sun disappeared below the horizon, the sky was stained with navy hues.","Once Lin Yuan sent Chu Ci home to the loft, he took a rest in the loft.","Lin Yuan realized that Cold Moon had meticulously decorated the loft with Chu Ci in mind.","Although the loft did not appear to be very elegant, it was actually extremely opulent. Even the decorative vases inside were made of amazonite.","Under the light, the gleaming amazonite vases were just as radiant as jade.","The amazonite had Yin energy and was very beneficial to women’s skin.","A table completely made of amazonite sat in the main room of the loft.","The amazonite seemed familiar to Lin Yuan.","It suddenly dawned upon him that the amazonite table was Cold Moon’s favorite that used to be in her own residence.","Cold Moon had placed her favorite item in Chu Ci’s room without a second thought for how precious it was.","Cold Moon’s love and adoration for Chu Ci were almost tangible.","A few spirit fruits were washed and stacked on an amazonite platter in a classy display. These spirit fruits were harvested lately. Shortly after being exposed to the nourishing aura of the amazonite, the spirit fruits were even fresher than before they were harvested.","Lin Yuan could not shake the feeling that the room was missing something.","In a stroke of genius, Lin Yuan decided that when the time came, he would place the jade Black Back Mountain Boar made by Hu Quan in Chu Ci’s accommodation. Chu Ci would probably like that.","Lin Yuan prepared to leave.","Before he left, Lin Yuan pressed down the stray hair on the top of Chu Ci’s head.","“Rest early tonight. I’ll be taking you to our other home tomorrow morning,” said Lin Yuan.","The sight of the dark circles under Chu Ci’s eyes made Lin Yuan’s heart ache.","I was in a coma for so long. Chu Ci must have been worried about my safety and hasn’t been able to sleep properly.","Chu Ci nudged Lin Yuan’s hand with her head and stretched lazily.","“Big brother, I want to watch another battle on Star Web. I want to learn when to release defensive abilities from other defense-type spirit qi professionals. I’ll go to sleep after I battle on Star Web for half an hour,” said Chu Ci.","As Chu Ci spoke, her delighted smile overtook her features.","Chu Ci might not have admitted it, but the past seven days had been a rollercoaster for her. Her mind had been consumed with worry for Lin Yuan, and she could not be bothered with anyone else.","Once Lin Yuan woke up, Chu Ci reflected on all that she experienced in Leaning Moon Mountain. She felt as though she was living in a dream.","Chu Ci knew that Lin Yuan had a Master.","However, Chu Ci did not expect her big brother’s Master to be one of the top three Class 5 Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation—the Moon Empress.","She also did not know that the doting Auntie Cold was one of the two Moon Envoys.","Chu Ci had known that Cold Moon initially stayed with her in Redbud City because of Lin Yuan’s Master, but not once did she question Cold Moon’s background or try to dig into it.","Besides her initial shock, Chu Ci did not have many other thoughts. She focused on her current environment. Chu Ci felt that everything that had transpired the past few days did not feel like reality.","Now, with Lin Yuan right in front of her, Chu Ci’s heart abruptly calmed down.","To Chu Ci, as long as Lin Yuan was around, there would be his supporters there to help her.","This was not just dependency but also the feeling that wherever Lin Yuan was would be home.","In the past 15 years of Chu Ci’s life, Lin Yuan and her had been depending on each other for as long as she could remember.","They were a small family.","Yet, now they had two huge families. Lin Yuan’s presence was in both of them, and Chu Ci was glad for that.","Lin Yuan initially wanted to advise Chu Ci not to burn the midnight oil if she had not been sleeping well, but somehow he could not bring himself to say it.","His little sister was working so hard, and she wanted to learn more fighting skills for the next one and a half hours. She even wanted to put the fighting skills she learned to the test during the half an hour of battle. Working hard had become a part of her lifestyle.","There was no reason for him to oppose such a commendable habit.","Although Lin Yuan could tell her that there were many opportunities to learn in the future, he knew that the process of maturing involved taking any and every step possible to broaden one’s horizons.","Today’s effort could not be replaced no matter how hard one worked tomorrow because today’s harvests belonged solely to today.","Lin Yuan was proud of Chu Ci.","When he heard how she wanted to learn about defense, he was happy for her. His sister had finally become a mature iron bucket, and she knew how to strengthen herself.","Lin Yuan returned to his own accommodation after he departed from Chu Ci’s loft.","After spending seven days in a coma, it was high time for him to take a soak and scrub off all the grime.","Later that night, he logged on to Star Web using his Creation Master identity and settled all the tasks that had piled up while he was comatose.","Taking into account the time he was sucked into the dimensional rift, a total of ten days had passed.","He auctioned off the ten heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls he had prepared for the Purchase With No Loss store that he had not managed to put to use.","It should have started two days ago.","Lin Yuan had logged on to Star Web two days late because he had been in a coma, which meant he had wasted two days of group welfare time.","Now that he had regained consciousness, he wanted to quickly auction off the ten heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls."]},{"number":539,"title":"Chapter 539: You Are Imagining Things and Creating Lies","paragraphs":["Otherwise, the other people in the group might not only say that the group leader was lurking but also that he had run off after robbing the group welfare.","On the way back, Lin Yuan found that a slight breeze in the night air was enough for the chill to pierce his bones.","There should still be three days till New Year’s, after which came spring.","It should be deep winter now, but the cold night breeze carried a sliver of warmth normally associated with spring.","Lin Yuan played his experiences in Indigo Azure City like a movie in his mind. Once he was done, other than sighing at the sheer intensity of the peril he was in, Lin Yuan felt that his life had become more fulfilled.","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard a lovely female voice laced with the haughtiness of a lady of high society call out, “Don’t be so competitive. We should compare who can get up earlier. If you don’t sleep, I won’t either. We’ll eventually be together. Count it as your blessing. You’ll never be able to escape me!”","Lin Yuan was shocked to hear such a voice.","Where in Leaning Moon Mountain would such an obviously elite lady’s voice come from?","Shortly after, Lin Yuan heard another slightly familiar voice.","“Who are you talking to, Pan Yue? Are you dating someone online?”","Jin Qi stared suspiciously at Pan Yue.","Spirit attendants spent their days in the Radiant Moon Palace and rarely left unless they were tasked to do so.","When they were on a task, they mostly interacted with top experts and the heads of powerful factions.","Those people were definitely advanced in age. Moreover, even if they were attracted to Pan Yue after discovering that she was a spirit attendant, they would never dare to make a move on her.","What Pan Yue said over the phone was indeed peculiar.","Her saying ‘we’ll eventually be together’ was too obvious!","Although the Radiant Moon Palace spirit attendants were not forbidden from dating, very few of them were willing to do so. They knew that being in a relationship would cost them their role as a spirit attendant, and they would be demoted to a mere servant.","Additionally, Pan Yue had placed first in every category of the spirit attendant exam. If she lost her role as a spirit attendant and was demoted to a servant for the sake of a relationship, she would have tossed all her hard work down the drain.","Pan Yue rolled her eyes at Jin Qi’s words and said sarcastically, “A partner? I have a boyfriend? My boyfriend is perfect. He’s mature, serious, not clingy, and non-existent.”","Pan Yue felt that this woman was really lame, but she knew what kind of person Jin Qi was.","If Jin Qi had misunderstood, all the other spirit attendants would come to share the same misunderstanding by the next morning.","Pan Yue did not want to bring trouble upon herself, so she decided it was best to clarify the situation with Jin Qi.","“I was talking to Ji Mei. We’ll be protecting the stunning Teacher Guo together tonight.”","Jin Qi was confused by Pan Yue’s explanation, and she could not help but feel as though she and Pan Yue were from different planets.","Jin Qi did not understand how someone like Pan Yue, who only ever spent her time prancing about, could attain the power of a Creation Master.","Even if Jin Qi spent 25 hours a day learning and put in 101% of effort, the Creation Master power she would attain would still fall short of that of the ever-halfhearted and playful Pan Yue.","Jin Qi was beginning to think that the world was too fake.","Jin Qi thought, I’m much better looking than Wen Yu. When it comes to talent, I used to be below her before she was injured on behalf of someone else.","Now, I’m definitely better than the Wen Yu, whose source is damaged! So how did that wild chicken suddenly become a phoenix?","Why can’t I, a pigeon, who tries so hard to gain attention but is ignored, be treated like a common quail?","I can’t remember the last time I had a good night’s rest. Although Wen Yu hasn’t targeted me all this time, I can’t shake the feeling that she will stab me in the back the moment I lower my guard.","Jin Qi took out a piece of chocolate from inside her yellow spirit attendant long robes.","Eating something as sinful as chocolate soothed the pressure building up in Jin Qi’s heart.","When Pan Yue saw Jin Qi eating the chocolate, she became aware of how hungry she was.","“Your chocolate looks pretty good. How about I exchange it with you for this?”","Pan Yue fished a round item out of her Diamond fey storage box.","As the sky had darkened, Jin Qi took a while before she realized what the round item in Pan Yue’s hand was.","It looked like a furry potato to her.","“What do you think?”","Jin Qi did not understand what Pan Yue was trying to say.","Suddenly, Pan Yue’s phone started to ring.","After she picked up the call, Pan Yue’s expression grew stern.","“You’re imagining things and creating lies. You are spouting nonsense, and you are totally useless. All you can do is run your mouth. You’ll get what you deserve.”","Pan Yue spoke so quickly that she became short on breath.","“You’re blindly stubborn and a fake. You’re grasping at straws, you scum. You’re disgusting. How dare you tell me that Teacher Guo’s live-streaming room is locked? I’m so pissed! I want to riot on behalf of Teacher Guo on Star Web. We’re going to stand up for Teacher Guo. Go, go!”","After Pan Yue put down the phone, she was extremely dispirited.","Her palm instinctively moved quicker, and her hand movements were soon a blur.","Lin Yuan happened to jump over the stone wall in front of them. He came across the young girl dressed in yellow spirit attendant attire, and her hand was spinning rapidly.","Lin Yuan suddenly wondered if this spirit attendant had transmigrated too.","If she did transmigrate as well, she must be delusional. Otherwise, she would not be spinning the sword in her hands like a madwoman.","As the fury in Pan Yue’s heart reached a peak, Jin Qi burst. “What did you say was in your hand? I didn’t catch what you said.”","The demon within Pan Yue was unleashed the moment she heard about Teacher Guo’s live-streaming room being locked.","She felt that someone must have used some evil method to report Teacher Guo.","It must not be because Teacher Guo had run out again to fetch a parcel.","However, triumph would always succeed. Pan Yue believed that Teacher Guo would find some way to bounce back from this.","If Teacher Guo could not hold out, Pan Yue would have to be a traitor and switch to watching someone else’s live-streaming room."]},{"number":540,"title":"Chapter 540: The Ambition to Swallow Everyone’s Resources","paragraphs":["Pan Yue’s heart was full of anger. It happened that Jin Qi had hit the muzzle this time.","She stared at Jin Qi and realized that there was a fair bit of melted dark chocolate smeared at the corners of the latter’s lips.","Pan Yue snorted and said, “Your whole mouth is dirty.”","With that, she turned around and returned to her residence to log onto Star Web and meet with her friends.","Jin Qi really did not understand. She had only asked, “What did you say just now?”","Why did Pan Yue have to say that her whole mouth was dirty?","I wasn’t even scolding you!","Jin Qi was not stubborn, but because she simply hadn’t been able to keep up with Pan Yue’s rhythm, she hadn’t had time to immediately counterattack.","Hence, she could only mess around in the wind by herself.","At that moment, Lin Yuan happened to pass Jin Qi by and saw her in the wind.","He quickly realized who the girl before him was. She had been with Wen Yu when the latter’s source had been damaged and was the spirit attendant who always troubled the latter.","Upon seeing the girl frozen in place, Lin Yuan felt that he should explain what had happened just now.","“She said that your whole mouth was dirty because you had dark chocolate smeared at the corners of your mouth.”","In the darkness, Lin Yuan felt that the dark chocolate at the corners of the girl’s mouth looked like nose hair sticking out of her nostril.","Jin Qi had not expected someone to speak beside her and subconsciously looked in the direction of the voice.","As she glanced over, she immediately bowed.","“Good evening, Master Lin Yuan.”","If Jin Qi had had a lot of other thoughts about Lin Yuan before, then her fear of facing him at this time far outweighed them.","Who knew if Wen Yu had spoken ill of her during the long period she had been with Lin Yuan?","Lin Yuan had always had a bad impression of Jin Qi.","It was not that whatever Jin Qi did was wrong. It was just that some people’s hearts were like flowers and trees when they advanced, growing toward the sun.","Others were like lycoris, growing toward the dark.","Compared to those who grew toward the dark, Lin Yuan undoubtedly viewed the ones that grew toward the sun in a more positive light.","However, even if he didn’t like Jin Qi, he wouldn’t do anything about it.","He nodded at her and walked toward his own pavilion.","Jin Qi quickly let out a breath after seeing Lin Yuan leave. She realized that when Wen Yu had been beside Lin Yuan, Wen Yu hadn’t done anything to her and had even nodded at her.","He held absolutely none of his previous intention of helping Wen Yu recover from her shame.","Jin Qi was a little surprised. Wen Yu had seen her on her return to the Radiant Moon Palace and had also nodded at her without doing anything to her.","With this thought in mind, Jin Qi stood rooted to the spot in the darkness. She felt that she had been too harsh to Wen Yu previously.","That harshness now seemed despicable to Jin Qi.","Jin Qi stood for a long time in the night, staring blankly at a long, slightly bent willow.","Perhaps it was because the new year was coming that a new branch had been drilled out of the bent willow.","This new branch was growing vigorously upward on the curved trunk of the curved willow. It was growing straight as a rod!","Upon returning to his pavilion, Lin Yuan lifted the ban on the hot spring.","Hot spring water immediately filled it.","Lin Yuan soaked quietly in the hot spring, enjoying the rare peace.","Although his private faction, Sky City, had only recently started, it already had a general structure.","In terms of combat power, the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer possessed emperor-class power. At present, this would be enough to contend with the veteran factions.","In terms of resources, Morbius’ Spirit Lock spatial zone was a treasure house that constantly produced resources.","It was also the base for his operation of Sky City.","In terms of martial force, Lin Yuan had never stopped recruiting people.","He had also wanted to recruit someone like Zhou Luo, who had comprehended many Willpower Runes in the name of his Purchase With No Loss store.","However, this was no easy matter when he did not have king-class experts with powerful main feys.","Finding Zhou Luo had been akin to a blind cat finding a dead mouse.","Moreover, apart from the king-class white-clothed followers who could be recruited, those with greater combat power would be impossible to recruit with the current reputation of Lin Yuan’s private faction.","After all, Sky City hadn’t yet displayed something that was enough to attract pinnacle king-class experts.","To Lin Yuan, operating a private faction was a different path to the same goal. The most important support lay in the accumulation of resources.","He felt that it was time for him to convert Sky City into a formidable business machine.","Using “business” as its operating model, it would swallow all of the other parties’ resources.","Lin Yuan was also under pressure when it came to the collection of resources.","With so many partners and subordinates who had pledged their loyalty to him, he always had to find resources for them as Sky City’s leader.","Besides that, the two Heaven and Earth Feys, the Floating Island Whale and Clouded Crane had not hatched.","Even when the Floating Island Whale absorbed the pure and great spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it always needed to expend qi-type and water-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls to do so.","However, to Lin Yuan, what cost the most money was not the Floating Island Whale preparing to hatch from the crystal egg.","Instead, it was the question of how to raise the Floating Island Whale after it truly hatched.","In order for it to take to the sky and become a giant beast that could carry a city, then it needed to at least evolve to the Suzerain grade.","The resources that would be depleted in this process would make even the veteran factions feel discouraged.","And for such a high investment in resources, Lin Yuan had to figure out a solution on his own.","Moreover, as a spiritual-type Heaven and Earth Fey, in order to increase the Clouded Crane’s mental strength for its transformed clouds to completely envelop the Floating Island Whale, it needed to feed on enough spiritual-type spiritual ingredients.","It was not only the Heaven and Earth Fey that needed to consume spiritual-type spiritual ingredients.","The Burning Sunflower, the fairy source-type lifeform that Chu Ci was about to contract; Liu Jie’s Insect Queen, and Wen Yu’s Illusory Fox were all spiritual-type feys that consumed spiritual-type spiritual ingredients throughout their growth.","Amongst the spiritual ingredients that Lin Yuan had on hand, spiritual-type ones were the most scarce.","At the same time, they were the rarest of all the spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan rose from the hot spring and went ashore to dry his body. He changed into a set of spirit qi clothes that Wen Yu had previously designed.","Even though he had only been on the road for two days, it was as if he had run away.","However, when he had spoken to Listen on the phone in the daytime, Listen had already helped him to inform those in the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club.","Lin Yuan had already been gone for two days, so he had to abide by tonight’s agreed time."]},{"number":541,"title":"Chapter 541: Aquarium of Bliss","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Now, there was only one hour left before the group welfare auction that would be held at 10 o’clock.","Making use of this one hour, Lin Yuan planned to buy some spiritual-type spiritual ingredients on Star Web.","It was just that the ingredients that he wanted to buy were not those that he would normally purchase from the Rare Lifeform Pavilion. Instead, he needed to go to a veteran faction’s private faction on Star Web to reserve a particular fey.","This fey was the signature fey of the veteran faction.","It was a type of aquatic fey that could produce Lin Yuan’s required spiritual-type spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan used his identity as a Creation Master to log into Star Web before visiting his Purchase With No Loss store.","There, he put away the gains that he had previously blind traded using his Flower Brocade Pearls.","He had actually obtained 515 mid-grade strange flames through this blind trade.","More and more people knew that they couldn’t buy group welfare on Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club through word-of-mouth.","Lin Yuan was extremely pleased when people were willing to consume a large number of resources to join the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club so that they could participate in the group welfare auction.","This proved that the network he had built through his Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club was growing increasingly.","As Lin Yuan put the 515 mid-grade strange flames away, his mouth could not help but twitch.","Because he had been unconscious for ten days, he had not been able to log onto Star Web.","If not, he would have been able to sell two batches of Flower Brocade Pearls through a blind trade.","It was very likely that a lot of the people or factions who wanted to join his Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club would be willing to pay the price in exchange for heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","This was definitely a good opportunity for him to reap the benefits.","In other words, he did not need to reap the benefits himself at all. As long as he stretched his sickle out, the benefits would come forth themselves.","Then, they would urgently press their bodies against the sickle’s blade.","After logging onto Star Web, Lin Yuan immediately received a message from Listen.","Lin Yuan had already spoken to Listen on the phone that day.","After Listen had assured that Lin Yuan was well, he didn’t continue to ask about his condition. Instead, the former had directly sent Lin Yuan a document.","Lin Yuan’s eyebrows raised involuntarily upon opening the document and looking through its contents.","The majority of the document was attacking his Purchase With No Loss store.","The attack pointed to the fact that he, as the group admin, had run away for two days in order to avoid hosting the group welfare auction.","As the document’s contents were arranged in chronological order, Lin Yuan slowly discovered that the problem had arisen at the very beginning with the group welfare on the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club.","Slowly, his own identity had been dragged into the problem.","The document also repeatedly mentioned his codename, Black. Many had compared his identity as a Creation Master to his identity as Black.","Amongst these people, Lin Yuan saw Ancestor Peace and Poison Beauty’s usernames making an appearance.","He froze.","Wasn’t Ancestor Peace the group admin of Black’s official fan club?","And what was going on with Poison Beauty?","His Creation Master identity had not come in contact with Poison Beauty at all. Why was the latter siding with him?","She was going eye to eye with many of Black’s fans with meager power.","Could it be because he had killed Poison Beauty twice in duels on Star Web’s Celestial Stairway using Black’s identity?","Lin Yuan calmly skimmed through the document twice before closing it.","His two identities were like his left and right hand, incomparable.","When Lin Yuan had decided to separate these identities, it was precisely because of their differing capabilities. Hence, he had decided to split the two into a Creation Master and a combat-class spirit qi professional.","He could not believe that his fans were quarreling amongst themselves on Star Web!","Just then, Listen sent him another message.","“Young Master, this matter is indeed rather unusual. How should we handle it?”","When Lin Yuan read the word “unusual”, he imagined that Listen must have been suppressing a grin when he had written that!","Wasn’t it unusual for the left and right hands to be fighting each other?","However, Lin Yuan did not plan on looking too much into the matter.","He did not know how to solve the main issue. After all, he couldn’t possibly expose his own identity!","Besides, even if he did expose his identity, he expected that people’s first reaction would definitely be to assume that he was joking.","In contrast, as long as he organized the group welfare auction as usual at 10 o’clock, this storm surrounding the Purchase With No Loss store’s Star Web group welfare would die down.","After giving Listen some instructions, Lin Yuan visited the veteran faction’s ‘Aquarium of Bliss’ faction territory using an ordinary Star Web user identity.","Upon seeing its name, Lin Yuan knew that it was a veteran faction that specialized in cultivating aquatic feys.","However, compared to Lin Yuan, a spirit qi professional who had comprehended a Willpower Rune and wanted to let Sky City soar, it was different from creating high-grade Bronze feys according to comprehended Willpower Runes.","This ‘Aquarium of Bliss’ sold rare Normal aquatic feys as its mode of operation. It was just that these rare Normal aquatic feys were mostly extremely delicate.","After tens of years of cultivating these rare, delicate feys in large quantities, the Aquarium of Bliss could farm them on a large scale, which was very profitable.","The fey that Lin Yuan wanted to purchase from the Aquarium of Bliss was its signature fey—Angelfish of Bliss.","In the Angelfish of Bliss’ growth process, all of its scales would fall off.","Following which, its scales would become five-colored fish coats and sink to the bottom of the water.","These fish coats were the best food for cultivating spiritual-type feys.","Actually, it was not that there weren’t other spiritual-type spiritual ingredients that could replace the Angelfish of Bliss’ fish coat.","It was just that most ingredients produced by other spiritual-type feys were inseparable from their bodies. Hence, extracting the ingredient from the spiritual-type fey would kill it.","Lin Yuan would need to kill countless spiritual-type feys if he were to use this method of obtaining spiritual ingredients.","The Angelfish of Bliss was superior in that it could develop spiritual ingredients continuously like the Usnea.","Its fish coat would soon regenerate upon being removed like a person’s fingernails.","Even if it was extremely difficult to cultivate the Angelfish of Bliss, this was not a particularly difficult issue for Lin Yuan.","As long as he could obtain the outstanding Angelfish of Bliss, all would be good.","Lin Yuan arrived at the Aquarium of Bliss’ faction territory through Star Web’s teleportation function."]},{"number":542,"title":"Chapter 542: Lin Yuan Is Reaped for Benefits","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan felt as though he had entered a rippling underwater world upon stepping onto the Aquarium of Bliss’ territory.","Just the rippling blue waves made the territory look quite extraordinary.","Looking at the mosaic blue crystals at his feet, Lin Yuan understood the meaning behind the decorations in the Aquarium of Bliss’ territory.","The Aquarium of Bliss had inlaid a large amount of amazonite sand in the ground, such that there must have been some top-class energy ores containing vast spirit qi beneath the ground.","Under the rendering of the spiritual qi seeping from these energy ores, the amazonite sand rippled with sparkling blue water.","It was just that Lin Yuan was accustomed to seeing nice things. He felt that although the blue waves had momentum, their color was a little patchy and not sufficiently smooth.","This was especially so because Lin Yuan had just come from the loft that Cold Moon had decorated for Chu Ci.","All of the turquoise ripples around the Aquarium of Bliss’ territory could not compare to the transparent blue water of Chu Ci’s loft.","They could not compare to the amazonite table in the loft.","They even paled in comparison to the amazonite decorative vases.","After all, amazonite sand was only the mineral encapsulated within amazonite.","Nevertheless, this large amount of amazonite sand must not have cost a small sum.","Star Web’s private territories were not small. It was a show of grandeur to mix amazonite sand on the ground over such a large territory.","If not, if there was not enough to fill some places,","The rippling blue waves would not fuse smoothly into one piece, immediately making the Aquarium of Bliss’ private territory lose its feel as a water world.","Lin Yuan sighed. If he were to inlay so much amazonite sand in his own private faction territory,","he really would not be able to afford to trade without selling the foundational spiritual ingredients that he had hoarded.","Lin Yuan would not easily trade the source-type items or the Suzerain Myth Breed feys’ bodily items that he had hoarded, especially essence blood and law crystals.","Moreover, he would not easily use the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls continuously produced by the Bronze/Legend Elemental Shellfish in the Spirit Lock spatial zone without first trading foundational spiritual ingredients.","After all, good steel must be spent on the blade.","While Lin Yuan had been unconscious for so long, a new batch of completely jade-textured wood had matured.","This wood had supplemented Lin Yuan with a large sum of money to spend.","Before he could meticulously inspect the other decorations in the Aquarium of Bliss’ territory, he caught sight of a blue-robed middle-aged man walking toward him. After sizing him up once over, the man said, “To trade aquatic feys here, you need to first buy an Immortal Bliss tablet. Each Immortal Bliss tablet allows you to trade an aquatic fey from the Aquarium of Bliss. ”","With that, the man handed Lin Yuan a white carved fish tablet, speckled with sky blue crystals.","Looking at the tablet, Lin Yuan noticed only the fine bone patterns on it.","He quickly knew that the Immortal Bliss tablet was made primarily of a fish fey’s bones.","The blue crystals on it were obviously better than the amazonite sand on the ground.","However, the blue of these crystals was not as intense as that of amazonite itself.","Lin Yuan raised his eyebrows. He immediately understood that the tablet was part of the Aquarium of Bliss’ operation method.","This method was similar to his own Fate Letter.","It not only reflected the influence of one’s private faction but could also absorb resources.","Upon noticing that Lin Yuan had not spoken after seeing the Immortal Bliss tablet, the blue-robed middle-aged man cleared his throat before continuing. “You cannot enter without purchasing an Immortal Bliss tablet.”","Lin Yuan blinked, feeling only mildly unaccustomed to the situation before him.","Previously, he had always been the one reaping other people’s benefits.","Now that he was trading in another veteran faction territory, he was the one being reaped for benefits.","Lin Yuan glanced at the tablet and asked, “How much does one fish tablet cost?”","The man furrowed his brows as he said, “This tablet is not called a fish tablet but an Immortal Bliss tablet. An ordinary Immortal Bliss tablet costs 50,000 Radiance dollars.”","The man had furrowed his brows not because Lin Yuan had called the Immortal Bliss tablet a fish tablet, but because he could not believe that someone coming to the Aquarium of Bliss to trade didn’t know the price of its entry certificate.","The Aquarium of Bliss’ private territory on Star Web was not a fey marketplace where one could look around as they pleased.","Most of its clients had a clear fey in mind that they wanted to trade for.","Anyone who came to the Aquarium of Bliss merely to look around was blacklisted. The person would be directly kicked out of the Aquarium of Bliss’ private territory on Star Web.","Never to be allowed entry again.","As a veteran faction, the Aquarium of Bliss was qualified to be such a merciless merchant.","That was the benefit of its monopoly of several rare aquatic feys.","The blue-robed man spoke again. “You’d best be here to trade, not to look around aimlessly.”","Then, he continued patiently. “With an ordinary Immortal Bliss tablet, you can’t choose the fey you want when you enter to trade. You can only tell us, and we will help you to select the fey.","“Of course, the Immortal Bliss tablet only qualifies you to trade. When you trade specific aquatic feys, you will also need to pay for them.","“Because each aquatic fey has different grades, their prices are also different.","“One thing to take note of is that even if you buy a lot of ordinary Immortal Bliss tablets to select multiple aquatic feys, as long as you don’t buy the last fey you see, you can’t continue looking even if you have the Immortal Bliss tablet.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan’s brows knitted together.","This Immortal Bliss tablet mixed with a bit of amazonite sand was probably not as expensive as an item mixed with completely jade-textured wood powder.","It could definitely be bought at a price of 10,000 Radiance dollars or less.","At 50,000 Radiance dollars, he could buy a fish tablet with amazonite fragments.","Of course, Lin Yuan did not mind this. Besides, buying an Immortal Bliss tablet was equivalent to buying an entrance ticket.","However, it was really too bad that he couldn’t choose the fey himself!"]},{"number":543,"title":"Chapter 543: I Want Two","paragraphs":["The Aquarium of Bliss was really a damn talent. It even incorporated a lucky-bag model into the transaction of feys.","Were they not saying, “Even if you buy my aquatic feys, if you don’t buy enough of them, don’t even think about buying high-grade ones!”","If you want a high-grade fey, you will still have to take everything else you don’t need along with it.","This way, the Aquarium of Bliss really didn’t need to worry about sales!","It could even get others to buy low-grade feys without having to pay for any losses themselves.","This was really too vicious!","Since Lin Yuan wanted to purchase the Angelfish of Bliss to produce spiritual-type fish coats,","he needed to minimally evolve it to Epic.","If the Angelfish of Bliss had a juvenile grade, then all of Lin Yuan’s efforts would have been in vain.","Lin Yuan felt that he could not buy tens of these ordinary Immortal Bliss tablets mixed with amazonite sand before preparing to buy a large number of defective Angelfish of Bliss in a fish-betting process!","When the blue-robed man had mentioned the Immortal Bliss tablet, Lin Yuan had noticed the key word ‘ordinary’.","That meant that higher-end Immortal Bliss tablets existed.","Hence, Lin Yuan asked, “Might there be an Immortal Bliss tablet that isn’t an ‘ordinary’ one?”","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, the blue-robed man took out a slightly larger Immortal Bliss tablet with a motion of his hand.","The specks of blue on this larger tablet were far more transparent than those on the smaller one.","With one glance, Lin Yuan knew that amazonite fragments had been mixed into this tablet.","The blue-robed man only said, “Buying this high-end Immortal Bliss tablet will make you a VIP at our Aquarium of Bliss.","“High-end Immortal Bliss tablets cost 200,000 Radiance dollars each. However, you can enjoy two more privileges compared to the ordinary 50,000 Radiance-dollar Immortal Bliss tablet.","“The first privilege is that upon entering, our employees will immediately take out 100 of the aquatic feys you desire.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up.","Although the price of a high-end Immortal Bliss tablet could buy four ordinary ones, he could use it to see 100 Angelfish of Bliss at once.","That was equivalent to spending four times the money to enjoy 100 times the happiness.","Just the first privilege was so great. Lin Yuan could not help but begin to look forward to hearing about the second one.","The blue-robed man continued. “The second privilege is that you can let go of a batch of 100 aquatic feys once in exchange for a new batch.”","Before Lin Yuan could spend four times the price to experience 200 times the happiness, the blue-robed man cleared his throat and cautioned, “Of course, besides these privileges, you must remember that the high-end Immortal Bliss tablet allows you to buy 100 of the specified feys in one batch at once instead of selecting a few individually.","“Nevertheless, within this 100 feys, there are bound to be exceptional ones if nothing goes wrong.","“On their second visit, most customers who come to our Aquarium of Bliss will not choose the ordinary Immortal Bliss tablet. All of them will choose the high-end one.”","After hearing the man’s words, Lin Yuan’s previous notion of spending money to experience happiness disappeared completely.","Ultimately, the high-end Immortal Bliss tablet was equivalent to buying a big lucky bag. It was just that he could spend less on the ordinary Immortal Bliss tablet that served as a gambling counter.","However, the prerequisite for economizing by getting the ordinary Immortal Bliss tablet was to buy 100 Angelfish of Bliss with different grades.","Who could stand this!?","Moreover, the man had said, ‘there are bound to be exceptional ones if nothing goes wrong’ and ‘on their second visit, most customers who come to our Aquarium of Bliss will all choose the high-end Immortal Bliss tablet’.","From his words, Lin Yuan could tell just how difficult it was to catch an Angelfish of Bliss with an exceptional grade.","It was possible that only one or two high-grade fish existed amongst hundreds.","Lin Yuan did not want only one or two high-grade Angelfish of Bliss.","Very early on, Hu Quan had discussed his plans to expand the man-made lake in the mansion with Lin Yuan.","Then, he would use winding walkways and pavilions to surround a water garden.","In the water beneath the water garden, Lin Yuan had planned to cultivate several Angelfish of Bliss.","These fish were extremely beautiful, even if they weren’t amongst the top ten most beautiful feys like the Blue Flash Butterfly.","However, they were definitely within the top 100.","Not only would the fish be beautiful to admire, but they would also be able to produce spiritual ingredients to cultivate spiritual-type feys. This was truly catching two birds with one stone.","Given that Lin Yuan’s demands were so high, he felt that no matter the benefits the Aquarium of Bliss could reap from him, it would not be able to reap everything.","Lin Yuan had chosen to come to the Aquarium of Bliss to buy Angelfish of Bliss only for convenience’s sake.","Although Angelfish of Bliss were extremely delicate and rare, the Aquarium of Bliss was also named after them.","However, Angelfish of Bliss were not unique to the Aquarium of Bliss.","Previously, Lin Yuan had meticulously researched information on Angelfish of Bliss.","The thickness and purity of the fish coats shed by the Aquarium of Bliss’ Angelfish of Bliss paled in comparison to those bred in the wild.","It was just that the Aquarium of Bliss’ Angelfish of Bliss could breed large numbers to become signature feys after improvement.","Ultimately, Lin Yuan could not be bothered to issue a trade message on his Purchase With No Loss store to buy the fish one by one.","He had originally wanted to leave after seeing through the Aquarium of Bliss’ sham.","Yet, he immediately thought that since he had already come, he might as well buy two high-end Immortal Bliss tablets and select two batches to try his luck.","Even if his gains were truly mediocre, he could still evolve the angelfish’s grade to Bronze/Flawless before selling them to make some money.","They would not rot in his hands unnecessarily.","Thus, Lin Yuan said to the blue-robed man, “Give me two high-end Immortal Bliss tablets.”","With a motion of the hand, the man produced another high-end Immortal Bliss tablet.","He then passed this tablet, along with the one that had already been in his hand, to Lin Yuan.","He said, “Two high-grade Immortal Bliss tablets cost 400,000 Radiance dollars. You can transfer the money to me directly.","“You will definitely have gains with these two tablets.”","Lin Yuan realized that the blue-robed man tended to speak literally.","After Lin Yuan had asked for two high-grade Immortal Bliss tablets, the man had changed pretty much everything that came out of his mouth.","Lin Yuan faintly guessed that there would only be a high-grade Angelfish of Bliss in every 200 at the Aquarium of Bliss."]},{"number":544,"title":"Chapter 544: Lin Yuan Who Was Kicked Out","paragraphs":["Just when Lin Yuan was about to transfer the 400,000 Radiance dollars, the blue-robed man said, “The Aquarium of Bliss’ private territory only receives ten customers at a time. You are the 27th customer in line, so you need to wait a while.”","Lin Yuan did not hurry to pay the 400,000 Radiance dollars upon hearing this.","He looked at the time.","Lin Yuan found that there were only 40 minutes left before the group welfare auction at 10 o’clock and asked, “How long do I need to wait?”","The blue-robed man widened his eyes, feeling as though he was trying to see through the young man’s strange mask.","The man thought, How could you still have an urgent matter when you come to our Aquarium of Bliss to trade?","No matter what excuse this kid gives, as long as he doesn’t buy two high-end Immortal Bliss tablets, he is playing me.","Asking this and that, I’ve been talking for half a day already!","The blue-robed man decided that as long as the young man wearing a mask did not pay, he would kick the latter out.","The man said with a fake smile on his face,","“Two hours at least.","“A two-hour waiting time is already very short. Unlucky people who come in the afternoon sometimes have to wait till the next morning.”","Upon hearing this, Lin Yuan knew that he could not buy the tablets then, so he said, “I have something on later. Since I need to wait two hours, I’ll come back after I’m done buying the two—”","Lin Yuan found that Star Web had directly sent him back to the Purchase With No Loss store before he could finish his sentence.","According to the notification, the blue-robed man had suddenly kicked him out of the Aquarium of Bliss.","Moreover, he had been blacklisted and could never enter it again!","Lin Yuan could not stand this!","Even with his good temper, Lin Yuan could not help but feel rather annoyed at that moment.","The veteran faction Aquarium of Bliss was being too overbearing.","Was it not afraid of suffering losses?","Previously, Lin Yuan and the Aquarium of Bliss had had nothing to do with each other.","However, it had now been added to Lin Yuan’s invisible blacklist.","Since the blue-robed man had kicked him out of the Aquarium of Bliss’ private territory, Lin Yuan had no other choice but to issue a trade message on his Purchase With No Loss store.","Although Angelfish of Bliss lived in both seawater and freshwater, these aquatic feys appeared more frequently in the ocean.","Presumably, there must have been a rich and powerful family like the Gao family striving to develop marine resources in the sea.","After all, the Gao family was the top faction when it came to trading Elemental Shellfish and Floating Island Whales.","New Year’s was only a few days away, so Lin Yuan did not want to bother Gao Feng at this time.","If not, Lin Yuan would have settled this matter by giving Gao Feng a phone call.","Back at the Aquarium of Bliss, the blue-robed man suddenly felt that he had been somewhat reckless. He really shouldn’t have kicked that man out.","He should have reprimanded him mercilessly before kicking him out!","Otherwise, hadn’t he just wasted all the time he had spent talking to the man?","The blue-robed man cracked his knuckles. He already couldn’t remember how many casual visitors he had kicked out that day.","Back at the Purchase With No Loss store, Lin Yuan displayed ten Flower Brocade Pearls again.","It was just that he did not plan to blind trade these Flower Brocade Pearls for mid-grade strange flames this time.","Instead, he would exchange the pearls for a spiritual ingredient called Aurora Pollen.","Lin Yuan had so many mid-grade strange flames on hand that he wouldn’t be able to finish using them.","Hoarding spiritual ingredients like mid-grade strange flames did not bring many benefits.","To Lin Yuan, their only function was to accelerate Chimey’s evolution.","As for the Aurora Pollen, it was the best food to feed Angelfish of Bliss. It allowed the fish to quickly grow scales and shed the fish coat on their bodies.","Moreover, the Aurora Pollen could allow the delicate Angelfish of Bliss to grow stronger.","Even if the three Mountain River Eternal Life Carp in Lin Yuan’s mansion had the exclusive skill of Place of Life, which was enough to shelter the delicate Angelfish of Bliss from death, it would still be good to feed the angelfish Aurora Pollen so that they could produce the best fish coats.","Aurora Pollen was the powder on the fey Aurora Morning Glory’s buds.","If Lin Yuan were to cultivate Aurora Morning Glories himself, he could also collect Aurora Pollen.","However, even compared to the delicate Angelfish of Bliss, the Aurora Morning Glory was so fragile that it was torturous.","One needed to constantly scrape off the Aurora Pollen from its stamens so that they could secrete more pollen.","Lin Yuan had no interest in personally cultivating such an infuriating fey. He also didn’t think of exchanging the Flower Brocade Pearls for Angelfish of Bliss.","The value of a few wild Angelfish of Bliss was not equivalent to that of a Gold lotus flower.","Even if someone wanted to exchange an Angelfish of Bliss from the Aquarium of Bliss with Lin Yuan, the latter would not accept it.","After setting up the blind trade, Lin Yuan sat idly as he waited for the group welfare auction to begin.","He also spent the time looking at what the group members were discussing.","Upon opening the group chat on Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club, he received 9,999+ notifications.","Lin Yuan could not help but gag. Were the mouths of all these members made of machine guns?","However, he found out how dozens of group members had gotten the total number of messages to 9,999+ after scrolling through the group’s chat history.","It seemed that the only way to defeat a machine gun was with a sound repeater.","Almost half of the messages were either repetitions or some strange expressions.","Lin Yuan thought that even if he starved to death, he wouldn’t be able to scroll through everything in the group chat to find something useful.","Nevertheless, group notifications flooded in quickly.","Lin Yuan did not feel bored as he waited. He just quietly opened the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club’s chat and browsed through the members’ discussions.","WIth this one glance, he was drawn to something that a member called Recluse Study had said.","Recluse Study: “Does anyone here live in Indigo Azure City? I have a juicy piece of gossip here that keeps its fragrance and sweetness for consumption.”","Lin Yuan had just woken up that day after being unconscious in the dimensional rift outside Indigo Azure City.","He could not help but wonder what kind of gossip had appeared in Indigo Azure City.","There were only those few people in his Purchase With No Loss store.","Every time someone sold gossip, there would always be a group of people around.","Time: “What gossip could there be now but news about the dimensional rift?”","Territorial Sleeping God: “Indigo Azure City is near the sea. Could a Class 4 dimensional rift have appeared?”","Jerky: “I’ll hear the gossip from the front row. If it’s not juicy, I’ll scrape your brains out.”","Recluse Study: “My gossip is definitely fragrant and sweet! Top secret news: I heard that some time ago, the bright moon hanging in the sky was linked to a young man.”"]},{"number":545,"title":"Chapter 545: Guessing Identity","paragraphs":["After he saw that the news was posted on the Purchase With No Loss store fan club, Lin Yuan’s eyes immediately narrowed.","The usually active fan club instantly erupted into chaos after seeing the news.","Island Blossom: “Bro, you even managed to eat this? Impressive!”","Lake Spirit: “Bro, is this real? Did you mistype?”","The original poster, Recluse Study, had anticipated that people would find his post hard to believe.","Instead of offering an explanation, Recluse Study posted: “I’m not impressive. I’m also not boasting. However, my uncle is a very powerful nomad spirit qi professional. He saw it with his very own eyes. There’s no way it’s wrong!”","Despite his assurance, many people still expressed their disbelief, and they started to conduct their own investigation.","In the beginning, the Purchase With No Loss store fan club only consisted of a small group of Lin Yuan’s online friends. Most of them came from the group that liked to snatch up Usnea and Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","The number of people in the group did not increase up until Lin Yuan removed the Usnea and Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","Since they had joined the group the earliest, they stood by it through thick and thin. They visited the Purchase With No Loss store almost every day to wait on Lin Yuan’s newest Usnea and Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","As such, they were the ones who usually snapped up all the new stock.","Thus, it became more difficult for newcomers to join the group based on their interest in Usneas and Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","Ever since Lin Yuan started using the Flower Brocade Pearls to conduct blind trading, more and more people who had a wealth of resources started joining the group.","Recluse Study had entered the group by using a large amount of mid-grade strange flames to blind trade for Flower Brocade Pearls.","People of a similar milieu to Recluse Study dared to say that one of their family members saw it with their own eyes.","This meant that there was a good chance that he was telling the truth.","Nine days ago, the bright moon had hung high in the sky, and the moonlight had been stained with blood. The radiant moon had totally eclipsed the proud sun that should have been taking center stage.","Such an earth-shattering event might boggle the minds of both people.","However, anyone with a little knowledge would link it to the ever-quiet moon.","That was why Recluse Study’s post attracted the attention of almost every person in the group almost immediately.","A member of the group called Sleep Addiction asked Recluse Study a question that many other people had also been asking.","Sleep Addiction: “Bro, you said that the daytime moon had something to do with a young person. Who is this young person?”","Recluse Study instantly replied. “My uncle said that it had something to do with a pair of Master and disciple.”","Recluse Study had just posted the message when Sleep Addiction followed up with a response.","Sleep Addiction: “I envy this young person!”","Lin Yuan’s eyes narrowed when he saw that the most recent message received a constant stream of likes.","80 more posts were swiftly uploaded.","Lin Yuan originally took a look at the people from Indigo Azure City that he had not had access to during his coma.","Yet somehow, the conversation had turned the spotlight onto himself.","Lin Yuan was completely oblivious to all that had taken place ever since he had been sucked into the dimensional rift.","Now, as Sleep Addict continuously posted news related to Lin Yuan, he could only watch on in a daze.","Although he was the person in question, Lin Yuan could not confirm the validity of what Recluse Study was saying.","However, it was rather juicy news.","Lin Yuan could tell from Recluse Study’s posts that the Moon Empress had been beside herself with anxiousness during the time that he had been sucked into the dimensional rift.","He could not experience this as the person in question, but he was exceptionally touched when he heard it from others.","During his chat with Recluse Study, Lin Yuan found out a piece of news.","Recluse Study: “My uncle said that this incident has something to do with the Zheng family of Indigo Azure City. You can’t tell anyone about this because I only came to know about it after eavesdropping on my uncle and mother’s conversation.”","Once he posted the message, Recluse Study’s concerns did not occur.","This was because Recluse Study was immediately deemed a liar by some of the group’s bigshots, and they branded him with disdain.","In the eyes of the bigshots, it was as though Recluse Study was saying that the Zheng family was in contact with the youth that was the Moon Empress’s disciple.","The Zheng family had no right to be standing on high horses just because they had the power to summon an eclipse.","Lin Yuan was stunned by Recluse Study’s most recent post. He could not help but be curious who this uncle Recluse Study spoke of was.","Recluse Study happened to know quite a lot. Not to mention he had also mentioned the Zheng family.","Lin Yuan could be sure that what Recluse Study said was true since his clash with the Zheng family was imminent and being sucked into the dimensional rift was in his past.","Two days had passed without anything happening.","He had definitely made his identity known to the two Guard Envoys who had the Moon Empress’ crest on them.","Those two Guard Envoys had also promised to keep this matter from getting out.","Since the two Guard Envoys had journeyed alongside the Captain of the Guard Envoys, they were sure to give him a head’s up.","There were only three people present who could be Recluse Study’s uncle.","One of them was Jiao Hanzhong.","Another one was Duan He, who had accompanied Jiao Hanzhong to aid him and helped his contracted fey Cold Snow Pine to break through Myth II and gain the ability to transform into a human.","There was also Nightmare VI, which had suddenly appeared to help Jiao Hanzhong.","Jiao Hanzhong and Nightmare VI were already dead, and dead men told no tales.","Hence, the only person left who understood the whole situation was Duan He.","It was impossible that the Zheng family had released the news on their own.","Lin Yuan was not in denial that the matter could be leaked out, but the reactions of the people in the group told him that they had no clue the event had taken place.","When he had called Liu Jie in the morning, Wen Yu also mentioned the Zheng family’s present situation.","Evidently, the Moon Empress had not done much to the Zheng family.","Lin Yuan felt that sometimes, a little push was needed for the truth to reveal itself.","However, he could not be sure whether or not his guess was 100% accurate.","In order to prove his hypothesis, he needed to put it to the test."]},{"number":546,"title":"Chapter 546: The Changed Group Welfare","paragraphs":["While the group members discussed Recluse Study’s behavior, Lin Yuan took the risk and posted a message.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “Looked at the time and realized that the auction for group welfare will begin in ten minutes.”","Lin Yuan’s message rescued Recluse Study.","Lin Yuan once again witnessed the power of the fan club of Purchase With No Loss store’s broken record.","After seeing line after line of messages saying that the group admin was showing off, Lin Yuan felt that he should offer something up.","Moreover, the more that Lin Yuan offered, the more he earned.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “I had some business to attend to and was delayed for two days. As such, I’ll make it up to all of you by offering a bonus. I’ll be throwing in two more heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.”","Lin Yuan’s bonus immediately garnered enthusiastic responses.","I’m Your Fairy: “Group admin is the best!”","Old Black Crow: “Throwing in two heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls after two days? Group admin is so thoughtful!”","Amber Button: “Even if the group admin adds two more, I still can’t afford it. I’ll just have to watch as the bigshots fight over them.”","The sight of the group members’ vigorous responses made Lin Yuan feel all the more embarrassed for having delayed the group welfare auction by two days.","After pondering for a while, Lin Yuan posted another message.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “The ten fire-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearls had a purity of about 9.8. I’ll now be switching those with 12 elemental pearls with a purity of about 9.9. I won’t be specifying the elemental energy of these elemental pearls. The people who join the auction can decide for themselves if they want them to be of the water, wind, earth, or fire element.","The eyelids of the Creation Masters in the group immediately started to twitch after seeing Lin Yuan’s message.","The eyelids of the two Class 4 Creation Masters in the fan club twitched the most fiercely.","Only Class 4 Creation Masters would know how difficult it was to nurture heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with 9.9 purity.","Shortly after he mentioned the 9.8 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, many people in the group were shocked by how high of a quality of fire-elemental pearls the group admin had put out.","Now, he was offering 9.9 purity elemental pearls instead.","Besides being startled by Lin Yuan’s generous offer, those who were preparing to enter the auction quickly started to get their chips ready.","Although both 9.8 purity and 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were considered to be of the highest quality, and they even had similar usages to the 9.5 purity elemental pearls, 9.9 purity elemental pearls were priceless collectibles.","The Class 4 Creation Master Duan Li also happened to be reading the group chat.","Master Duan Li had helped Zhou Luo to nurture the Iron Bone Tearing Lizard. She knew that the Iron Bone Tearing Lizard needed five fire-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearls to activate its evolution.","This would enable the earth-type fey to evolve into a fire-type fey.","She had met Zhou Luo in the Purchase With No Loss store, and Zhou Luo had said that the Iron Bone Tearing Lizard was now fine.","The Purchase With No Loss store already held a high place in Master Duan Li’s heart.","But the moment that Lin Yuan offered the 10 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, Master Duan Li elevated the Purchase With No Loss store even further.","Lin Yuan had changed the offer to the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls as compensation for pushing the group welfare auction back.","It suddenly struck Master Duan Li how this humble store had already managed to wrap a fair number of veteran factions around their fingers. The Purchase With No Loss store had already secured the most influence.","Master Duan Li felt that letting 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls go was a huge stab to oneself.","This was true group welfare.","Being a Class 4 Creation Master, Master Duan Li did not often speak in the group. However, this time she could not hold back and ask.","Duan Li: “Group admin, can we be assured that no matter which of the four elements we choose, the elemental pearls will all be 9.9 purity?”","Master Duan Li had voiced the question that was in almost all of the group members’ minds.","Lin Yuan earnestly replied to the question.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “Since it’s welfare, they all have to be the same. Thus, I can guarantee that no matter which element you decide on, they will all be 9.9 purity. This will also eliminate the issue of you guys ending up with an incompatible elemental pearl.”","Lin Yuan’s response put an idea in the minds of almost all the group members.","Why did the group admin’s seemingly polite message come off as arrogant and pretentious?","Only an idiot would trade away elemental pearls with 9.9 purity.","When elemental pearls reached 9.9 purity, another layer of pearl would form around the exterior.","These pearl-in-a-pearls were a rare collectible whose softness and beauty was unmatched.","The pearl cover over every 9.9 purity elemental pearl was unique, making each elemental pearl one of its kind.","This meant that an equally valuable collectible needed to be offered in order to trade for the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","Master Duan Li took a sharp intake of breath. From Lin Yuan’s tone, she could tell that Lin Yuan had a large number of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls on hand.","It would be no problem for her to shelve out 20 of them.","Initially, Master Duan Li was rational about the offer of the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, but now that she confirmed they were 9.9 purity, she knew that she had to shoot her shot.","Master Duan Li was conflicted over her dilemma.","Should I take out the treasure I’ve been hiding away and use it to trade?","Lin Yuan watched as his new announcement sent the group members into a frenzy. Even Recluse Study seemed to be very excited.","Lin Yuan mentioned Recluse Study.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “@Recluse Study Is your uncle’s surname Duan?”","Lin Yuan’s random message rendered the group chat speechless.","Shortly after, Recluse Study popped up and asked in surprise.","Recluse Study: “Damn! @Deep Mountain Elder Lin, did you become a psychic in the last two days?”","Recluse Study’s reaction confirmed Lin Yuan’s guess.","Recluse Study’s uncle was none other than Duan He.","Recluse Study was mentioning Lin Yuan continuously and was asking him how he knew.","Lin Yuan’s lip curled upward, but he did not answer Recluse Study’s question because he was already sure that Recluse Study’s uncle was Duan He."]},{"number":547,"title":"Chapter 547: Lin Yuan Wants to Recruit","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan remembered Recluse Study mentioning that he did not come from an influential family. His uncle, Duan He, was also a spirit qi professional.","This meant that Duan He had not joined any faction.","Although Duan He initially wanted to help Jiao Hanzhong’s fey to undergo World Cleansing, from the way that Duan He interacted with Jiao Hanzhong, it was clear that Duan He was not colluding with the Zheng family.","He had only gone to the deserted island to repay Jiao Hanzhong.","Lin Yuan’s private faction Sky City’s top fighting force only consisted of Endless Summer and the Mother of Bloodbath.","Although Lin Yuan only got to see the Diamond X/Fantasy V Sword Plume Sea Hawk instead of Duan He’s true power, Duan He’s main fey had to be the peak of Suzerain since Jiao Hanzhong had enlisted his help for his Suzerain II fey to go through the World Cleansing.","Lin Yuan thought, If I can get Recluse Study to bring his uncle over, and I manage to gain Duan He’s loyalty, Sky City’s fighting ability will be greatly boosted for sure.","As Lin Yuan schemed how he would be able to bring Duan He over to his side, he silently took stock of his own advantages.","If I manage to snag the emperor-class Duan He, what will I be able to offer him in return? I can’t just use rare source-type items to convince him to join my team. They can easily use their own connections to find Class 4 Creation Masters if they want Bronze/Epic feys. There aren’t many Class 4 Creation Masters who will reject a deal with an emperor-class expert. Emperor-class experts also make up the main fighting force for veteran factions. As long as an emperor-class expert is willing to pledge their loyalty, any veteran faction will be glad to pump in as many resources as necessary. If I want Duan He on my side, I’ll need to fork out quite a lot.","However, Lin Yuan had something that veteran factions and top factions did not have—Bronze/Legend feys.","Lin Yuan had just manifested the idea of wanting to recruit Duan He.","Although Duan He was a true blue emperor-class expert, Lin Yuan’s criteria for recruitment consisted of more than power.","When it came to potential, Lin Yuan also emphasized his subordinates having good character.","Unfortunately, Lin Yuan was not certain about what kind of person Duan He was.","Lin Yuan might have had the idea, but he still needed Wen Yu to look into Duan He’s affairs and information before he approached Duan He.","Inside the Radiant Moon Palace’s Hidden Moon Pavilion, every expert’s information was logged by the hidden servants.","From the expert’s personality to their life experiences, all information was collated in what was essentially a personalized magazine.","As events took place, the hidden servants would constantly update and record the new information.","After the death of an expert who was worthy of being recorded in the Radiant Moon Palace, their personalized magazine would be sealed away.","Sky City was able to sort out all the information regarding the veteran factions and rising factions in such a short amount of time due to Wen Yu’s hard work and the information kept in the Hidden Moon Pavilion.","The Hidden Moon Pavilion was controlled solely by the Moon Empress’ intelligence team.","To other people, Leaning Moon Mountain was an impenetrable territory, so naturally, they would never be able to lay eyes on the Hidden Moon Pavilion.","However, Lin Yuan had unrestricted access to the Hidden Moon Pavilion, and he could enter it with the same ease that he did his own room.","Lin Yuan’s hand gently cupped his chin as he was deep in contemplation.","Although attracting an emperor-class expert to join my faction will use up resources, it will provide us with a good future.","Lin Yuan had always been insistent on relying on his own power to expand Sky City, but he knew that there were some things he could not force on his own.","On several occasions, the Moon Empress had subtly suggested that she wanted to invest resources into Sky City, but Lin Yuan had rejected her each time.","The Moon Empress was still his Master, nonetheless.","Although Lin Yuan did not receive a direct input of resources from the Moon Empress, he did not collect all the intelligence and secret information on his own.","He used the information provided by the Hidden Moon Pavilion in order to establish Sky City’s own intelligence connections.","Lin Yuan felt that information was more useful than resources.","Wen Yu had already finished collating all the information on the veteran factions and rising factions.","Consequently, Lin Yuan needed to start putting in the effort so as to collect his own intelligence reports rather than relying on the Hidden Moon Pavilion to help Sky City.","At his present level, Lin Yuan did not have the courage to try and recruit other emperor-class experts.","However, Duan He was an exception.","The difference between Duan He and other emperor-class experts was that Duan He was acquainted with Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan knew that his wealth of resources was more than capable of meeting Duan He’s needs.","By allowing Duan He to become acquainted with him, Lin Yuan could provide him with a bright future.","If Lin Yuan did not want to reveal his identity to the rest of the world, his best course of action would be to recruit Duan He.","During the few minutes that Lin Yuan was deep in thought, Lin Yuan guessing Recluse Study’s uncle’s surname had already been long forgotten.","Most of the group member’s attention had shifted to the 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that were 9.9 purity.","Only Recluse Study was still left reeling.","Recluse Study’s curiosity could not be satisfied without Lin Yuan’s response.","There were many bigshots in the group, and the group admin did not appear to know anyone in the group.","Recluse Study did not think that the group admin knew who he was.","Recluse Study suddenly remembered how powerful his uncle was, and then it hit him.","Could the group admin know my uncle?","Recluse Study thought more about it, and his uncle seemed to know that he was buying the Flower Brocade Pearls from the Purchase With No Loss store for him.","After Recluse Study joined the fan club through the blind trade for the Flower Brocade Pearls, he did not notice his uncle’s presence in the group.","At that moment, Recluse Study realized that his uncλe was online on Star Web.","Since he could not get an answer from Lin Yuan, Recluse Study decided to try to get some from his uncle. Thus, he sent him a message."]},{"number":548,"title":"Chapter 548: I’ve Found My Master","paragraphs":["Recluse Study: “Uncle, do you still remember the small premium-goods store on Star Web that you recommended I visit to buy Flower Brocade Pearls?”","At present, Duan He was still in Indigo Azure City, helping the two Spirit Guard Envoys kill some of the advanced water world dimensional lifeforms during the active stage of the dimensional rift.","At the same time, he was also entering each open dimensional rift to scrape source-type items for supplies.","Even if Duan He was an emperor-class expert with extraordinary power, it required frequent struggle to kill high-grade dimensional lifeforms between active dimensional rifts that could appear anywhere, which made him feel unusually tired.","Part of the reason Duan He worked so hard was indeed because the degree of spatial fluctuation in the active stage of this dimensional rift was much greater than those of previous ones.","Even if the two Guard Envoys brought close to 1,000 Spirit Guards to work together with Indigo Azure City’s Indigo Azure Guards, there would still be slightly insufficient manpower.","Secondly, Duan He was really in short supply of resources during this period.","This had already put him under a significant amount of stress.","At that moment, no one hated Jiao Hanzhong more than Duan He. He was the one who had lent the expensive spiritual ingredients that Jiao Hanzhong’s main fey Cold Snow Pine needed to evolve to Myth II.","At that time, Jiao Hanzhong had given Duan He a relatively good return price and had thickened his skin to speak to the latter many times.","Only then had Duan He been willing to lend his spiritual ingredients to Jiao Hanzhong.","However, Duan He never would have thought that Jiao Hanzhong would actually renege on their deal.","Duan He really didn’t know who to visit to collect the debt.","He couldn’t possibly go to the Zheng family, could he?","Before considering whether the Zheng family would repay their debt, just by looking at the fact that they had lost two emperor-class experts consecutively, it was very likely that they would see Duan He as a ready-made punching bag if he were to go to them now.","By that time, he wouldn’t be able to recover not only his precious feys but also the billions of ashes that remained on his nose.","Duan He’s natural endowment was considered relatively strong. Besides his Diamond X/Fantasy V Sword Plume Sea Hawk, he had two other feys. These two feys were both main feys that had attained the pinnacle Suzerain/Myth I, one step away from Myth II.","Duan He didn’t have the slightest clue how he would obtain the money required for his two feys to evolve from Suzerain/Myth I to Suzerain/Myth II.","Moreover, he had comprehended another Willpower Rune under the moonlight a few days ago.","His spiritual energy could continue to contract feys. To comprehend one more Willpower Rune was equivalent to the need to contract and cultivate a new high-grade Bronze fey.","This should have been the extremely joyous occasion that Duan He had spent the past few years anticipating.","One more fey could enrich Duan He’s combat system, giving him more possibilities.","However, this joyous occasion had arrived at the awkward moment when his two main feys were about to evolve to Myth II.","Hence, what was meant to be a joyous occasion now seemed like it had come too late.","Duan He had not originally been in a good mood. Whenever he thought about how he had become a Creation Master at a young age but had then become obsessed with fighting his nephew—who was not even a Class 2 Creation Master—on Star Web, he felt repressed rage.","There was no damn point to the combat-class spirit qi professionals being born and dying every day to Duan He.","No matter how strong they were, they would still be working for those Creation Masters, wouldn’t they?","Besides, Duan He had come to this conclusion after so many years.","Fundamentally, when cultivating feys, most of the resources earned from birth and death were entrusted to the Creation Master.","Cut Off the Flowing River: “Why are you still on Star Web at this time? Don’t tell me you need to go on Star Web to train to become a Creation Master? If you have nothing to do, go to the breeding room more often to spare our entire family the worry!”","Cut Off the Flowing River: “Quickly advance as a Creation Master. When you become a Class 2 Creation Master, I’ll help you find a Class 4 Creation Master to be your Master.”","Recluse Study had originally been a bit hesitant when messaging his uncle privately.","Now, once Recluse Study privately messaged his uncle, he found that he had been right—his uncle was lecturing him again.","His uncle was built big and tall like a boor.","However, even his father, who taught at Advanced Spirit Qi Occupation University, was no match when it came to lecturing.","When it came to his power as a Creation Master though, Recluse Study had a lot to say.","Recluse Study: “Uncle, my power as a Creation Master has already improved greatly!”","Duan He had initially planned to continue lecturing, but upon seeing that his nephew had suddenly delivered good news, he felt the weariness that had hung over him the whole day disappear.","Yet, Recluse Study’s next words immediately caused Duan He’s vision to blacken.","Recluse Study: “Uncle, with the Flower Brocade Pearls you gave me previously and the ones I bought with my New Year’s money, I’m now more powerful than some Class 2 Creation Masters!”","Recluse Study: “Of course, I’m talking about my success rate in blending spirit fluid!”","Duan He had been contacting a few agreed-upon sellers for the price of the rare and precious spiritual ingredients he needed while waiting for good news from his nephew.","However, upon receiving his nephew’s news, Duan He felt himself shut down.","His nephew was really a little genius to even come up with such a comparison!","The spirit fluid concocted by a Class 1 Creation Master did not require more than a few spiritual ingredients.","As long as one’s basic skills were solid enough when given two Flower Brocade Pearls, a Class 1 Creation Master should have had a success rate of at least 30%.","To really compare success rate, his nephew’s was comparable to that of even some low-level Class 3 Creation Masters.","But why don’t you, a Class 1 Creation Master, compare yourself to Class 2 Creation Masters in your ability to heal damaged fey roots?","After a long while, Duan He finally recovered from his breakdown.","He answered explosively.","Cut Off The Flowing River: “You’re already 19! If you don’t become a Class 2 Creation Master before you turn 20, I’ll be too ashamed to even ask around and find you a good Master.”","Recluse Study felt somewhat wronged. His uncle was always worrying about everything.","Was it very difficult to find a Master?","He was doing fine in the group chat and had received a few words from Master Duan Li. He also had no trouble acting cute all day long.","Now, Master Duan Li had accepted him as an in-name disciple.","After being lectured by his uncle the whole day, Recluse Study finally found a way to retaliate.","Recluse Study: “Uncle, I’ve already become the in-name disciple of the Class 4 Creation Master, Master Duan Li.”","Recluse Study: “Master Duan Li said that as long as I become a Class 2 Creation Master before I turn 20 and pass her exam, she will accept me as her personal disciple.”"]},{"number":549,"title":"Chapter 549: Duan He Breathes Raggedly","paragraphs":["Duan He was stunned when he saw the message from Recluse Study.","What? Did this brat find himself a Master?","Duan He’s first reaction was to wonder if his naive nephew had been scammed, but he soon remembered how devious his nephew was.","Rather than being worried that his nephew was scammed, he should be more worried that his nephew was scamming someone else.","When has my nephew ever gotten the short end of the stick? Wait. Is he trying to scam me too?","Other than the rare Class 3 Creation Masters, all the people who had attained a title and had come to be known by that title were Class 4 Creation Masters.","As long as a Class 4 Creation Master was willing to accept his nephew as a disciple, there would only be gains and no losses.","Even if he was only a disciple in name, he would already be able to receive the teachings of a Class 4 Creation Master.","As long as his nephew could learn from the Class 4 Creation Master and use the knowledge to strengthen his own skills, Duan He did not mind if his nephew was an in-name or direct disciple.","Duan He had no idea which Class 4 Creation Master his nephew was able to snag.","His nephew spent five hours every day on Star Tower and had reached level 60 at least.","Did he meet the Class 4 Creation Master in one of the matches on Star Tower?","This thought seemed ludicrous to Duan He.","Even if the Class 4 Creation Master was not skilled at fighting, their feys could sustain a significant amount of damage.","Cut Off The Flowing River: “Where did you find a Master?”","Recluse Study was slightly regretting messaging his uncle privately.","All of the available group members had come online, and the group welfare auction was going to start in three minutes.","However, his uncle was asking questions incessantly.","How am I supposed to watch the show if I’m too busy answering all my uncle’s questions?","Recluse Study decided to go for the quick fix.","Recluse Study: “We met in a group chat.”","Duan He was shocked by Recluse Study’s reply.","What kind of group chat allows you to chat up a Class 4 Creation Master into becoming your Master? This is like a blind man going fishing and ending up with Heaven and Earth Rouge Queen Scallop.","Cut Off The Flowing River: “What group chat? How does that land you a Class 4 Creation Master as a Master? Don’t lie to me! Otherwise, I’ll tell your mother about how you got your staff to do all your holiday homework. She’ll beat you up!”","His uncle’s message almost drove Recluse Study mad.","Those two things are completely irrelevant! We were just talking. Why did he have to use such a cruel tactic? If my mother finds out that I had help finishing my homework, I’ll never recover from the beating she’s sure to give me.","Recluse Study wanted to argue, but the group welfare auction was starting in one minute!","Recluse Study decided to lay in the bed he made.","Recluse Study: “The small fan club on Star Web where you bought the Flower Brocade Pearls for me. Uncle, didn’t we agree that I’ll spend every day focusing on training Creation Master skills in the breeding room in exchange for your discretion? You can’t go back on your word! Uncle, I can’t talk anymore. There’s an auction for heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in the group. I have to go see how it goes!”","His nephew’s message befuddled Duan He.","What’s going on?","Duan He thought his nephew’s words over. He still remembered the small store on Star Web where he bought the Flower Brocade Pearls through blind trade.","Duan He had managed to snag a trade for a batch of Flower Brocade Pearls. He had only spent ten mid-grade strange flames to obtain a stalk of Flower Brocade Pearls.","An expert like Duan He did not care much for something like Flower Brocade Pearls, but he had thought that the owner of the store that had accepted the trade was insane.","He sold the Flower Brocade Pearls in his Star Web store even though they would be auctioned off within seconds in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion.","But after talking to his nephew, Duan He felt that his perspective as an emperor-class expert had completely changed.","Since when did small stores on Star Web start selling precious items like the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, which even emperor-class experts found challenging to procure?","Duan He did not have a habit of buying from Star Web, and he checked his transaction history. He discovered that he had bought the Flower Brocade Pearls through blind trade from a store called Purchase With No Loss Fey Store.","He had deleted all messages other than private messages.","As such, Duan He had not received an invite to the group chat after he traded for the Flower Brocade Pearls.","However, now that Duan He thought about it, he would not have joined the group chat anyway. If he did, he would probably just turn his nose up at the trinkets being sold and eventually turn off the chat notifications.","Yet, he joined the Purchase With No Loss store without hesitation now.","Duan He did not do it to prove the validity of his nephew’s words, but because he understood his nephew. His nephew might be spiteful, but he was not a liar.","Duan He joined the Purchase With No Loss store fan club because his main fey needed several heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in order to evolve.","Since his nephew had mentioned that there would be an auction taking place in the group, joining it would save Duan He the effort of having to negotiate a trade with a Creation Master that nurtured Elemental Shellfish.","Although he was poor and lacked resources at the moment, Duan He was confident in his status as an emperor-class expert, and he was certain that no one in the group would be able to snatch it from him.","Lin Yuan planned on starting the group welfare at ten o’clock. However, he did not expect a newcomer to swoop in right at ten o’clock.","Lin Yuan knew that the Purchase With No Loss store was not currently selling any items, which meant that this person had purchased from the store before but had not decided to join then.","Although the group welfare auction was about to start, a welcome was still necessary for the newcomer.","The ever-active Recluse Study suddenly fell silent. He felt like a heavy stone had landed on his foot. If his uncle was in the group, how was he going to continue acting freely in the group?","Duan He did not anticipate the enthusiasm from the group members of the fan club.","A few tens of them had the same level of activity as a few thousand people.","Shortly after, Duan He noticed the 12 9.9 purity water-, wind-, fire-, and earth-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearls that Lin Yuan was auctioning off.","Along with Duan He’s astoundment, his breathing became ragged."]},{"number":550,"title":"Chapter 550: Loved to Cause His Uncle Trouble","paragraphs":["Duan He chided himself for not joining the group sooner after thoroughly studying the elemental pearls being auctioned off.","After ascertaining that the elemental pearls were indeed 9.9 purity, Duan He started looking into the information about the Purchase With No Loss store.","If he had not seen it for himself, Duan He would not believe that a Star Web store would sell something like 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","When Duan He was still a pinnacle king-class expert, he had used up many favors in order to evolve his feys to Great Suzerain.","He had also used up a massive amount of resources to convince a Class 4 Creation Master to help him nurture several heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that had a purity of about 9.7–9.8.","Although heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were available on the market, those mostly had a purity of 9.5–9.6.","It was impossible to find heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with 9.7–9.8 purity. If one needed it badly enough, they could only approach Class 4 Creation Masters to create it for them specially.","Even pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters needed to count on a significant amount of luck if they wanted to produce heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of 9.9 purity.","No one would sell such peak-quality heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls on the market, much less auctioning them off as group welfare.","Now that Duan He had reached emperor-class, he did not need to work as hard to convince a Class 4 Creation Master to produce heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls for him.","It was improbable that Duan He would be able to find a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master who could produce 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls for him.","He did not have any grounds to build a connection with a Class 4 Creation Master who he could ask to help him.","Duan He was only a medial emperor-class expert at the moment. Class 4 Creation Masters would not even spare him a second look. Only pinnacle emperor-class experts had the right to stand on equal ground as Class 4 Creation Masters.","Duan He was not as specific about the purity of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls as he was in the past when he was trying to evolve his feys to Suzerain.","The pure elemental energy in the elemental pearls was mainly used to trigger the transformation suppressed in the feys’ bloodline.","As such, high-quality heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were very useful.","Now, both of Duan He’s main feys were about to break through Myth II to take human form.","In order for the transformation to occur, Duan He needed spiritual ingredients that aided in evolution.","Pure elemental energy only amplified the effects.","Duan He felt as though he had accidentally stumbled upon a goldmine.","Although he had used many resources to evolve his feys from Myth I to Myth II, an emperor-class expert like him still had some savings.","Duan He had come into a fair amount of source-type items from the water world dimensional rift in Indigo Azure City.","He decided that he was going to be the one to bring home the 12 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","Duan He intended on enquiring about the rules of the auction. After all, he was new to the group and was still unsure of the rules of the group welfare.","Duan He had a feeling that he was about to suffer a loss if a specific item was needed to trade for these heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","At which point, Duan He would really blow his top.","Duan He remembered that this group admin had set a specific item during the blind trade for the Flower Brocade Pearls.","The specific item was the mid-grade strange flames.","Before Duan He posed the question, he glanced through the group messages and instantly froze.","Someone was mentioning his nephew, Recluse Study, and the question made Duan He want to haul Recluse Study out and teach him a lesson he would never forget.","Someone in the group asked.","Stream in the Cloud: “Thank God I made it! I’m sure to win! @Recluse Study, I scrolled through the group chats. You said that the daytime mood had something to do with the Zheng family. If so, why does the Zheng family not know anything about it?”","Duan He felt that his nephew loved to cause him trouble.","It was decreed at home that not a word of this matter was to be leaked. Yet this brat had not only eavesdropped, but he had even posted it in the group chat.","If news of this reached the people involved and came after Duan He, even his status as an emperor-class expert would not save him.","When Duan He first had left the deserted island, he had no idea who Lin Yuan was.","He had seen the persistent moonlight in the direction of the dimensional rift the second time he was on the deserted island and had been unable to find a way to see past the moonlight barrier.","He had felt that the figures immersed in the concentrated moonlight were familiar.","Eventually, the Moon Empress had stepped out of the moonlight barrier with a floating body in her arms. Duan He had only dared to lift his head at that moment, but he saw the two Suzerain/Myth Breed feys that had killed Jiao Hanzhong emerging from the moonlight.","When he had seen the unmasked youth next to the two Suzerain feys, realization dawned upon Duan He.","It turned out that the youth wearing the odd mask that had sent out the kill order for Jiao Hanzhong was the Moon Empress’ disciple.","Duan He had speculated about Lin Yuan’s identity. When he had heard Lin Yuan mention Sky City, Duan He was certain that he had never heard of a faction by that name.","Now that he thought about it, Sky City was not a legendary hidden faction. It should be a new faction created by the mask-wearing youth.","Duan He knew this secret because he had watched the events on the deserted island unfold like a spectator.","Since his nephew had spilled this incident in the group, if the people involved caught wind of this, they would be able to zero in on the source of the leak and figure out who was behind it."]},{"number":551,"title":"Chapter 551: Offline, In-Person Auction","paragraphs":["Recluse Study kept waiting for others to ask about his gossip so that he could spill everything.","However, his uncle had just entered the group. Not only did Recluse Study not dare to share his gossip happily, but he also felt that he had closed up completely.","Yun Xi did not bother with this issue but started speaking to Lin Yuan in the chat.","Stream in the Cloud: “@Deep Mountain Elder Lin, group admin, your group welfare this time was so good. Why don’t we stop auctioning in the group chat?”","Stream in the Cloud: “We could go to the Purchase With No Loss store to hold a heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl auction.”","Lin Yuan was just about to stop the constantly refreshing group notifications and conduct the group welfare auction on heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","However, upon seeing Stream in the Cloud’s words, he only felt annoyed.","The 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were to be auctioned as a bundle in the group welfare auction.","Hence, they could only be considered one auction good.","Auctioning one good was already enough to throw the entire Purchase With No Loss store into a state of restlessness.","Moreover, the Purchase With No Loss store was a one-star store. Although the store had long accumulated enough points, Lin Yuan had still not upgraded it all this time.","If everyone congregated in the small area of the Purchase With No Loss store, wouldn’t it become a ‘primary school class gathering’?","Lin Yuan was about to say that the auction would be carried out in the group chat when he realized that.","Almost everyone in the group agreed with Stream in the Cloud’s—in other words, the braised egg head’s—opinion.","Amongst those who entered the Purchase With No Loss store first, Buddha-Tempered Person, Violent-Tempered Woman, and Zhou Jiaxin all @ Lin Yuan.","They hoped that he could regard this group welfare auction as a networking activity for members of the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan group.","Lin Yuan was fine with it as he didn’t have anything urgent to attend to at the moment.","Since the members had been chatting for so long in the group and were so eager to take this as an opportunity to get to know each other, Lin Yuan was naturally willing to grant and create this opportunity.","Deep Mountain Elder Lin: “Everyone, come to the Purchase With No Loss store then. I’ll open the entry access.”","After issuing this news, Lin Yuan hurriedly visited a Star Web furniture store near his Purchase With No Loss store and bought 100 common wooden chairs.","These chairs cost 200 Federation dollars each and could only be used within Star Web. They could be considered the most common piece of furniture on Star Web.","When Lin Yuan had first opened the Purchase With No Loss store, he had come to this same furniture store to see furniture.","Back then, he had been itching to spend a penny as 100 dollars, so he had been really reluctant to buy such useless furniture.","Now, Lin Yuan wanted to buy so many useless wooden chairs in one go because he thought that there was nothing inside his store. He couldn’t possibly make all the group members coming to the store to participate in the group welfare auction stand, could he?","After Lin Yuan had bought the chairs and returned to his store, there were already 20 to 30 group members waiting inside.","He quickly began arranging his newly bought chairs.","Upon seeing this, Listen immediately walked to Lin Yuan’s side.","Because Lin Yuan was wearing the mask engraved with the majestic sky city on his face, Listen could not clearly see the former’s expression.","However, just by looking at Lin Yuan’s eyes, Listen knew that he was in a good mood.","While Listen was helping Lin Yuan arrange the chairs, Zhou Jiaxin and Violent-Tempered Woman entered.","They joined Lin Yuan and Listen in arranging the chairs neatly in the Purchase With No Loss store.","As others saw Lin Yuan wearing his strange mask, they could not help but think that he was a strange person.","This was especially true for the newly-joined group members, who really couldn’t understand how someone who could easily produce 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls would use the tables that Star Web gave for free upon opening one’s own store and Star Web’s 200-Federation dollar wooden chairs.","Was this what it meant to hide one’s wealth from others?","However, no matter how one looked at it, the store’s shabby decoration did not appear to match what the truly rich did to conceal their wealth.","In contrast, it looked like it was deliberately pretending to be poor.","Recluse Study did not directly enter the Purchase With No Loss store. Instead, he stood at its entrance with his head lowered, waiting for Duan He to arrive.","At that moment, Recluse Study heard a familiar cough in his ear.","“Li Xiaotiao! You eavesdropped on what I said and even told it to others! Are you waiting for me to tell your mother to give you a beating?”","Recluse Study smacked his lips and replied upon hearing this, “Uncle, I must formally inform you that although you are my uncle and like a father to me... I still have my own father! He’s called Li Benggao!”","Duan He had originally been rather upset.","However, Duan He felt so furious that he felt like fainting upon hearing Li Xiaotiao’s mocking words.","Even though Duan He was an emperor-class expert, he felt so angry that he couldn’t control his rage.","Duan He replied angrily, “Let’s go in to participate in the auction first. I must snatch up those 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls. Stop wasting time.","“About your eavesdropping, wait till I get home and let your mother teach you a lesson!”","Although Duan He often got angry at Li Xiaotiao, he never could bring himself to give the latter a beating himself.","Nevertheless, Duan He still had his ways of dealing with Li Xiaotiao. As long as he got home and spoke to his sister about Li Xiaotiao’s trouble-making behavior, Li Xiaotiao wouldn’t be able to escape from a half-an-hour beating from her.","Maybe they would even give Li Xiaotiao a ‘mixed doubles’ beating.","Li Xiaotiao smacked his lips and knew that he was in for it when he got home later.","Anyway, he was used to it by now.","Recalling that his uncle was about to auction for the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, Li Xiaotiao quickly said, “Uncle, let me help you bid for you during the group welfare auction later! Anyway, there’s no difference between my bid and yours.”","During the duo’s conversation, they had already stepped into the Purchase With No Loss store.","However, Li Xiaotiao noticed that his uncle had not spoken for a long time.","He couldn’t help but reach out to scratch his head.","It couldn’t be! Even if his uncle was angry, he couldn’t possibly refuse his own nephew a request like this!","Li Xiaotiao tugged at Duan He’s sleeves, but his uncle still didn’t respond. He raised his head in puzzlement, only to realize that his uncle was staring straight ahead.","Li Xiaotiao followed Duan He’s gaze. His uncle was looking at a young man wearing a strange mask with an unreadable expression on his face."]},{"number":552,"title":"Chapter 552: Beautiful and Magnificent Pearls","paragraphs":["Li Xiaotiao had only recently joined the group and hadn’t met Lin Yuan before that.","Now, it was his first time seeing Lin Yuan.","However, because Lin Yuan had been surrounded by many group members in the Purchase With No Loss store the previous time, the image of him wearing his strange mask had also spread through the fan club.","Li Xiaotiao glanced at Duan He with suspicion, who was staring at the group admin. Suddenly, a strange idea entered his mind.","His uncle was so powerful and not past middle age. By logic, he shouldn’t have had to worry about his son anymore.","Yet, Duan He had never found a wife for himself.","Could it be...?","Li Xiaotiao’s mind spun quickly while his heart sounded an alarm.","After he got home that night and received a beating from his mother, he would have to relay his discovery to her. Otherwise, when his uncle found himself a male partner, his mother might not be able to accept it.","Duan He wasn’t aware of what was running through his nephew’s mind. Nevertheless, even if he did know, he wouldn’t have been in the mood to kick Li Xiaotiao.","Duan He realized that although the masked youth before him was dressed in completely different clothes from the youth he had seen outside of Indigo Azure City, they both radiated the same special aura.","Moreover, Duan He had paid special attention to the strange mask on Lin Yuan’s face at that time.","This mask was extremely special as it had the majestic sky city engraved on it. Duan He was certain that he would not mistake this mask for another one.","Just by looking at this mask, Duan He would not have been able to confirm Lin Yuan’s identity.","However, Listen, who was standing beside Lin Yuan, was not wearing a mask. Hence, Duan He could clearly see his face.","After looking at Listen, Duan He soon confirmed that the masked youth before him was indeed the same one he had met outside of Indigo Azure City.","At the same time, Duan He also confirmed that this youth was the owner of the Purchase With No Loss store and the Moon Empress’ disciple.","When he finally realized the Purchase With No Loss store’s owner’s true identity, he felt a tingling sensation at the back of his head.","Duan He scanned the others seated in the store. It was possible that besides Listen, only he knew about the youth’s true identity.","If others knew that the Purchase With No Loss store’s owner was the Moon Empress’ disciple, they definitely wouldn’t have dared to sit on the stools that the youth had just arranged.","After confirming the youth’s identity, Duan He finally knew why there were 9,9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in the group welfare.","Only the Moon Empress’ disciple could so easily take out such a precious good that even pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters relied on luck to cultivate.","Soon after, Duan He returned to his senses. If the Moon Empress’ disciple was the Purchase With No Loss store’s owner, then when his nephew spread gossip in the group, was it not equivalent to spreading the gossip directly to the person being gossiped about and exposing one’s identity at once?","Duan He felt someone tugging at his sleeve. Upon lowering his head to find that it was Li Xiaotiao, he glared fiercely at the latter.","Under his uncle’s ferocious glare, Li Xiaotiao was so scared that his throat immediately constricted, and he did not mention that he wanted to help the former bid at the auction.","Rather, after looking around, Li Xiaotiao found that his cheap Master Duan Li still had a seat next to her and quickly trotted over.","Sitting innocently beside Master Duan Li, he ignored his uncle’s cold stare from behind him.","When Duan He raised his head to glance at the masked youth again, he suddenly realized that the latter was also looking in his direction.","Duan He looked coldly into Lin Yuan’s eyes and found that his and Lin Yuan’s eyes were in a straight match.","Immediately afterward, Duan He noticed that the masked youth’s mouth arched upward at the corner, revealing an indistinct smile.","Duan He quickly flashed an awkward smile at Lin Yuan before sitting down in the last row.","Lin Yuan was somewhat taken aback by this. He had hoped to seize the opportunity to contact Duan He through Recluse Study.","However, he hadn’t thought that Duan He would actually turn out to be a member of the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club.","Now, if he wanted to contact Duan He, it would undoubtedly be much more convenient.","Lin Yuan looked at Duan He’s awkward smile and was even more certain that the latter knew about his identity.","Nevertheless, it was presently not a good time to come into contact with Duan He. Lin Yuan had to wait at least till the end of the group welfare auction before he could contact the latter.","Seeing that almost everyone was seated, Lin Yuan announced clearly, “I had originally intended to conduct the group welfare auction in the group, just how I had auctioned the Flower Brocade Pearls the previous time.","“Since everyone requested the auction to be conducted in the Star Web store, then I might as well take this opportunity to let you take a look at the batch of elemental pearls in my hand before the auction.”","As Lin Yuan spoke, Listen walked to the former’s side with a tray.","With a wave of his hand, the four 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of water, air, fire, and earth appeared in the tray.","There were 12 pearls of each element and a total of 48 pearls.","When these 48 pearls appeared, every one of them had an outer layer that contained pure elemental energy and bloomed with a unique color.","The tray in Listen’s hands was shrouded in a layer of magnificent light.","At that moment, a voice whined impatiently,","“I want to know, besides the attributes of the 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, can I pick the pearls’ outer layer?”","As the woman with the whiny voice spoke, she looked at the 48 pearls in Listen’s tray that were exuding colorful light and inhaled two breaths.","The woman originally spoke subconsciously, but when the men around her heard it, they felt as though their bodies were out of their control.","It had simply been too whiny.","Even Stream in the Cloud, Zhou Jiaxin, and Violent-Tempered Woman felt themselves losing control over their bodies. They really wanted to use a righteous iron fist to beat the whining voice back into the woman’s belly.","Upon hearing this voice, Lin Yuan did not have any opinion on it. He only suddenly remembered that Genius was already 2,5 years old.","As a housekeeping beast, all Hundred Questions Beasts had to be neutered after reaching the age of 3.","If not, it would caterwaul non-stop throughout the day every spring."]},{"number":553,"title":"Chapter 553 - Top-NotChapter “Cloud Dream Lake”","paragraphs":["Upon entering the adolescent stage, most feys had sexual urges, but the majority were able to control their emotions and behavior.","They wouldn’t cry out or spiral out of control.","The main reason Hundred Questions Beasts had this sort of problem was that as housekeeping beasts, they did not even count as feys but could only be regarded as domesticated beasts.","As a beast, although the Hundred Questions Beast was very intelligent, it still lacked the instinct of self-control.","Moreover, Genius was now already a Bronze/Legend Thousand Questions Beast.","It should have been able to control its own beast instinct.","In any case, Lin Yuan didn’t want to let Genius become a “solitary warrior.”","No matter how miserable, it still had to be a “Santa Claus”.","Lin Yuan replied calmly after hearing the woman’s question.","“There are 12 pearls of each element in these 48 elemental pearls. The outer pearl layer is different for every pearl because every 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl is different.","“The type of pearl that everyone likes is also different. Later on, the person who gets the pearls can choose only 12 out of the 48 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.”","Lin Yuan’s words carried a sense of pride.","Letting the person who received the group welfare choose 12 out of the 48 pearls was equivalent to giving them the power to pick based on their preferences.","This allowed the person to maximize the value of the group welfare.","The people who had originally planned to bid on these 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls couldn’t help but grit their teeth and increase their bids again.","Lin Yuan raised his brows as he watched the crowd’s enthusiastic response.","After Lin Yuan had evolved the Elemental Shellfish of the four elements to Bronze/Legend, even if he wanted them to produce heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with a purity of less than 9.9, it would be very difficult.","They would only occasionally produce a few heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with a purity of 9.8 or so without the outer pearl layer.","Hence, Lin Yuan did not feel that the outer pearl layer on the elemental pearls was very rare or special.","In Lin Yuan’s eyes, although this outer layer was beautiful, it could not compare to the pleasure of stocking up on source-type items and various rare spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan already felt that he was becoming more and more of a hoarder.","Anyway, it was always good to stock up!","The woman with the whiny voice was sitting right at the front.","Holding the tray, Listen was about to let everyone participating in the auction take a look at the pearls.","Thus, the woman was the first to inspect the 48 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in the tray.","With this glance, the woman looked as though she had seen the treasure of her dreams and couldn’t help but exclaim, “God! All of these heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls are top-notch ‘Cloud Dream Lake’ pearls.”","While she was talking, the woman quickly grabbed a handful of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in her hand and investigated them.","Finally, she sighed to herself.","“If I hadn’t seen them with my own eyes and confirmed that these Cloud Dream Lake pearls were real as an expert, I would have thought that these were mass-produced fake goods upon seeing so many of them at once.”","The woman’s words immediately caused the men waiting to inspect the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in Listen’s tray, including Duan He, bubble with excitement.","“These are actually Cloud Dream Lake pearls! I must get the group welfare this time!”","“Oh! If these are Cloud Dream Lake pearls, even if I got the 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls at this auction, I couldn’t bring myself to use them but only collect them!”","“Cloud Dream Lake pearls are said to change with the person wearing them. Different lines and colors appear on the outer layer. Could this be true?”","“Anyway, I’m just here to watch the excitement. I can’t afford to auction this time. I mean, I could never have afforded to auction in the first place.”","Previously, Lin Yuan had only known that elemental pearls would accumulate a layer of pearl on their surface when they reached 9.9 purity.","He knew relatively little about the outer layer of pearls, which were only to be looked at but served no special function.","Although he wasn’t very sure about the grade of 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, the ones on the tray, which many people called Cloud Dream Lake pearls, were the ones most commonly produced by the four Elemental Shellfish with different attributes in his Spirit Lock spatial zone.","It could be said that of the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls produced in his Spirit Lock spatial zone, 95% were Cloud Dream Lake pearls.","With regards to the remaining 5%, even a man like Lin Yuan felt that they were too beautiful to be brought out.","Nevertheless, just by looking at the group member’s expressions upon seeing the Cloud Dream Lake pearls, he could see that they were already very extraordinary.","Lin Yuan understood that he had underestimated the Bronze/Legend Elemental Shellfish in his Spirit Lock spatial zone.","In other words, he had underestimated the pure and ample spirit qi in his Spirit Lock spatial zone.","This was extremely good news to Lin Yuan/","Since the outer layer of pearls on the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls could affect their value, it was intangibly tantamount to increasing the resources that Lin Yuan could produce infinitely.","This gave the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in Lin Yuan’s hands more purchasing power.","Listen had already allowed everyone participating in the auction to closely inspect the pearls in his tray.","After which, everyone’s breathing grew more rapid.","Their eyes were all fixated on the pearls in Listen’s tray.","Lin Yuan coughed softly and said, “Since you’ve all finished inspecting the elemental pearls, if you still have any questions, you can ask me directly. If not, we can begin the group welfare auction right away.”","By logic, everyone should have had a lot of questions about something as expensive and valuable as the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","However, Lin Yuan’s approach caused the men seated below to have nothing to ask about the pearls.","Everyone had already closely inspected the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that were about to be auctioned.","They had long known the quality of the pearls.","Even though these 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were all Cloud Dream Lake pearls, because they had been grown in lifeforms like Elemental Shellfish, each one of them was different.","Nevertheless, upon inspecting the 48 pearls, those who had set their minds on obtaining them had already decided which 12 they would choose.","Now, all of the men who were preparing to auction for them had their resources on standby and were ready to go."]},{"number":554,"title":"Chapter 554 - A Crazy Quote","paragraphs":["Seeing that nobody had any questions, Lin Yuan continued. “Because there is no need for so many rules at this group welfare auction, everyone can call out their bid within half an hour. The person with the highest bid at the end of this period will be able to take home the 12 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","“Of course, because the group welfare auction is for high-grade heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, common rare resources will no longer be allowed to be used in the bidding, unlike the last time.”","Before anyone could ask how to differentiate between common rare resources and precious rare resources, Lin Yuan spoke again.","“In this group welfare auction, the definition of precious rare resources is relatively loose. Everything that can be sent to the Star Web’s Rare Lifeform Pavilion’s quarterly auction is counted.”","Upon hearing this, the men seated below who had been planning to bid on the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls all fell into complete silence.","However, some of the men had obvious glee glinting in their eyes, while others who had worn confident expressions before now had their brows furrowed.","One of those in the latter group was Duan He.","When he had been preparing to participate in the group welfare auction for the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, Duan He had known that the bidding for the pearls would be defined.","Otherwise, if someone produced a Gold fey, another would produce 150 Silver feys or even 3,000 Bronze feys to top this.","No matter how one compared them, the actual price of 3,000 Bronze feys was higher than one Gold fey.","Yet, even an ordinary person would choose just one Gold fey over 3,000 Bronze feys.","It was just that Duan He would never have thought that Lin Yuan would set the bar so low in the auction.","Star Web’s Rare Lifeform Pavilion held an auction every day.","However, its quarterly auctions had very strict requirements for the lot; even some Gold spiritual ingredients were no longer accepted at these auctions.","Spiritual ingredients were only considered if they had reached the Platinum grade.","Duan He had thought that the 9.9 purity Cloud Dream Lake pearls could at least have been exchanged for materials at the same foundational grade, such as source-type items.","As an expert, Duan He naturally did not stock up on so many common rare resources.","He had long exchanged all of his common rare resources for source-type items.","However, Duan He now wanted to use source-type items as a bargaining chip to bid fairly for materials that were obviously not of the same grade as the former.","Duan He felt that he was getting the short end of the stick.","Nevertheless, Duan He would still bid on those Cloud Dream Lake pearls regardless of how he felt.","Upon seeing that the group members still didn’t have any questions to ask, Lin Yuan glanced at Listen beside him before sitting down on a chair behind him.","Sensing Lin Yuan’s intention, Listen immediately began hosting the group welfare auction.","As Lin Yuan’s representative in the group, it was natural to the group members that Listen was presiding over the auction.","Listen opened his mouth to speak.","Squinting his fox-like eyes, Listen said seriously, “Let’s all be livelier; you can just stand up and shout out your bids directly.”","Upon hearing Listen’s words, Duan He silently applauded the former.","This bidding method directly prevented bidders from using comparatively worse resources to bid.","If one used such a resource to shout one’s bid, they would likely be quickly called out by other bidders.","Every bidder was competing against one another. In an auction for something like heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, nobody cared about anybody else.","By using a sub-par resource, not only would the bidding be ineffective, but one would also lose face.","At the same time, this competitive bidding could mobilize the atmosphere very well.","This sort of atmosphere was not meant to promote liveliness but to make it easy for bidders to outbid one another.","As Listen presided over the auction, people were already beginning to shout out their bids in an endless stream.","It could be said that Duan He had guessed Listen’s thoughts correctly, but he had not guessed the latter’s main motive.","After Listen had begun managing the Purchase With No Loss store’s fan club, he had also started seeing it as one of his own resources.","Listen could now recognize every member in the group.","However, Listen was still unable to discern each member’s wealth through everyday interactions in the group.","Through this group welfare auction’s bidding method, Listen wanted to assess and rank each member’s wealth in order.","Moreover, he hoped to use his fan club connections when developing the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce in the future.","Lin Yuan sat behind listening to the bids and found that some men were throwing out spiritual ingredients that he had never been able to collect before.","It was just that many of these were soon quickly outbid by others.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help but swallow his saliva. If he could only obtain all of these rare spiritual ingredients, he would save himself so much effort.","In this group welfare auction, it actually stood to reason that Lin Yuan was already losing out by taking out 9.9 purity Cloud Dream Lake pearls.","However, Lin Yuan did not feel this way.","He was using the elemental pearls that were supplied continuously in his Spirit Lock spatial zone in exchange for large quantities of different precious resources at once.","This would undoubtedly save him the significant amount of time and effort required to search for these rare resources.","When the Floating Island Whale hatched, he couldn’t build the Sky City on its back using just heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls alone. He needed to accumulate large quantities of various previous resources.","From then on, Lin Yuan would begin accumulating these resources. This would also save him the trouble of searching for them later.","If not, he would be in a terrible fix if he couldn’t find some of these rare resources later on.","The auction continued unceasingly, the atmosphere growing so intense that it smelled like gunpowder.","20 minutes later, Lin Yuan was rather shocked by some of the bids being shouted.","Just then, the Class 4 Creation Master, Master Duan Li, stood up. Her face flushed with anger, and she said to the woman with the whiny voice, “I have eight source-type items, 500kg of Platinum Thousand Opportunities Secret Crystals, one Platinum Fortune Sea Willow, and 45 scales produced by the Diamond Shining Luster Amphiptere.”"]},{"number":555,"title":"Chapter 555 - The Second Source-type Item","paragraphs":["Master Duan Li’s price corresponded with the one Lin Yuan had in mind.","Not only was Lin Yuan shocked by the price and how it had reached his ideal amount with ten minutes to spare, but he was even more astonished by the item Master Duan Li brought out.","If Lin Yuan was not as certain as he was that he was unacquainted with Master Duan Li and had not had much interaction with her in the past, he might begin to suspect that she was offering such a bid in order to seduce him.","Platinum Thousand Opportunities Secret Crystal was a type of spiritual ingredient that Lin Yuan wanted to give Source Sand to swallow and transform into metal before it evolved to Platinum/Fantasy Breed.","The scales of the Shining Luster Amphiptere were a kind of spiritual ingredient that could be used to nurture the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly.","Lin Yuan had failed to procure the scales of the Shining Luster Amphiptere, despite having searched for it fervently.","Yet, now Master Duan Li was offering everything that he needed in one shot.","Lin Yuan was no longer as interested in the Fortune Sea Willow as it grew naturally in the bodies of matured feys.","As a fey that lived underwater and killed by strangling its targets, Hu Quan was jealous of the Fortune Sea Willow’s body.","Master Duan Li sat down after announcing all the bids. The girl with the whiny voice gracefully rose to her feet and glanced at Master Duan Li with disdain.","Although she continued to speak with that whiny voice, her words carried aggravating venomous intent.","“You old fart, I, Wang Fuxiang, have never been afraid of anyone. I cursed 32 husbands, 16 boyfriends, 27 lovers, and 81 suitors to death to get my hands on their wealth. Even if you are a Class 4 Creation Master, the amount of money I have will blow your mind. I won’t give in to you just because you’re old.”","Lin Yuan almost burst out in laughter when he heard the girl’s name.","Wang Fuxiang was such a strange name!","Lin Yuan was mortified by the girl’s revelation of the number of men she had cursed to death.","This girl was the epitome of terror.","Lin Yuan checked the girl’s username in the group and raised his eyebrow.","Wang Fuxiang—”signifies the beauty of spring and the coalesce of summer”—what a beautiful name!","Wang Fuxiang turned toward Lin Yuan elegantly.","“I can use 20 source-type items to exchange for your 12 pretty pearls. The pearls will look gorgeous around my neck. The innate glow of those pearls will be perfect for accentuating my beauty and unique complexion.”","As she spoke, she caressed her pale neck as though she was preening.","Everyone present’s eyelids twitched at her words.","She was actually planning on using something as precious as heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls as superficial accessories.","It was almost blasphemous!","But in honesty, 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were more precious than 9.8 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls not only because of the higher purity but also because 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls possessed a one-of-a-kind innate glow.","Although what she said could be construed as logical, everyone was still appalled by her opulence.","Several men were sneering inwardly.","No matter how many husbands, boyfriends, lovers, or suitors you have, all of their wealth combined won’t be enough to support your frivolous spending.","Master Duan Li’s face flushed with anger when she heard Wang Fuxiang’s words. She stood up and said brusquely, “The group admin has already greatly discounted the threshold for the valuable source-type items. Even if your 20 source-type items are of higher quality than the items I’m offering, they are comparable in terms of value. Hence, your bid doesn’t count!”","When she heard Master Duan Li’s response, Wang Fuxiang casually tucked her silky hair behind her ear. She turned, tilted her head, and said in a sweet voice, “Amongst the 20 source-type items I’m offering, one of them is an elemental source-type item. It’s also exceedingly easy to contract this elemental source-type item. As long as the contractor is female and her body has been cleansed of at least 10% of its impurities, she’ll be able to form the contract. How will you trade for what I have with your pathetic trinkets, old fart?”","Wang Fuxiang turned her head and took out a paper-like source-type item.","“I am entering this mutated wood-elemental source-type item. It is paper-element.”","Lin Yuan never expected that someone would enter an elemental source-type item in one of his group welfare auctions.","When he bought the Source Sand from the private auction, he had only spent a small amount because the Source Sand had a challenging set of conditions for contraction.","It was already difficult enough for spirit qi professionals to comprehend Willpower Runes. Thus, not many people were willing to sacrifice two Willpower Runes to contract one source-type item, even if it was a rare elemental source-type item.","Wang Fuxiang’s elemental source-type item sounded rather unorthodox, but the conditions for forming a contract were just too simple.","Firstly, the contractor of the paper-elemental source type item had to be female, which meant that half the spirit qi professionals in the world were eligible.","Although the condition of cleansing their body of at least 10% of impurities sounded challenging, it was not impossible for people who possessed enough resources.","One bowl of the nectar from the Radiant Moon Palace’s Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias would be able to clear a body of at least 90% of its impurities, maybe even 100%.","When the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia evolved to Suzerain, its nectar could even be used to cleanse a soul’s impurities.","Although there were not many spiritual ingredients that could cleanse a body’s impurities, a Class 3 Creation Master could combine different spiritual ingredients to form a concoction that could clear the body of at least 15% of its impurities.","Many top factions racked their minds to come up with a way to beg the Radiant Moon Palace for a drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","The drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar would greatly boost the effectiveness of the concoction and raise its cleansing abilities to at least 30%."]},{"number":556,"title":"Chapter 556 - The Greedy Lin Yuan","paragraphs":["Hence, the paper-elemental source-type item’s criteria for forming a contract were almost too simple.","For some reason, Lin Yuan thought back to a character in an anime he had seen in his previous life after he heard about the paper element.","A foolish thought entered Lin Yuan’s mind.","I’m definitely not stupid, but if I can get my hands on the paper-elemental source-type item, Chu Ci and Wen Yu would be eligible to contract it.","However, Chu Ci was going to contract the fairy source-type item Burning Sunflower.","The Burning Sunflower would not be compatible with a paper-elemental source-type item.","As a mutation of the wood element, the paper element would soon go up in flames when it came into contact with the Burning Sunflower’s all-engulfing flames.","Thus, the best candidate to contract the paper-elemental source-type item was Wen Yu.","Wen Yu was a support-type spirit qi professional, and both the Sunlight Egret and Earth Rush Golden Lotus did not have any combat abilities.","Wen Yu was like a blank canvas, and she could contract any source-type item she wanted. She did not need to worry that the source-type item she contracted would limit her.","Lin Yuan was in the throes of this dilemma. He wanted both the 500 grams of Thousand Opportunities Secret Crystal and Diamond Shining Luster Amphiptere scales as well as Wang Fuxiang’s paper-elemental source-type item.","As this was a group welfare auction, Lin Yuan could only trade with the person who offered the highest bid.","Although this was the most cost-effective course of action for Lin Yuan, it pained him to see such precious items slip out of his grasp.","Lin Yuan could not help but start scheming about how he could obtain the valuable items offered by both women.","“If there’s really an elemental-type amongst the 20 source-type items you’re offering, that means you’re clearly the highest bidder,” said Lin Yuan to Wang Fuxiang.","Wang Fuxiang giggled and said, “I adore the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls you’re selling. I wonder if you’ll be auctioning off more in the future?”","Everyone who was interested in the elemental pearls, including Duan He, perked up their ears at her question.","They waited with bated breath to hear what Lin Yuan had planned.","Lin Yuan was momentarily stunned by her question, but he replied without hesitation, “I’m auctioning off these 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls as group welfare instead of the ones that were 9.8 purity because I wanted to compensate for the two-day delay. The next group welfare auction will no longer be for heavenly-grade elemental pearls. The next item will be Flower Brocade Pearls like the first time.”","The disappointment was visible on the faces of the people who were waiting for Lin Yuan’s reply.","When he saw their reaction, Lin Yuan gently knocked on the table.","Lin Yuan was not stupid. If he auctioned off heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of such quality again next time, some of the group members who wanted them would hold back and wait to see if they could enter the auction with a low bid.","There were not many people in the group who could afford to participate in an auction for heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls. If he auctioned in such a way, how would he sell them for a profit?","Lin Yuan knew that the more precious the item, the more valuable it was.","Although Lin Yuan possessed the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in the greatest abundance among all his resources, he would not continuously conduct group welfare of such caliber.","However, Lin Yuan did not kill all their hopes. All he said was that the next item auctioned off as group welfare would be Flower Brocade Pearls.","How the group members took it was up to them, for everyone had different perspectives after all.","Wang Fuxiang glanced at the platter of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in Listen’s hands before saying, “If I’m able to put up more resources for bidding, is it possible for me to bid for 20 more heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls based on the price they end up being sold at?”","Lin Yuan shook his head determinedly and said calmly, “No.”","Lin Yuan was actually more than willing to comply with her request, and the current bid had reached the amount he had in mind. Moreover, the tense atmosphere and faces of the volatile bigshots told him that he was going to gain a huge windfall from this auction.","If he could multiply the winning bid by two, it would be twice the joy.","The fact that Wang Fuxiang posed the question meant that she had the purchasing power to back it up.","Lin Yuan was in awe of the amount of wealth she controlled.","She really was someone who had cursed 100 men to death and seized their wealth.","However, Lin Yuan had laid down the group welfare auction rules from the first time that he held one.","As the owner of the Purchase With No Loss store, as well as the head of Sky City, he could not change his mind at the last moment when it came to the group welfare auction.","Despite how badly he wanted it, he had to bite the bullet and said no.","After being denied by Lin Yuan twice, Wang Fuxiang pouted but did not sit down again. She stood gracefully as she waited for the rest of the people to make their bids so she could out-bid them.","Master Duan Li’s face was irked and reddened as she heard Wang Fuxiang’s syrupy voice. Just as she was about to rebuke her, she suddenly remembered a rumor. She looked exceptionally frightened as she pushed down the words that were already on the tip of her tongue.","Li Xiaotiao, who was next to Master Duan Li, heard his Master murmur, “Older than 100 years old.”","Li Xiaotiao dazedly scanned the flirtatious Wang Fuxiang, who looked no older than 30 years old.","However, he could not be sure if he had heard correctly since many people yelled out their bids.","The hesitation on Master Duan Li’s face was replaced by determination after she looked at the elemental pearls on the platter in Listen’s hands."]},{"number":557,"title":"Chapter 557 - The Langya Pavilion’s Master","paragraphs":["Once Master Duan Li composed herself, a pained expression appeared on her face.","It was soon replaced by an expression that indicated that she had a plan cooking up in her mind.","Master Duan Li had stopped her anxious bidding. She patiently sat in her seat and waited for the final moment when she could swoop in for the kill.","Li Xiaotiao did not notice that his Master had a plan in place. He assumed that she had been defeated by Wang Fuxiang and felt helpless in the light of Wang Fuxiang’s overwhelming financial prowess.","Li Xiaotiao knew that his uncle, Duan He, had also come to participate in the auction. However, up till that moment, Duan He still had not called out a single bid.","Li Xiaotiao turned his head and peeked at Duan He. But when he thought about the menacing glare that his uncle had shot him, Li Xiaotiao quickly fixed his posture and focused his gaze on Wang Fuxiang.","Compared to his uncle’s ferocious glare, Wang Fuxiang’s flirtatious demeanor was still easier to swallow, even if she really was a 100-year-old elderly lady.","At that moment, Wang Fuxiang called out another bid as she continued to crush others under the might of her wealth.","After she announced her bid of the paper-elemental source-type item, Wang Fuxiang did not display any other rarer items.","However, whenever someone called out a higher bid, she would add on a source-type item that could outbid them.","Amongst all the bidders, Wang Fuxiang’s bids were the most straightforward.","The way that she threw out source-type items reminded Li Xiaotiao of a rich older woman.","When he thought about Wang Fuxiang’s age and her dead husbands, boyfriends, lovers, and suitors, Li Xiaotiao thought it was best to comfort his Master, who was sure to lose the bidding war.","Behind Lin Yuan’s mask was a serene expression, which starkly contrasted with the rapidly turning gears in his head.","He was racking his brain to come up with a way he could auction off more elemental pearls without breaking his own rules while obtaining all the items he wanted.","Lin Yuan already had a general idea, but there was a difficult condition to fulfill in order for him to succeed.","Lin Yuan could only wait to see if the enthusiastically bidding group members could create the conditions he needed.","Duan He’s brow furrowed even tighter. His mind had been preoccupied with thoughts of Lin Yuan throughout the auction.","However, he had now turned his attention to Wang Fuxiang.","Duan He never expected to see someone like her in this fan club.","In Duan He’s opinion, this woman was a complex enigma.","Even at his most wealthy state, Duan He could not compare to Wang Fuxiang.","Wang Fuxiang had cursed a total of 158 partners to death, and none of them were ordinary men.","Half of the men she cursed to death were Creation Masters, most of which were Class 3, but three of them were Class 4.","One of the Class 4 Creation Masters had been a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master.","The last husband Wang Fuxiang had was a pinnacle emperor-class expert who owned a Suzerain/Myth III fey.","30 years ago, when Duan He had just reached king-class, he joined the Spirit Guards.","The first assignment he had was to investigate Wang Fuxiang under the leadership of a Guard Envoy.","Once the investigation was concluded, it was found that all of the men associated with Wang Fuxiang had died in accidents.","The pinnacle emperor-class expert was a member of that team who had gone with him to investigate.","Since all the evidence pointed toward accidents, the Guard Envoy could only write ‘Wang Fuxiang has an extremely resilient life’ on the investigation report.","Duan He had always been sure that there was more to Wang Fuxiang that met the eye.","He had left the Spirit Guards in less than a year.","During this year, Wang Fuxiang had used all the finances willed to her to form a team dedicated to appraising luxury goods—the Langya Pavilion.","In the beginning, the Langya Pavilion only appraised luxury goods made of rare spiritual ingredients and gave them credit ratings.","As time went on, some extremely valuable luxury goods would be afforded high credit ratings by the Langya Pavilion, and the price would continue to inflate afterward.","The Langya Pavilion had been running for 30 years.","Now, the Langya Pavilion’s appraisal and credit rating could define a luxury’s good exact worth.","Wang Fuxiang was the woman who had built this institution from the ground.","Duan He could not even begin to comprehend the earth-shattering amount of wealth that Wang Fuxiang possessed.","No one here knew Wang Fuxiang’s true identity other than him.","Duan He knew that if he had not coincidentally been assigned to investigate Wang Fuxiang, he would also be none the wiser about her background.","Despite what he knew, Duan He was not going to let his guard down during this auction.","Duan He stood up and said in a booming voice, “I’m bidding 27 source-type items, as well as a drop of essence blood from a Suzerain/Myth I Ancient Lake Toad.”","Lin Yuan narrowed his eyes at Duan He’s sudden additional bid. All the participants in the auction took a sharp intake of breath.","Although Wang Fuxiang’s paper-elemental pearl was rare, it was still just a source-type item.","Only an emperor-class expert had access to the essence blood of a Suzerain/Myth I fey.","The Ancient Lake Toad’s essence blood was difficult to be put to use as compared to the essence blood of other Suzerain/Myth Breed feys because it was poison-type. The essence blood of other Suzerain/Myth Breed feys could be used to nurture other feys once it was turned into a concoction.","However, the blood of a poison-type fey was an exception.","If the essence blood of a poison-type fey was used to nurture other feys, the fey could likely be poisoned to death.","That said, the essence blood of a Suzerain/Myth I Ancient Lake Toad was enough to overcome Wang Fuxiang’s bid of the paper-elemental item.","Lin Yuan was elated that Duan He had joined the auction. As much as he wanted to recruit Duan He, it was unknown if Duan He’s character could meet his standard, and he also did not know if Duan He would be interested in what Lin Yuan was offering.","Thus, Lin Yuan could only take the money Duan He was offering."]},{"number":558,"title":"Chapter 558 - Sunlight King Lotus","paragraphs":["Even if Duan He won the 12 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, they would remain his personal items regardless if Lin Yuan recruited him or not.","There was no doubt that Duan He was Wang Fuxiang’s strongest competitor.","Moreover, the bid needed to reach an unimaginable amount in order to meet the conditions Lin Yuan was hoping for.","When Wang Fuxiang heard that her bid had been outdone, she started to boil with rage.","Wang Fuxiang glared at Duan He and said, “Why does a disgusting man like you need these Cloud Dream Lake pearls? Something as magnificent as this should be hung around my neck. Only my snow-white neck is worthy of being adorned by them.”","Duan He glanced at Wang Fuxiang’s neck.","Somehow, he felt as though what she said was right.","The moment that the thought entered his head, Duan He could not help but be shocked at himself.","He hastily looked away and said in a low voice, “The maximum purity of the elemental energy in the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls is the best medicine to trigger metamorphosis in feys.”","Wang Fuxiang patted the chair in front of her and softly uttered, “I bid 30 source-type items. One of the source-type items is the paper-elemental source-type item that I mentioned before. How dare you speak of using the Cloud Dream pearls to nurture feys. It’s almost sacrilegious. Hehe, of course, someone like you is destined to be a pauper forever.”","Duan He’s expression darkened. He raised his bid above Wang Fuxiang’s without another word.","Listen, who was next to Lin Yuan, announced, “The auction will end in two minutes. All who still want to bid should do so now.”","After Listen spoke, one of the bigshots in the group joined the bidding war.","However, the moment that he called out his bid, Duan He outbid him.","The bigshot that had been outbid sat back down on his seat regretfully and crossed his legs.","It was obvious that he had abandoned bidding and was resigned to being a spectator.","Just then, the silent Master Duan Li stood up and said, “My bid remains the same, but I would like to add another 500 grams of Thousand Opportunity Crystal and a Heaven and Earth Sunlight King Lotus.”","Wang Fuxiang’s expression flattened, and she cursed to herself.","This old woman is a Creation Master. How is she willing to sacrifice the Sunlight King Lotus as a bid? She’s a lunatic!","Lin Yuan had a slight inclination to give up on his plan, and he decided to use other methods in the future to get his hands on all the rare spiritual ingredients Master Duan Li had that he needed.","However, he did not expect Master Duan Li to be so obstinate as to join the fray along with Duan He and Wang Fuxiang.","Master Duan Li’s bid immediately fulfilled half of the conditions Lin Yuan had been hoping for.","But, whether Lin Yuan’s expectations could come to fruition was still up to Duan He and Wang Fuxiang.","If Duan He and Wang Fuxiang did not continue bidding, Lin Yuan would be able to obtain everything that Master Duan Li had bid.","Her bid even included the Sunlight King Lotus. What a profit!","In order to expand the man-made lake in Return from Faraway Mansion, Lin Yuan wanted to build a water garden in the center.","The hardest part of the process was how to keep the garden buoyant.","As a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman, it was hard for him to design a water garden.","The foundation of the garden was already a huge project. If Lin Yuan could obtain the Sunlight King Lotus, he would plant it in the middle of the man-made lake.","The Sunlight King Lotus would eventually grow to the size of a small mountain, and he would build a beautiful pavilion on each of its 32 leaves.","The matured Sunlight King Lotus would form a natural basic structure for the water garden.","All of Hu Quan’s designs and buildings could take place on top of the Sunlight King Lotus.","As a Heaven and Earth Fey, the Sunlight King Lotus’ main ability was that it could store sunlight in its tusk-shaped roots that grew underwater.","After the sun set, the Sunlight King Lotus would release all the sunlight it had stored.","Above the surface would be dark, but underwater would be lit up warmly like daytime. Hence, the surface of the water would be alight and bright at all times,","Unfortunately, the Sunlight King Lotus was not a very strong Heaven and Earth Fey.","Nonetheless, the Sunlight King Lotus’ abilities could provide the plant-type feys in Lin Yuan’s water garden with twice the sunlight.","The increased amount of sunlight would allow the flowers that required more sunlight to bloom more illustriously than before.","With the Sunlight King Lotus, Hu Quan and Jiao Hanzhong’s collection of various rare flowers would be sure to turn the water garden into a magical place.","The only animals in the man-made lake would be the Angelfish of Bliss that Lin Yuan planned on breeding.","When nightfall descended, the water would be flooded with the glittering sunlight that beat down at noon.","After Duan He and Wang Fuxiang’s short pause, they both shouted out their addition of source-type items in unison.","Their prices had matched Master Duan Li’s.","Master Duan Li cursed internally, These two are insane!","Master Duan Li no longer looked like she had everything under control.","Li Xiaotiao was thrilled as his Master and uncle were bidding so intensely.","As the disciple and nephew of two bigshots, I’m so cool!","While Duan He and Wang Fuxiang were screaming out bids, Lin Yuan’s lip curled upward under the mask.","The conditions he had hoped for were finally fulfilled. Now was the time for him to reap his harvest.","Listen checked the time.","Wang Fuxiang, Duan He, and Master Duan Li’s bids were evenly matched.","Listen proclaimed, “Ten seconds left till the group welfare auction is over.”","Wang Fuxiang gnashed her teeth and said in a sweet voice, “I’m willing to add another three source-type items.”"]},{"number":559,"title":"Chapter 559 - The Righteous Lin Yuan","paragraphs":["Before Wang Fuxiang finished speaking, a clear voice exclaimed, “Your bids are too high. Stop increasing it.”","Wang Fuxiang was interrupted just as she was about to increase her bid. Her tightly knitted brow drew even tighter.","When she realized that the person who had interrupted her was the group admin, she raised an eyebrow in surprise.","Wang Fuxiang did not expect the group admin’s voice to sound so young. It had an indescribable magnetism to it.","The voice comforted Wang Fuxiang.","When Lin Yuan called for the bidding to stop, everyone’s eyes landed on him.","Lin Yuan could feel all their gazes on him. He grabbed the platter of elemental pearls from Listen’s hands and raised it in the air.","“The aim of the group welfare is to give out welfare. The bids for these heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls are already too high. It defeats the purpose of welfare,” said Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan uttered those words full of righteousness.","At that moment, the living embodiment of righteousness that was Lin Yuan stunned all the people present.","Although it was a group welfare auction, it was no different from a regular auction in the eyes of the people present.","The fact that Lin Yuan was willing to auction off the 9.9 purity Cloud Dream Lake pearls was enough to be considered welfare.","Moreover, the people who won them could take their pick from 48 types.","It was up to the participants and their resources to decide the final bid.","However, the people present felt a touch of warmth when Lin Yuan called for the bidding to halt.","Although the atmosphere in the Purchase With No Loss store was great, the group admin often only read through the logs and did not post messages.","The group members felt a tinge of gentleness from the group admin’s action of calling for the bids to stop.","Wang Fuxiang also felt the kindness of this strange mask-wearing youth.","Nonetheless, Wang Fuxiang was set on owning these Cloud Dream Lake pearls.","During the earlier bidding, Wang Fuxiang had already prepared herself for the trade-off.","“Before the group admin called for the bidding to end, I was the last to make a bid. How about you just hand these Cloud Dream Lake pearls to me?”","Duan He and Master Duan Li were both ready to fight when Lin Yuan called for the bidding to stop.","Duan He had nothing left, and he was ready to throw in the spiritual ingredients he had initially prepared to give to his main fey for it to break through to Myth II.","Logically, Duan He knew that he should not. Thus, he gave up the bidding war after a moment’s contemplation.","Whereas Master Duan Li still had some resources left in her bank. As a Class 4 Creation Master, Master Duan Li had about as many resources as Lin Yuan.","She worked hard to earn money, but she was very thrifty. Thus, she had stored up a sizable treasury of resources.","She took another look at the platter of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls and clenched her fist.","It’s just a few source-type items. I’ll work even harder and earn them back after I nurture a few feys.","After she made her decision, Master Duan Li stepped toward Wang Fuxiang and said, “If you bid again, so will I. You’re not the only one who has the means to bid. By hook or by crook, those elemental pearls are mine.”","Wang Fuxiang smiled in frustration at Master Duan Li’s words. She was about to rebuke her when Lin Yuan spoke out again.","“If you keep fighting, I don’t know how I should conduct the next group welfare. How about this? You both take a step back.”","Wang Fuxiang anxiously cried out, “I can’t take a step back when it comes to this.”","Master Duan Li hastily made her stand as well. “I’m not going to back down no matter how high the bid gets. If anyone else wants to take a step back, they can. But I won’t!”","Lin Yuan fell silent. The other people present assumed he was feeling troubled.","However, Lin Yuan was actually heaping praises on Wang Fuxiang and Master Duan Li in his heart.","Lin Yuan glanced at Duan He. He knew that Duan He’s silence indicated that he was not going to participate in the auction anymore.","Lin Yuan was not particularly interested in any of the items that Duan He was bidding.","It was not absolutely necessary for Lin Yuan to own the essence blood of the Suzerain/Myth I Ancient Lake Toad.","Lin Yuan had amassed a considerable amount of Suzerain/Myth II essence blood thanks to his enemies’ contribution as well as the Mother of Bloodbath’s frenzied collection efforts.","Even though Duan He no longer intended to participate in the auction, Lin Yuan followed protocol and asked, “Do you have any issue with the auction continuing?”","Duan He had reflected on his current situation. He felt that he had been rather impulsive previously.","If I really manage to buy the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, what am I supposed to do about the evolution of the feys? Even if I can sell these Cloud Dream Lake pearls, I have no experience doing so. I have no idea if I’ll be able to sell them at the same price as they were auctioned.","Duan He understood why Lin Yuan halted the bidding—the bids had gotten too high.","There were few people who were as crazy and rich as Wang Fuxiang.","Duan He said nonchalantly, “If those two are willing to take a step back, I’ll back out. It’ll save you some trouble.”","Lin Yuan thought, Duan He sure backed out like a gentleman. Since he’s definitely backing out, there’s no point in me focusing any attention on him during this group welfare auction.","Lin Yuan sighed what sounded like a conflicted sigh. He said to Wang Fuxiang and Master Duan Li, “Since both of you want them, I shall sacrifice a bit more. I’ll auction off two sets of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.”","Lin Yuan gestured for Listen to bring another platter.","The people present were startled by Lin Yuan’s actions. It might be the best way to stop the bids from climbing even higher, but they could not see in what way Lin Yuan was making a sacrifice.","How is the group admin making a sacrifice when the bids have reached such a price?","Listen had already carried another platter over.","With one wave of Lin Yuan’s hand, another pile of elemental pearls fell into the platter.","However, there were two elemental pearls in this pile that were obviously different from the Cloud Dream Lake ones.","The inner radiance of these two elemental pearls outshined the rest of the Cloud Dream Lake elemental pearls.","Lin Yuan picked one up and placed it onto the other platter.","The entire platter of Cloud Dream Lake pearls could not rival the inner radiance of this one elemental pearl."]},{"number":560,"title":"Chapter 560 - Defined Life","paragraphs":["The swirling radiance of this one pearl seemed to carry the lifeforce of the world. It was as though there was a glorious city within the pearl, and a magnificent world had been locked within this pearly cage.","Each time you glimpsed the pearl, you would experience a different feeling. It could be said that you were taking a stroll through the lush world inside the pearl.","The invigorating lifeforce inside the pearl gave the innate radiance a dense feeling.","When you looked at the pearl, you would be able to sense the graceful intelligence within.","This mesmerizing pearl would entrance even a person who did not fancy pretty trinkets.","Wang Fuxiang stared dazedly at the two platters in Lin Yuan’s hands. She softly muttered, “I can’t believe you have the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with the Defined Life inner radiance. You really are making a huge sacrifice! I can’t believe you’re giving away such a treasure as group welfare! Thank you for your generosity. With this Defined Life pearl, the one I acquired by luck 20 years ago won’t have to collect dust in my jewelry box anymore. Both of them will make an elegant pair of earrings for me.”","Lin Yuan had never heard of the Defined Life inner radiance.","Lin Yuan merely took out the 9.9 purity elemental pearls with the inner radiance that was second in abundance.","The Cloud Dream Lake inner radiance elemental pearls comprised 95% of the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, and the Defined Life inner radiance elemental pearls comprised 4%.","Judging from the statistics, Lin Yuan could tell that the Defined Life pearls were sure to be much more valuable than the Cloud Dream Lake pearls.","Master Duan Li marched right up to the platter and carefully studied the two Defined Life pearls. She looked like she was in seventh heaven.","Duan He, who had coolly withdrawn, now looked incredibly bitter.","He had given up such a prime opportunity without a second thought.","He didn’t deserve to have money!","The other group members participating in the group welfare auction had initially joined the group intending to easily pick up items.","But as time went on, the group admin seemed increasingly mysterious.","The items he produced were all magical treasures.","He also conducted his business in a detailed manner. He was too amazing!","Although Lin Yuan’s expression was as unreadable as ever, he was actually overjoyed that he could trade away some of the elemental pearls which were produced in the Spirit Lock spatial zone in a never-ending stream.","Not only could he trade for the paper-elemental source-type item in this group welfare auction which was suitable for Wen Yu, but he could also obtain the Sunlight King Lotus that he could use to nurture his feys and expand his mansion. Moreover, he also obtained a large amount of source-type items.","The impending harvest made Lin Yuan feel as though he had landed in a gold mine.","This group welfare auction was finally over.","Now that the group welfare auction was over, many of the members who had just come to watch the action left the Purchase With No Loss store.","However, the enthusiasm about the group welfare auction did not die down.","The enthusiasm merely transferred from inside the store to the fan club.","It quickly spread to the Star Web forum.","There were less than ten people left in the Purchase With No Loss store now.","Wang Fuxiang and Master Duan Li had started picking out the elemental pearls from the two platters in Listen’s hands.","Lin Yuan watched as Master Duan Li collected the Defined Life pearl, and her weathered face was stretched into a cherub smile.","Master Duan Li said to Lin Yuan carefully, “The Defined Life pearl I picked is water-type, but the one Wang Fuxiang picked is earth-type. I don’t want a water-type. I’m wondering if you can help me exchange it?”","Master Duan Li glared at Wang Fuxiang in annoyance.","Since Wang Fuxiang was the last to make a bid, she had the first pick of the elemental pearls.","Lin Yuan asked Master Duan Li, “What type of Defined Life peal would you like?”","Master Duan Li had posed the question because she was indignant that Wang Fuxiang had first pick.","Master Duan Li knew that it was very rare to own even one piece of a treasure like the Defined Life pearl.","Hence, she was not hopeful that Lin Yuan would agree to the exchange.","However, Lin Yuan’s response delighted her.","She happily replied, “I’m fine with anything as long as it’s not water-type.”","Lin Yuan turned to ask Wang Fuxiang, “Do you have any specifications about the Defined Life pearl?”","Wang Fuxiang had scrutinized the other 47 Cloud Dream Lake pearls, and she deemed them to all be of similar quality. However, they did differ in the shade of their inner radiance as well as hue.","Hence, Wang Fuxiang had chosen extremely carefully.","Wang Fuxiang did not anticipate Lin Yuan’s question. Her eyes lit up, and she said happily, “The one I acquired 20 years ago is wind-type. If you can provide me with one of a matching type, I’m willing to work with you privately in the future.”","Wang Fuxiang suddenly swept her inky black hair behind her shoulder, making her look even more flirtatious.","Wang Fuxiang looked toward Lin Yuan and subtly shuffled nearer to him till there was only a half a step of separation between them.","Lin Yuan almost choked on his own saliva as alarm bells rang in his mind.","What is this woman trying to do? One might lose their money if they’re seduced, but this woman is out to take lives. How terrifying!","With his expression unchanged, Lin Yuan coughed and took out a wind-type Defined Life pearl. He placed it on the platter in front of Wang Fuxiang."]},{"number":561,"title":"Chapter 561 - Did I Get Special Treatment?","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan transferred the earth-type Defined Life pearl from Wang Fuxiang’s platter to Master Duan Li. He then stored away the water-type Defined Life pearl Master Duan Li had chosen.","Wang Fuxiang stood there and blinked. She could not believe that her flirtatious performance was ignored.","She chuckled and said, “I don’t know what I can do to thank you for granting me a matching pearl. If you happen to encounter any rare items that you’re uncertain about in the future, please feel free to contact me on Star Web.”","Wang Fuxiang lowered her head and started to carefully pick and sort through the platter of elemental pearls.","Lin Yuan did not know how to react.","What’s going on? Why did she say I granted her a match? Somehow it feels like I’m cursing some poor soul .","Duan He did not immediately leave after the auction was over because he had business with Lin Yuan. Thus, he overheard the conversation between Wang Fuxiang and Lin Yuan.","Duan He thought, If the Moon Empress finds out that Wang Fuxiang is trying to seduce her precious disciple, I wonder if the bright moon in the sky will suddenly appear in the sky. It might very well be stained red. Wang Fuxiang’s love might be more dangerous than the Zheng family.","While Master Duan Li and Wang Fuxiang were picking the elemental pearls, Lin Yuan noticed that none of the water-type elemental pearls were chosen.","Lin Yuan could not understand why.","The water-type elemental pearl was usually popular, so he could not understand why they did not want them.","Wang Fuxiang and Master Duan Li left satisfied after they were done picking their elemental pearls.","At this moment, Lin Yuan realized there were two other people left in the store besides Listen, who was packing up the benches that had been laid out for the group welfare.","One of them was Duan He.","The other was the store’s first customer—Stream in the Cloud, or rather the braised egg head.","Lin Yuan could still remember how excited Stream in the Cloud was during the group welfare auction. However, she was visibly disappointed after the group welfare ended.","She looked like a trampled flower that had been wrenched around by a ferocious storm.","Lin Yuan walked up to Stream in the Cloud and said, “What happened? You could stuff a donkey in your mouth.”","Lin Yuan noticed that Stream in the Cloud was wearing the same bumblebee hat she wore the first time they met.","In half a year, her previously bald head was now full of luscious hair that hung past her face.","It seemed that Stream in the Cloud with hair was rather quiet.","When the miserable-looking Stream in the Cloud heard Lin Yuan’s comment, she immediately rolled her eyes.","“Did the donkey run out of the Deep Mountain Elder Lin’s mouth?” She huffed.","The moment the words left her mouth, Stream in the Cloud cringed at herself.","Stream in the Cloud had come in order to buy a fire-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearl. If they were ordinary heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, she would try her hand at bidding as well.","However, the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that Lin Yuan offered were of 9.9 purity and had inner radiance.","Stream in the Cloud did not have enough resources to make a bid.","After all her excitement, she was reduced to a spectator.","Lin Yuan glanced at Stream in the Cloud doubtfully. He suspected that Stream in the Cloud was distributing resources behind the scenes, but he did not have any evidence.","Duan He walked up to Lin Yuan and cleared his throat.","“Sir group admin, Is it possible for me to trade 10 9.8 purity wind-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearls with you? I’m willing to fork out two source-type items for each elemental pearl.”","Lin Yuan was surprised to hear Duan He address him in such a manner. He cocked an eyebrow.","For an emperor-class expert like Duan He to address Lin Yuan as Sir, Lin Yuan was certain that Duan He had found out the truth behind his identity.","Lin Yuan turned to look at Duan He. Just as Duan He’s hair started to stand under Lin Yuan’s scrutiny, Lin Yuan said, “The price is acceptable. No problem. It’s almost New Year’s. Let’s trade afterward.”","Lin Yuan did not reject Duan He’s request for a trade. The price he was offering of two source-type items for one 9.8 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl was already three times the market price.","The 9.8 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were just a spiritual ingredient. It was completely different from the luxury good that was the 9.9 purity heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","There was no reason for Lin Yuan to reject Duan He’s offer.","He had numerous elemental pearls in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. This deal was also a good chance for Lin Yuan to establish a connection with him.","Once he was done investigating Duan He’s character, Lin Yuan would be able to use that connection to move in on Duan He.","Duan He thanked Li Xiaotiao and bustled out of the Star Web store to find Li Xiaotiao.","Stream in the Cloud’s eyes lit up when he heard the discourse between Duan He and Lin Yuan.","“Lin Yuan, I also want to buy three fire-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls from you!”","As Stream in the Cloud spoke, Lin Yuan did not miss the flash of happiness that streaked across her gaze.","Lin Yuan immediately realized that Stream in the Cloud was not disappointed because she did not manage to win the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl auction.","Lin Yuan had nothing against Stream in the Cloud’s intention to buy from him.","Stream in the Cloud was Lin Yuan’s first customer at his Star Web store, and he had custom-ordered the Web-Spraying Spider for her, which allowed him to earn his first remuneration that was more than 1 Radiance dollar.","It was because Stream in the Cloud had earned Lin Yuan his first pot of gold that he had the financial ability to quickly improve himself through the use of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He had also created the Purchase With No Loss store fan club after his deal with Stream in the Cloud.","Stream in the Cloud had also been by his side when Lin Yuan had taken in the high-level match between White Devil and Unknown Flame and set his first goal as a spirit qi professional.","Now that he thought about it, Stream in the Cloud was always by his side.","A few exchanges of words later, Lin Yuan completed his deal with Stream in the Cloud.","Stream in the Cloud revealed a dazzling smile as she said, “Lin Yuan, did I get special treatment?”","Lin Yuan could only think about how wonderfully cool high-class Creation Masters were.","The rarer the good, the more valuable it was. On a certain level, this statement underlined the truth behind pricing.","Lin Yuan had charged Stream in the Cloud the lowest market price and did not make a profit.","Meanwhile, Stream in the Cloud felt that she had gotten a great deal.","Upon seeing Stream in the Cloud’s broad grin, Lin Yuan could not help but say, “Is the special treatment the reason why you’re so fat?”","Since it was almost New Year’s, it was inevitable that Stream in the Cloud had gained weight.","The smile on her face was immediately replaced with a look of outrage.","She was literally hopping with anger.","Stream in the Cloud suddenly resented Lin Yuan as much as the fellow that had taught her a cheating method online, causing her to come in last in class for the exam.","I should let the Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider take a bite out of Lin Yuan. Then, I’ll instruct him to drink some hot water with Indigo Load Root and clean the wound thoroughly. Finally, I’ll find a nice shady tree for him to lay under to prevent his corpse from turning pungent. If I have enough money, I’ll lay a cooling mat under him!"]},{"number":562,"title":"Chapter 562 - Change, Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls","paragraphs":["Stream in the Cloud scoffed softly.","“Deep Mountain Elder Lin, a big spider might pay you a surprise visit!”","She proceeded to skip out of the Star Web store.","Lin Yuan scratched the back of his head and wondered if the new hair on Stream in the Cloud’s head turned her dumb.","Why was her reaction so exceptionally slow?","As he watched Stream in the Cloud skip away, he was about to remind her about something, but he was too late.","When Stream in the Cloud stepped over the threshold of the door, she tripped, and her bumblebee hat fell to the ground.","Lin Yuan had never seen such a sight before.","...","It was already well into the night. Lin Yuan left Star Web and went into his Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He switched out the jade-textured wood that had matured while he was in the coma.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to nurture the Flower Brocade Pearls that had completely changed under the influence of the concentrated spirit qi, he realized that one of the green and pink Flower Brocade Pearls had turned completely gold.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’ True Data to check and discovered that this fey was no longer called the Flower Brocade Pearls.","Instead, it was called the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls.","[Fey Name]: Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls","[Fey Species]: Crassulaceae genus/Cyperus-type","[Spirit-Lifeform Grade]: Bronze (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Elite","Abilities:","[Copious Juices]: Increase the juice stored in the leaves and congeal it into protein when properly nourished.","[Wrap Leaves]: When the leaves are matured, a layer of wood protein will form on the exterior, which will store all the energy from inside the leaves.","Exclusive Skill:","[Lively Plant Pearls]: After training, the plant pearls will form new plant pearls if they are sufficiently nourished. When nutrients are depleted, the new pearls will provide the main pearl with some nourishment. However, if the new pearls grow newer Lively Plant Pearls, they will separate from the main body to form an independent plant pearl.","After Lin Yuan saw the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls’ True Data, it immediately dawned on him that the Flower Brocade Pearls must have transformed in an unexpected way under the influence of the concentrated spirit qi.","When Lin Yuan saw the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls’s exclusive skill, Lively Plant Pearls, a spark of possibility burst into existence in his mind.","With these Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls, can I grow the Lively Plant Pearls on a large scale, just like the veteran faction’s Aquarium of Bliss?","Judging from the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls’ abilities, it was clear that they were much more effective than the Flower Brocade Pearls.","The ability Copious Juices allowed the juices stored in each leaf of the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls to exceed what the Flower Brocade Pearls could accomplish.","The ability Wrap Leaves solved the Flower Brocade Pearls’ issue of naturally decaying after the Flower Brocade Pearls’ leaves matured.","Lin Yuan was sure that the appearance of the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls would drive a Creation Master crazy.","Regardless of how much stronger the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls were as compared to the Flower Brocade Pearls, a real Creation Master still needed to experiment on them to be sure.","As Lin Yuan clutched the brilliant Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls, he had a feeling that he was about to be gifted an enormous amount of wealth.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls could also be used as landmark goods.","With these Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls, Lin Yuan could not utilize the space inside the Spirit Lock spatial zone more efficiently.","He no longer needed to use the space inside the Spirit Lock spatial zone to nurture Flower Brocade Pearls.","After organizing the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan checked on the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","Lin Yuan found that the Blood Brew Grapevine looked completely different from before he was in a coma.","Previously, all the leaves of the old vines of the Blood Brew Grapevine had fallen.","The new leaves had grown and risen rapidly. Many of the new grapevines had sagged to the ground due to the limited space on the supporting structure.","Lin Yuan hastily grabbed a few strong pine logs and nailed them together to create a giant supporting structure.","He took a larger jade basin and filled it with Revival Soil that had been dampened with Grasswood Fountain Water.","Lin Yuan attached the supporting structure to the large basin and carefully re-potted the Blood Brew Grapevine.","The Blood Brew Grapevine was greedy indeed. It had not grown any Blood Brew Grapes even after absorbing a large number of Eyes of Relinquish. Instead, it had decided to release all the growth potential it had been suppressing.","In the past, all of the Blood Brew Grapevine’s owners had not wanted to waste the essence blood of feys and only allowed it to keep one main vine, which it could use to produce Blood Brew Grapes.","Each new vine that the Blood Brew Grapevine grew would be promptly cut off.","The Blood Brew Grapevine in front of Lin Yuan now had already started to expand itself after being nurtured with Eyes of Relinquish.","Its lively and lush appearance was the true form of the Blood Brew Grapevine.","Lin Yuan shrugged at the Blood Brew Grapevine’s greed.","No matter how greedy the Blood Brew Grapevine was, it was just a tool that produced Blood Brew Grapes for the Mother of Bloodbath.","As long as he had Red Thorn and the Eyes of Relinquish, Lin Yuan did not need to put effort into nurturing the Blood Brew Grapevine.","The fully formed Blood Brew Grapevine could bring Lin Yuan an even better harvest at once.","It was not like when it existed as one main vine. During that time, the Blood Brew Grapevine would need to enter a slow recovery period after each newly grown vine was cut.","It was difficult to re-pot the Blood Brew Grapevine.","Lin Yuan needed to stay alert lest he damaged one of the Blood Brew Grapevine’s young and vulnerable roots.","After he was done, Lin Yuan snuggled up with Genius and fell into a deep slumber.","...","Meanwhile, at the inner palace of the Radiant Moon Palace, Cold Moon and Mystic Moon were next to the Moon Empress.","The Moon Empress was gently pruning a Diamond Fragrant Peony.","With each movement of the Moon Empress’ fingers, the branches of the Fragrant Peony snapped off.","The Moon Empress glanced at the rippling pond water and casually stuck one of the Fragrant Peony’s branches into the pond.","“Eight Pages of Tower Canon, the Battlefield Division’s Seventh Page War, as well as its war machine of an Ashes Team, actually dared to secretly move to Radiance. Hehe, it looks like the Seventh Page War from a decade ago still hasn’t learned its lesson.”","As the Moon Empress spoke, she looked at the small rabbit that was using its long ears to rub the carrot in its paws.","“Zixi, summon your corporeal body that’s outside.”","Mystic Moon and Cold Moon shared a look. They could see the grimness and joy in each other’s eyes.","It looks like Young Lord is in trouble. Thanks to this, the Moon Empress, who has not raised her sword in over ten years, is finally going to take this opponent seriously."]},{"number":563,"title":"Chapter 563 - Have to Live","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","It was well into the night, and frigid rolling waves crashed against a decayed wooden plank on the shore.","The grunts of sea creatures could be heard in the surroundings.","Despite the darkness of night, the starlight gently illuminated the silhouette of an enormous sea creature underwater.","The silver fish had a tail, which was tens of centimeters long, and wagged it at the front of the wooden plank. A thin thread connected the wooden plank to the tail as the fish towed the wooden plank forward.","The aura emanated from the silver fish slightly terrified the hibernating deep-sea creatures.","There were jagged cracks all around the silver fish’s body, as though it was about to shatter at any moment.","Despite the silver fish’s impressive aura, its lifeforce was incredibly weak.","An old man sat on the wooden plank. Half of his body was already gone. He sighed as he looked at the short-haired woman next to him. Her face was as white as a sheet, and she was sweating cold sweat.","Worry, sorrow, and subtle despair were interlaced within the sigh.","The short-haired woman had her head in her hands as she curled up into a ball. Her body was quivering violently.","In a flash, she seemed to recover.","She resembled a fallen leaf in the blizzard, thin and flimsy.","The old man used the remaining half of his body to lift a dead fish from the wooden plank and handed it to the short-haired woman.","“Yiren, your sacred source lifeform is on the cusp of death. You will continue to experience the painful spasms that come from your damaged soul until the Absolute Love Poppy recovers.”","The short-haired woman’s hands were tightly clasped together. She was already aware of this injury. Using a marrow contract to allow a sacred source lifeform to combine with one’s soul was the equivalent of sharing a soul with the sacred source lifeform’s body.","Her Absolute Love Poppy was only left with half a rhizome and one cluster of roots. It was nearly impossible for it to recover.","“It’s too bad that all my feys are linked to the Absolute Love Poppy. Now that the Absolute Love Poppy is almost dead, the rest of my feys have all fallen asleep,” muttered the short-haired woman.","The short-haired woman gnashed her teeth and hissed. “I never expected that Seventh Page War wasn’t a human. Otherwise—”","The short-haired woman once again cradled her head between her hands and started trembling vigorously before she could finish speaking.","It was clear that she was feeling the pain of her damaged soul again.","The old man gazed at the anguished short-haired woman with hatred. He mustered his strength and used the hand that remained to forcefully hit the short-haired woman’s head.","“Yiren, you are the Dark Envoy chosen by the Seven States of Darkness. You are the Dark Envoy Lordess of the Seven States of Darkness. You are capable of more than revenge. At the very least, you need to live!” bellowed the old man.","A second later, the short-haired woman stopped trembling, but she continued to hang her head.","Hot tears cascaded down the short-haired woman’s cheeks and landed on her already soaked spirit qi clothes.","Under the night sky, the bitter tears fell and mixed with the even more bitter sea.","Su Yiren blamed herself immensely.","If I hadn’t been so confident of my Absolute Love Poppy’s abilities and used my title as Dark Envoy to order Elder He to ambush Seventh Page War with me, Elder He would not be in this sorry state now.","Elder He was a god-class expert and possessed a Creation Breed fey. Even if his body was destroyed, he would be able to fully recover if he received treatment.","However, Seventh Page War had killed Elder He’s Nether Sea Jellyfish.","Elder He’s Shuttle Arrow Shark had also been shattered when it forced itself through the cage surrounding the Radiance War Chariot.","Elder He had paid by burning his soul, and the Shuttle Arrow Shark led the two of them forward in the deep sea full of powerful creatures.","Su Yiren knew in her heart that Elder He was allowing his life to burn up so he could accompany her as her life reached its end.","The inevitable goodbye sliced as deeply and painfully as a knife.","Elder He regretted hitting Su Yiren.","However, he felt that he needed to say what had to be said.","He sighed, inhaled deeply, and said in a low voice, “Yiren, look up at me.”","Su Yiren slowly lifted her head to meet the dilapidated sight that was Elder He.","Su Yiren’s lips were tightly pressed together, and fresh blood dripped down the side of her mouth. It rolled down her chin and landed on the wooden plank.","Elder He was about to speak, but the waves suddenly grew larger.","The Shuttle Arrow Shark, which was towing the wooden plank, suddenly slowed down. Although it was in the sea, it seemed as though it was stuck in mud as it could only inch forward.","“Damn, the Shuttle Arrow Shark has been targeted by a wild Creation Breed fey in the sea.”","A fountain of spirit qi burst forth from Elder He. His god-class expert power suddenly gripped the tumultuous sea, and the water pulsed.","All the organisms in the sea escaped to its depths.","During the explosion of Elder He’s god-class expert power, the cracked Shuttle Arrow Shark’s body was suddenly alight with silver spatial energy.","The spatial energy on the Shuttle Arrow Shark’s body formed an intricate map of spatial etchings.","The spatial etchings swirled around the Shuttle Arrow Shark’s body before being transferred to the sea. They formed strips of solid spatial conveyor belts.","As Su Yiren watched this scene unfold, tears flowed down Su Yiren’s face and mixed with the bloodied water below her.","Su Yiren had witnessed such a sight numerous times when the Dark Federation was being attacked by Seventh Page War’s 32 Chanter team.","Elder He’s expression was exceptionally solemn as he instructed Su Yiren, “We’re near the Divine Wood Federation. The distance can be covered by one of the Shuttle Arrow Shark’s conveyor belts. I’ll send you there. Dark Envoy Lordess, you have to live. Yiren, you have to live.”","Elder He did not say much more.","The last two statements were a blessing, and those words came directly from Elder He’s heart.","Living was the basis of everything.","Regardless of Su Yiren’s title as a Dark Envoy, or because he had watched over her as she grew up, it was all Elder He’s final hopes for her.","A steady flow of tears was streaming from Su Yiren’s eyes.","Before Su Yiren could react, the silver river of a conveyor belt had completely enveloped Su Yiren.","Su Yiren was soon swept away by the silver river and disappeared over the horizon.","The silver light had not even disappeared when crimson tentacles had already reached upward from the sea’s depths.","The tentacles curled over the dimly lit Shuttle Arrow Shark and pulled it down into the deep sea, dragging Elder He down with it."]},{"number":564,"title":"Chapter 564 - Continuous Messages","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan had already woken up and gotten dressed.","It was New Year’s, and Lin Yuan put on spirit qi clothes with red accessories that he rarely wore.","Occasionally, Lin Yuan wore brightly colored clothes. They made him look younger.","Genius, which was in Lin Yuan’s arms, was still rolling around lazily. When Lin Yuan dressed Genius in a red armor set that Wen Yu had made, Genius immediately perked up. It wagged its three tails and said in a child-like voice, “Yuan, do I look good in these clothes?”","Lin Yuan reached out his hand and affectionately pinched Genius’ small nose.","“You little brat. You’ve already asked this question ten times. Of course, you look good!”","The idea to make this armor had sparked in Wen Yu’s mind out of nowhere. It suited Genius well.","Since Wen Yu had never seen Genius wearing any clothes, she gave the red armor to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had decided to dress Genius in it on a whim. It was only then that he realized how much Genius liked wearing such clothes.","Genius reveled in Lin Yuan’s praise.","Although it had already heard Lin Yuan’s reply more than ten times, Genius was still waving its tail around just as happily.","Lin Yuan smiled and asked, “How about I ask Wen Yu to make more clothes for you?”","Genius jumped into Lin Yuan’s arms in delight.","Lin Yuan stoked Genius’ head and thought to himself about how sensible Genius still was.","However, the Lin Yuan of today was different from the Lin Yuan, who used to struggle to make a living in the Xia Region.","“Genius, let me know what you like from now on. We can afford many things now,” said Lin Yuan to Genius seriously.","Lin Yuan heard knocking on the door of the loft and opened it to see Cai Cha standing there.","Cai Cha bowed to Lin Yuan and said, “Young Lord, the Moon Empress is calling on you to dine in the inner palace. Xicha went to call the Little Cold Moon Envoy.”","It took a moment for Lin Yuan to respond to the words ‘Little Cold Moon Envoy’, but he soon realized Cai Cha was referring to Chu Ci.","Lin Yuan nodded and replied, “Let’s go to the inner palace together.”","Lin Yuan could not help but think, Now that I have the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls, the space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone that I was using to nurture the Flower Brocade Pearls is now empty. What should I do with the empty space?","Every inch of the Spirit Lock spatial zone was intended for Lin Yuan to store and accumulate resources.","Hence, Lin Yuan needed to carefully think about what was the best way to use the Spirit Lock spatial zone. It was imperative that he did not make rash decisions.","When they arrived at the entrance of the inner palace, Cai Cha bowed and said, “Young Lord, the Moon Empress personally woke up at the crack of dawn to cook today’s breakfast.”","Lin Yuan suddenly thought that he should make something for his Master during New Year’s.","Once they were done eating, Lin Yuan said to the Moon Empress before he left, “Master, you don’t need to cook during New Year’s. I’ll prepare the food in the afternoon.”","Initially, the Moon Empress thought that Lin Yuan wanted to take something from Leaning Moon Mountain. She was about to tell him that the Radiant Moon Palace had everything and that he did not need to prepare anything when she heard the rest of what he had to say.","A warm smile blossomed on the Moon Empress’ face.","She gazed at Lin Yuan with adoration and said, “Okay.”","Liu Jie was decently confident in his cooking skills. Although he was not as skilled as Liu Jie, Lin Yuan had eaten his own food before and found it acceptable.","It was just that after Lin Yuan met Liu Jie, he no longer had the opportunity to cook.","Lin Yuan contacted Ostrich Logistics on the way back to the mansion. He tasked them to give away the elemental pearls from last night’s group welfare auction and the private trades’ ones.","Once he was done liaising with Ostrich Logistics, Lin Yuan could tell that Chu Ci was very nervous.","Instead of saying something, Lin Yuan only raised an eyebrow.","They were about to arrive at the Return from Faraway Mansion that was on the outskirts of the Royal Capital.","The people who were anxious to see Chu Ci had to be far more nervous than her.","Lin Yuan saw Wen Yu and another young girl with purplish-red hair at the mansion entrance.","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan, she exclaimed, “Young Master.”","The purplish-red-haired girl waved at Lin Yuan and yelled, “Mister Deep Mountain Elder Lin, I’m back to being your dedicated courier again!”","Lin Yuan knew that Ah Neng had been busy participating in the Guild Alliance’s S Tournament.","“Ah Neng, how did you do at the S Tournament?” asked Lin Yuan.","Ah Neng’s eyes shone as she replied, “I ended many people’s misery with a rain of bullets. I’m just a substitute this year, so I don’t need to enter the competition anymore. But, I’ll be able to be in the main team in next year’s S Tournament!”","Ah Neng started waving her fists around as though she was cheering herself on.","Lin Yuan laughed and cheered Ah Neng on.","Ah Neng had not been a courier for some time.","The current Ah Neng was no longer the same as the careless child she used to be.","After Ah Neng left, Lin Yuan saw that Chu Ci and Wen Yu had linked arms.","Chu Ci had just been acquainted with Wen Yu in the video call, but they were already so close despite having only just met.","Was this why they said that women only needed one second to become friends with each other?","Wen Yu could finally lay her worries to rest after she saw Lin Yuan.","During Lin Yuan’s absence, Wen Yu had been tending to every aspect of the mansion, especially when Liu Jie and Zhou Luo had been in a coma.","Nothing special had taken place in the mansion during this time.","The Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce’s old rival, the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce, had started trying to overcome the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce. Thus, Listen needed to constantly handle this issue.","Only a few surprise guests had turned up at the mansion recently.","“Young Master, the main descendant of Wind Mist City’s Gao family, Gao Feng came looking for you a week ago. You were still in a coma, and I told him that you had left the mansion on business. Every few days, the phone that you gave to the Mother of Bloodbath would ring with messages from Gao Feng. He must have some urgent matter to see you about.”","Lin Yuan cocked an eyebrow.","Gao Feng sure is anxious to see me. I wonder what urgent matter he has to see me about.","Coincidentally, Lin Yuan also intended to ask Gao Feng for help after New Year’s.","He wanted to obtain some Angelfish of Bliss through Gao Feng."]},{"number":565,"title":"Chapter 565 - Friends Reunite","paragraphs":["This was the best season to cultivate Angelfish of Bliss because they grew up quickly in cold environments.","Once they were full-grown fishes, Angelfish of Bliss would increase the rate at which they shed their fish coats when they were in warm weather.","If he nurtured the Angelfish of Bliss now till they matured, they would start shedding a layer of fish coat after a set period when the weather turned warm.","Initially, Lin Yuan planned to approach Gao Feng after New Year’s.","Lin Yuan did not want to disturb Gao Feng during the holiday for fear of causing Gao Feng to be too preoccupied with procuring Angelfish of Bliss for him.","Now that Gao Feng was looking for Lin Yuan, the latter would be able to broach his request with Gao Feng before New Year’s.","The Angelfish of Bliss were less than a finger long. Even fully matured, they were only about the size of a palm.","The man-made lake was already extremely large, and the size would increase by at least twice once it was expanded.","Thus, Lin Yuan would gladly take however many Angelfish of Bliss that Gao Feng could get his hands on.","When the rainbow-scaled Angelfish of Bliss swam around together, they formed an exquisitely lovely picture of movement.","Lin Yuan nodded in acknowledgment and said to Wen Yu, “I’ll give Gao Feng a call later to ask him what he needs.”","While Lin Yuan was speaking, he heard Liu Jie’s voice from behind him.","“Young Master, it’s great that you’re fine!”","After the close shave with death they experienced together in the dimensional rift, Liu Jie had used his body to carry out his service to the shield on his crest by blocking Lin Yuan from the deadly blow.","Because of this, Liu Jie’s consciousness had slipped into a daze.","However, there had still been enemies in the dimensional rift at that time, and Liu Jie was well aware of how perilous the situation had been.","Liu Jie had not been worried ever since he saw Lin Yuan during his internship. But now, he could truly relax after seeing Lin Yuan with his own eyes.","Lin Yuan saw Liu Jie carrying many rare spirit ingredients.","Most of the spiritual ingredients he was carrying were sea-type feys.","Liu Jie had asked Lin Yuan in advance what Chu Ci liked to eat and had gotten an idea of her tastes.","The mansion’s occupants did not always eat fish, and it was clear that Liu Jie had bought so much for the sake of Chu Ci.","Lin Yuan was still rather worried about the state of Liu Jie’s Insect Queen.","“Big Brother Liu, you mentioned that there’s a problem with your Insect Queen’s transformation. How is it now?” asked Lin Yuan.","At the mention of the Insect Queen, Liu Jie thought back to the issues that had persisted from yesterday afternoon to morning today. It seemed like a dream to him.","However, during this dream-like period, Liu Jie had watched as the transformation was completed.","“The Insect Queen is done transforming. It’s now much stronger.”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow.","Liu Jie was not a boastful person. In fact, he was exceptionally humble and down to earth.","If Liu Jie said that the Insect Queen was now much stronger, it meant that the Insect Queen’s powers had increased tremendously.","Liu Jie was elated for Liu Jie.","“Congratulations, Big Brother Liu.”","When Liu Jie heard Lin Yuan’s congratulations, his heart felt heavy yet relaxed.","Before falling into a coma, Liu Jie understood the injuries that he and the Insect Queen had sustained.","There was only one way that he could have survived those injuries—Lin Yuan must have done emergency treatment on him.","Hence, when Liu Jie had woken up and found out that Lin Yuan was in a coma, he blamed himself immensely. He felt that Lin Yuan had wasted too much spiritual power trying to heal him, which was why Lin Yuan had suffered such severe injuries and had been comatose for a week.","Now that Lin Yuan was right there before him, Liu Jie felt the knot in his heart loosen.","Liu Jie thought to himself that he was finally worthy of being the strongest shield for Lin Yuan on his journey to the top.","Lin Yuan’s sharp eyes caught sight of the change in Liu Jie’s gaze. It was obvious that Liu Jie was now much more confident.","Liu Jie looked toward Wen Yu and Chu Ci, whose arms were linked.","“Miss, you...”","Before Liu Jie could finish, Chu Ci had already stretched out her hand to him.","“Big Brother Liu, I’ve heard my brother talk about you. You know my name is Chu Ci.”","Chu Ci even winked at Liu Jie.","Liu Jie took Chu Ci’s outstretched hand, and his large hand shook her smaller one.","“Chu Ci, I bought some Shiny Star Groupers and Fire Tail Snow Sea Bass. I remember Lin Yuan saying that you don’t like eating spicy food. I’ll cook some sweet and sour fish, as well as honeyed steam fish for you.”","Chu Ci, who had grown up alongside Lin Yuan, was exceptionally sensitive. She was skilled at sensing the emotions of others.","She had initially been nervous about meeting all the new people.","However, she could tell from Wen Yu and Liu Jie’s attitudes that they were brimming with kindness.","They gazed at her with an affection that only older siblings had for their younger sister.","Chu Ci felt a surge of warmth from the sudden influx of people who cared about her.","There was a hint of astringence.","Chu Ci used to be unaware of what kept Lin Yuan so busy. Whenever they spoke on the phone, Lin Yuan would always ask about how she was.","Lin Yuan was not a talkative person.","However, whenever they were about to hang up, he would remind her to take care of her health and some other advice.","Lin Yuan had never said that it was hard for him, but having seen all this, Chu Ci could imagine how hard Lin Yuan had been working all this time.","At that moment, the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Hu Quan walked out of the mansion. They must have heard the discourse at the entranceway.","Endless Summer walked up to Lin Yuan and placed its hand on his shoulder to sense his condition.","Once it assured itself that he was fine, it moved on to Chu Ci and handed her a purple flower-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","After Chu Ci received the fey storage box, Endless Summer said, “My cherished accessories and clothes are inside. Feel free to wear any of them if they’re to your liking.”","When Lin Yuan heard what Endless Summer said, he hastily snatched the Diamond fey storage box out of Chu Ci’s hands and returned it to Endless Summer.","“You should keep these treasures for yourself, Endless Summer. Don’t give them to Chu Ci,” said Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan remembered that Endless Summer had gone through an unconventional style and rural heavy metal phase.","Endless Summer had bought the most accessories and spirit qi clothes.","Chu Ci had not come of age, and her style had yet to be decided.","What if she was influenced by the things that Endless Summer gave her?","From behind Endless Summer, the Mother of Bloodbath noticed the glint in Lin Yuan’s red eyes.","The Mother of Bloodbath had many things to say to Lin Yuan, but once it remembered what Mystic Moon and Moon Empress had said, as well as how it had failed as a Path Protector, the Mother of Bloodbath suddenly found it difficult to talk to Lin Yuan."]},{"number":566,"title":"Chapter 566 - A Beautiful Misunderstanding and Liu Jie’s Sacred Source Lifeform","paragraphs":["Hu Quan touched his balding head and said, “Let’s go in! How much longer do you want to stand these bracing winter winds? When we go in, Chu Ci can see if she’s satisfied with the feature wall I rushed to finish long ago.”","The Mother of Bloodbath turned and walked into the house. It realized that Lin Yuan had quickened his pace and was now walking alongside it.","Lin Yuan pulled a Gold fey storage box out of the amber-button-shaped Diamond fey storage box and gave it to the Mother of Bloodbath.","Lin Yuan’s bright expression stunned the Mother of Bloodbath.","After it received the Gold fey storage box, Lin Yuan said, “The three Red Water Blood Snakes have all evolved. There are numerous old leaves that had fallen from the Blood Brew Grapevine inside. You can check to see how much blood energy you’re able to absorb from them.”","The Mother of Bloodbath had been wanting to speak to Lin Yuan, but it did not know how to start the conversation.","Now that Lin Yuan was talking to it, a troubled expression appeared on the Mother of Bloodbath’s face.","Its troubled expression was a combination of guilt, happiness, and relief.","However, when the Mother of Bloodbath looked inside the Gold fey storage box that Lin Yuan gave it, it only felt touched and shocked.","The Mother of Bloodbath saw that the three Red Water Blood Snakes had evolved to Bronze/Legend.","The incredible amount of blood energy in the Blood Brew Grapevine’s leaves made the Mother of Bloodbath feel ravenous.","This ravenous state was due to the Blood Law Rune in the Mother of Bloodbath’s body and the fact that it was a blood-type fey. Its body was automatically sending out signals in response to the pure blood energy.","This demonstrated how much the Mother of Bloodbath craved for pure blood energy.","The Mother of Bloodbath had seen the Blood Brew Grapevine in the Indigo Azure Sea Market.","However, all of the Blood Brew Grapevine’s Blood Brew Grapes had just been harvested at that time, and it had been in a weak state.","At that time, the entire Blood Brew Grapevine had a similar amount of blood energy in it as the leaves in front of the Mother of Bloodbath now.","Who knew how the Blood Brew Grapevine was nurtured?","The Mother of Bloodbath could not help but form a misunderstanding.","The Mother of Bloodbath thought about how Lin Yuan had asked the Mother of Bloodbath to help strengthen the three Red Water Blood Snakes and the Blood Brew Grapevine shortly after he had woken up from the coma.","The Mother of Bloodbath knew that only a Class 5 Creation Master like the Moon Empress could evolve all three Red Water Blood Snakes to Bronze/Legend in one night.","The Mother of Bloodbath’s hand tightly clutched the Gold fey storage box.","It solidified its resolve to become even stronger.","The Mother of Bloodbath’s troubled emotions disappeared. It only felt the determination and alertness that a Path Protector should feel.","Lin Yuan did not know what the Mother of Bloodbath was thinking. Even if he did know, he would not be able to explain it.","When he was refining his Creation Master skills and nurturing feys, the Mother of Bloodbath would also leave him alone. Even though it was his Path Protector, it did not want to disturb Lin Yuan during that time.","Thus, the Mother of Bloodbath did not know what Lin Yuan was capable of.","Lin Yuan could not expose his powers to the Mother of Bloodbath.","This was all a beautiful misunderstanding.","Once they arrived at the mansion, Chu Ci’s eyes were immediately drawn to the detailed feature wall.","It depicted her standing next to Lin Yuan.","The feature wall’s background showed a blue sky and lush green grass. Under the jade-tinted light, the mansion’s furniture seemed incredibly heartwarming.","Chu Ci remembered Hu Quan saying that the feature wall had been finished in a rush early on.","It turned out that long before she met these people face-to-face, she had already assimilated into their lives through this.","Although this was the first time they had met, it was nice that there had not been an absent feeling.","Liu Jie changed and dashed toward the kitchen to start cooking lunch.","Lin Yuan wanted to prepare a meal for his Master during New Year’s, so he followed Liu Jie to the kitchen with the hopes of learning the ropes. He wanted to try and see if he could pull off a miracle and learn a few of Liu Jie’s techniques within two days.","Wen Yu, the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Chu Ci became friends and played the Fey Battle Flag game.","Lin Yuan did not know when the four women started to resemble the same person. They even took a page out of Liu Jie and Listen’s book and made a bet. The loser would have to eat a piece of lemon.","Hu Quan stood at the kitchen entrance and yelled, “Lin Yuan, I called Listen, and Zhou Luo like you asked. I told them to come for lunch.”","Hu Quan had not gone to Indigo Azure City. He had stayed in the mansion like the ultimate introvert and worked on his crafts in the dead of night.","Hence, Hu Quan was not fully certain of what had happened to Lin Yuan.","Although he did not know when Lin Yuan had started treating Zhou Luo and one of their own, he had managed to glean some details from listening to Liu Jie and Wen Yu’s conversation.","From these details, Hu Quan had fully accepted Zhou Luo as well.","Liu Jie held the ladle and was frying up the sliced cuttlefish.","While the sliced cuttlefish were tossed around in the pan, they curled and formed a pretty flower shape. Each piece glistened with oil.","Lin Yuan’s stomach started to rumble as he smelled the fragrance from the pot.","Liu Jie told Lin Yuan about the Insect Queen’s condition, and he suddenly thought about what Night Leaning Moon had told him.","Never tell anyone about your sacred source lifeform.","Liu Jie had already told Lin Yuan that he had taken Night Leaning Moon as his Master. He had also been open with Lin Yuan about the fact that he had contracted a sacred source lifeform.","However, Liu Jie was watchful of his words and did not tell Lin Yuan about his sacred source lifeform’s abilities.","It was not that Liu Jie did not want to tell Lin Yuan or because he was afraid of Lin Yuan knowing about his sacred source lifeform’s abilities. It was just that Liu Jie’s sacred source lifeform had a rather special ability.","He was afraid that Lin Yuan would forbid him from using the sacred source lifeform’s ability for his own good after Lin Yuan found out about his sacred source lifeform’s ability.","As such, Liu Jie decided to keep his sacred source lifeform’s ability to himself. He would only reveal it in Lin Yuan’s hour of need. Then, he would become Lin Yuan’s magnificent shield and sword.","He would be the epitome of defense.","Although Liu Jie did not usually use the sacred source lifeform’s ability, the sacred source lifeform was a type of fey that could share an existence. It was already sharing the Insect Queen’s existence.","After the Insect Queen’s transformation, it gained the ability to coexist with the sacred source lifeform.","It had metamorphosed and was now living a whole different life."]},{"number":567,"title":"Chapter 567 - Gao Feng’s Plan","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan listened to Liu Jie as he recounted his fateful encounter and experiences when Lin Yuan was unconscious.","Lin Yuan used his hand to pat Liu Jie’s shoulder repeatedly to express his congratulations.","Now that Liu Jie contracted a sacred source lifeform, Lin Yuan could reserve his sacred source lifeform for the Mother of Bloodbath.","After the meal, Lin Yuan looked for Zhou Luo to discuss some matters.","As soon as Lin Yuan returned to the manor, the Mother of Bloodbath had already returned his mobile phone, and it suddenly rang now.","Lin Yuan lowered his head and realized that the phone call was from none other than Gao Feng.","Lin Yuan raised his brows and picked up the phone call.","Gao Feng went straight to the topic and said, “Brother, I wish to discuss a deal with you.”","Lin Yuan was rather startled to hear Gao Feng’s tone.","Gao Feng was normally very forthright when speaking and would give off the feeling of an abnormally carefree youth. But now, Gao Feng was speaking in an abnormally solemn tone.","Lin Yuan knew that Gao Feng had a very important matter to discuss with him.","However, since Gao Feng said he wanted to have a serious business talk, Lin Yuan turned serious and asked, “Gao Feng, are you representing the Gao family to negotiate with me or are you negotiating with me personally?”","Gao Feng turned silent for a moment after hearing Lin Yuan’s question. Gao Feng then asked in a serious tone, “Is there a difference if it is the Gao family or me?”","Lin Yuan immediately answered, “If it is the Gao family negotiating business with me, I can naturally refuse and think of the best method to get the most profit.","“But if you are personally negotiating with me, if I can do it, I will agree to it as a favor for a friend.”","When Gao Feng heard Lin Yuan’s words, he felt a surge of warmth.","“Brother, I am personally doing business with you. But this favor might be a little hard. If you think that it is too much effort, then you can just reject me.”","During this period, Gao Feng had sought out help from many others apart from Lin Yuan. He had basically used up all of his connections. However, he hadn’t been able to obtain any practical help.","When Lin Yuan heard Gao Feng’s words, he could roughly guess what kind of favor Gao Feng wanted.","Gao Feng had been making transactions of completely jade-textured wood and high-quality Bronze feys. Therefore, these two things were excluded, but it should be related to what Creation Masters could do.","As expected, Gao Feng continued saying, “Brother, I wonder if you have any Creation Master resources you can lend me? You can just name your price!”","Lin Yuan immediately knew he had guessed it correctly. However, Lin Yuan’s guesses were still a little deviated. Gao Feng didn’t just want a specific thing; he wanted Creation Master resources.","Lin Yuan was entirely different from regular Creation Masters.","Lin Yuan’s current weakness was that he couldn’t enhance any high-grade fey. Therefore, in terms of nurturing high-grade feys, Lin Yuan couldn’t do anything as long as he didn’t advance his spirit qi professional rank.","The enhancement of high-grade feys was Lin Yuan’s most obvious shortcoming.","Lin Yuan might have plenty of superior items that only high-class Creation Masters could produce, but Lin Yuan didn’t have any Creation Master resources.","Previously, Lin Yuan had been taking the burden of the Creation Master’s job for the entire Sky City. Now that Gao Feng wanted to borrow Creation Master resources, Lin Yuan couldn’t possibly pack himself up and mail himself to Gao Feng, right? He also couldn’t just introduce his Master, the Moon Empress, to Gao Feng, right?","Even if he were to introduce the Moon Empress, Gao Feng wouldn’t dare to invite her.","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan had a thought that he had to recruit Creation Masters. However, Lin Yuan would have his own requirements when recruiting a Creation Master... They had to be high-class Creation Masters.","Only high-class Creation Masters could compensate for Lin Yuan’s lacking Creation Master ability.","Creation Masters were the most precious spirit qi professionals in the entire Radiance Federation. Lin Yuan would need to do a lot of planning in order to recruit a high-class Creation Master.","Even though Lin Yuan couldn’t immediately give Creation Master resources to Gao Feng, he still asked, “What kind of Creation Master resources do you need?”","Gao Feng explained as though he was complaining about something to a friend, “Brother, did you not hear about the difference between this active period of the dimensional rifts and the past?”","Lin Yuan replied upon hearing that, “I am not very clear of the things that happened during this period.”","Gao Feng felt it was a little weird that Lin Yuan didn’t even know these things. Even if Lin Yuan had not been at the seaside of the Royal Capital, he should have witnessed the incident that most factions were speechless and complaining about, right?","“This year’s active period opened up several times more dimensional rifts than before. Among them, the water world dimensional rifts are the largest in number at the sea regions.","“When the dimensional rift’s source-type items are extracted, it will release a large amount of spirit qi before closing.","“For feys on land, the massive release of spirit qi is a great thing.","“However, it isn’t entirely good for the feys in the sea region.","“Brother, I was actually able to find the infant-stage Elemental Shellfish that you wanted previously. But now, even if my grandfather makes a move, it is impossible to get any.","“The massive spirit qi released by the water world dimensional rifts evolved all of the deep-sea Elemental Shellfish into the damned Explosive Pearl Shellfish.”","Lin Yuan couldn’t help getting dumbfounded. He suddenly understood why during the group welfare auction, be it Master Duan Li or Wang Fuxiang, they had avoided choosing the water-elemental heavenly-maiden-grade pearls.","The concentrated spirit qi in the sea had evolved most of the Elemental Shellfish into Explosive Pearl Shellfish.","As a result, it would be a long time before anyone could find any infant-stage Elemental Shellfish from the deep sea.","Most of the factions nurtured Elemental Shellfish in order to nurture foundation-class resources like the Island Whale.","Therefore, the Aquamarine Elemental Shellfish were the most common Elemental Shellfish.","Even though the water-elemental pearls had the highest consumption rate among all the elemental pearls, this was the time when supply and demand came in.","The water-elemental pearls were now the cheapest among all the elemental pearls.","However, this was actually great news for Lin Yuan as he had a limited number of water-elemental pearls.","Lin Yuan had used most of the water-elemental pearls to nurture the Floating Island Whale, while the rest of the elemental pearls would have increasing values.","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard Gao Feng saying, “I have discussed with my grandfather and wish to create my own rising faction.","“Therefore, I am planning to construct a marine fey breeding base.","“Brother, I don’t wish to hide it from you. I am looking to borrow Creation Master resources because I hope that the Creation Master on your side can help me to nurture some Spotted Coral Jade.”"]},{"number":568,"title":"Chapter 568 - Lin Yuan Becoming a Boss","paragraphs":["“The Gao family has been exploiting deep-sea resources.","“Due to massive spirit qi released by the water world dimensional rifts, many of the deep-sea feys are abnormally active.","“This allowed the Gao family to capture plenty of production-type deep-sea feys. The capture of the deep sea feys has made the Gao family’s Creation Masters so busy that they are going crazy.","“However, my marine fey breeding base has just been constructed, and because all the Gao family’s Creation Masters are busy, I am in a situation where I have no Creation Masters to use.”","Gao Feng explained in an abnormally honest manner and didn’t hide anything from Lin Yuan.","When constructing a marine fey breeding base and artificially nurturing those fragile marine feys, a careless mistake might just cause all of them to die.","A single marine fey’s death would mean that Gao Feng’s breeding technique had a problem. It might possibly be accompanied by a large number of deaths among the marine feys, causing Gao Feng losses that he might not be able to compensate for.","The coral jade that Gao Feng required from Creation Masters was turned into jade-textured corals from regular corals.","Once the coral jade was nurtured by the Creation Master’s highly concentrated spirit qi, it would activate the coral polyps that formed the corals and start to develop dense spots inside the coral jade.","If these Spotted Coral Jade were crushed and ground, they could be scattered into the marine fey breeding base pool to create a deep-sea environment.","Once those marine feys ate the crushed Spotted Coral Jade, it would speed up the development of the marine feys and also keep them in a healthy state.","The Spotted Coral Jade also gave a significant boost to the marine feys’ breeding ability.","Gao Feng wanted to use the Spotted Coral Jade to nurture some female breeding feys in his newly constructed marine fey breeding base.","Lin Yuan silently contemplated for a moment and said, “I can help you solve the problem of the Spotted Coral Jade.”","Gao Feng was overjoyed like a blooming flower, but he said softly in a shy tone, “Brother, the quantity of Spotted Coral Jade might be rather large.”","Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone had already spared out a piece of land, and he had been thinking how to use it. Now, it just so happened that he could use it to help Gao Feng to nurture large quantities of Spotted Coral Jade.","Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone might be able to nurture Spotted Coral Jade, but he couldn’t nurture corals into regular coral jade. After all, regular coral jade would need an extremely long period to be produced, even in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The formation of coral jade would only happen after hundreds of thousands of years in the deep sea after the coral absorbed the nutrients from the spirit qi. It was a kind of mineral that could only be produced at the bottom of the sea.","Lin Yuan could buy them if he wanted to, but since the Gao family had been exploiting the deep-sea resources, they should have plenty of regular coral jade.","“As long as you can provide me with regular coral jade, then I can supply you with 300 catties of Spotted Coral Jade every ten days.”","Gao Feng let out a violent cough after hearing Lin Yuan’s reply. His lips shook as he said, “300 catties? Brother, I have plenty of coral jade, but 300 catties of Spotted Coral Jade are simply too much!”","“Even if you can supply them to me, I will not be able to afford them.”","Lin Yuan had a quick thought as he asked, “You’ve personally constructed his marine fey breeding base. Since I can supply you the Creation Master resources that you require, why don’t you think about building a bigger breeding base?”","Gao Feng’s eyes flickered with radiance after hearing Lin Yuan’s question and subtly understood Lin Yuan’s meaning.","He said that he couldn’t afford 300 catties of Spotted Coral Jade, but Lin Yuan still insisted on supplying them to him. It meant that Lin Yuan wished to join as a shareholder in this deal in exchange for the supply of the Creation Master resources.","As for the method of becoming a shareholder, Gao Feng had been very resistant. If someone was to join as a shareholder, it would mean that a portion of the marine fey breeding base would belong to that shareholder.","If Lin Yuan were to express his intention to join as a shareholder when Gao Feng first called Lin Yuan, even if Gao Feng treated Lin Yuan as a friend, Gao Feng wouldn’t hesitate to refuse.","But now, it was different as Gao Feng was at his most difficult time. Lin Yuan didn’t hesitate to provide help to Gao Feng and was willing to invest an unexpectedly huge amount of Creation Master resources. It would allow Gao Feng to establish a rising faction that was far beyond his expectation.","Gao Feng muttered for a long time before making a reluctant decision and gnashed his teeth as he said, “Brother, if you can provide me 300 catties of Spotted Coral Jade every ten days, then you don’t need to bother about the other matters of the marine fey breeding base. We shall split the shares in half.”","Lin Yuan was shocked when Gao Feng said they would be evenly splitting the shares.","Spotted Coral Jade was impossible to form in the deep-sea environment. Even if there was a very high concentration of spirit qi, it still wouldn’t reach the conditions for the coral jade to produce the spots. It could only be nurtured with a high-class Creation Master’s pure spirit qi.","However, the Spotted Coral Jade had very small effects and could only be considered to be a useful spiritual ingredient for marine feys. Only people like Gao Feng, who was preparing to construct a marine fey breeding base, would have such a huge demand for it.","If Lin Yuan could provide 300 catties of Spotted Coral Jade, it was the same as providing Gao Feng with high-class Creation Master resources. But Lin Yuan never expected Gao Feng to value these resources for 50% of shares.","With 50% of shares, Lin Yuan was now suddenly transformed into a boss of a marine fey breeding base like Gao Feng.","Logically speaking, if Gao Feng wanted to establish a rising faction, he wouldn’t possibly want to share any control and authority with others. However, Gao Feng chose to split the shares equally with him.","It was enough to see Gao Feng’s sincerity for this collaboration.","In regards to Gao Feng’s sincerity, Lin Yuan immediately made a response. “Apart from the Spotted Coral Jade, when you are breeding a huge quantity of marine feys, you will probably need pure elemental energy.","“I have plenty of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls. If you need them, you can just request them from me.”","Gao Feng suddenly felt relaxed after hearing the response.","Earlier on, when Gao Feng had decided to give Lin Yuan 50% of the shares, it might be a little impulsive, but now Gao Feng felt he was abnormally at ease to collaborate with Lin Yuan.","There weren’t many rising factions nurturing marine feys, so the competition between these rising factions was very intense.","Especially with the investment of Creation Master resources, it would immediately increase the competitive edge of a rising faction that relied on the breeding of marine feys.","Gao Feng could actually make use of the Gao family’s massive resources in the deep-sea business to establish his rising faction. However, it was apparent that Gao Feng didn’t want to rely on the Gao family for everything. Otherwise, there would be no meaning for him to establish a rising faction himself."]},{"number":569,"title":"Chapter 569 - Happy Delivery","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls were things that Gao Feng was too embarrassed to mention to Lin Yuan.","Gao Feng knew that Lin Yuan should have elemental pearls after obtaining the infant-stage Elemental Shellfish from him previously. However, due to the huge quantity of Elemental Shellfish that evolved into Explosive Pearl Shellfish, elemental pearls were truly too precious.","Gao Feng was planning to see if he could get the Gao family to think of some methods to obtain some. But as soon as Lin Yuan spoke, he was immediately investing resources like the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","It made Gao Feng feel that he had suddenly found a pillar to hug, even though he was from the richest family in Wind Mist City.","This was a kind of feeling that Gao Feng felt for the first time, but he felt it was truly satisfying!","“Brother, if you can supply me with resources like the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, I will be truly grateful to you.","“For each heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl that you supply to me, I will purchase it at the market price.","“However, now that I have given you 50% of the shares, I cannot give you any more. But I can give you 10% of the profits from my shares. What do you think, brother?”","Lin Yuan didn’t reject Gao Feng’s proposal. He was negotiating a deal with Gao Feng; in fact, he was actually collaborating to develop a rising faction together.","Gao Feng was providing the Gao family’s ample resources and business channels in the deep-sea sector, while Lin Yuan was providing Creation Master resources.","Lin Yuan would provide help to Gao Feng, but when discussing business, Lin Yuan would want to obtain the profits that he should have.","From Gao Feng’s words, Lin Yuan could feel that Gao Feng wished to obtain the market leader position in the marine fey breeding base business.","Lin Yuan didn’t have any opinions toward this and was actually very approving of it. In any case, Lin Yuan didn’t have the effort and time to develop the breeding base together with Gao Feng.","To Lin Yuan, the most profitable method was to simply wait for the dividends.","As such, Lin Yuan said upfront, “Even if I have 50% of the shares, I will only be involved in the dividends and will not be managing it. Therefore, I will need to trouble Brother Gao in the development of the rising faction.”","Gao Feng felt that Lin Yuan was too particular. When he expressed his intention to negotiate a deal with Lin Yuan, the latter immediately gave a response, unlike others who knew what was going on but acted confused.","Even though Gao Feng was discussing a deal with Lin Yuan, Gao Feng felt he was very relaxed.","After settling the collaboration for the rising faction with Gao Feng, Lin Yuan blinked his eyes with some surprise.","Because of two deals he made with Gao Feng, they became acquaintances. Now, because of this marine fey breeding base, he had become business partners with Gao Feng.","It meant that Lin Yuan could make use of this deal he had with Gao Feng to easily obtain the deep-sea resources from the Gao family.","After discussing the deal with Gao Feng, Lin Yuan didn’t forget to mention his own matter. “Brother Gao, are you able to obtain any supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss from your side?”","Gao Feng laughed in response and said, “Brother, supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss isn’t that easy to obtain. If you asked me for help a month ago, I might just recommend you to try your luck with the veteran faction, Aquarium of Bliss.","“However, it just so happens that during the increase of spirit qi at the surface of the sea, and in the deep-sea area where our Gao family is exploring, we found a school of Angelfish of Bliss and immediately captured them.","“The school of Angelfish of Bliss is around 2,000 in quantity, but if we really sort it out, there should be around 50 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss.","“Our Gao family is also planning to nurture this batch of supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss.","“Brother, if you want them, I can get at least 20 for you.","“But it is a pity that when we captured them, the most superior supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss, which is a female, was actually pregnant. Therefore, it resisted abnormally violently and is now severely injured.","“The price for healing the injured female is too much, and it isn’t guaranteed that the roes within its stomach will be saved.”","Gao Feng heaved a sigh and said, “It is truly a pity.”","Upon hearing Gao Feng’s reply, Lin Yuan thought, If I am a little thrifty on the fish coat shed from the 20 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss, it might be enough for the daily consumption for spiritual-type feys in the manor.","However, Lin Yuan actually wanted to nurture the Angelfish of Bliss to use as the lake scenery in the man-made lake after the expansion. For this objective, let alone 20 Angelfish of Bliss, not even all 50 of the Gao family’s stock would be enough.","However, Lin Yuan was rather interested in that injured female Angelfish of Bliss.","With the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s spirit pool and the three Mountain River Eternal Life Carps’ exclusive skill, Place of Life, Lin Yuan had absolute confidence he could heal the female Angelfish of Bliss and also successfully hatch the roes in its stomach.","This wasn’t the first time Lin Yuan served the role of a midwife.","The female Five Fortune Ranchu that Lin Yuan had obtained from Zhou Jiaxin had also received Lin Yuan’s help for the delivery.","“Brother Gao, then I shall trouble you to obtain 20 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss for me. You can also include that injured female too.”","Gao Feng could tell that Lin Yuan wanted to try healing the female Angelfish of Bliss. Thus, he immediately agreed.","Before hanging up the phone, Lin Yuan said, “Before the new year, transport some regular coral jade for me to nurture first.”","Every empty space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone was a huge loss. Therefore, it was best to make use of the space as soon as possible.","After ending the phone call, Lin Yuan realized he had unknowingly opened up a huge stall. Apart from the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce, he now had another physical business.","When Lin Yuan called Zhou Luo earlier, the latter had been sitting beside Lin Yuan, waiting for Lin Yuan to finish his phone call. Seeing that Lin Yuan ended the call, Zhou Luo asked, “Young Master, do you need help from me?”","Lin Yuan looked at Zhou Luo and asked, “Brother Zhou, how is your Dark Snake Dragon Lizard’s nurturing?”","Zhou Luo scratched the back of his head and replied, “Young Master, I have just contracted the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard and didn’t have time to nurture it yet. It is still in the same condition as the time you bestowed it to me.”","Zhou Luo said that he didn’t have time to nurture the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard not because he didn’t have time but because he was too embarrassed to say that he didn’t have the resources to nurture it.","After all, it was truly too shameful to say such things.","Lin Yuan let out a breath of relief after hearing Zhou Luo’s reply.","It was fortunate that Zhou Luo hadn’t immediately nurtured the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard after receiving it. If Zhou Luo nurtured it immediately and evolved it from Bronze to Silver, then Lin Yuan wouldn’t know how to invest resources in Zhou Luo."]},{"number":570,"title":"Chapter 570 - Fusion of the Sacred Source Lifeforms Completed","paragraphs":["“Brother Zhou, since you have yet to nurture the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard and merely contracted with it. Why don’t you leave the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard with me first? I will help you to enhance its quality.”","When Zhou Luo heard Lin Yuan’s response, his eyes nearly popped out of his eye sockets.","Unlike the others, Zhou Luo didn’t know Lin Yuan’s foundation, but Lin Yuan’s words were definitely implying that he was going to enhance the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard’s quality to Legend.","It didn’t matter if Lin Yuan was going to upgrade the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard’s quality to Legend at Bronze or Silver. These were things that Zhou Luo could only dream about in his current situation.","“Y-Young Master—”","Before Zhou Luo could finish, Lin Yuan continued saying, “I remember that Brother Zhou still has an unused Willpower Rune. Brother Zhou, let me take a look at your third Willpower Rune.","“By then, Brother Zhou can upgrade both your second and third feys to Fantasy Breed!”","Zhou Luo’s face immediately glowed with delight.","Zhou Luo understood that during the battle within the dimensional rift outside Indigo Azure City, his performance had been good enough for Lin Yuan to treat him like his own men. Therefore, Lin Yuan was now beginning to invest massive resources in Zhou Luo to enhance his strength.","Zhou Luo had already given his loyalty to Lin Yuan, and this was definitely Zhou Luo’s best chance to receive Lin Yuan’s praises. Zhou Luo was naturally going to hold tight to this opportunity.","When Lin Yuan sensed Zhou Luo’s comprehended third Willpower Rune, he pursed his lips.","The Willpower Rune Zhou Luo had comprehended had a sticky, muddy feeling. It was considered an easily compatible Willpower Rune and was very suitable for defense fey.","During these two days, Lin Yuan hadn’t been as hardworking as before. Instead, he had slowed down his pace and had a relaxing lifestyle for two days.","After experiencing a life-and-death situation, Lin Yuan enjoyed the bustling new-year atmosphere in the Radiance Federation and felt that the entire world was abnormally wonderful.","During these two days, the manor members would go out and shop around on the streets, the manor was now stocked up with new-year merchandise in fey storage boxes, and it should already be enough to use until the next new year.","Chu Ci had been pulling Lin Yuan along to paste plenty of ‘Fortune’ words inside the manor. Even the red sandalwood fish tank had been pasted with two patterned wordings, ‘Abundance Year After Year’.","These ordinary patterned words and fortuitous words didn’t affect the manor’s overall beauty, but they made the manor cozier and warmer.","Two days ago, when Lin Yuan had finished negotiating the business with Gao Feng, in just less than half a day, 3,000 catties of regular coral jade had already been delivered in fey storage boxes by Ostrich Logistics.","As for the 19 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss and the severely injured female Angelfish of Bliss, Gao Feng had also arranged them to be delivered together.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up when he saw those 19 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss. All of them were in five colors, while the tail and the fins were thin like silver veils.","But when they were swimming, the fins and tails of the Angelfish of Bliss would glisten with a six-colored radiance and were exceptionally enchanting.","When Lin Yuan looked at the postures of these Angelfish of Bliss, he felt as though he was looking at young ladies that were covered in veils. It did give off blissful feelings at a glance.","Lin Yuan simply settled the 19 supreme-grade Angelfish of Bliss into the man-made lake. Even though the man-made lake’s current environment wasn’t the same as the Angelfish of Bliss’ original habitant, due to the Mountain River Eternal Life Carp’s exclusive skill, Place of Life, the Angelfish of Bliss were abnormally at ease and didn’t have any signs of them not adapting.","As for that female Angelfish of Bliss which was at its dying breath, Lin Yuan settled it inside the spirit pool.","The injuries of the female Angelfish of Bliss were overly severe. It was no wonder why the Gao family had decided to give up on it and wouldn’t invest their efforts to heal it.","Lin Yuan could see that this female Angelfish of Bliss’s tail and fins were dilapidated. Its body also had plenty of massive wounds as it was violently struggling during the capture.","Those massive wounds were already starting to fester. However, after two days of nourishment in the spirit pool, the festering wounds had already grown a thin layer of new flesh.","Lin Yuan had already instructed Blackie to take good care of the dying female Angelfish of Bliss.","Otherwise, Lin Yuan was really afraid that the carcinoma fey, the Sea Burial Lotus Flower, might just make a move on this injured female Angelfish of Bliss.","With two days of rest, this female Angelfish of Bliss already had the strength to occasionally eat the Butterfly Shells at the bottom of the spirit pool.","Lin Yuan only had to wait for this female Angelfish of Bliss to fully recover and release the roes within the spirit pool.","Unlike Lin Yuan’s relaxed two days, Hu Quan had been working overtime for the past two days.","Hu Quan would be creating exquisite and artistic fireworks during the quiet nights. In fact, Hu Quan wasn’t just working overtime and overnight for these two days. Ever since Lin Yuan had visited Indigo Azure City, Hu Quan had been working overtime and overnight without stopping.","Wen Yu naturally didn’t approve of Hu Quan working overtime late into the night, however, she didn’t expect Hu Quan to secretly contract a special fey, the Vitality Sloth.","The Vitality Sloth would be sleeping for the entire day and accumulating vitality. With all the accumulated vitality, the Vitality Sloth could then use its ability to transfer it to the contractor.","Due to each individual’s spiritual energy, the number of feys that could be contracted would be different, however, that number would be limited.","For combat-class spirit qi professionals, in order to maximize their combat strength, they would need to consider carefully when contracting each fey.","As a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman, Hu Quan had decided to contract a Vitality Sloth that could help him to sleep so that he could work overtime with more efficiency. He was truly a little stubborn. This stubborn nature of Hu Quan was something that Wen Yu couldn’t do anything about.","At present, even if Hu Quan didn’t sleep, it would affect his body. Wen Yu couldn’t possibly force Hu Quan to lie on the bed either. As such, Wen Yu had to allow Hu Quan to do as he pleased.","Even though Wen Yu had grown up in the Radiant Moon Palace and was a knowledgeable person, she was still convincingly impressed by Hu Quan and sincerely gave Hu Quan the title of Liver Emperor.","After working overtime for half a month, Hu Quan had already perfectly materialized most of Lin Yuan’s thoughts and designs with his capability as a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman.","Especially for the room’s interior design for the Star Web private territory, Hu Quan had already created all the required things.","Lin Yuan watched as Hu Quan created these things and said to himself, “I have already bought the private faction territory on Star Web for a very long time. But it has been empty, so I haven’t made use of it yet. Now that everything is prepared, my Star Web private faction will be announced soon.”","However, it was going to be the new year soon, and Lin Yuan still had plenty of things to do.","As for the interior of the Star Web private faction territory, Lin Yuan still had to scan the things that Hu Quan created and arrange them inside. After having a discussion with everyone, Lin Yuan set the start of operations for the Star Web private faction territory to be three days after the new year.","Originally, Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, Chu Ci, Liu Jie, the Mother of Bloodbath, and Endless Summer were seated on the water rhinoceros leather sofa and watching the quarterfinal Guild Alliance’s S Tournament matches.","Liu Jie was a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, so he was giving Chu Ci an explanation of all the Hundred Sequence members’ abilities and their contracted feys.","Since Liu Jie was a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, he naturally knew things that couldn’t be found on Star Web.","Liu Jie’s explanation was truly an eye-opener for Chu Ci.","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan felt a throbbing sensation from the depths of his soul.","Lin Yuan heard an abnormally distinct and ethereal voice echoing in the depths of his soul.","“My Lord.”","After hearing this voice, Lin Yuan immediately returned to his room.","At that moment, the sacred source lifeforms, Grace Queen and Sword of Punishment, had already completed their fusion.","Lin Yuan circulated the power deep in his soul and summoned the newly fused sacred source lifeform."]},{"number":571,"title":"Chapter 571 - Sacred Source 12 Stars","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When Lin Yuan summoned the sacred source lifeform, he saw the young lady with closed eyes who was originally deep in his soul. She was in a knee-length dress with a sacred sword in hand, standing in front of him now.","At present, the young lady’s tightly shut eyes were shaking lightly. The moment the young lady opened her eyes, an aura burst out from her body.","As the contractor, when Lin Yuan’s sacred source lifeform released its aura, it wouldn’t affect Lin Yuan at all. Therefore, Lin Yuan didn’t feel anything special from this aura.","However, the expressions of the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer that were sitting together on the water rhinoceros leather sofa turned cold. They were both Myth Breeds that had comprehended Law Runes.","The aura that was emitted from Lin Yuan’s room made the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer feel that the Law Runes they comprehended were just decorations or toys waiting for someone to pick.","This sensation made the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer exchange appalled glances. The two of them could see each other’s shocked emotions.","When Liu Jie felt the aura, he only felt something moving in the depths of his soul. Since Liu Jie possessed a sacred source lifeform, when another possessor of a sacred source lifeform emitted an aura, he should be able to sense it.","Liu Jie immediately knew that the aura he felt should be the first cry released when Lin Yuan finished forming the contract with the sacred source lifeform.","As for the aura emitted from Lin Yuan’s room, the people who could sense it clearly were Liu Jie, who had contracted a sacred source lifeform, and the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer that had comprehended Law Runes.","Chu Ci had also comprehended Willpower Runes, so she could also feel the aura emitted from Lin Yuan’s room that made her Willpower Rune abnormal.","Chu Ci immediately stood up and wanted to knock on Lin Yuan’s door to find out what was happening inside. However, when Chu Ci stood up, the Mother of Bloodbath stopped her and said, “Chu Ci, your elder brother is a Creation Master. If he returns to his room at this time, he should be doing some work.”","After experiencing the previous incident, not only the Mother of Bloodbath, but even Endless Summer was constantly alert 120% of the time.","The mansion couldn’t have any danger inside. With Endless Summer, a Suzerain/Myth III fey that was adept at scouting and had the Enlightenment Law Rune, it wasn’t possible for any enemy to sneak into the mansion without getting detected unless it was a Creation Breed that was adept at hiding and had sneaked inside.","The Mother of Bloodbath was rather curious as to what was happening inside Lin Yuan’s room to emit such an aura. However, the Mother of Bloodbath knew the reasoning that when a Creation Master was working, it should not disturb the Creation Master no matter what was happening.","When Chu Ci heard the Mother of Bloodbath’s reminder, she immediately reacted and felt that she was overly concerned and didn’t consider things thoroughly.","If Lin Yuan was working on a Creation Master project, her knock on the door might just distract Lin Yuan and cause him to make a mistake.","Chu Ci might still be sitting on the water rhinoceros leather sofa to watch the S Tournament, but she would constantly look toward Lin Yuan’s room. She looked to be very distracted.","Wen Yu grinned when seeing the scene and recalled how Lin Yuan would always talk about Chu Ci. She couldn’t help lamenting the sibling love between Chu Ci and Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan looked at his contracted sacred source lifeform and sensed its first cry.","At that moment, Lin Yuan found out that the new sacred source lifeform, which was a fusion of the Grace Queen and the Sword of Punishment, was now finally able to be used.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on his sacred source lifeform.","[Sacred Source Name]: Sacred Sword Wielding Queen","[Sacred Source Species]: Source genus/Sacred Source species","[Sacred Source Star Grade]: 0 star","[Sacred Source Type]: ???","Lin Yuan finally learned the name of his sacred source lifeform. However, Lin Yuan realized that the data of the sacred source lifeform was entirely different from regular feys.","The grade of a sacred source lifeform wasn’t separated according to the Normal, Elite, Bronze, Silver, Gold, and Platinum grades. The quality wasn’t separated into the Normal, Elite, Flawless, Epic, and Legend either.","True Data stated that sacred source lifeforms were separated by star grades.","Since Lin Yuan didn’t know something, he had to find out the principle. He checked on the time and realized it was only 8:00 p.m., so he made a phone call to the Moon Empress.","The phone merely rang a few times before the Moon Empress accepted the call. Lin Yuan then immediately asked about the things he didn’t know.","When the Moon Empress heard Lin Yuan’s questions, she suddenly had a delighted feeling.","As a Master, apart from the routine question-and-answer sessions, she was finally useful for dispelling confusions too. But after a brief moment of delight, the Moon Empress felt that she didn’t fulfill her obligations as a teacher.","She already knew that Lin Yuan had contracted a sacred source lifeform, but during the question-and-answer session, she mainly talked about the knowledge on forming a contract with sacred source lifeform and forgot to explain the difference between sacred source lifeforms, regular feys, and source-type lifeforms.","The Moon Empress explained in detail. “What you say is correct. Each sacred source lifeform has an ability that is unique and will never be replaced.","“There are no weak and strong abilities, so the sacred source lifeform cannot be separated with grade and quality.","“At the same time, because sacred source lifeforms don’t need to fuse with the contractor’s Willpower Runes, the sacred source lifeforms are no longer the same as regular feys and source-type lifeforms which can evolve to Fantasy Breed, Myth Breed, and Creation Breed.","“Sacred source lifeforms have their own unique grading, from 1 star to 12 stars with a total of 12 grades, also known as the Sacred Source 12 Stars.","“However, the star grade of the sacred source lifeform doesn’t represent the strength of the sacred source lifeform. It represents the development extent of the sacred source lifeform’s ability.","“When the sacred source lifeform is just contracted, it will have one ability. Afterward, the sacred source lifeform will go through a transformation with each increase of 3 star grades and unlock another ability.","“According to the star grade, 0 to 3 stars will be the infant stage of the sacred source lifeform. 4 to 6 stars will be the adolescent stage. 7 to 9 stars will be considered the mature stage of the sacred source lifeform.","“10 to 12 stars is called the sacred source lifeform’s complete stage.”","After hearing the Moon Empress’ explanation, Lin Yuan immediately understood the principle behind the grading of sacred source lifeforms. It made Lin Yuan more aware of the importance of knowledge.","Lin Yuan suddenly had a thought in his mind that knowledge was power. The moment he had this thought, he felt the Willpower Rune in his mind that was related to knowledge had increased a little more."]},{"number":572,"title":"Chapter 572 - The Queen that Disregarded Rules","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Just as Lin Yuan was about to gather the Willpower Rune that was related to wisdom, an accident occurred.","Lin Yuan failed to gather this Willpower Rune as smoothly as planned.","Instead, it was stuck.","Lin Yuan had been a membrane’s breath away from understanding this wisdom-related Willpower Rune.","Now, the membrane had a hole in it, and it had become stuck just as it was about to leak out of the hole.","This dilemma of being neither here nor there frustrated Lin Yuan.","For the first time, Lin Yuan felt that it was difficult to comprehend a Willpower Rune.","But since he had an inkling of this Willpower Rune, he was one step closer to comprehending it.","In contrast to the frustrated Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress was ecstatic after the call ended.","Mystic Moon walked into the inner palace and said to the Moon Empress, “Moon Empress, I’ve taken care of the matter you assigned me to complete. I can head to the Startling Lines Continent anytime to pick a suitable location to build the Young Lord’s space tunnel.”","The Moon Empress placed her teacup on the jade table and said, “Mystic Moon, I recall that your sacred source lifeform is stuck on Star 8. It’s a hair’s breadth away from Star 9. Zixi’s main body brought you something when it came back from the outskirts. It might be able to push your sacred source lifeform up to Star 9. Zixi’s main body will be back in a few days. After you enjoy New Year’s, let’s try improving your sacred source item to Star 9.”","Despite Mystic Moon’s composed expression, his brows exemplified his excitement.","“If I can really improve my sacred source lifeform to Star 9, it will gain a new ability. The entire Star Web should also be updated.”","The Moon Empress nodded.","“Star Web was originally the product of the abilities of three sacred source lifeforms. If I’m not wrong, the Space Elder’s Hollow Crystal Shellfish also evolved not long ago. It looks like the first Radiance Hundred Sequence exam on Star Web will be even more interesting.”","...","After the phone call, Lin Yuan shook his head and shook out all his feelings of frustration.","He checked the abilities of his sacred source lifeform.","Abilities:","[Queen Form]:","1. Queen’s Skirt Hem: Able to absorb the Willpower Runes from the bodies of dead feys or source-type items. The Willpower Runes or Law Runes from Myth Breed feys’ Law Crystals will be carved on the queen’s skirt. The Law Crystals which have their laws absorbed will become Law Crystals that possess pure law power.","[Sacred Sword Form]:","1. Blade of Sacred Sword: When the spirit qi in the body is depleted, the blade will pierce the skirt hem to unleash all the laws and willpower stored within.","Lin Yuan almost bit his tongue off.","His sacred source lifeform really lived up to the fact that it was a combination of two sacred source lifeforms.","Not only did it have two forms, but each form also had its own ability.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, there was no difference between the two forms having an ability each and having two overall abilities.","It seemed as though both abilities could be used in conjunction.","However, the Blade of Sacred Sword ability was fully dependent on the Queen’s Skirt Hem ability’s laws and willpower.","Without the Queen’s Skirt Hem, the Blade of Sacred Sword would be useless.","This indicated that when the Grace Queen and Sword of Service combined, the Grace Queen took the lead.","Nonetheless, this brought Lin Yuan twice the joy.","Amongst the two abilities, the Queen’s Skirt Hem made Lin Yuan feel that he had the power of a Class 5 Creation Master.","He could now nurture pure law power.","However, Class 5 Creation Masters used a variety of rare spiritual ingredients in Law Runes to concoct spirit fluid with pure law power.","Lin Yuan needed to rely on the ability of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Queen Form.","Different Law Crystals were just like different flavored drinks. Once the flavorings were removed, only the base water was left.","The Queen’s Skirt Hem removed all the special law energy from Law Crystals, leaving the Law Crystals with only pure law power.","Presently, Lin Yuan could not quickly evolve his feys’ quality.","With the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, Lin Yuan’s Creation Master abilities were now at Class 5 level.","It was different from the Law Crystals that formed naturally after the deaths of Myth Breed feys.","Once a Myth Breed fey died, the Willpower Rune in its body would continue to exist in its body if its body was still viable.","However, if the Myth Breed feys’ body was separated into different spiritual ingredients, the Willpower Rune left in the mangled fey carcass would dissipate during the separation process.","Not even a Class 5 Creation Master could extract Willpower Runes from a Myth Breed of source-type lifeform unless Law Stripping took place, like when the Mother of Bloodbath encountered Fei Qianqiong’s Blood-Toothed Cricket.","The Queen’s Skirt Hem’s ability made it easy for Lin Yuan to garner law energy to supply the Blade of Sacred Sword ability.","Even if Lin Yuan possessed a few Law Crystals, it would not be easy for him to procure more unless it came from his enemies.","If every person was a fey, Lin Yuan felt that he had to be a production-type fey.","Morbius’ Spirit Lock spatial zone and the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen turned Lin Yuan into a bonafide top producer.","With regards to the Sacred Sword Form using willpower and laws as a means of attack, Lin Yuan could not help but feel as though his sacred source lifeform treated the venerated willpower and laws as toys.","It seemed less like a feeling and more like the truth.","When Lin Yuan checked his Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, it had opened its eyes and was also looking at him.","After forming a marrow contract with a sacred source lifeform, one basically acquired a highly intelligent newborn.","It was completely ignorant of how the world worked.","As the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen looked at Lin Yuan, its expression kept changing. It thought that its contractor was a rather dull mute."]},{"number":573,"title":"Chapter 573 - Why Not Name It White Pill","paragraphs":["The highly intelligent Sacred Sword Wielding Queen blinked. It could not help but be worried for its future.","Why if this contractor of mine is actually stupid?","It really needed to think deeply about this problem.","After struggling for a second, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen noticed that its contractor seemed to be studying it. His expression changed from admiration to deep pondering, to uneasiness, and finally back to admiration.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen cleared its throat and said in an ethereal voice, “Master, I have only just descended into this world. Please bestow upon me a name.”","After hearing the sacred source lifeform speak, Lin Yuan was certain that it was smarter than ordinary feys.","Only highly intelligent beings who were capable of independently contemplating life would be curious about their name the moment they were born.","It was as though it required some sort of marking or name to prove itself.","Lin Yuan understood why the Moon Empress had emphasized on forming a marrow contract with such an intelligent lifeform.","If only a blood contract was formed with a sacred source lifeform, once there was a difference in opinion between the contractor and such a highly intelligent lifeform, it was likely that they would be unable to cooperate during battle.","However, Lin Yuan did not need to worry about this.","No matter how intelligent the sacred source lifeform was, Lin Yuan had formed a marrow contract with the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, and it had been subsumed into his soul. Now, it was a part of Lin Yuan’s soul.","Lin Yuan did not know that his sacred source lifeform regarded him as rather dull.","Lin Yuan felt that he specialized in naming.","Genius was a genius, which was why it was named so.","Chimey was a Sound Bird and could sing, which was why it was named Chimey.","The Spirit-Drawing Ichthyosaur had an all-black body, which was why it was named Blackie.","Simple, sweet, and majestic.","Lin Yuan took note of the long ivory skirt that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was dressed in.","“What about Whitey?”","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen immediately squeezed its sword tightly.","After merging with Lin Yuan’s soul, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen digested all of Lin Yuan’s memories and knowledge.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was full of questions when it heard Lin Yuan say ‘Whitey’.","A name like Whitey should be given to a small and friendly white dog.","In order to prevent Lin Yuan from naming it Whitey, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen quickly suggested, “Master, I should be called Pill.”","The newly-born Sacred Sword Wielding Queen came up with its first-ever idea.","It wanted to plant an idea in the mind of its contractor.","The name ‘Pill’ was meant to inspire him to treat it like a pill.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen wanted to turn its contractor from a dull mute to the smartest person in the world.","Lin Yuan was shocked to hear the sacred source lifeform name itself.","Isn’t that name too common?","How is it as nice as Whitey?","Lin Yuan offered a friendly suggestion, “How about White Pill?”","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen accepted Lin Yuan’s suggestion without protest.","Its contractor was not very smart, and it had already taken the liberty of naming itself. If it still did not accept its contractor’s suggestion, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen would be disrespecting its contractor.","That would not be allowable.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen balled its fists tightly. It was confident that its contractor would eventually come up with a better name than ‘White Pill’ for it with it around.","Who cares what color of pill I am? I’ll be a good pill as long as I help my contractor to become more clever!","Lin Yuan had never seen the sacred source lifeforms of others.","But from the name Hollow Crystal Shellfish, Lin Yuan could tell that it was not a humanoid lifeform but rather some sort of shellfish.","Previously, one of his sacred source lifeforms was the Sword of Punishment before fusing with the Grace Queen. It was a weapon instead of a humanoid being.","Thus, Lin Yuan landed on the conclusion that sacred source lifeforms could take all kinds of forms.","Although his sacred source lifeform had a human form, Lin Yuan had carefully observed that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had a different type of human form than Myth II feys.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen did not have a fully corporeal form. It existed as a half-corporeal entity.","Lin Yuan remembered that he still had the two dead dark-type Fantasy Breed feys given to him by Endless Summer in his Diamond fey storage box.","Those two dark-type feys were the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger and Dark Spirit Eye Tadpole that Endless Summer had encountered while protecting Listen","Both the dark-type feys’ corpses were completely preserved.","Lin Yuan had not had the time to deal with the bodies of the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger and the Dark Spirit Eye Tadpole, so he had left them in the fey storage box.","It was a good opportunity to test the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Queen’s Skirt Hem ability of absorbing the willpower of dead feys.","Lin Yuan entered his room to summon the two dead feys.","Luckily for Lin Yuan, his room was large enough. Otherwise, the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger could have ruined the valuable jade artifacts in the room.","When the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen saw Lin Yuan summon the two dead feys, a hungry look appeared on its face. It looked like it had just seen a scrumptious delicacy.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen pointed at the two dead feys and said to Lin Yuan, “Can I eat them?”","It looked like a child who had just spotted a tasty snack and was asking their parent for permission to dig in.","Lin Yuan was slightly surprised. He initially felt that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was toying around with willpower and laws.","However, he now felt that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen did not toy around with willpower and laws. It treated them as food.","Lin Yuan gladly nodded.","“Of course, you can.”","With Lin Yuan’s permission, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen walked up to the two dead feys.","The two dead feys were skinned with a bright flash of the sacred sword while the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt suddenly expanded to form two balls of string.","The two balls of string entered the two dead feys’ bodies through the sacred sword’s slash."]},{"number":574,"title":"Chapter 574 - Dress-up Game?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen rose to the tips of its toes, and its skirt started to sway.","Shortly after, Lin Yuan realized that the carcasses of the two feys started to glow with a dark light.","Inside the dark glow was an immense amount of dark-elemental particles. It almost seemed though the two dead feys had been revived through the balls of string inside their bodies.","Less than a minute later, two motes of willpower emerged from within the two massive dark energies.","The two motes of willpower followed the strings and moved toward the dancing queen.","Although they were both dark motes of willpower, the willpower from the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger leaned toward the murderous intent aspect of darkness.","On the other hand, the Dark Spirit Eye Tadpole’s willpower leaned toward the silence aspect of darkness.","Lin Yuan’s sharp eyes caught sight of the two motes of willpower moving along the string to enter the queen’s skirt. Color and light markings started appearing on the white skirt.","Both the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger and the Dark Spirit Eye Tadpole were strong Fantasy Breed feys, and a king-class expert had lovingly nurtured them.","The Diamond X/Fantasy IV Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger had almost reached the highest point of a Fantasy Breed fey.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen quickly leached away the willpower in the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger’s Willpower Rune.","In a mere five minutes, there was not one ounce of willpower left in the long-dead Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger and Dark Spirit Eye Tadpole for the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to absorb.","Lin Yuan had been observing the two dead feys. He noticed that despite losing their willpower, the dark energy around the bodies of the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger and the Dark-Eyed Scorpion Tiger had not decreased.","Lin Yuan’s lip curled into a smile. It seemed that dead feys whose willpower the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had absorbed could still be separated and used as spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan looked away from the dead feys and turned his attention back on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","He was astonished by the sight of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s white skirt had been completely simple and unblemished.","After absorbing the two dead feys’ motes of willpower, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt had turned an inky black.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s aura had also changed completely.","There were now two kinds of willpower etched on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt. It now looked like an adventurer who was lost in the night.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s black skirt did not exude the same opaque darkness that regular cloth had.","It carried the illusive darkness of fog and the silence of an enduring night.","With a closer look, one would notice a terrifying murderous intent behind the darkness. It was like there was a scorpion tiger shrouded by the darkness of night and poised to attack its prey.","Not only had the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s entire appearance changed, but the True Data sacred source type information about the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, which used to be blank, now stated dark-type.","However, it still had zero stars.","Lin Yuan thought, Is the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s type decided according to the willpower and laws it absorbs?","Lin Yuan’s hand shook, and a blue crystal with two gold cracks appeared in his hand.","This crystal was the Law Crystal that the Mother of Bloodbath had taken from the Cold Snow Pine when it had just broken through to Myth II.","Judging from the subtle gold cracks, it was obvious that the Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal was the weakest Law Crystal that a Myth II fey could produce.","The Cold Snow Pine’s cold-flames law was also extremely unorthodox.","However, the Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal could be considered complete, with one full law.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, which had just snacked on two kinds of willpower and was now satisfied, locked its eyes onto the Law Crystal in Lin Yuan’s hand.","When Lin Yuan noticed the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s expression, he immediately handed her the Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal.","After the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen received the Law Crystal, it felt that its contractor was extremely good to it despite him being unintelligent.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen pressed the Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal to the top of its head.","It embedded the Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal into the jewel-less crown that sat atop its head.","The crown was suddenly alight with icy blue flames. The Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal emitted the glow of brilliant icy blue flames.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt swayed, and its petite crystal shoes were revealed.","Lin Yuan realized that the darkness on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt was quickly overwhelmed and replaced with the pattern of a large snowflake that consisted of a variety of runes.","The pine needles were lit up with the icy blue flames, turning the entire skirt an icy blue color.","The initial darkness on the skirt was reduced to a shadow under the Cold Snow Pine’s pattern.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check, and he saw that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s sacred source type had changed from dark-type to ice-type.","It was not ice-type and dark-type.","Lin Yuan was sure that the two dark-type willpowers on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt had not disappeared.","The willpower of two dark-type Fantasy Breed feys could not compare with the laws of the Myth II Cold Snow Pine’s Law Crystal.","It became evident that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s sacred source type was decided according to the type of willpower it had absorbed.","The dominant willpower and laws would take precedence of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s sacred source type.","Lin Yuan watched as the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen changed its appearance again. Its skirt was now burning with icy blue flames.","The air around had become extremely chilly.","Lin Yuan felt like he was playing a sort of dress-up game.","After a moment’s consideration, Lin Yuan took out his remaining two Law Crystals. It was better to give them to the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen than to have them lying around.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen swayed its skirt around, and it felt that it was the happiest sacred source lifeform in the world.","One of the Law Crystals came from the crow that had ambushed Endless Summer, and the other came from Nightmare VI of the Zheng family’s Nightmare Squad.","Both Law Crystals came from the bodies of pinnacle Myth II feys, so the two gold cracks on each crystal were blinding.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen embedded both Law Crystals into its crown."]},{"number":575,"title":"Chapter 575 - Allstar Match","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan felt that all the space in his room had been dyed black by the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt.","It was like the night.","After an hour, when the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed all the laws in the Law Crystal into its skirt, it changed its appearance again.","When Lin Yuan looked at it, he felt as though he was staring at the embodiment of darkness.","It was like he was standing in an abyss and looking directly at the darkness.","There were now two dark-type willpowers, and two dark-type laws etched on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt.","The endless darkness of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s skirt seemed like a continuous nightmare full of decay and death.","Under the darkness sprouted a blue snow pine, giving the nightmare a hint of life.","At the top branch of the snow pine sat a crow and a bat. They looked extremely strange.","The three Law Crystals on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s crown had turned a pure white.","The pure white Law Crystal shone from within.","Lin Yuan knew that the shine came from the pure law power.","Lin Yuan noticed from True Data that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s initial zero stars had increased to 1 Star.","However, Lin Yuan was not happy about this improvement; rather, he felt mounting pressure.","How much willpower and laws will I need to collect to reach top stars for the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen?","Despite the pressure Lin Yuan felt, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was very satisfied.","It felt great to increase its stars the moment it was born!","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had no clue that it would not be easy for it to experience such a feast again.","After he thought about it, Lin Yuan decided not to test the Sacred Sword Form’s ability.","He did not know if the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was willing, but he could not bear to rip the skirt that he had just set up after much effort.","No matter how he thought about it, Lin Yuan felt that the Blade of Sacred Sword ability was definitely a self-sabotaging ability.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen handed the three Law Crystals that were full of pure law power to Lin Yuan and said, “Master, here’s the rubbish leftovers of what I ate.”","Lin Yuan almost fainted after he heard what it said.","My sacred source lifeform is crazy! It actually regards these Law Crystals with pure law power as rubbish. It has no clue how many emperor-class experts and Myth Breed feys would treat these as treasures. They would do anything to get their hands on these.","But Lin Yuan reflected on the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s style of consumption.","It was not wrong to see these three Law Crystals as the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s waste.","Lin Yuan carefully stored the three Law Crystals.","No matter how the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen thought of these pure white Law Crystals, the Mother of Bloodbath would definitely need them to evolve to Creation Breed.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was no longer a picture of white that it was in the beginning.","It was now mostly black.","Lin Yuan suggested, “I don’t think White Pill is suitable anymore. How about Black Pill instead?”","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen stared blankly at its contractor, feeling that it should give up on its plan to make its contractor smarter.","In less than two hours, its contractor had already changed its agreed-upon name.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen did not want to critique Lin Yuan’s naming ability.","There was no difference between White or Black pill.","It felt that it might be of more use if Lin Yuan changed its name to ‘Retarded Pill’.","Lin Yuan walked out of his room and sat on the water rhinoceros leather sofa to watch the S Tournament with the rest of the group.","The others could clearly tell that Lin Yuan’s aura had changed.","Lin Yuan used to be an affectionate and bright youth.","Now, there was an added layer of mystery around his original foundation.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was now a part of Lin Yuan’s soul.","After the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen absorbed three types of laws and two types of willpower, Lin Yuan was also feeling the effects.","The willpower and law energy helped to prevent Lin Yuan from being scoped out.","The Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer realized that they could no longer sense Lin Yuan’s spirit qi professional rank.","The Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer secretly activated the Law Runes in their bodies and found that they still could not accurately pinpoint Lin Yuan’s spirit qi professional rank.","Evidently, Lin Yuan had undergone a huge change when he went into his room. He had gained the ability to hide his abilities.","If this was anyone else, Endless Summer and the Mother of Bloodbath would be incredulous.","However, it had happened to Lin Yuan. There were already too many unbelievable circumstances that had surrounded Lin Yuan. The Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer were already used to it.","After they watched the S Tournament, Chu Ci felt said with yearning, “We don’t get to experience the atmosphere of the S Tournament watching it like this. If only we could go and watch it in real life.”","A thought seemed to strike Liu Jie, and he said, “On the second day of the new year, there’ll be an Allstar Match S Tournament. Although the Allstar Match is meant for entertainment as it is not as formal as the S Tournament, it involves all the A-level and B-level guilds. Chu Ci, if you want to go, I’ll be able to get tickets. We’ll all be able to go together. The highlight of the S Tournament is that the audience will enter a lucky draw. The winner will get the chance to challenge an Allstar member.”","Chu Ci was already very interested in the opportunity to attend the S Tournament. As an impulsive defense-type spirit qi professional, her eyes lit up the mention of the chance to challenge a member of the S Tournament.","“Big brother, do you want to go?” Chu Ci asked Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan smiled ruefully.","You’re clearing raring to go. What’s the point of asking me?","Chu Ci usually called Lin Yuan by his name. Lin Yuan had no reason to refuse since she had even gone as far as to call him ‘Big brother’.","“The third day of the new year will be the day that Sky City announces itself to the other rising factions and veteran factions. The second day after the new year will be a good time for us to watch the Allstar Match S Tournament.”"]},{"number":576,"title":"Chapter 576 - Nickname ‘Happy Hu Quan’","paragraphs":["When Chu Ci heard Lin Yuan’s response, an expectant and thrilled smile appeared on her face.","She made a peace sign toward Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan smiled warmly back at her, revealing his pearly teeth.","Liu Jie had taken out his phone and said to Chu Ci, “I’ll book front row tickets now.”","Liu Jie immediately made the call.","Lin Yuan thought, The S Tournament’s Allstar Match is almost as large of an event as the S Tournament’s finals. There are only two days left until the start of the Allstar Match. Liu Jie will easily be able to get front row tickets with one call. It’s nice to have connections.","Liu Jie soon hung up the phone. He said to the group with an odd expression on his face, “I’ve settled the front row tickets. There are ten tickets in total, and we’ll all be sitting together.”","As he spoke, Liu Jie thought back to the pure yet sorrowful voice on the other end of the phone.","Could it really be depression? It’s almost New Year’s. Why does Bai Hao sound so devoid of life? Is that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess really so magnetic?","After she had disappeared for such a long time, she was still able to keep Bai Hao wrapped around her finger. Whenever he had any spare Radiance dollars, he would throw them into Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s empty live-streaming room.","Liu Jie was slightly doubtful.","How did that arrogant Bai Hao become so obedient?","The Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ continuous disappearances were as newsworthy as the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","When Zhao Xiaochun had eaten the last buffet restaurant in the Royal Capital out of business, it was still a step below the news of Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s disappearance.","Liu Jie thought that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ long-term disappearance could be good for Bai Hao. As time went on, Bai Hao would be able to bounce back from his current state of despair.","Hu Quan was currently instructing his Wood Weaving House Centipede to swallow wenge and spit out completed jade-textured string that had markings.","However, Hu Quan’s attention was focused on Lin Yuan.","When he watched Lin Yuan interact with Chu Ci, Hu Quan could not help but marvel at how much he spoiled his sister.","The others were not aware of how many things Hu Quan had created for Lin Yuan’s private faction territory. He only presented the items to Lin Yuan once they were done.","Lin Yuan decided to debut his new private faction on Star Web to the other rising factions and veteran factions on the third day of the new year.","This meant that he was going to open their Star Web territory to other factions. Thus, Lin Yuan needed to ensure that the territory was properly decorated.","Lin Yuan also needed to prepare the feys who were going to decorate the territory. Hu Quan knew that it was not an easy task.","Yet Lin Yuan was still willing to sacrifice a day to accompany Chu Ci to watch the Allstar Match.","This proved how much Lin Yuan cared about Chu Ci.","In the eyes of a traditional man like Hu Quan, one did not need to outwardly express their care for someone else. It was proven in the times that they unconditionally took time out of their busy schedules to be with the one they cared for.","Hu Quan poked the Wood Weaving House Centipede’s back armor to tell it to continue working hard.","He summoned the recently contracted Vitality Sloth.","The Vitality Sloth was slightly confused after it was summoned. It loped its long claw over Hu Quan’s neck and clung to his shoulder. It looked rather coy.","However, the Vitality Sloth was too lazy. It closed its eyes and settled into a comfortable position to continue sleeping.","Hu Quan carried the Vitality Sloth over to the water rhinoceros leather sofa and took a seat. Their combined weight caused the water rhinoceros leather sofa to sag.","The rest of the people present were stunned by Hu Quan and the Vitality Sloth.","What’s with this loving pose?","Wen Yu thought as she suspiciously eyed Hu Quan, Hu Quan is a man who spends his days crafting. Could he have a skewed idea of love after being alone for such a long time? But that can’t be because he reads too. I’ll have to find time to take a look at the books he reads.","Hu Quan patted the Vitality Sloth like he was comforting a child and said, “Vitality Sloth, show the boy holding the teacup your Vitality Flow ability.”","Lin Yuan had just picked up the teacup that was full of Wen Yu’s freshly brewed Three Treasures Tea when he suddenly felt a flow of qi entering him and filling him with energy. He was filled with so much energy that he felt like he did not need to sleep that night.","Lin Yuan looked up at Hu Quan, and the latter’s eyes were twinkling as he said, “Young lad, with all this energy, you won’t feel burnt out after working all night.”","After Hu Quan spoke, everyone fell silent except Chu Ci. They looked at Hu Quan with an odd expression.","Only Chu Ci found their reactions weird. She could not understand why they were all looking at the honest Uncle Hu that way.","Hu Quan thought, There’s no way Lin Yuan will be tired tonight after being exposed to Vitality Flow. He won’t be tired the next day, even after working hard the whole night. This way, he’ll be able to finish all the work he was supposed to do on the second day of the new year tonight.","Hu Quan was still slightly reluctant. The Vitality Sloth’s recovery of vitality was only just enough for its contractor.","When it was not busy, it would rest, and the vitality would be slowly stored up.","However, when the Vitality Sloth recovered the vitality of someone other than its contractor, it would be significantly depleted.","The Vitality Sloth had used up all the vitality it had stored up in the last half month on that Vitality Flow.","Hu Quan scratched his head as he mulled.","It looks like I should increase the Vitality Sloth’s grade. Silver grade does not seem to be enough. Even if it doesn’t recover anyone else’s vitality, as long as I read a book, I’ll have to sleep at night. If I can evolve the Vitality Sloth to Platinum, I won’t have to be worried about this. I haven’t decided on my nickname as a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman. How about ‘Happy Hu Quan’?","At that moment, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s ethereal voice sounded out in Lin Yuan’s head. “Master, how about the name Extremely Lazy and Arrogant?”"]},{"number":577,"title":"Chapter 577 - Online and Offline Auctions","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was sneering inward at the Vitality Sloth’s name.","When he heard the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s question, he answered without hesitation, “Isn’t that name a little too childish? How is it as nice as your name, Black Pill?”","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen initially wanted to discuss with Lin Yuan its issue with naming seriously.","However, after hearing Lin Yuan’s answer, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen decided against bringing up its issue.","It only swayed its skirt woefully in the depths of Lin Yuan’s soul.","If he comes up with something strange during our discussion, he might change my name again.","Lin Yuan could feel the vitality reinvigorating him. He felt as energized as if he had just slept for two days straight.","Lin Yuan praised Hu Quan’s Vitality Sloth to himself.","Hu Quan noticed the way that Lin Yuan was looking at the Vitality Sloth. He forcefully carried the snoring Vitality Sloth and said carefully, “As a Creation Master, you should know how difficult it was for the Vitality Sloth to inject you with vitality. Don’t you come up with any ideas for my baby Vitality Sloth from now on.”","Lin Yuan had initially planned to burn the midnight oil that night and bring the ingredients he had picked with Liu Jie, along with Chu Ci, up to Leaning Moon Mountain the next morning.","Lin Yuan had been afraid that he would be more tired than usual the next morning because of his previous night’s hard work.","Now that he had Hu Quan’s help, Lin Yuan no longer needed to be worried about lacking energy the next day.","Listen and Zhou Luo only returned after 11 o’clock at night.","They sat down and had a cup of tea.","“Young Master, the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce has taken over a significant amount of the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce’s resources.","“I asked Fei Qianqiong to transfer the resources which are poorer in quality and which will cause us to make a loss over to the other factions. Since selling off these resources, the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce has started transforming luxury goods.","“However, their sponsor, the Zheng family, has stopped providing them with resources.","“According to Fei Qianqiong, Bi Chengxiong, and Bi Chenghu are very worried. Bi Chenghu has already gone to Indigo Azure City to contact the Zheng family’s third lineage.","“He handed management of the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce to his brother, who is a hedonistic layabout that does not care about the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce.","“Fei Qianqiong is in charge of handling most of the matters regarding the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce,” said Listen to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan did not voice his thoughts about Listen’s report.","“Handle it however you see fit,” said Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan instructed Listen to continue managing the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce, he had planned on taking a hands-off supervision role.","Wen Yu had already told Lin Yuan about the recent tussles between the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce and the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce.","With the help of Fei Qianqiong as their spy, the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce was continuously eating away at the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce’s roots.","Lin Yuan was gaining more and more faith in Listen’s capabilities.","Listen’s eyes lit up when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","After going to Indigo Azure City, Listen now knew what was going on with that patch of coastal sea.","Listen had started to wonder if the deaths of his elders were not accidental after the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce gave the resources belonging to the Creation Masters that they had taken from the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce to the Zheng family’s third lineage.","From the moment that Jiao Hanzhong called out the Sea Burial Lotus Flower’s name to slander Lin Yuan, Listen had become certain that everything that had happened to the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce was related to the Zheng family.","After learning the truth, Listen could step out of the storm of doubt and conflict. Once his doubt and conflict were gone, Listen was left with hatred for the remaining members of the Zheng family.","“Young Master, since you were unconscious for some time, I have been secretly expanding the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce. I haven’t had the chance to sell the goods mixed with jade-textured wood powder. We’ve accumulated a large number now, and I think it’s time to display them. However, if we display these luxury goods as regular goods, we won’t be able to gain the greatest profit. As such, I want to sell them through an auction.”","Listen’s idea was inspired by Lin Yuan’s auction of the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls on Star Web.","Due to their rarity and beauty, the non-useful elemental pearls with inner radiance had been auctioned off at inflated prices. It was an attractive concept. Thus, Listen wanted to create a brand with the large number of luxury goods that the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce had stored up.","He wanted to earn the maximum profits off them by packaging them to the nines.","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment after hearing Listen’s proposal.","“Since you want to conduct an auction, are you going to hold it in real-life or on Star Web?”","It was clear that Listen had his own plan in mind.","“I plan on auctioning them off in a live-streaming room on Star Web. A host will introduce these luxury items continuously the entire day.","“Uncle Hu has already set up the Heavenly Craft Pavilion. The Class 3 Spirit Craftsmen created unique designs for every item. Instead of selling them in bulk, each item will only be sold at a high price to the person who appreciates their unique beauty.","“Although it might be a slow start and the initial low participant rates could drive down the bids, I believe that the live-streaming room will gain steam and improve tremendously with time.","“I’ve found a store in the busy district of the Royal Capital. We can also select some of the luxury goods to sell there using the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce and the Heavenly Craft Pavilion’s reputation,” replied Listen.","Hu Quan’s eyes lit up after he heard what Listen had said.","Although Hu Quan had created the Heavenly Craft Pavilion out of service to Lin Yuan, he was more than happy to see the place become reputable. Otherwise, he would not have had the idea to create the Heavenly Craft Pavilion in the first place.","He had also put a lot of thought into how he could boost the Heavenly Craft Pavilion to fame.","Unfortunately, Hu Quan’s mind was only suited to crafting, and it lacked the skills to think about anything else.","But with Listen’s idea, Hu Quan’s problem had been resolved.","The Heavenly Craft Pavilion only needed to produce luxury goods daily, and the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce would take care of the rest.","Lin Yuan had not expected Listen to be so ambitious to want to tackle both online and offline.","However, whether it was a live stream auction on Star Web or a real-life auction, it would not be a success without some cornerstone items."]},{"number":578,"title":"Chapter 578 - The Anonymous Message From Afar","paragraphs":["The jade-textured wood in Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone was constantly maturing.","Almost all the furniture in the mansion’s main residence was made of jade-textured wood, and each was well-made. Thus, Lin Yuan no longer needed to set aside the jade-textured wood for the mansion’s construction.","This allowed the jade-textured wood to become resources that Lin Yuan could trade.","Lin Yuan waved his hand, and ten large jade-textured wood planks appeared by his feet.","“Since you’re going to hold an online auction, I’ll provide you with some good materials so that Hu Quan can make some cornerstone items,” said Lin Yuan to Listen.","Lin Yuan took out a handful of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with Cloud Dream Lake inner radiance and handed them to Hu Quan.","“Uncle Hu, what do you think will be the effect of embedding these heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls into goods made of the jade-textured wood?” asked Lin Yuan.","Although Hu Quan was already used to creating goods out of the jade-textured wood, the sight of so many shining jade-textured wood planks made him squint his eyes.","When he saw the handful of Cloud Dream Lake pearls, he could not help but want to ask Lin Yuan if he had been born in a goldmine.","How else can he produce precious items time after time? How is an old man like me supposed to hold back?","The Spirit Craftsman’s soul in Hu Quan trembled with excitement. All sorts of designs popped into his mind.","“Fusing any one of the elemental pearls into a sculpture made of jade-textured wood will result in buyers clambering after it. It will definitely become even more of a luxury good! You can rest assured that the elemental pearls and jade-textured wood are in good hands with me. My skills will create luxury goods that are sure to shock them,” said Hu Quan hurriedly.","Listen was now full of questions.","He had only come up with the idea to create goods with the jade-textured wood because he wanted to fulfill his promise to Lin Yuan to make the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce into a rising faction.","He was surprised to see Lin Yuan support his idea and even provide him with precious goods that could be the star of the auction.","With sculptures made of jade-textured wood that are embedded with Cloud Dream Lake pearls in my possession, why am I still worried about management and publicity? All these issues will eventually be sorted out.","The Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce was immediately boosted to the same level as veteran factions with such cornerstone items.","Even though the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce could not compare with the veteran factions in any other way, they would be able to fake a style similar to that of the veteran factions.","Listen had recently built up their labor force as the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce had poached many of the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce’s employees. He had also been preoccupied working with Fei Qianqiong to buy up the resources that the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce was selling.","He was especially focused on buying up all the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce’s fey-related resources.","Initially, Listen had not planned on returning to the mansion that night.","However, the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce had received a letter, and Listen had no choice but to return to the mansion to show it to Lin Yuan.","Listen took the letter out of the Diamond fey storage box and gave it to Lin Yuan.","“Young Master, there’s something off about this letter. Please take a look.”","Lin Yuan received the letter from Lin Yuan doubtfully.","At first glance, Lin Yuan could not see any words written on the envelope.","The envelope had already been torn open. Clearly, Listen had taken a look at its contents.","When Lin Yuan looked at the letter’s contents, he frowned.","There was only one line written on the letter—”On the coastal sea off Indigo Azure City, Jiao Hanzhong of the Zheng family’s third lineage, Nightmare Squad of the Nightmare Squad, Zheng Kaiyuan.”","Lin Yuan thought deeply about these words as he passed the note to Wen Yu.","Lin Yuan asked Listen, “Do you know who sent this letter?”","“This letter was found in the body of a Silver Messenger Pigeon. This evening, a Silver Messenger Pigeon landed on the tree in the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce’s yard. It spat out this letter and was about to fly away when Big Brother Zhou captured it,” replied Listen.","Lin Yuan had come to a conclusion after some contemplation.","The Messenger Pigeon was a messenger-type fey, but because of Star Web, they were rarely used.","They were mostly used by factions who wanted to communicate secrets to each other.","The Messenger Pigeon had a nickname amongst the top factions—Anonymous Messenger Pigeon.","The Messenger Pigeon was extremely good at passing secrets around. If someone tried to pry the message from it, the Messenger Pigeon would automatically move its digestive muscles to destroy the message.","Lin Yuan concluded that given the Messenger Pigeon’s speed, it required nine days to travel from Indigo Azure City to the Royal Capital. Thus, the letter had been written soon after the incident occurred.","Since he had entrusted the secret of his identity to the Guard Envoy, the bad blood between him and the Zheng family had not been leaked out. Only the eyewitnesses were aware of the incident.","The eyewitnesses included the two Guard Envoys, Duan He, and the Indigo Azure Guard Captain.","Lin Yuan felt sure that none of them would bother with doing such a thing. Ergo, there was only one faction that knew the detailed truth of the matter.","Lin Yuan turned and said to Wen Yu, “It seems like the Zheng family’s internal affairs is a seemingly clear lake that’s hiding murky and insidious depths.”","“Young Master, the letter’s contents coincide with my investigation. Nightmare VI did belong to the Nightmare Squad. The nine members of the Nightmare Squad stick by the Zheng family’s three young masters. Nightmare VI was part of the team guarding the Second Young Master, Zheng Kaiyuan. Judging from the handwriting, if the writer wanted to give us information, he must be someone with a frail body. I can tell that the writer lacks strength from the writing force profile,” said Wen Yu.","Wen Yu studied the handwriting again and traced the paper with her hand. She could not help but feel that besides the first-word stroke, the rest of the word strokes were written higher than average. It was as though the writing hand had been resting atop something."]},{"number":579,"title":"Chapter 579 - The Involved Colossus","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan didn’t really mind this letter and message slip. He wasn’t interested to know who wrote the message either.","It didn’t matter if the owner of this message was an enemy or friend, the Zheng family was definitely the enemy.","Furthermore, the owner of this message slip wouldn’t send him this information without a reason. If there were any motives, they would certainly look for him again.","Lin Yuan was going to respond without action.","The Zheng family’s third lineage might have made a move on Listen, but Lin Yuan wasn’t going to put the blame on the Zheng main family because of the relationship between the Zheng main family and the third lineage.","However, the Zheng main family’s Second Young Master had already sent an emperor-class expert to make a move on him. It meant that Lin Yuan had finally fixed a grudge with the Zheng main family.","Lin Yuan wouldn’t have any hesitation when dealing with the enemy who wanted to kill him and his faction.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan still had the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen waiting for him to feed her with the willpower inside the Willpower Runes and the law inside the Law Runes.","Lin Yuan asked Wen Yu, “How much do you know about Zheng Kaiyuan?”","Wen Yu thought for a moment and said, “Zheng Kaiyuan is considered a rather special individual in the Zheng family. Zheng Kaiyuan’s Master is the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master, Miao Qi.","“Even though the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master Miao Qi doesn’t only have one disciple, Miao Qi views Zheng Kaiyuan with abnormal importance.","“At the same time, Zheng Kaiyuan’s mother, Miao Zhi, is also a core member of the elite faction, Miao family. Back then, because Miao Zhi married to the Zheng family’s current family head, it allowed the Zheng family to rise up from one of the weaker families to stand at the top of Indigo Azure City’s three major families.","“The pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master Miao Qi is the blood sister to Zheng Kaiyuan’s mother. Zheng Kaiyuan can address Miao Qi as Master and also his aunt.”","After the information Wen Yu provided, Lin Yuan lightly tapped his finger on the water rhinoceros leather sofa.","The Zheng family was actually involved with an elite faction.","When speaking about elite factions, they were factions that were significantly higher in level than the veteran factions.","They were considered the true colossus, just like the Gao family where Gao Feng was from. After developing their faction using the deep-sea resources, they had finally gained recognition from the other elite factions in the recent few years and had been promoted from a veteran faction to an elite faction.","The Miao family had been an elite faction for close to 30 years, and their foundation was obviously deeper than the Gao family.","The Zheng family’s Second Young Master, Zheng Kaiyuan, actually had the backing of the Miao family. As compared to the other descendants from veteran factions, he was truly worthy of being called noble.","“I remember the Zheng main family has three direct descendants. Since Zheng Kaiyuan is considered special, then what about the other two?”","When Wen Yu heard Lin Yuan’s question, her eyes lit up as she suddenly recalled the information she had read on the Zheng family’s main members in the Hidden Moon Pavilion after the accident happened to Lin Yuan.","“The Zheng family’s Eldest Young Master is the previous Zheng family head’s child. The previous Zheng family head is also the current Zheng family head’s elder brother. He has great combat talent and is greatly valued by the Zheng family’s old lord.","“As for the Third Young Master, he is the child of the current Zheng family head, but his mother isn’t Miao Zhi. As for the identity of the mother, it isn’t recorded as it is considered trivial information.","“It is said that the Third Young Master’s mother died after giving birth to the Third Young Master. As for the Third Young Master, he isn’t crippled by birth, but it is unknown why he has been sickly and sitting in a wheelchair all the time.","“Young Master, do you think the Zheng family’s Third Young Master sent the message?” After speaking, Wen Yu stuck out her tongue awkwardly and felt that her judgment was truly too subjective. How could she speculate based on written information?","Lin Yuan listened to the introduction of the three direct descendants of the Zheng family and silently clicked his tongue.","The relationship between the members of such prestigious families was truly complicated.","The reason Lin Yuan poured in so many precious and luxurious resources to Listen was that he planned to make a move on the Zheng family from a business method.","The Zheng family was a veteran faction whose business method was to use luxurious resources.","Lin Yuan might not be managing the daily operations of the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce, however, he had already set down its business direction together with Listen.","As the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce was getting developed, they were also going to be like burrowing insects. By using the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce as a medium, they would slowly penetrate into the Zheng family’s business empire.","As for the elite faction, the Miao family, Lin Yuan already had his plans.","In order for Sky City to develop, they would definitely have to offend veteran factions and elite factions during the process.","The Zheng family wouldn’t be the first veteran faction they offended. If the Miao family made a move on them, then the Miao family wouldn’t be the first elite faction either. No matter what, an act of revenge that should be taken shouldn’t be forgotten.","“Wen Yu, when you have time, help me check on an emperor-class expert called Duan He.”","Wen Yu was seriously noting down Lin Yuan’s request.","After finishing the serious discussion, Lin Yuan realized that Chu Ci had already fallen asleep on the sofa.","With proficiency since young, Lin Yuan carried Chu Ci and carried her into her room inside the mansion. He then placed her on the bed, took off her slippers, and gently pulled over the blanket for her.","Just as Lin Yuan was preparing to exit, he suddenly remembered that Chu Ci had the habit of waking up in the middle of the night and was afraid of the dark.","Lin Yuan then took a Five Fortune Ranchu out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone and placed it in a porcelain bowl before putting it on the bedside table.","The bedside had a decorative Black Back Mountain Boar, which was made of completely jade-textured wood. When it made contact with the spirit qi released from the Five Fortune Ranchu, it started to glow.","With the jade-like luster’s illumination, Chu Ci was sleeping soundly and even had a blissful smile.","After carrying Chu Ci back to her room, Lin Yuan started to work overtime.","The Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer had also returned to their rooms to diligently increase their strength.","Liu Jie went to the training room to familiarize herself with the transformed Insect Queen through live combat.","Lin Yuan logged into the Star Web and started searching in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion to set up and decorate the private territory.","Lin Yuan was very clear with what he wanted to search in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion, he immediately searched for the Starlight Grass and Floating Cloud Flower.","These were considered expensive plant-type feys. They might not have any functional use, but their prices were high based on their aesthetics.","Lin Yuan did his best to pick those Floating Cloud Flower and Starlight Grass that were of higher quality. Finally, he bought 36 Bronze/Elite Floating Cloud Flowers and 108 Bronze/Elite Starlight Grass.","There weren’t any Bronze/Flawless Floating Cloud Flowers or Starlight Grass.","However, Lin Yuan felt that it would be truly a loss to purchase Bronze/Flawless Floating Cloud Flowers or Starlight Grass. Just the mere difference in one grade of quality was enough to flip the price by at least 20 times.","Of course, Lin Yuan had picked the best out of the Elite quality Floating Cloud Flowers and Starlight Grass.","After selection, Lin Yuan didn’t pick any that was lower than Bronze VII."]},{"number":580,"title":"Chapter 580 - The Avian Cry That Echoed in the Entire Spirit Lock Spatial Zone","paragraphs":["After purchasing the Floating Cloud Flower and Starlight Grass, Lin Yuan also purchased all the feys that were required to set up the private territory in the Star Web.","However, Lin Yuan was still planning to look around to see if he could find a suitable fey for Zhou Luo’s third Willpower Rune.","After the search, Lin Yuan silently felt that Zhou Luo’s luck was truly good. He actually found a Decayed Mud Lizard.","Zhou Luo’s third Willpower Rune contained a willpower that was compatible with this Decayed Mud Lizard.","Furthermore, the Decayed Mud Lizard was a very rare mutated Swamp Lizard with dual types of earth and poison. It was considered a fey that would be missed out once you didn’t take this chance.","As a fey with earth/poison types, the Decayed Mud Lizard’s poison element could significantly increase Zhou Luo’s pitiful attack methods.","The Decayed Mud Lizard might not have any dragon-species bloodline and couldn’t evolve into a dragon-species fey, but during the process of evolution, there was a certain chance it might enhance its physical properties.","In terms of evolution direction, the Decayed Mud Lizard wouldn’t evolve into something weaker than a dragon-species fey.","Back when Lin Yuan was fighting the Star Web promotion matches, he had met the Dragon Gate Guild Club’s Chen Hongfeng. His main combat fey was a Gold Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard.","However, Chen Hongfeng’s Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard evolved from a Swamp Lizard instead of a Decayed Mud Lizard. Otherwise, Chen Hongfeng’s combat strength could be increased by another level.","This Decayed Mud Lizard had been in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion for an entire day. Plenty of people came to the Rare Lifeform Pavilion to make an earning by flipping feys and spiritual ingredients to earn profits.","The Decayed Mud Lizard had been in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion for an entire day, and someone should already take it. However, this Decayed Mud Lizard was an exception. It was due to the transaction price, and it wasn’t in Radiance dollars.","It was a rather rare kind of spiritual ingredient, the Sea Willow Branch. Furthermore, the requirement was for 50 catties.","As such, people who relied on flipping as a living couldn’t possibly take in this Decayed Mud Lizard. After all, they couldn’t possibly go find 50 catties of rarely traded Sea Willow Branch for this Decayed Mud Lizard, right?","What if this Decayed Mud Lizard was taken by someone else? Wouldn’t the Sea Willow Branches have to rot in their hands?","If the rarely traded Sea Willow Branches were stuck in their hands, their capital would be trapped, and they would be in trouble.","Lin Yuan didn’t hesitate and immediately accepted the deal.","Before dealing with the person, Lin Yuan still had to go search for the Sea Willow Branches first. However, during the group welfare auction, Master Duan Li had already staked a Fortune Sea Willow.","Lin Yuan merely had to go trim the Fortune Sea Willow and would have 50 catties of Sea Willow Branches.","After settling the deal, Lin Yuan logged out of Star Web and read a little in his room while he waited for Ostrich Logistics to deliver his purchases.","At that moment, Lin Yuan’s phone suddenly rang.","He looked at the phone and noticed it was actually Gao Feng.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help thinking in his heart, I just settled the deal with Gao Feng today. There wouldn’t be any accidents at Gao Feng’s side, right?","As soon as Lin Yuan picked up the call, he heard Gao Feng’s furious yell, “Lin Yuan, I am really angered to death!”","Lin Yuan was rather dumbfounded by Gao Feng’s furious yell. Why is he so angry at night? Did Gao Feng find out that he doesn’t have the family name of Gao and isn’t a direct descendant of the Gao family?","Before Lin Yuan could ask Gao Feng what happened, Gao Feng was already spilling the beans. “Lin Yuan, let me tell you. I, Gao Feng, have never been so angry since I was young. That damned Aquarium of Bliss. I merely asked a few more questions, and they actually dared!”","After hearing Gao Feng’s description, Lin Yuan had a strange expression and seemingly knew why Gao Feng was suddenly so angry.","“Why did you go to the Aquarium of Bliss at this late time?”","When Lin Yuan asked this question, he heard a teeth-grinding sound from the other end of the call.","Gao Feng didn’t answer Lin Yuan’s question. Instead, he answered evasively, “Lin Yuan, didn’t you ask me about the objective for setting up the marine fey breeding base? I haven’t thought of it before, but now I know what my objective is. I want to destroy the damned Sea Bliss Clan.”","Just as the enraged Gao Feng was going to berate the Sea Bliss Clan for the next minute, Lin Yuan asked in a calm voice, “Did you get kicked out of the Sea Bliss Clan’s Star Web private territory?”","Gao Feng felt a chill on his back as he asked in surprise, “Are you a fortune-teller? This incident just happened less than ten minutes ago. How did you know?”","Lin Yuan raised his brows and didn’t think he would actually guess it correctly.","The Gao family was an elite faction that was exploiting deep-sea resources. A veteran faction like the Sea Bliss Clan would probably target to befriend them.","If Gao Feng was the Gao family’s only direct descendant in the Gao family’s young generation, he would definitely be treated as a VIP if he visited the Aquarium of Bliss.","Lin Yuan thought that the only reason they would provoke Gao Feng was probably those attendants in the Star Web private territory that would simply kick people out without any good reasons.","Hearing how Gao Feng was so enraged and complaining to him, Lin Yuan felt that he should console Gao Feng a little.","Thus, he said, “The Aquarium of Bliss has also kicked me out. I cannot even enter their Star Web territory even if I want to now.”","As soon as Lin Yuan finished his statement, Gao Feng was in silence for a long time before he suddenly laughed heartily.","Lin Yuan had countless black lines appearing on his head. Is it that funny?","Immediately after, Lin Yuan listened to Gao Feng as he blabbered on about the plans of the breeding base and the nurturing direction of the marine feys.","While listening, Lin Yuan lamented silently. No wonder Gao Feng is a core descendant of an elite faction. His ability is definitely not inferior to his status.","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard a feminine yell from Gao Feng’s side. “Gao Feng, you disobedient child. Didn’t you promise this old lady that you will sleep before 12 a.m. every day!? It is already 2 a.m.! Do you need to make this old lady angry even on New Year’s!?","“Do you want me to call your father, who is sleeping like a pig now, so that he can teach you a lesson on what time to sleep!?”","After hearing the feminine yell, Lin Yuan heard Gao Feng’s embarrassed voice. “Brother, good night. Let’s talk again tomorrow.”","After finishing his statement, Gao Feng ended the call.","Lin Yuan clicked his tongue. Isn’t Gao Feng’s domestic discipline too strict!?","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan recalled the feminine voice that said it was already 2 a.m.","Lin Yuan lowered his head and couldn’t help feeling numb in his scalp as he felt it was terrifying. I actually talked over the phone with a man for two hours in the middle of the night. What is going on!?","After another 20 minutes, Ostrich Logistics delivered everything that Lin Yuan purchased from Star Web.","Lin Yuan then brought the thing straight to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","But as soon as Lin Yuan entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone, he realized that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree was burning with golden flames while an immortal-like avian cry echoed in the entire Spirit Lock spatial zone."]},{"number":581,"title":"Chapter 581 - Sparrow Swallowing the Luan","paragraphs":["When Lin Yuan heard the immortal-like avian cry, he immediately looked up at the golden nest that was on the branch of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree. The golden nest was like the sun that was brewing a radiant sunrise.","Just like the resplendent sunrise, the golden flames burning on the leaves of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree had been overshadowed.","A three-tailed cat was currently crouching on the snow-white Pure Land of Bliss. It was wagging its tails as it looked at the golden nest while its petite face was filled with happiness.","At that moment, the little cat’s ears twitched as it detected someone behind it. It immediately turned around and ran. In just a few steps, it entered Lin Yuan’s embrace and said with a meowing voice, “Yuan, Chimey is about to wake up!”","As Lin Yuan listened to Genius’ meowing voice that was filled with happiness and expectation, he placed Genius on his shoulder. He then rubbed Genius’ head and said, “Chimey’s awakening this time will be the most thorough transformation throughout the evolution journey.”","While speaking, Lin Yuan looked in the direction of the golden nest. He noticed that the sunrise-like radiance was covering his vision, and he couldn’t even see Chimey’s figure clearly within the bundle of radiance.","Apart from expectation, Lin Yuan was actually more worried about Chimey’s quality upgrading to Fantasy III.","Fundamentally, Chimey was actually just a Sound Bird that wasn’t even considered a fey. But due to Lin Yuan’s ability, it had evolved after receiving large amounts of pure spirit qi.","It meant that every step that Chimey took was actually a new frontier for the Sound Bird’s bloodline. Every step was an exploration of life that was filled with obstacles and troubles.","For a low-grade lifeform like Chimey that evolved with one step at a time, upgrading its quality as a Fantasy Breed was truly very difficult.","If Lin Yuan hadn’t coincidentally obtained the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree, which was suitable to upgrade Chimey’s quality, Lin Yuan wouldn’t dare to guarantee that he could help Chimey to reach Fantasy III at this moment, even with all the resources in his hands.","It was due to the fact that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree could purify the avian-type fey’s bloodline while upgrading its quality.","There was also a certain chance that it would allow the avian-type fey’s bloodline to mutate toward the luan[1]-species.","While making use of the upgrade to Fantasy III, it would allow Chimey to firm down on its bloodline. This obstacle could be said to be Chimey’s great obstacle in its evolutionary history.","If it made it across, it would be able to flap its wings and fly up into the clouds.","Given Genius’ wisdom, it was naturally able to understand Lin Yuan’s words. Genius then tensed up and asked nervously, “Yuan, will Chimey be in pain like its previous evolution?”","Genius still remembered how Chimey let out the painful mourns when it evolved into the Twilight Starbird. Furthermore, Lin Yuan had said that this was Chimey’s greatest transformation in its evolution, so it made Genius very worried.","Lin Yuan quickly replied, “Chimey’s evolution process might be painful, but the chances of accidents are very small.","“When a Fantasy Breed’s bloodline is getting purified during the evolution, it will rarely encounter any danger, unlike Myth Breed that will need to experience a World Cleansing with each upgrade of the quality and might be burned to ashes.","“Therefore, when Chimey is purifying its bloodline, it will only suffer a little at most.”","Genius finally felt at least and laid down on Lin Yuan’s shoulder. It then didn’t blink as it stared in the direction of the golden nest.","Lin Yuan was amazed by the relationship between Genius and Chimey.","At that moment, a concentrated luster was emitted, and Chimey’s figure was finally revealed.","At present, Chimey’s azure blue feathers had very distinctive cloud patterns, and even the stars within the cloud patterns were shining intensively.","All of a sudden, Chimey let out an abnormally painful cry as though its blood was getting drained.","After the painful cry, Chimey’s body was covered in a layer of resplendent sunlight again. But this time, the sunlight was able to conceal Chimey’s figure, but it couldn’t conceal the blood mist.","Upon seeing the blood mist inside the sunlight, Genius’ worried claws involuntarily extend out, scratching a deep tear on Lin Yuan’s spirit qi clothes.","Lin Yuan’s heart was also feeling the pain, but he couldn’t do anything. He knew that Chimey was going through a bloodline evolution that was mandatory.","Genius was a Hundred Questions Beast which also wasn’t considered a fey. When Genius evolved into a Fantasy Breed and upgraded to Fantasy III, it would also need to go through the same process as Chimey.","When the resplendent light reflected off the golden leaves on the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree, it looked exceptionally beautiful. However, Chimey didn’t stop its painful chirping, even for a moment.","Lin Yuan was sensitive enough to notice that Chimey’s painful cry suddenly had a special aura.","It was a similar kind of aura that was emitted when Blackie was awakening the flood-dragon-species bloodline.","However, the feeling of the aura was greatly different.","The aura emitted from Chimey was much purer than the aura emitted by Blackie.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up as he associated it with Chimey, which had been resting on the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree, allowing the luan-species bloodline to awaken in Chimey’s body.","For an avian-type fey to awaken the luan-species bloodline was considered a great fated opportunity.","It was the same for fish-species feys which had the chance to awaken the flood-dragon-species bloodline.","If the flood-dragon-species fey continued to upgrade, there would be a trace of chance to upgrade the bloodline into a true dragon-species bloodline.","If a luan-species fey continued to upgrade, there was a chance for it to upgrade into a phoenix-species bloodline.","Just as Lin Yuan thought that the luan-species bloodline was going to finish the evolution process, there was an accident. The aura and feeling from Chimey’s painful cry had changed.","There was an original bloodline that belonged to Chimey that burst out from Chimey’s body.","Chimey’s original bloodline was very weak as compared to the luan-species bloodline.","However, with Chimey’s willpower, the original bloodline wasn’t willing to be engulfed by the luan-species bloodline.","Instead, the sparrow power was clashing with the luan-species bloodline.","Lin Yuan immediately understood Chimey’s intention. Chimey was trying to consume the luan-species bloodline and make it into a part of its own bloodline.","Feeling Chimey’s insistence and changes in its body, Lin Yuan immediately knew it wasn’t good.","[1] The Luan is a mythical avian that is related to the Phoenix"]},{"number":582,"title":"Chapter 582 - Using the Evolution to Gold in Exchange for a Chance","paragraphs":["Chimey was using its own willpower to alter the original evolution path of its own bloodline. To a major extent, it was the same as disrupting one’s own evolution.","Inside the bundle of light, Lin Yuan felt that he could vaguely see Chimey’s body getting ripped and transformed by the luan-species bloodline in its body. It looked like Chimey was being crushed into a distorted meatball.","While seeing that Chimey was getting twisted and crushed into a meatball, Lin Yuan’s heart violently shrank. His thoughts were stunned for a moment too.","If Chimey’s body was in such circumstances, it would have already lost consciousness due to the intense pain. It also meant that everything that was happening was Chimey’s subconsciousness guiding its body’s Sound Bird bloodline to consume the Luan bloodline.","Lin Yuan suddenly remembered the time when Chimey evolved into the Stream Cloud Azure Bird in the Xia Region’s little fey store and how it was noisily chirping by his ears.","Chimey’s chirps might not be audible to most people, but Lin Yuan, who had formed a contract with Chimey, was able to understand the meaning of what Chimey was trying to say.","“Look, Yuan, isn’t my Sound Thrust incredible? Chimey’s singing is also so nice now, and I can also protect Yuan and Genius!”","Lin Yuan hadn’t really paid any mind to what Chimey was chirping about back then. After all, he was still unsure if he could become a combat-type spirit qi professional yet.","However, when Chimey had evolved into the Twilight Starbird, Lin Yuan had noticed that Chimey was very obstinate toward its Sound Bird bloodline, the unpopular sound-type.","Otherwise, when Chimey had evolved into the Twilight Starbird, it should have transformed into a light-type fey instead of keeping the original sound-type and becoming a dual sound/light type fey.","Chimey’s insistence on keeping its original Sound Bird bloodline was still there. In order to allow its Sound Bird bloodline to be preserved, it was frantically trying to use the Sound Bird bloodline to consume the Luan bloodline.","Toward Chimey’s insistence, Lin Yuan naturally had to give his support as Chimey’s contractor.","Lin Yuan had never treated Chimey just as his fey—he treated Chimey as his family.","Therefore, Lin Yuan couldn’t bring himself to alter Chimey’s subconscious choice as the contractor during the process of evolution. Otherwise, Lin Yuan could use his spiritual power and his status as the contractor to command Chimey’s subconsciousness to stop consuming the Luan bloodline with its Sound Bird bloodline. It would allow the Luan bloodline to consume the Sound Bird bloodline, making it a successful evolution.","Lin Yuan brandished his hand with anxiety as he activated the Pure Land of Bliss within the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The white sand that shone with a white jade luster was emitting a moist radiance. The moist radiance was just like pure white fireflies that flew out of the Pure Land of Bliss, and it was constantly gathering around the bundle of light that was enveloping Chimey. The moist radiance was nourishing and healing Chimey’s distorted body.","However, the Pure Land of Bliss’ capability to heal the damaged roots could only ensure that Chimey’s body wouldn’t be torn into pieces due to the violent resistance to the Luan bloodline. It couldn’t completely heal Chimey.","At that moment, Genius had gently leaped off Lin Yuan’s shoulder and looked at Chimey inside the bundle of light. Its worried eyes had already turned from blue to red now.","There were multiple occasions when Genius wanted to ask Lin Yuan about Chimey’s situation, but seeing that Lin Yuan was using the Pure Land of Bliss to heal Chimey, Genius didn’t dare to ask any questions that might distract Lin Yuan. It could only look at Chimey with bloodshot eyes.","Genius was putting its front paws together as though it was praying for Chimey to make it through this obstacle.","There was a stalemate of 15 minutes between the Pure Land of Bliss’ healing the roots and the damage from the Luan bloodline.","Lin Yuan realized that the Sound Bird bloodline might have been forced to withdraw by the Luan bloodline in the beginning, but thanks to the healing from Morbius’ Pure Land of Bliss and with Chimey’s subconsciousness constantly trying to use the Sound Bird bloodline to grind down the Luan bloodline, the Sound Bird bloodline had already absorbed a small portion of the Luan bloodline.","This gave Lin Yuan some hope, and it seemed like the Sound Bird bloodline could consume the Luan bloodline. Therefore, Lin Yuan immediately looked for the spirit qi crystals inside the button-shaped fey storage box.","Previously, when Lin Yuan used the spirit qi crystals to enhance the Jasmine Lily to Platinum/Fantasy III, only 71 spirit qi crystals were left.","Lin Yuan had also taken out another spirit qi crystal to help the Insect Queen to heal its injuries. As a result, before losing his consciousness in the dimensional rift, Lin Yuan had been left with 70 spirit qi crystals.","But when Lin Yuan had been unconscious, the Spirit Lock spatial zone produced two more new spirit qi crystals. As such, Lin Yuan now had a total of 72 spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan took 20 of the 72 spirit qi crystals and tossed them into the radiance that was enveloping Chimey.","Since Chimey wanted its Sound Bird bloodline to consume the Luan bloodline, then the only chance was the split moment when Chimey evolved to Gold/Fantasy, when its condition was at its best.","As the bundle of light eroded the 20 spirit qi crystals, the massive spirit qi burst out from the crystals and surged into Chimey’s distorted body.","When the 20 spirit qi crystals were injected along with the healing capability of the Pure Land of Bliss, it allowed Chimey’s body to have a split moment of vitality.","Chimey might not be letting out the painful cry anymore, but it was still possible to see that its body was constantly changing shape due to the conflicts of the two bloodlines.","As time passed by slowly, Lin Yuan felt that he didn’t have enough spiritual power to maintain the Pure Land of Bliss, so he was preparing to unseal the Spirit Qi Imprint on his body.","All of a sudden, an abnormally gentle and clear chirp echoed from the twilight.","Upon hearing this clear chirp, Lin Yuan felt as though he was basking in the clearest and most refreshing sunlight.","It allowed him to see the horizon of blue sky and the gentle splashes of a stream. He could hear the breeze, the moving clouds, the water dripping, the grass rustling, and the morning dew that was going to scatter.","Among all these natural sounds, the purest and the most wonderful sounds were actually blending together. However, they were still not as pleasant as this clear chirp.","The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s leaves that preserved more than 100 mid-grade strange flames suddenly shone along with the clear chirp.","Each leaf was sealed with a mid-grade strange flame that had different traits, and those traits determined the color of the flames.","Over 100 different colored flames made the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree turn into a golden immortal tree that had a rainbow aurora.","Inside the resplendent sunlight, the multi-colored mid-grade strange flames’ aurora was blending into a halo.","There was a pair of wings that was even brighter, overshadowing all the radiance."]},{"number":583,"title":"Chapter 583 - Fantasy III Clear Sound Luan Sparrow","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was once again shocked by the life miracle during the process of the fey evolution.","Chimey’s originally distorted body had now reverted into a blue sparrow. But this time, the feather on Chimey’s head didn’t grow longer. It actually became much more curled up than before.","Chimey’s feathers also had a much more intense azure blue. Previously, Chimey’s feathers were considered the purest blue in the natural world, but now, Lin Yuan already had no other descriptions for Chimey’s blue feathers.","When he took a glance at Chimey’s blue feathers, it felt like a patch of azure blue that came from the deepest cognition in his heart.","But after seeing Chimey’s post-evolution appearance, Lin Yuan couldn’t help raising his eyebrows. Why did Chimey evolve into such an unadorned look?","Right as Lin Yuan was having that thought, Chimey’s azure blue feathers suddenly burst out with mist. There was another clear chirp that was refreshing like the spring rain. At the same time, Chimey’s azure blue feathers turned into a golden gilt color.","The golden luster was like the warm radiance that was emitted during the winter solstice. On the back of Chimey, there were a few sudden appearances of feathers that had a purer gold pattern. They felt just like the sun of the winter solstice.","When Chimey’s extended its wings, the golden patterns were just like the sun.","The mist emitted from Chimey’s body was just like the clouds, and Chimey’s wings were just like a rising sun.","At the same time, Chimey’s originally sparrow-shaped tail had turned into a different shape.","Chimey’s body was only the size of half a palm, but the tail was now so long that it was at least the length of Lin Yuan’s arm.","Chimey’s previously short sparrow tail had now transformed into eight graceful tail feathers.","Each of the tail feathers had the same colors as Chimey’s wings, and they were filled with gorgeous cloud patterns.","The ends of the tail feathers had small impressions of stars, and when flying, it felt like eight shooting stars that flew across the starry sky.","When seeing this scene, Lin Yuan was certain that Chimey had used its Sound Bird bloodline to completely consume the Luan bloodline. Otherwise, Chimey wouldn’t be able to maintain the looks of a blue sparrow when it didn’t have any energy.","If Chimey was the ‘dawn among the stars in the cloud’ when it evolved into the Twilight Starbird previously, then it was now considered the ‘sun that shines brighter than the starry sky’.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’ True Data to check on Chimey’s attributes.","[Fey Name]: Clear Sound Luan Sparrow","[Fey Species]: Plume Sparrow genus/Luan species","[Fey Grade]: Gold (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Sound/Light","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy III","Abilities:","[Shattered Jade Sound]: Fire a giant musical note at the designated target that emits a beautiful jade-shattering sound. The jade-shattering sound has a certain disruption effect. When struck by the giant musical note, it will split into ten spiraling Sound Thrusts.","[Bathed in Light]: Bath the body in clear sunlight. When the sunlight shines on the body, it can quickly recover one’s exhausted vitality.","[Sunlight Rays]: Emits various rays from the sun that will cause negative weakening to the target. At the same time, the Sunlight Rays can help to increase a plant-type fey’s cellular activity.","[Nirvana Light Swansong]: Leaving just a trace of one’s vitality and sealing it inside the sun on the wings. The rest of the vitality will burn into sunlight energy. Before the sunlight energy vanishes, it will negate most of the physical and elemental damage.","Exclusive Skill:","[Clear Sky]: After a clear chirp, the clouds will disperse, summon the morning sun, and clear up the sky. The darkness will be repelled.","[Radiant Body]: Rapidly absorb the power of the sun and form a Radiant Body from the huge amount of solar energy gathered in the body.","After providing 20 spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan realized that Chimey had actually progressed to Gold I/Fantasy III.","Furthermore, Chimey’s name had changed from Twilight Starbird into Clear Sound Luan Sparrow.","The Luan was at the front, while the Sparrow was at the back, meaning that Sparrow was the main name.","Chimey had used its Sound Bird bloodline to suppress and consume the Luan-species bloodline that was extremely noble among the avian-type feys.","Chimey’s evolution was on an unprecedented path that no one walked on; even its bloodline was on a path that no other sparrow-species fey could walk on.","When Lin Yuan looked closely at Chimey’s abilities, his eyes couldn’t help widening. He noticed there was a significant change to the abilities after Chimey’s bloodline evolution.","Lin Yuan remembered that Chimey’s Normal ability, Sound Thrust, was supposed to form three thrusts of sound and fire them at the designated target. But now, Chimey’s first ability has turned into a shattered sound attack.","The shattered sound attack could send a giant musical note that had a jade-shattering sound.","This ability didn’t have any highlight by itself as the giant musical note could be easily blocked. However, Chimey’s giant musical note wasn’t actually an attack, it was meant for control.","After the control, the giant musical note would shatter, and the ten hidden spiral-shaped Sound Thrusts were the killing factor.","The transformation of Chimey’s Normal ability was already a pleasant surprise for Lin Yuan. However, after seeing the Elite ability, Bathed in Light, Lin Yuan frowned a little.","Previously, Chimey’s Elite ability wasn’t Bathed in Light but Scattered Light.","Chimey could allow its body to emit scattered rays of light, allowing them to have scorching and control effects.","The control and scorching effects of the Scattered Light might not be powerful, but they were increasing the attack methods for Chimey.","Now that Scattered Light had turned in Bathed in Light, the attack and control ability had turned into an endurance ability.","But when talking about healing capability, Lin Yuan was already a healing-type spirit qi professional.","In terms of grade, Lin Yuan’s Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade) had already reached Platinum/Fantasy III.","Even though the Jasmine Lily’s path as a healing-type fey wasn’t very proper, one had to admit that it was considered one of Lin Yuan’s strongest fey.","The Jasmine Lily was enough for Lin Yuan to effectively heal most of his own feys.","As for the Silver ability, Sunlight Rays, there wasn’t much difference as compared to before. However, it had an additional trait which was to increase the cellular activity of plant-type feys.","Seeing this ability, Lin Yuan immediately thought of Red Thorn.","It wasn’t just Red Thorn; even the sea of flowers produced by Red Thorn were also plant-type feys. To increase the plant-type feys’ cellular activity was to increase their regenerative ability. It was a rather good synergy with the Red Thorn’s sea of flowers."]},{"number":584,"title":"Chapter 584 - Chimey’s Mantra","paragraphs":["As Chimey used Sunlight Rays to attack the enemy unit, if the latter had Red Thorn’s spread sea of flowers beside them, then the sea of flowers’ overall combat ability would also be improved under the increased activity of Sunlight Rays.","When Lin Yuan checked Chimey’s newly gained ability of Nirvana Light Swansong after evolving to Gold/Fantasy, he subconsciously patted his forehead with his hand.","Lin Yuan shook his head helplessly, glancing at Chimey, which was flying toward him joyfully and preparing to land on his outer ear.","It was understandable during Chimey’s evolution that it stubbornly persisted in its Sound Bird bloodline, but when had it become so reckless?","Its Nirvana Light Swansong could burn all the vitality in Chimey’s body into sunlight energy, which was equivalent to providing it with a means to exchange vitality for a means to injure through an explosion.","When used in conjunction with its Radiant Body, it could directly erupt with multiple attack tactics.","Moreover, before Chimey’s vitality-turned-sunlight energy disappeared, it would be immune to most physical and elemental damage.","After using Nirvana Light Swansong to enter Radiant Body, Chimey’s defensive ability would be greatly improved. This allowed it to deflect the enemy’s attacks and counterattack to the maximum extent.","Of course, Nirvana Light Swansong’s defensive ability did not protect from mental damage or poison.","Nevertheless, being immune to most physical and elemental damage was enough.","Lin Yuan suddenly felt that Chimey’s Bathed in Light no longer seemed useless upon seeing the Nirvana Light Swansong ability.","Its Bathed in Light could effectively supplement the Nirvana Light Swansong ability to limit the shortcomings of Chimey’s vitality to a mere wisp.","Together with the Jasmine Lily’s healing ability, this could speed up Chimey’s recovery process and very likely allow Chimey to launch a second attack in a battle.","Chimey’s Radiant Body had not undergone many changes.","Nevertheless, in Lin Yuan’s eyes, Clear Sky had changed a fair bit.","Previously, its exclusive skill, Clear Sky, did nothing more than let the dark clouds recede and clear the sky, which strongly affected water-type attacks.","However, besides clearing the sky, Clear Sky could now also evoke the rising sun.","When it was a Silver/Fantasy Breed, Chimey’s Clear Sky had only allowed the light of stars to shine in the sky when used at night.","Now, when Chimey used its exclusive skill, Clear Sky could make the entire sky bloom with sunlight, such that even if it was fighting at night, Bathed in Light could also play a role.","At the same time, Lin Yuan thought that Clear Sky seemed to have become a little special after the evolution.","True Data had shown that Clear Sky could evoke the rising sun, which was naturally impossible for Gold/Fantasy Breed feys.","Currently, Chimey could only summon daylight at night at best.","However, if it evolved to Myth Breed when it used Clear Sky, would it be able to evoke the sun at night and transform the darkness into light?","Clear Sky’s new effect of causing darkness to fade away made Lin Yuan scratch his head.","It seemed that Clear Sky could even restrain dark-type feys now.","Lin Yuan had gone through Chimey’s abilities and exclusive skills so many times that he was extremely familiar with them. Yet, their concrete effects in battle could clearly not be demonstrated in his Spirit Lock spatial zone.","If Lin Yuan let Chimey use its Nirvana Light Swansong ability now, followed by its Radiant Body, as an impact test of their attack ability in his Spirit Lock spatial zone, it would be equivalent to Lin Yuan demolishing his Spirit Lock spatial zone himself.","He felt that he couldn’t be doing things like demolishing houses. After all, he was not a husky.","Chimey flew to Lin Yuan’s outer ear and pecked at Lin Yuan’s stray strands of hair affectionately before rubbing his cheek with its little head.","When Chimey was rubbing Lin Yuan’s cheek, it saw that Genius was looking at it worriedly with bloodshot eyes, so it immediately jumped on Genius’ head.","There, Chimey used its exquisite beak to comb Genius’ fluffy fur. It then proceeded to cry out like its old tittering chatterbox self.","However, while Chimey’s previous calls were all in birdsong, they were now all in fluent Mandarin.","“Yuan! Yuan! Yuan! Genius! Genius! Genius!","“Yuan! Yuan! Yuan! Genius! Genius! Genius!”","Lin Yuan had previously already discovered that Chimey was fond of calling out six times no matter the time.","Even if Lin Yuan’s intentions were the same as Chimey’s, the latter obviously called out without using its brain.","Lin Yuan was also unable to use his spiritual energy to clearly discern the intended meaning of Chimey’s calls.","He had always taken Chimey’s six calls to be its mantra.","However, now that Chimey could speak coherently, Lin Yuan finally understood.","It turned out that the six calls that he had taken to be Chimey’s mantra were actually three calls of his name and three of Genius’.","Originally, Lin Yuan had wanted to wait and see if Chimey would still be unable to speak coherently after evolving to Fantasy III. If that happened, he had planned to coach it properly.","However, Chimey could now communicate like any other person.","Moreover, Chimey’s human voice could not be rejected by any voice-activated device.","Its human voice was not only pleasing to the ear but also brimming with spirit qi, lending it a bubbly tone.","This made anyone who heard it feel unusually at ease. A refreshing sensation would wash over the person as if they were sitting in the grass and looking up at a blue sky bathed in sunlight.","Lin Yuan extended a finger in Chimey’s direction, and the bird immediately flew toward it.","With the plumy feathers on its head scratching Lin Yuan’s palm, Chimey said, “Yuan, Yuan, Chimey had had a lot of dreams while sleeping. 80% of Chimey’s dreams were about you and Genius.”","Having said that, Chimey suddenly felt uneasy and did not continue.","It wouldn’t reveal what the other 20% of its dreams were about, even if beaten to death; they were about its own Star Web live streams.","Although Chimey had successfully evolved and ventured into uncharted territory in terms of its bloodline and evolution, Lin Yuan still felt unusually anxious whenever he thought about Chimey’s previous evolution process.","Looking at Chimey, Lin Yuan asked a question that he had always been meaning to pose, “Chimey, why do you care so much about the Sound Bird bloodline inside you?”","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, Chimey subconsciously thought about one rainy evening.","Its entire body had been dirty when a young man stored it in a cardboard box and brought it home.","Back then, the young man had used a handkerchief to dry its rain-soaked feathers before beaming at it with his white teeth.","“Don’t lose heart, little buddy. Can I call you Chimey? I’ll definitely teach you a song.”","To Chimey, the young man’s encouragement had been a ray of light in its avian existence. It was also the brightest ray of light Chimey had ever seen.","Even the radiant sunlight that Chimey had released during its evolution could not compare to the dazzling light of the strength that the young man had given it.","Because that ray of light had been its salvation when Chimey had been treated as garbage after failing to evolve and being sold as an add-on due to its inability to qualify as a commodity.","This redemptive light had given Chimey a warm home in its icy-cold world.","Chimey landed on Lin Yuan’s outer ear again and whispered, “Because Chimey wants to always be able to stand on Yuan’s outer ear and sing for Yuan and Genius, just like before.","“Sing Yuan and Genius’ favorite songs.","“Sing the song that Yuan taught me over and over back then!”"]},{"number":585,"title":"Chapter 585 - The Best Songstress in the Universe","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Upon hearing this, a smile immediately bloomed on Lin Yuan’s face.","“Chimey, I remember that you asked me to teach you how to sing songs before your deep sleep. Coincidentally, I have a song that I want to teach you.”","After speaking, Lin Yuan began to hum.","Once Chimey heard that Lin Yuan wanted to teach it how to sing, its eyes instantly lit up.","“Drops of dew land on my sleeves,","The delicate sun shines gently on the lotus boat,","As the reeds sway, swallows and sparrows twitter,","Between the white rocks at the creek’s edge, the setting sun chases the flowing stream.","Yet, blame the autumn wind and the green leaves for the long journey.","With hearts aligned and shared plans,","We scale the rugged roads, guarding each other.","A hundred years I spend with you from dusk till dawn,","Surrounded by rivers and mountains, scenery of old.","And in my eyes, your beauty surpasses that of the breathtaking landscape.”","Chimey leaped from Lin Yuan’s outer ear to his shoulder, listening carefully to every note in the melody of Lin Yuan’s song with its head tilted.","It could be said that as a Sound Bird, Chimey’s first teacher had always been one person, and that person was none other than Lin Yuan.","However, ever since Chimey had begun live streaming on Star Web without informing Lin Yuan, it felt as though it had done something wrong with regard to learning how to sing.","Hence, every time Lin Yuan sang, Chimey could never work up the courage to tell him that it wished to learn how to sing. It could only rely on its natural musical talent as a Sound Bird to learn Lin Yuan’s songs secretly.","However, the feeling of learning in secret was completely different from that of receiving Lin Yuan’s voluntary teaching honestly as it perched on his shoulder.","Chimey’s small brain could not help but think about how Lin Yuan would feel when he received its surprise box next year.","Nevertheless, Chimey had a premonition that its online cover as Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess would soon be blown.","Chimey could not remember how long it had slept to evolve its bloodline, and it didn’t know if its fans on Star Web still remembered it.","Previously, when Chimey had been singing on Star Web, it would only sing, never uttering a single word beyond the lyrics.","Suddenly, Chimey had the idea of greeting its audience in the live-streaming room the next time it did a live stream.","However, before Chimey could solidify its thoughts, it became completely enraptured by Lin Yuan’s crooning.","As a Sound Bird, Chimey had a strong talent for music engraved in its genetics.","Naturally, it had its own understanding and preferences when it came to music and could easily differentiate between good and bad songs.","This song that Lin Yuan was currently teaching was surprisingly similar to the first song he had tirelessly taught.","The more Chimey listened, the more moved it became. It began flapping its wings and dancing in midair to Lin Yuan’s voice.","At that moment, Genius climbed on Lin Yuan’s shoulder and lay down quietly as though it couldn’t get cozier, enjoying the rare peace of the years.","Genius and Lin Yuan had ventured into a dimensional rift once and survived.","It could be said that surviving inside the dimensional rift had been an afterthought at that time.","This had caused Genius to mature significantly.","After that calamity, Genius had seen Chimey wake up from a deep slumber and felt unusually fortunate.","Nevertheless, Genius now suddenly noticed two scratches on the cloth at Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","Genius soon realized that these two scratches had been made as it had been watching Chimey’s body being mashed into a fleshy ball. Genius had accidentally scratched the fabric with one of its sharp claws within its pink paw pad.","Genius immediately used its small paw pad to rub the area on Lin Yuan’s shoulder where the fabric had been scratched like a child who had done something wrong.","As it rubbed, Genius lowered its head, opened its mouth, and exhaled two soft breaths.","Learning from how Lin Yuan had been taking care of it when it was younger, it murmured softly in its heart, “Yuan, after Genius blows on this, it won’t hurt any longer.”","After singing the song from his memory, Lin Yuan grew quiet.","Although his singing could not be considered very good, it was still better than average.","Moreover, Lin Yuan had a habit when he listened to songs; he would firmly remember the lyrics to his favorite songs.","Hence, Lin Yuan knew most of the words to the songs that he knew how to sing. While he might not have remembered a few of the words, he would still fill in his own lyrics based on the song’s melody and meaning.","After hearing Chimey’s human voice just then, Lin Yuan had thought that it would still have been most suitable for singing traditional-style songs.","The rhetoric of such songs was elegant and graceful, like fragrant tea with a light wine.","In its refreshing tranquility, there was a subtle but meaningful charm.","Lin Yuan had long known that Chimey enjoyed singing. Now, he knew that it really liked learning songs too. Thus, he decided to periodically teach Chimey traditional-style songs from his repertoire.","It was very easy to teach Chimey as it was a Sound Bird. Lin Yuan only needed to sing a song once before Chimey mastered the fundamentals of the piece.","Upon seeing Chimey flapping its wings in rapture, Lin Yuan asked with a smile, “How much has Chimey remembered? Do you still need me to repeat it again?”","Upon hearing this, Chimey immediately spread its wings and landed on the cinnamon stick of the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","Because the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus had received a large amount of pure spiritual power in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and had been bathed in World Grace when planted on the Pure Land of Bliss, its originally sparse branches were now blossoming with sweet-smelling, vermilion osmanthus.","Chimey landed like the last bundle of rice straw that would crush a camel.","The osmanthus that had barely been clinging to the branches fell down, beginning a colorful rain of red flowers.","The faint fragrance of osmanthus permeated the air, its sweetness making the air a little gentler.","At that moment, Chimey learned Lin Yuan’s tune and began to sing softly.","Upon hearing Chimey’s voice, Lin Yuan was immediately drawn to it.","A painting surfaced in his mind.","In other words, Lin Yuan himself seemed to have stepped into the painting, becoming the person inside it who was admiring the scenery before him.","He saw a young girl in front of him, rowing a boat under the bright sun.","“Love songs are sung elegantly,","Picking lotus and living,","From day to night,","Spring and autumn together.”","By the white banks of the creek, she would wait for her lover’s return, begging the easterly wind’s tenderness to reunite them.","Lin Yuan had long grown accustomed to Chimey’s singing voice, but he was still taken aback by its evolved voice.","Now that Chimey had learned to speak like a human, both its voice and technique had improved greatly.","Even its clear enunciation made the entire song come alive.","If Chimey’s voice had been comparable to those grand singers in Lin Yuan’s previous life in all aspects before evolving, it was now so beautiful that it would have been named the Best Songstress in the Universe by music fans.","Even the Trisolaran natives would love flowers and peace if they heard the sound of Chimey’s singing.","Nevertheless, it was also at that moment that Lin Yuan’s heart suddenly quivered.","He had seen the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia on the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus falling in the rain of flowers.","This scene implanted itself in Lin Yuan’s eyes, making him feel as though his life was being shaken to the core.","He quickly stepped forward and used True Data to scan the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia’s attributes."]},{"number":586,"title":"Chapter 586 - Evolve, Acid Corrosion Queen Bee!","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan immediately felt at ease wIth one glance and revealed a delighted expression.","By looking at True Data, Lin Yuan knew that the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia had fallen from the branch of the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus not because something was wrong with it but because it had accumulated enough energy to evolve to Platinum.","It had become a fully-grown Heaven and Earth Fey that could now bear fruit and no longer needed to rest on the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ branch.","Everything in nature was dependent on each other, and there was always a give-and-take relationship, just like the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia and the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","While the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus had been using its own energy and nutrition to cultivate the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia all this while, it did so not out of selflessness. Its main reason for doing so was because the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia was like a child to it.","In other words, the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia was its fruit.","As a parasitic-type Heaven and Earth Fey, the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia was not very intelligent.","However, it still knew that someone was looking out for it.","Now, Lin Yuan was witnessing the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia flee to produce its own fruit after sucking the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ energy.","Lin Yuan just wanted to say that the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia was worried for nothing, and the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus was looking out for nothing...","Because the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ child could only be Lin Yuan’s.","Lin Yuan dug a hole in the white Sandy Soil of the Pure Land of Bliss and placed the mature Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia within it.","Then, he summoned the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope with a wave of the hand and said to it, “When you see that the small buds on this turn from green to silver, pluck a few of them.”","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope understood Lin Yuan’s meaning and nodded its small head.","Stroking the antelope’s head, Lin Yuan looked at the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia and thought, With the big housekeeper here, don’t think about keeping your children.","Lin Yuan had initially wanted to return to his Spirit Lock spatial zone to do some work and hadn’t expected to be just in time to see Chimey’s evolution.","Now, it was about 3:00 a.m., close to 4:00 a.m. in the middle of the night.","Nevertheless, Lin Yuan still felt that he had enough time.","After inspecting the 52 remaining spirit qi crystals by his side, he pondered for a moment and directly summoned Red Thorn from the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","He planned to take advantage of Chimey’s evolution to evolve the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee from Gold I/Legend to Platinum to make up for Red Thorn’s Sea of Flowers combat ability, giving the assassins hidden in the Sea of Flowers better killing opportunities.","After experiencing the danger in the dimensional rift, Lin Yuan had gained a kind of cognition.","Since he had spirit qi crystals on hand, there would be no harm in maximizing his own strength.","The number of spirit qi crystals needed to evolve the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee from Gold I/Legend to Platinum I/Legend was roughly equivalent to that needed to evolve a Silver/Fantasy fey to Gold/Fantasy.","Hence, Lin Yuan would still be left with around 30 spirit qi crystals after evolving the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","This would be more than enough for daily consumption.","After plundering a fey’s World Cleansing and obtaining a large quantity of spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan’s view of the spirit qi crystals had also changed subtly.","Unlike in the past, he no longer kept careful tallies of his collection of spirit qi crystals.","Moreover, he had already planned in his heart to let Pure Land of Bliss engage in a wave of World Grace again.","After coming up with this idea, Lin Yuan concluded that he was the Myth Breed feys’ most hated type of person.","The Pure Land of Bliss was akin to greedy Myth Breed feys and seemed to undergo the World Grace that descended after World Cleansing.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was the Law Crystal in the greedy Myth Breed feys’ bodies.","Thinking about it this way, Lin Yuan did find himself rather annoying.","He might even change his name from Lin Yuan to Annoying Lin.","Now, he still had one unused Willpower Rune in his spiritual energy.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, Genius, and Blackie were all stuck at Bronze X/Legend because there wasn’t a suitable Willpower Rune for them to evolve to Fantasy Breed.","Moreover, Red Thorn could only evolve upon consuming flesh and blood.","Hence, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, Genius, Blackie, and Red Thorn were all unable to enjoy the spirit qi crystals.","Now, the only feys that could consume spirit qi crystals were the Jasmine Lily, Chimey, the Source Sand, and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Chimey and the Source Sand had already evolved to Gold/Fantasy Breed, so they needed to consume 10 spirit qi crystals just to evolve a small grade.","Lin Yuan admitted that he simply could not afford to feed them any longer.","Even if the Jasmine Lily were to squeeze Lin Yuan dry now, it would only be able to evolve one small grade.","Hence, Lin Yuan could only cultivate the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee now as it was the only fey he could afford to cultivate.","After being summoned by Lin Yuan, Red Thorn’s smooth vine wrapped around Lin Yuan’s waist and refused to loosen its grip.","Its Mouth of Relinquish was even issuing a roaring noise.","Needless to say, Lin Yuan knew that Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish was rapidly digesting the flesh and blood of water world dimensional lifeforms at present.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan summon Red Thorn, Chimey and Genius landed on either side of Red Thorn’s gill-shaped petals.","The gill filaments on Red Thorn’s gill-shaped petals opened directly such that the red flowers’ original one-meter diameter was now more than doubled.","The gill filaments shrouded Genius and Chimey like a gauze net before swaying lightly.","This allowed Genius and Chimey to swing on the gill filaments comfortably.","Lin Yuan touched Red Thorn’s smooth vine with his hands and suddenly felt that it was unusually smooth.","He said, “Red Thorn, call the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.”","Upon receiving Lin Yuan’s order, Red Thorn immediately shook its Mouth of Relinquish, and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee sleeping inside toppled out like trash from a bin.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee pounced on Red Thorn like a ‘simp’ instead of being upset.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help getting chills as he watched the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s performance.","In his heart, he viewed the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee as an artist.","It was a source-type lifeform that had completely mastered the art of ‘simping’.","Lin Yuan extended his hand to pinch the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s fluttering wings, bringing it before him.","He inspected its grade.","After which, his brows raised in surprise.","Previously, after Lin Yuan had just strengthened the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, it had only evolved to Gold I.","He didn’t know how much the bee had drunk in Red Thorn’s belly that it had actually evolved to Gold IV during this period.","After being restrained by Lin Yuan, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee appeared obviously reluctant.","Nevertheless, once it thought about Red Thorn’s attitude toward Lin Yuan, its reluctance vanished instantly. Instead, it thought about how it could soften its wings so that Lin Yuan could pinch them more comfortably.","Lin Yuan cut to the chase, immediately taking out and crushing 16 spirit qi crystals.","The abundance of pure spiritual power spiraled toward the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee,","letting it directly evolve to Platinum/Legend.","The evolution of Normal feys was completely different from that of Fantasy Breed feys.","Nevertheless, Lin Yuan found the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s posture a bit abnormal as it evolved.","It was even comparable to Chu Ci’s Sharp Iron Horn Bull when it evolved to a Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull."]},{"number":587,"title":"Chapter 587 - Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s Transformation","paragraphs":["The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s original length was only about 15 centimeters long.","Its slender body had a dark red metallic luster, and strange dark green markings with a cruel and hideous beauty were hidden underneath its body.","Suddenly, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s back became illusory.","This illusionary effect wasn’t because its wings vibrated too fast for Lin Yuan to see its actions clearly. Instead, it was because the dark red and green markings on the bee’s body were constantly fading.","It was as though the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was peeling off the color inside its body bit by bit.","Immediately afterward, the bee’s metallic color intensified.","This strong metallic luster made the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee appear transparent.","At that moment, it seemed to have become the metallic surface of a mirror.","Lin Yuan could still see the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s existence even though his focus was on the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","However, its presence was undoubtedly greatly reduced.","Lin Yuan thought, If the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee flies amidst the flowers formed by Red Thorn’s child ramets, its mirror-like body will reflect the flowers, allowing it to hide perfectly in the flowers as an assassin waiting to kill its target.","Moreover, the two bee needles on the bee’s forelimbs had also become more slender.","The tip of the sharp needles now had a penetrating cold light. Obviously, its penetration ability and sharpness had been greatly improved.","Nevertheless, in Lin Yuan’s eyes, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s biggest transformation had occurred in the two stingers behind its tail.","Its stingers had shortened significantly, appearing far less threatening than they had before.","However, Lin Yuan noticed that the bee’s two stingers had each become sectioned into two upon close inspection.","His eyebrows raised slightly. Then, he waved his hand lightly.","The amber-button-shaped Source Sand by his wrist landed on the ground, transforming into tumbling quicksand.","This quicksand accumulated at Lin Yuan’s feet, protecting him like a guard.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s evolution was now complete. It had become a Platinum/Legend fey.","After a moment’s thought, Lin Yuan ordered, “Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, use your exclusive skill, Two-Strike Kill, against this wall of sand.”","He pointed in the direction of his feet before immediately shaping the Close Guard Sand into a wall.","The Source Sand had already completely digested the Mountain-Containing Embryo.","However, after digesting the Mountain-Containing Embryo, the Source Sand had not evolved to Fantasy III as expected.","It appeared that to evolve the Source Sand to Fantasy III in the future, it needed to undergo a huge transformation.","Lin Yuan still needed to exert another round of effort.","Nevertheless, when the Source Sand had evolved to Fantasy II, Lin Yuan had been delighted upon seeing the Close Guard Sand that it had spawned.","It could be said that in terms of defensive ability, the Close Guard Sand was second only to his four wings of Day and Night Spirit Silver.","Upon receiving Lin Yuan’s order, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee did not fly toward the sand wall as it would have done before. Instead, its tail lifted, and two earth-shattering sounds immediately echoed.","Lin Yuan saw two short and small stingers appear in the Close Guard Sand’s wall.","He immediately looked at the bee’s tail and saw that each stinger now only had one section left of the original two.","After its attacking blow, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was obviously quite weakened.","However, under Lin Yuan’s gaze, the one-section stingers again grew until there were two sections.","After looking up from the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s tail, Lin Yuan was shocked to find that the central area of the Close Guard Sand’s wall had disappeared.","It had turned into a stream of liquid.","Clearly, the poison in those two stingers had disintegrated the Source Sand’s simple elemental body.","The Source Sand was now Gold I/Fantasy II and about to evolve to Gold I/Fantasy III, while the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a Platinum I source-type lifeform.","In terms of grade and quality, the Source Sand was stronger.","Furthermore, when Lin Yuan had been cultivating the Source Sand, an elemental source-type item, he had made it follow the defensive route.","Even so, the Close Guard Sand containing high-purity ferromanganese still disintegrated into liquid.","If the stingers stung a body of flesh and blood, one could only imagine the effects...","Previously, in the Star Web battle, Lin Yuan had commanded the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to use Two-Strike Kill.","However, at that time, while Lin Yuan had discovered Two-Strike Kill’s destructive power, he had uncovered its limitation at the same time.","The latter being that Two-Strike Kill required the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to fly close to the target and pierce its two tail stingers into the same position on it.","In combat, this could be said to be an extremely demanding requirement.","Nonetheless, as the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had evolved to Platinum, its Two-Strike Kill had also become more flexible.","Lin Yuan used True Data to scan the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s attributes.","[Fey Name]: Acid Corrosion Queen Bee","[Fey Species]: Vespidae/Bactrocera","[Fey Grade]: Platinum (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Poison","[Fey Quality]: Legend","Abilities:","[Wing Stealth]: Flaps its wings at high frequency. The fast-flapping reflective wings allow the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to be stealthy.","[Bone-Penetrating Stingers]: The super-hard and impactful rotating stingers rapidly cause deep injuries.","[Parasitic Pupa]: The stingers on the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s forelegs can release a fast-hatching parasitic pupa into the target’s body while stinging.","[Acid-Swallowing Larvae]: With sufficient acid, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee will hatch numerous Acid-Swallowing Larvae that can be used as food for it to rapidly restore its consumed energy and venom reserves. At the same time, the Acid-Swallowing Larvae will replicate part of the Acid-Swallowing Queen Bee’s mother genes so that if the latter dies, the former can activate the genes to become the new mother.","[Acid Corpse Poison Bee]: A large amount of acid in the body is consumed to produce an Acid Corpse Poison Bee, which will reside in the body of a dead lifeform or dimensional lifeform and control the latter’s actions. These Acid Corpse Poison Bees will turn into Poison Silkworm Pupae again if the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee does not activate them.","Exclusive Skill:","[Two-Strike Kill]: The two abdominal stingers contain two different kinds of acid-corrosion venom. If the abdominal stingers hit the same part of the target, the two types of venom will instantly disintegrate the target’s part.","Lin Yuan had initially planned to look at the Platinum Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s newly-comprehended abilities.","However, he was drawn instead to its Gold ability, the Acid-Swallowing Larvae."]},{"number":588,"title":"Chapter 588 - Sure Enough, It Took After Its Mother","paragraphs":["The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had not evolved to Fantasy Breed, so its abilities had not changed as they would have when a fey evolved to Fantasy Breed.","When an ordinary fey evolved, there was only a very small chance that its abilities would improve.","However, it was still something that Lin Yuan, someone who evolved feys as a form of practice, had encountered before.","When the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee evolved to Platinum, the change of its Gold ability, Acid-Swallowing Larvae, was rather unusual.","If the Blade Queen Bee’s Blade Worms that Lin Yuan had encountered in the dimensional rift had possessed this ability, then it was very likely that Zhou Luo would not have been able to survive.","Lin Yuan could not help but wonder if the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had understood the true meaning of ‘simping’ when it ‘simped’ after Red Thorn.","It had gone from an outstanding ‘simp’ to one that wasn’t afraid of death.","Moreover, this ‘simp’ that wasn’t afraid of death had also mastered the ability to reincarnate from the soil.","This enabled the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to become an assassin that was more terrifying than a terrorist specializing in suicide attacks.","Who knew how many Acid-Swallowing Larvae the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had already stored in Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish?","These Acid-Swallowing Larvae gave the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee the freedom to happily balance on the edge between life and death.","The bee could even use its larvae as a tool in combat.","During a battle, Red Thorn could transport its larvae through the channel formed by Red Thorn’s child ramets.","By dying and being rebirthed through the Acid-Swallowing Larvae, it could then launch a sneak attack on its target.","With this thought, Lin Yuan felt his hair stand on end.","Lin Yuan gazed at it in astonishment once again upon checking the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s Gold ability. He felt that the bee was not only a ‘simp’ that was unafraid of death but also a super fan who spent no money.","As the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a parasite in Red Thorn, it could ‘simp’ for the latter without expending any of its own resources.","Being a Queen Bee, it indeed had the ability to produce larvae.","It was just that the Acid-Swallowing Larvae were only being used as rations.","It was difficult for any Parasitic Pupa that incubated inside its target’s body to escape being consumed by the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee after coming out of incubation.","It was clearly a queen bee, but it acted like a commander without an army.","Moreover, its Platinum ability, Acid Corpse Poison Bee, was what gave it the opportunity to have the minions that it had now.","However, the birth of these minions required it to leech off of other feys’ bodies.","To Lin Yuan, the Acid Corpse Poison Bee was worthy of being the child of the parasitic-type, source-type Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Sure enough, it took after its mother, sharing the same virtues as the latter.","Lin Yuan planned to test the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s Platinum ability.","Lin Yuan thought that the Acid Corpse Poison Bee’s decision to be a fan that didn’t spend money was rather strategic.","Not only could it reside in the bodies of dead feys, but it could also reside in those of dead dimensional lifeforms.","Compared to those of feys of the same grade, the bodies of dimensional lifeforms were always stronger.","Lin Yuan did not know if it was because the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a source-type lifeform or because the Acid Corpse Poison Bees that it produced could adapt itself to the highly acidic, highly toxic, and highly corrosive internal environment in the dimensional lifeform,","but In short, the Acid Corpse Poison Bee’s adaptability was truly good news for Lin Yuan.","It was just that, at the moment, Lin Yuan didn’t know what kind of dead dimensional lifeforms would be the most suitable for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to produce the Acid Corpse Poison Bee in.","Suddenly, his eyes lit up. What about water world dimensional lifeforms?","Lin Yuan currently didn’t possess any strong underwater combat capabilities. Could he use this method to make up for it?","Lin Yuan immediately rejected this idea.","While the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was in Red Thorn’s body, the two could be seen as a single existence.","The dimensional lifeforms in which the Acid Corpse Poison Bees fed were undoubtedly suitable for fighting among the flowers.","If he used water world dimensional lifeforms, they wouldn’t be able to support Red Thorn in terms of fighting ability.","Although Red Thorn could now breathe underwater and could be counted as one of Lin Yuan’s underwater combatants, Lin Yuan’s chance of engaging in underwater combat was as slim as someone who couldn’t swim.","Hence, it would be most cost-effective to use dimensional lifeforms that were suited for land combat as hosts.","There were countless dimensional lifeforms suitable for land combat to choose from.","It was just that Lin Yuan felt that those strong land dimensional lifeforms would all not be too suitable to fight in Red Thorn’s Sea of Flowers.","Abyss dimensional lifeforms like Horn Demon were indeed strong, but if they were to fight in the sea of flowers, they would destroy the child ramets.","This would instead restrict Red Thorn’s fighting ability.","After thinking for a long time, Lin Yuan sighed in resignation and took the Platinum alien insect, Heart-Penetrating Ironline, out of his leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","In order to possess strong fighting ability without damaging the sea of flowers, Lin Yuan’s Heart-Penetrating Ironlines were undoubtedly the most suitable amongst his dimensional lifeforms due to their small size and assassination abilities.","However, Lin Yuan thought that this was obviously not the best option.","There were so many different types of dimensional lifeforms in dimensional rifts that would evolve and mutate as they matured.","Lin Yuan planned to pay greater attention to the auction of precious deceased dimensional lifeforms in the future. He would see if he could get the existence of evolution and mutation. If there were suitable lifeforms, he would then bring them back for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s use.","Besides, as long as the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had enough acid in its body, the Acid Corpse Poison Bees it produced would not have any concrete limitations.","Nevertheless, Lin Yuan’s idea was defeated by reality.","He let the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee choose a Heart-Penetrating Ironline that the Acid Corpse Poison Bees could control to the limit out of his different Heart-Penetrating Ironlines.","After a round of selection, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee chose a Platinum I Heart-Penetrating Ironline.","Lin Yuan’s eyelids jumped as he watched it pierce the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s body.","After evolving to the Platinum grade, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s stingers had become unusually sharp. However, it still required much effort to pierce the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s body.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help but sigh at the might of the Heart-Penetrating Ironline as an alien insect dimensional lifeform.","After the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee pierced the Heart-Penetrating Ironline, its body trembled furiously. Once it pulled out its stingers, the bee fell to the ground, losing the strength to even fan its wings.","Lin Yuan hurriedly used True Data to scan the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee."]},{"number":589,"title":"Chapter 589 - The Thoughtful Source Sand and a Wave of Evolution","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan realized that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee became weak after producing one Acid Corpse Poison Bee.","It would remain weak for three days.","According to True Data’s assessment of the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s acid, Lin Yuan estimated that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would need a month to recover after producing the Acid Corpse Poison Bee once.","Lin Yuan felt that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was like a woman. It needed to recuperate for three days after birth and a month of downtime after that before it could give birth again.","Although, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had a much shorter period of downtime.","Lin Yuan stored away the rest of the Heart-Penetrating Ironline that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had not chosen with a wave of his hand.","This test allowed him to understand the Acid Corpse Poison Bee’s limit when controlling a dimensional lifeform’s body.","The dimensional lifeform could not be more powerful than the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","After a few minutes, Lin Yuan noticed that something seemed to be crawling around inside of the Heart-Penetrating Ironline that had been injected with the Acid Corpse Poison Bee.","When the thing crawled to the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s head, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s body started to move.","Lin Yuan sensed the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s condition. Even though the Acid Corpse Poison Bee was controlling it, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline was acting no different from when it was alive.","If there was a difference to be considered, the puppet Heart-Penetrating Ironline did not feel fear or pain.","It was a mindless puppet that only obeyed the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee that was collapsed on the ground let out a buzzing noise.","Suddenly, the puppet Heart-Penetrating Ironline retracted its body.","It slowly turned into a black pupa about half as long as Lin Yuan’s pinky.","The weakened Acid Corpse Poison Bee could not move its body, so Lin Yuan instructed Red Thorn to use its vines to collect the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee and black pupae into its body.","One month might seem like a long time, but Lin Yuan was not upset about it.","At this rate, twelve puppets could be created per year. This number greatly exceeded Lin Yuan’s expectations.","Once the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee evolved, Lin Yuan stored Red Thorn away in the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box. He then ordered Red Thorn to continue to absorb Eyes of Relinquish and nurture the Blood Brew Grapevine.","Lin Yuan noticed that Genius and Chimey were perched on the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree branches and acting secretively.","He did not know what they were twittering about.","Lin Yuan shook his head but did not disturb them. He went back to his affairs.","At that moment, the Source Sand started to expand and contract rapidly, spitting a bunch of things out of the sand.","Lin Yuan saw that the things were the golden discs he had not had the time to store back in the dimensional rift and the 30 source-type items that he had snatched from the dimensional hub before falling unconscious.","He was surprised to see that his Source Sand had stored all these items for him after he had fallen unconscious.","Lin Yuan felt that the Source Sand was too thoughtful.","The 30 source-type items were rather valuable to Lin Yuan as well. However, he was more pleasantly surprised to see the big pile of golden discs.","Lin Yuan no longer needed to spend his days doggedly replenishing the energy ores in the spirit pool with these golden discs.","Lin Yuan stored the close to 100 golden discs in the beetle-shaped Diamond fey storage box, and they devoured all the energy ores in there.","Lin Yuan stacked up the golden discs in the spirit pool and, coupled with the almond leaf-shaped butterfly shell flowers, it made for a pretty scene.","Now, he would not need to worry about Morbius evolving the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan shook his body and took two Golden Curtain Peonies out of the fey storage box and placed them with the 108 Starlight Grass and 36 Floating Cloud Flowers.","He also summoned Zhou Luo’s Bronze/Epic Dark Snake Dragon Lizard and Decayed Mud Lizard, as well as the Burning Sunflower and Chu Ci’s Bronze X/Epic Vajra Butterfly.","After some calculations, Lin Yuan took out the remaining 36 spirit qi crystals and crushed two of the spirit qi crystals in his hand.","Since Morbius was still sleeping, Lin Yuan had to direct the spirit qi from the spirit qi crystals into the Burning Sunflower, the Vajra Butterfly, the Dark Snake Dragon Lizard, and the Decayed Mud Lizard on his own.","Soon, the four feys evolved from Bronze/Epic to Bronze/Legend.","Lin Yuan continued to move the spirit qi around, spreading it on the 108 Starlight Grass, 36 Floating Cloud Flowers, and two Golden Curtain Peonies.","The Starlight Grass and Floating Cloud Flowers Lin Yuan chose were mostly Bronze VII/Elite.","This saved Lin Yuan from depleting too much spirit qi.","All the plants started to evolve their grades and qualities. However, Lin Yuan’s calculation was slightly lacking.","Since the two spirit qi crystals were already used to evolve the four feys, there was not enough leftover spirit qi. Thus, more than 20 of the Starlight Grass were unable to reach Bronze X/Epic.","After some thought, Lin Yuan crushed another spirit qi crystal.","However, there was leftover spirit qi this time even after the rest of the Starlight Grass evolved to Bronze X/Epic.","There was a considerable surplus amount.","Lin Yuan mulled over his next step before directing the leftover spirit qi into the two Bronze X/Epic Golden Curtain Peonies, and they both evolved to Bronze/Legend.","The four evolved feys did not experience any major changes.","The only change to note was that the Decayed Mud Lizard had evolved to become the Decayed Mud Shield Lizard.","The Decayed Mud Shield Lizard had stronger defensive abilities than the Decayed Mud Lizard, but it did not look any different.","The two Golden Curtain Peonies, which relied on their looks, retained their easy-on-the-eyes exterior when they evolved."]},{"number":590,"title":"Chapter 590 - Ambush! Youth!","paragraphs":["The golden petals bent backward quickly while the small inner petals multiplied and stretched outwards.","The beautiful Golden Curtain Peonies became at least twice as large.","To Lin Yuan, the Golden Curtain Peonies became at least ten times more beautiful.","Lin Yuan did not have any use for the Golden Curtain Peony itself. He had chosen to evolve them because Chu Ci’s Vajra Butterfly needed their pollen in order to become a Fantasy Breed.","Moreover, the Golden Curtain Peony’s pollen greatly benefited the Vajra Butterfly if consumed.","The Golden Curtain Peony stood out because of its looks, and it did not even have any special fragrance.","It was because the Golden Curtain Peony lacked fragrance that made it suitable to be a decorative item in the manor.","Lin Yuan felt a sting as 33 spirit qi crystals remained.","However, time was tight. Lin Yuan had decided to announce his private territory on the third day after the new year. Thus, it was impossible for Lin Yuan to take the time to slowly evolve the 108 Starlight Grass and 36 Floating Cloud Flower to Bronze/Epic using his own power.","After splurging this time, Lin Yuan resolved not to do it again.","Since Lin Yuan had used the spirit qi crystals, the massive project was completed in less than half an hour.","Once Lin Yuan was done working, he realized that Genius and Chimey had disappeared. He looked up and caught sight of the silhouette of two figures snuggled together amongst the leaves of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree.","Lin Yuan assumed they were resting, so he left the Spirit Lock spatial zone to enter Star Web.","He did not know that at the same time that he entered Star Web, those two imps in the Spirit Lock spatial zone were about to leave an impact on Star Web on New Year’s Eve.","At the Orchid Mouth Guild Club’s training center...","Two young men were seated at a table in a uniquely decorated room.","A young man with peach blossom eyes was sipping on alcohol. When he swallowed the hard liquor, he choked.","The mature young man sitting next to him smirked.","The mature young man looked around the closet-like room and said to the peach blossom-eyed young man, “Bai Hao, I’m not going to be with my girlfriend on New Year’s tomorrow. How about I go shopping for clothes with you? I’m guessing you haven’t bought any new clothes in two months.”","Wang Fan thought about how Bai Hao could fill up an entire house with new clothes in the span of a month. He knew that Bai Hao was not pretending to be dispirited.","Wang Fan knew that Bai Hao liked to listen to music. Bai Hao would log on Star Web to listen to people sing in the past during his free time.","However, he never pressed like frantically.","He’s like this because his host hasn’t live-streamed in two months. I don’t understand what’s going on, but I’m worried about him.","Bai Hao glanced at Wang Fan before saying flatly, “If you don’t accompany your girlfriend, she might order her bears to jump on me and crush me when we’re in a team competition.”","Wang Fan awkwardly scratched his head. His wife was indeed rather fierce.","That said, his wife’s bears were not fierce in the slightest. They often spent nights being punished by his wife and standing outside the door with him.","Wang Fan felt that the bears were simple-minded.","“The day after tomorrow is the Allstar Match. We both have to attend. Please don’t sabotage yourself by drowning yourself in alcohol for the next two days. If someone ends up challenging you or you have to participate in a guidance battle, it won’t look good when the Star Web reporter takes your picture.”","Bai Hao rubbed his red eyes and said nonchalantly, “Either way, the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess won’t be live streaming. Nothing else in life brings me joy. I might as well drink myself to death.”","Wang Fan pursed his lips vexedly and pretended he had not heard Bai Hao.","Bai Hao’s bark was worse than his bite. He was a veritable tsundere.","As his comrade and teammate, Wang Fan had long become accustomed to Bai Hao’s personality.","Wang Fan wanted to try to persuade Bai Hao, but Bai Hao’s phone started to ring.","Bai Hao picked up the call sadly. At the same time, Wang Fan noticed an eye-catching gaze overtake Bai Hao’s eyes. It was like he had regained something he had lost. There was surprise, excitement, and preciousness.","Wang Fan had no clue what had just happened. Hence, he went to finish the speech that he had been in the middle of.","“Bai Hao, I remember that you enjoy traditional-style songs. The Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ songs aren’t that style. Why not—”","Before Wang Fan could finish, Bai Hao’s depressed expression changed into one of unbridled delight.","His red eyes curved with his bursting joy.","“You don’t know anything. I might like traditional-style songs, but I love listening to anything that comes out from the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s mouth.”","Wang Fan pursed his lips. He could already guess what had perked up Bai Hao. It must have been the news that the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess had returned to streaming.","“I shall grant you the pleasure of shopping with me tomorrow! You’re welcome!” exclaimed Bai Hao.","Wang Fan was done with this.","“You are completely fine now. You’re even happier than me! I won’t go shopping with you anymore. Otherwise, I’ll have to stand outside with those bears on New Year’s night. I’m not going! Spending time with my wife is more important.”","Bai Hao scoffed. “Even if you don’t go with me, you’ll still be punished on New Year’s night. I’ll send you some food then.”","Even though Wang Fan was still present, Bai Hao immediately logged onto Star Web. He entered the live-streaming room that he had spent countless dazed nights in.","The moment he entered, he was surprised to hear an ethereal and raspy voice say, “Everyone, thank you for supporting me all this time. I’m going to sing a song I just learned.”","Bai Hao’s heart skipped a beat.","The Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess is talking!","Bai Hao immediately gifted 1,000,000 Radiance dollars.","He was initially going to gift it in ten rounds, but her singing voice ambushed him!"]},{"number":591,"title":"Chapter 591 - Constellations that Control Fate","paragraphs":["Bai Hao saw the figure of a woman standing next to the white rock river. Her back was facing him, and she was singing the song that was playing in his ear.","A mellow song was the most gentle form of punishment. It could slink into a heart unnoticed and chain it up before one even noticed what was happening.","When Lin Yuan logged onto Star Web, he went into his private territory.","Since Lin Yuan wanted to go into his private territory on Star Web, he brought along the mask Hu Quan had made for him.","He assumed that it would be rather empty since he had not announced his private faction’s role.","However, when Lin Yuan entered, he realized that about seven or eight people were standing outside his private territory and talking.","Lin Yuan was slightly suspicious, but he felt annoyed when he heard what they were discussing.","“Why are the bunch of you here in the middle of the night? There’s nothing exciting to see.”","“Why are you talking about us? You’re rather sinister! You come here at the same time every day to mock Sky City.”","“I’m not mocking Sky City. I just think that Sky City is a little pitiful.”","“My rising faction, Nut Mercenaries, is also new. However, if I happen to meet any member of Sky City, I’m willing to donate some outstanding items for them to spruce up their entranceway.”","The other people present were disgusted at this Nut Mercenaries member.","We’ve agreed on a time to leave here together to take a look at Nut Mercenaries’ private territory. It’s not like your private territory has anything valuable. Why are you acting all high and mighty here and trying to lord above other rising factions? How are you worthy? What a joke!","Lin Yuan pursed his lips as he scanned these few people. He sighed to himself at how silly they were.","Why aren’t they asleep at this hour?","Lin Yuan ignored them and went into his private territory.","The group of people had noticed Lin Yuan when he entered. They initially thought that he was just here to see if anything exciting was going to happen.","They did not expect that he would turn out to be a member of Sky City.","Inside his private territory, Lin Yuan checked his private territory’s visitor log.","Even after five minutes, he was not done checking through the visitor logs from today.","Lin Yuan gave up checking the visitor logs.","He noticed that there was mail from the Star Web officials in his private territory’s mailbox. After taking a look at it, numerous questions popped into his mind.","In the last month, his private territory had achieved a ranking in the Visitor’s Ranking.","There were many rankings for private territories on Star Web.","Most of the ranked private territories were a cut above the rest, and they represented the institution of private territories on Star Web.","Although the Visitor’s Ranking was not a particularly powerful ranking, it did carry significant weight amongst all the rankings.","After all, it represented the number of people who visited private territories every day.","Lin Yuan might have been happy if his private territory had been ranked after he announced its role.","However, his private territory had not even debuted. It was no different than a patch of empty land.","It was impossible for empty land to be attractive!","Hence, all the visitors had just come to see if there was anything exciting happening.","It was because of this that Sky City’s highest ranking on the Visitor’s Ranking was 87th.","Although, it had currently dropped to 98th.","Lin Yuan had not been investing time into his private territory, so he did not expect that so many people had been ridiculing him for carelessly leaving his private territory’s security access rights open.","Although Lin Yuan felt that this was rather ridiculous, he had no plans to stop this situation.","Those people who had come to join the crowd were only providing Sky City with free advance advertisement.","Lin Yuan did not plan on decorating the exterior of the private territory. Nonetheless, he and Hu Quan had put a lot of effort into the interior design.","Lin Yuan used the Star Web Card to bring in all the items and placed them on the floor of the large hall.","He hung all the jade-textured wood roulettes made by Hu Quan on the walls.","The jade-textured roulettes hanging all around the walls starkly contrasted with the white walls and created a classy atmosphere.","Then, Lin Yuan used the golden strings from the jade-textured phoebe zhennan and strung all the roulettes together.","There were a total of 108 jade-textured wood roulettes.","There was a notch in the center of every roulette where Lin Yuan placed a strand of Bronze/Epic Starlight Grass.","As a mainly decorative fey, the Starlight Grass could also release weak spirit qi.","The star patterns on the Starlight Grass’s leaves swayed naturally.","The swaying movements of the Starlight Grass’s leaves caused the roulette to turn, and in turn, each of the roulettes along the golden phoebe zhennan strings started to turn as well.","The weak spirit qi also caused the roulettes and golden phoebe zhennan strings to glow dimly.","The glowing golden strings and the shining Starlight Grass leaves lined up and seemed to form numerous constellations.","It could create the feeling of a star-filled sky during the daytime.","The turning roulettes looked like skipperless steering wheels turning in the sky.","In this artificial sky, these self-turning steering wheels seemed to be controlling the fates of mortals using the golden strings.","Now, the interior design of this private territory was utterly stunning."]},{"number":592,"title":"Chapter 592 - Recruiting Duan He","paragraphs":["Although the interior design was already immaculate, Lin Yuan was not done decorating.","Lin Yuan also set up the 36 Bronze/Epic Floating Cloud Flowers, placing one flower between three spinning roulettes.","Shortly after, elusive clouds rose from the flowers and shrouded the bright constellations and roulettes.","The light could not be completely hidden. The clouds were only meant to add an air of mystery and create the magical atmosphere of being amongst clouds.","Lin Yuan was basically done with decorating.","Lin Yuan thought for a while before raising his hand and storing away the jade-textured wood table Hu Quan had made.","He did not replace the complementary ordinary wood table that was given to all faction territories.","The ordinary wood table was extremely common. There was a Bronze/Legend Oath Lily of the Valley placed on it.","Each of the white bell-like flowers of the Oath Lily of the Valley gleamed softly. It was like the flowers were collecting the promises of the mortal world under the clouds and roulettes in the sky.","After Lin Yuan left his private territory, he noticed that the number of people gathering outside had increased by at least five times.","There were even more who were coming over.","Those first few people must have called more people over after seeing Lin Yuan go in.","Lin Yuan could not help but sigh as he wondered why these people were not enjoying the new year or sleeping.","Do they just gawk all day?","Lin Yuan did not have time to waste on these people.","On the third day of the new year, Sky City’s spectacle of clouds would be even more stunning.","After leaving Star Web, Lin Yuan plucked the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus from the Pure Land of Bliss. He intended on planting the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus in front of the mansion’s entrance.","Lin Yuan had been keeping the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus in the Spirit Lock spatial zone because of the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia growing on it.","Lin Yuan really needed the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia to increase his energy.","Since the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia had left the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus, Lin Yuan wanted to pour out the soil on the Pure Land of Bliss.","The Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus without its tree core would never recover.","Planting a new flower species in the mansion added a hint of elegance to the mansion.","The sky was starting to brighten. While Lin Yuan was instructing the Source Sand to dig in front of the door, he heard Wen Yu’s voice.","“Young Master, you haven’t slept the entire night. Why don’t you drink some of the purple sesame lamb soup that Liu Jie slowly simmered last night.”","Wen Yu knew that Hu Quan’s Vitality Sloth had replenished Lin Yuan’s vitality.","He would not have been able to sleep that night.","However, she did not expect to find him gardening at the break of dawn.","Wen Yu was a spirit attendant in the Radiant Moon Palace and immediately recognized that Lin Yuan was about to plant the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","The Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus was not an outstanding species of osmanthus.","It was considered upper-middle, and its most interesting aspect was that it changed drastically when it evolved.","The legendary extinct species of osmanthus was an evolved form of the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","Even the Moon Empress had chosen to plant several Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus in the Leaning Moon Mountain’s garden.","Several of them had evolved to the higher grade of osmanthus feys.","According to Wen Yu’s memory, not even the lushest Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus in Leaning Moon Mountain’s garden was half as lush as Lin Yuan’s Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","The clustering tufts of scarlet flowers were already weighing down the strong branches.","Lin Yuan took a sip of the purple sesame lamb soup Wen Yu served him.","When his taste buds were drenched in the freshness of the lamb meat and the spiciness of the purple sesame, Lin Yuan felt a warmth enter his body.","When he swallowed the soup, small beads of sweat appeared on his nose.","Liu Jie could not help but marvel at Liu Jie’s improving cooking skills.","Recently, Liu Jie liked to cook medicinal food.","Medicinal dishes made of fresh ingredients and some feys with medicinal properties had a special flavor.","Lin Yuan checked the time and saw that it was only a little past 6:00 a.m.","“Why are you up so early?” asked Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie was usually the first one to wake up in the mansion. He usually woke up at 7:00 a.m.","When Liu Jie started making breakfast at around 7:30 a.m., Wen Yu would walk out of her room.","Wen Yu received the medicinal soup that Lin Yuan drank and explained softly, “Last night, you said that you wanted information on Duan He, so I asked a spirit attendant in Hidden Moon Pavilion to help me look through Duan He’s personalized magazine.”","Wen Yu was always aware of her skills and the role she needed to play in Sky City.","When she was a spirit attendant in Radiant Moon Palace, Wen Yu had regarded herself as extremely talented.","Apart from her aptitude as a Creation Master, she was considered rather powerful amongst the spirit attendants.","However, ever since becoming Lin Yuan’s personal assistant and getting to know Liu Jie, Listen, and Chu Ci, Wen Yu came to understand that power was innate. It could not be compared with others no matter what.","Hence, Wen Yu had taken Mystic Moon’s suggestion and had started focusing her efforts on managing the information and organizational aspects of Lin Yuan’s private faction.","She was not determinedly striving toward governance.","Up till then, Wen Yu had been rather downtrodden.","It was because she had not managed to gather even one Willpower Rune.","After hearing what Wen Yu said, Lin Yuan knew that she had not slept last night as well.","“Wen Yu, what do you think about us recruiting Duan He?”","Wen Yu pondered over his statement.","“Young Master, I think it’ll be good for us to recruit Duan He,” replied Wen Yu.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow. Ever since establishing Sky City, he had not contributed as much as Wen Yu.","Wen Yu was usually the strictest when it came to picking new talented individuals.","Duan He’s character and skills must be impressive if he managed to tear a compliment from Wen Yu.","“Tell me about the information you learned about Duan He last night.”","Wen Yu did not look through the organized information in her hands. She had already memorized all of the information surrounding Duan He.","“Duan He’s character is beyond reproach. When he was king-class, he was once Captain of the Spirit Guards.”","Lin Yuan was stunned to hear that he had been a Spirit Guard Captain.","Lin Yuan’s parents had both been part of the Spirit Guards. Thus, the title of Spirit Guard Captain held a special meaning to him.","Any person who protected the sanctity of life in the face of danger was worth respecting in Lin Yuan’s books.","They were also the most adorable people!"]},{"number":593,"title":"Chapter 593 - Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake and Thunderwave Sky Chaos Snail","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan thought for a moment before asking, “Has Duan He been a part of any factions other than the Spirit Guards?”","Wen Yu shook her head.","“Duan He has never joined any other factions. He was once a part of a team of emperor-class experts. However, he left for some reason. He is quite powerful. Duan He prefers to contract water-type feys that are skilled at attacking. According to the records in Hidden Moon Pavilion, as of three years ago, his main feys are the Suzerain/Myth I Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake and the Suzerain/Myth I Thunderwave Sky Chaos Snail.”","Lin Yuan frowned upon hearing the names of the feys that were compatible with Duan He.","When Lin Yuan had first met Duan He, the latter had been using a Diamond X/Fantasy V Sword Plume Sea Hawk.","Not only was the Sword Plume Sea Hawk incompatible with what Wen Yu said about Duan He, but it also did not exist in his team of main feys.","“Doesn’t Duan He have the Sword Plume Sea Hawk as one of his main feys?”","Wen Yu shook her head.","“Duan He can’t afford to nurture another fey after the Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake. However, he did contract the Unmatchable Bird five years ago. The Sword Plume Sea Hawk might be the Unmatchable Bird’s evolved form.”","Lin Yuan immediately understood.","The Unmatchable Bird was the same as his strengthened Red Thorn and Source Seed. It also transformed and evolved according to its contractor’s desired path.","Few Unmatchable Birds and Source Seeds could be found at the Radiance Federation. It was not a source-type lifeform that existed on its own.","Source Seeds were easily mistaken as rubbish, while the Unmatchable Bird was considered an extremely expensive source-type lifeform.","It was almost as valuable as fairy source-type items.","Lin Yuan remembered the Sword Plume Sea Hawk’s abilities and exclusive skills that he had seen on True Data. He could not help but lament how Duan He had failed to properly nurture it.","It was too one-sided and harsh to only nurture the Sword Plume Sea Hawk’s offensive side.","However, Wen Yu had said that Duan He’s only main fey was the Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake.","Lin Yuan felt that Duan He was only making his own life more difficult by nurturing the Sword Plume Sea Hawk in this way.","A multi-directional group attack managed to quickly harvest the pieces of dimensional lifeforms in the dimensional rift.","The more Lin Yuan thought about it, the more he felt that he had found the truth.","The Bamboo Monarch had declared the Sea Demon Snake as the strongest fey in quality-wise.","However, being the strongest also caused the Sea Demon Snake to suffer consequences in the manifold.","The consequences would be shifted onto the Sea Demon Snake’s contractor.","Whenever the Sea Demon Snake grew a new head, it needed to absorb twice the resources as compared to the other feys of the same quality.","Duan He’s main fey was a Suzerain/Myth I Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake. This meant that Duan He could have nurtured six other Suzerain/Myth I feys in the time that he had invested into the Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up!","On the one hand, Duan He’s Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake was very strong.","If Lin Yuan could recruit Duan He, he would gain an unrivaled in its own quality and ferocious asset.","On the other hand, due to how difficult it was to nurture the Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake, Duan He had to be very poor!","This is great! The poorer, the better! The poorer he is, the more desperately he’ll need resources, and the happier I’ll be!","While talking to Wen Yu, Lin Yuan was done planting the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus in the hole the Source Sand had dug.","The Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ petals had fallen and scattered all over the soil, a blanket of red covering the ground.","The air was tinged with the osmanthus’ fragrance.","Wen Yu hurriedly grabbed a broom and started sweeping up the fallen osmanthus flowers.","“Young Master, we’ll be able to make our own honeyed osmanthus wine out of this Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus from now on,” said Wen Yu.","Lin Yuan smiled from ear to ear.","“Yes. This Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus is about to evolve to Gold grade. I don’t know if Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus that had its tree core removed will start a new lease of life once it evolves to Gold grade.”","Wen Yu knew that Lin Yuan wanted to cultivate the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus.","“Young Master, I’ll bring back some plants and water from Leaning Moon Mountain later. Then, I’ll carefully water this Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus,” said Wen Yu.","A crystal bottle and a flat and unassuming paper item appeared in Lin Yuan’s hand.","Wen Yu was a Creation Master. She immediately recognized the paper item as the mutated paper-elemental source-type lifeform.","When she saw the amber fluid in the crystal bottle, Wen Yu was stunned.","One drop of the amber fluid had saved her and was the reason she had resolved to start a new chapter of her life. It was the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","As Lin Yuan handed the items to her, Wen Yu’s heart trembled vigorously.","The paper-elemental source-type item aside, there were at least 200 drops of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","A single drop was already unbelievably precious.","Top factions had come to Leaning Moon Mountain to humbly plead with the Moon Empress in the hopes of gaining the contents of this small bottle.","Lin Yuan saw that Wen Yu was making no move to receive the items.","“This paper-elemental source-type item is more suitable for you. If you drink this bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, your body will be completely cleansed of impurities. Once you’ve been cleansed, you’ll be able to contract the paper-elemental source-type item. Then, you should rest well tonight and replenish all the energy you lost from staying up all night,” said Lin Yuan.","Wen Yu gazed at Lin Yuan with several odd emotions. She then took a deep breath and accepted the items from Lin Yuan.","“Thank you, Young Master,” said Wen Yu earnestly.","The sun had risen.","Wen Yu summoned the Earth Rush Golden Lotus and bathed in the sunlight together.","Lin Yuan headed toward the kitchen and checked the soup that Liu Jie had cooked for him.","Liu Jie usually prepared a separate soup in the kitchen when he made meals.","Whenever this pot of soup was used up in cooking, Liu Jie would add more.","Lin Yuan was cooking the jar of soup that Liu Jie had helped him to prepare with special ingredients last night.","This jar of soup was the product of Lin Yuan’s cooking skills after not stepping into the kitchen for some time.","Wen Yu clenched her fist over the crystal bottle and the paper-elemental source-type item.","Suddenly, a gust of wind kicked up."]},{"number":594,"title":"Chapter 594 - Second Young Master has the Final Say","paragraphs":["A rain of osmanthus flowers fell with that gust of wind.","One of the osmanthus flowers landed on Wen Yu’s hair.","Wen Yu plucked the osmanthus flower from her hair and realized that there were subtle markings on the petals.","Although the flower had fallen from the tree, it still bore the markings of the tree’s growth.","Wen Yu looked between the flower and the paper-elemental source-type item in her hand. A dream took root in Wen Yu’s mind.","“If only I could become a white paper engraved with all the memories of you and Sky City,” murmured Wen Yu.","Wen Yu spoke under her breath, and the wind was still whistling. Perhaps only the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus caught what she said.","“If I could become paper, my front side would display proclamations while the back would be full of secrets.”","This time, Wen Yu spoke louder. Before her words could sink in, she entered into a trance.","A transparent, paper-shaped Willpower Rune materialized in Wen Yu’s mind, and the spiritual energy surrounding Wen Yu started to swirl rapidly.","...","Mystic Moon reached out his arm and peered at the food in his chopsticks. He felt that there was nothing special about the dish, but the knife-work was solid.","All the humble foods had the taste of an aged soup.","The taste of the aged soup was the finishing touch that elevated the dish.","If it was one year ago, Mystic Moon would never have believed that someone would cook a home-cooked meal for the Moon Empress during a New Year’s visitation.","Although the Moon Empress liked all kinds of food, she was picky about what was allowed to enter her mouth.","Ordinary dishes were not permitted to enter the Moon Empress’s mouth.","However, she was now beaming as she feasted on these common dishes.","Cold Moon’s usually frigid expression had also thawed as she drank the soup that Chu Ci ladled for her.","Now, Mystic Moon’s desire for a disciple was stronger than ever.","Suddenly, he remembered the young girl that he had once guided.","When they were done eating, the Moon Empress said to Lin Yuan, “Little Yuan, Mystic Moon will be leaving the continent on the 7th day after the new year. The space tunnel will be set up before the 15th. Previously, I didn’t advise you because there was a lot of time before you had to go to the Spirit Wood Federation. Now, I have to tell you with the utmost seriousness that all of the places in the outskirts will be completely different from the Radiance Continent. You have to be able to stay composed wherever you go.”","Lin Yuan nodded seriously.","“Don’t worry, Master.”","Even if Lin Yuan had not understood the dangers of foreign places after being in the abyss dimensional rift, he had definitely learned what he should do in the face of foreign factions from his experience in the evolving water world dimensional rift.","The Moon Empress took Lin Yuan’s words into account and went on to say, “Do you want me to help out with some of your problems?”","A flash of coldness and murderous intent streaked across the Moon Empress’s gaze.","Lin Yuan knew that the Moon Empress was referring to the Zheng family because there were no other current problems in his life.","The Moon Empress had offered him once before. She had to be asking again because the Zheng family was about to make a move.","Lin Yuan shook his head and replied with a smile, “Master, I’ll seek you out if I can’t handle it myself.”","The Moon Empress stretched out her hand and gently caressed Lin Yuan’s head, and then placed the Extreme Token with the Flowing Cloud Beeswax inside around Lin Yuan’s neck.","“I’ve already filled the Extreme Token with the moonlight domain. Don’t hesitate to activate it when you’re in danger.”","Lin Yuan lowered his head to look at the Extreme Token hanging around his neck. He could feel that there was something different about the Extreme Token.","However, he could not pinpoint where the difference was.","...","Unlike the happiness brimming in the Radiant Moon Palace, the atmosphere in the Zheng family’s manor was extremely tense.","Zheng Jiangliu and Zheng Wenbo stood off to one side and stared at the austere youth sitting on the main seat.","Despite the raging fire burning in the fireplace, Zheng Jiangliu and Zheng Wenbo felt a chill that resonated from within their bones.","Bi Chenghu from the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce was kneeling on the floor with his head down. He was terrified of offending the important person seated on the main seat.","He had lost track of how long he had been kneeling.","Bi Chenghu did not dare to use his spiritual power while he was kneeling. Hence, this king-class expert’s legs had already gone numb.","The youth on the main seat scoffed. The kneeling Bi Chenghu twitched, and the terror in his eyes intensified.","Bi Chenghu’s main reason for coming to the Royal Capital was that he had no idea why the Zheng family’s third lineage, which had been supporting him and the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce all along, was suddenly ignoring him.","He did not expect to meet the Zheng family’s main family’s core member—the Zheng family’s revered Second Young Master.","If this was any other time, Bi Chenghu would have been over the moon at the chance to meet someone like the Second Young Master.","But now that Bi Chenghu knew that the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce had caused trouble, he wanted nothing more than to dive into a crack in the floor to avoid Zheng Jiangliu’s piercing gaze.","However, Bi Chenghu was even more terrified of the Second Young Master, who had not even thrown him a glance.","Zheng Jiangliu looked at Zheng Kaiyuan and tentatively said, “What do you think about this matter, Second Young Master?”","Zheng Kaiyuan slammed his hand down on the table forcefully.","He startled the small black and white sable in his arms. It tunneled into Zheng Kaiyuan’s blooming sleeves.","“What do I think? Let’s ignore the death of the Zheng family’s third lineage’s Jiao Hanzhong. However, my guardian is now on his last legs, not to mention deaf and mute. The Zheng family’s third lineage is actually asking what I think?”","Zheng Kaiyuan spoke like a haughty elite that was chastising his subordinates. His tone indicated that he did not consider the Zheng family’s third lineage as part of his family at all.","Zheng Wenbo had already been scared silent. He stood hunched behind Zheng Jiangliu.","Zheng Jiangliu’s expression had soured significantly, but fear lay underneath his sour expression.","Zheng Jiangliu said with a resigned air, “Second Young Master, we’ve been collecting resources from the coastal shores outside of Indigo Azure City. The third lineage only asks for 20% of this business. You can have the remaining 80%.”","Zheng Kaiyuan’s sharp gaze penetrated Zheng Jiangliu.","“The third lineage is now struggling with gaining control of the coastal sea owned by the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce despite having schemed for so long. Hehe, it looks like the third lineage has been hiding many things from me!”","Zheng Jiangliu’s body froze.","“The third lineage dared not hide anything from you, Second Young Master. From now on, you can have the final say when it comes to the third lineage.”"]},{"number":595,"title":"Chapter 595 - I Think I’ll Be Chosen!","paragraphs":["Zheng Jiangliu thought to himself, Only Jiao Hanzhong and I know about the Sea Burial Lotus Flower that was found in Indigo Azure City’s coastal sea. Jiao Hanzhong had taken care of everyone else who knew. Not even Zheng Wenbo is sure of the details. Since Jiao Hanzhong died, I’m the only one left who knows. Now that the Sea Burial Lotus Flower is dead, I have to keep this information to myself if it’s the last thing I do. If Second Young Master finds out about the Sea Burial Lotus Flower, he’ll punish the third lineage for sure.","Jiao Hanzhong had been the strongest person in the Zheng family’s third lineage.","Jiao Hanzhong was dead. Hence, the third lineage had now become the weakest link in the four lineages, which initially stood side by side.","Zheng Jiangliu needed to find a reliable source of support for the third lineage, even if the new source of support was greedier than a fearsome tiger!","Zheng Kaiyuan glanced at Zheng Jiangliu.","“Since the third lineage wants to side with me, they better focus on developing the coastal sea. Other matters are unimportant. I want 90% of the profits.”","Zheng Jiangliu almost cracked his teeth with the force that he was grinding them together.","An evil smile appeared on Zheng Kaiyuan’s cold face. He looked askance at Zheng Jiangliu and said lightly, “What’s wrong, Third Uncle? Do you disagree with me?”","Zheng Jiangliu’s tightly gritted teeth trembled. The tremors were so strong that he tasted blood.","He yanked Zheng Wenbo, who was behind him and knelt on the floor.","“Your ideas are always the best, Second Young Master.”","The kneeling Zheng Jiangliu started to guess to himself.","The moon has been bright the past few days. The concentrated moonlight illuminated Indigo Azure City’s coastal sea. That’s the exact location where I sent Jiao Hanzhong to kill the masked youth.","However, this guess was terrifying, and Zheng Jiangliu dared not dive in too deeply.","Although the Zheng family had not experienced any disasters in the past two weeks, Zheng Jiangliu thought it would be best to stay on his guard.","If the Zheng family crossed someone that was untouchable, even the Miao family who supported the Second Young Master would burst into flames.","The top faction that was the Miao family would be burnt to a crisp.","When Zheng Kaiyuan heard Zheng Jiangliu’s response, he glanced at Zheng Jiangliu haughtily but did not address him again.","Instead, he turned to look at Bi Chenghu, who wanted nothing more than to disappear.","“The source is the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce. Hehe, I can’t believe they’re capable of so much,” said Zheng Kaiyuan.","There was a hint of solemness in Zheng Kaiyuan’s eyes.","Although Zheng Kaiyuan was arrogant, he was not stupid. He had even sought out the Indigo Azure Guard Captain to understand the circumstances.","After Zheng Kaiyuan’s numerous visits to the Indigo Azure Guard Captain, he only managed to find out the name Sky City.","He was clueless as to the power that Sky City held.","After one match that had the power to kill two emperor-class warriors, Zheng Kaiyuan could not disregard them.","Bi Chenghu would never have expected that the Zheng family’s Second Young Master would talk to him in such a condescending manner.","Although the Second Young Master seemed to be talking to Bi Chenghu, he might as well have been talking to himself.","Bi Chenghu, who thought that he knew the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce rather well, dared not interrupt.","While Bi Chenghu was struggling, he was unexpectedly called out by Zheng Kaiyuan.","“Third Uncle said that your name is Bi Chenghu. What a bold-sounding name. I know you came to Third Uncle for resources. Whether he decides to give you any or not, I can help you out. Are you interested?”","Bi Chenghu, whose legs were already numb, assumed that he was doomed.","Little did he know that he would be granted such a blessing.","Bi Chenghu’s eyes lit up as he cried out, “I’m willing. If you’re willing to help the Iron Wall Chamber of Commerce, we’ll do anything in for you in return!”","Zheng Kaiyuan knocked on the armrest of the main seat.","“While the dimensional rift remains closed, all beasts should hide their claws. Nothing good will come out of baring their teeth. However, the Zheng family cannot stay idle! Bi Chenghu, I shall give you the luxury resources that you desire. All you have to do is make sure that you squeeze the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce dry.”","Bi Chenghu was delighted by this unexpected surprise and thanked the Second Young Master happily.","Zheng Jiangliu looked at Bi Chenghu with a troubled gaze.","Now that he had formed a connection with the Second Young Master, Bi Chenghu could stand on the same level as Zheng Jiangliu and no longer needed to play the role of the obedient dog.","However, Zheng Jiangliu’s uneasiness has diminished.","Although this matter stemmed from the Zheng family’s third lineage, they had managed to dig themselves out of the hole by offering the coastal sea’s resources.","Zheng Jiangliu just needed to focus on developing the coastal sea resources and increasing profits.","Zheng Kaiyuan would handle all the problems.","By reading in between Zheng Kaiyuan’s words, he was prepared to fight the faction behind the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce.","...","Lin Yuan and Chu Ci were done spending New Year’s at the Radiant Moon Palace. They returned to the mansion the next day.","Back at the mansion, Lin Yuan and the rest had a reunion dinner together. They initially planned on going shopping in the afternoon, but the first snow of the year arrived.","The snow was heavy. It covered the Royal Capital like a blanket of white goose feathers.","The Return from Faraway Mansion’s plants and Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus were covered with a thick layer of snow.","The group watched as the snow became heavier and discarded their plans to go shopping. Instead, they made a variety of intricate dishes with Liu Jie.","The snow descending from the sky gave Lin Yuan a good feeling.","The snow was a good omen that heralded a warm and healthy spring.","The snow bore the hope that the coming year was going to be smooth sailing.","Chu Ci had always been the quiet type. However, she was rather restless now. All she could think about was going to watch the Allstar Match tomorrow.","Lin Yuan felt that Chu Ci was even more lively than Genius and Chimey combined at that moment.","He watched Chu Ci pace around him.","Lin Yuan knew that Chu Ci had something to say to him, so he patted the seat next to him on the sofa and said, “Stop pacing. You’re making me dizzy. You can tell me anything.”","Chu Ci planted herself next to Lin Yuan and giggled. “Big Brother, there might be a challenge match at the Allstar Match tomorrow. I have a feeling that I’ll be picked! That’s why I want to evolve the Varja Butterfly to Fantasy Breed today.”","Lin Yuan affectionately pinched Chu Ci’s nose and said, “When did you become so superstitious? I can’t believe you’re trusting a sixth sense. If so, I think I’ll get picked too!”"]},{"number":596,"title":"Chapter 596 - What Do You Need to Join Sky City?","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan helped Chu Ci to press down the stray hairs on the top of her head and said, “Next time, don’t hesitate to say what you’re thinking. Let’s evolve the Varja Butterfly to Fantasy Breed in the training room after dinner. I’ve also prepared your third fey.”","Hu Quan, who stood off to the side, held the jade-textured strings and was crafting Sky City’s special mask on the shelf made of metal spiritual ingredients.","When he heard the conversation between Lin Yuan and Chu Ci, Hu Quan pursed his lips.","Lin Yuan is such a hypocrite! He told his sister not to believe in her sixth sense, yet he does the exact same thing. If so, I’ll just say that I have a feeling both of you will be chosen!","Chu Ci happily reached out her hand and tousled Lin Yuan’s pristine hair before sticking out her tongue and running to the kitchen to cook with Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan hastily fixed his hair as he sighed.","“This little brat is becoming too impetuous.”","As he spoke, Hu Quan noticed that Lin Yuan’s lips were stretched into a wide smile.","Before they sat down to eat, Lin Yuan decided to do something that was very important to Sky City.","It was about Duan He’s recruitment.","Lin Yuan had sent out the elemental pearls that he traded for with Master Duan Li, Wang Fuxiang, and Stream in the Cloud through Ostrich Logistics. The only exception was Duan He’s elemental pearls.","Instead of immediately going through with the trade, Lin Yuan told Duan He to come after New Year’s. He wanted to give himself some time to look through Duan He’s information.","However, Lin Yuan did not expect that Wen Yu would be so efficient.","She had organized all of Duan He’s information in one night.","Now that Lin Yuan had thoroughly checked out Duan He’s information, he intended on pulling Duan He into Sky City.","Thus, Lin Yuan was not opposed to taking the initiative to recruit him.","Lin Yuan had obtained Duan He’s contact details.","Besides adding Duan He as a friend on Star Web, Duan He had also sent his phone number.","Lin Yuan checked Duan He’s phone number and dialed it.","The phone rang for almost a minute.","Just when Lin Yuan thought the call would fail to go through, Duan He picked up.","Lin Yuan could hear a sound that resembled whistling winds, and it was accompanied by the neighing of a herd of strong horses and the thunderous crackle of lightning.","From the sounds, Lin Yuan knew that Duan He was out killing.","“Hello, who is this and what do you want? If you try to promote some lousy spirit ingredients, I suggest you hang up now. I don’t have the extra cash to buy whatever nonsense items you’re selling.”","Lin Yuan heard Duan He exclaim loudly, “Thunderwave Sky Chaos Snail, use Eight Thousand Lightning Strikes!”","Duan He did not expect that he, an emperor-class expert, would be trapped by these gross Class 3 water world dimensional lifeforms.","His body was covered in the sticky fluids spat out by the Class 3 water world dimensional lifeforms, making him dizzy.","Thus, Duan He could not help but lash out at this stranger’s phone call.","Lin Yuan had not anticipated this tongue lashing when he called Duan He.","“So, does this mean that you don’t want the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls anymore?” asked Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan promptly hung up the call.","After he hung up, Lin Yuan did not set down the phone.","Less than three seconds later, Lin Yuan’s phone rang.","Lin Yuan waited till a minute was almost up before he picked up the call.","When he picked up the call, Lin Yuan heard Duan He’s embarrassed and apologetic voice.","“Sir, I, I didn’t know it was you! I’ve been receiving too many calls from salespeople trying to sell spiritual ingredients, and I thought it was happening again.”","Emperor-class experts always needed an abundance of rare spiritual ingredients, and many of them would leave their contact details at auction houses and shops where they had just bought spiritual ingredients.","Whenever these places had precious items, they had specialized employees who would contact emperor-class experts.","Most emperor-class experts were happy to receive such a service.","The spiritual ingredients promoted by these businesses were mostly aligned with the items that the emperor-class experts had bought previously.","These businesses would not have the courage to flippantly disturb emperor-class experts.","However, Duan He was an exception.","Duan He’s pocket was empty. He was close to donating his organs in order to nurture the Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake.","He spent every penny in his possession on his blade.","Thus, Duan He felt pained whenever the businesses promoted items to him that he wanted to buy.","Duan He did not expect that his way of speaking on the phone would offend the Moon Empress’ disciple.","The Moon Empress’s disciple also had the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls that Duan He desperately needed.","Duan He had not returned home to rest during New Year’s as he wanted to gain more resources that he could use to trade for Lin Yuan’s heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","A few days ago, Duan He had been desperate for spiritual ingredients and had no choice but to buy some. Thus, he spent the source-type items he had initially planned to trade for the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","There was no other reason that could result in Duan He working so hard over New Year’s.","Duan He assumed that Lin Yuan would either ignore him after being offended or go through with the agreed-upon deal.","Instead, Lin Yuan said, “How about this? You should set a time to come to my store on Star Web. I left an access control for you. Let’s talk face to face.”","From Lin Yuan’s words, Duan He had the feeling that Lin Yuan wanted to seek him out for more than the deal about the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","Duan He thought to himself, Is this about what my nephew said in the group? But it’s already been a few days, and he didn’t say anything when I was right next to him. From the way he casually tossed out those Floating Life pearls, he must be a generous person. I don’t think he’s someone who wants payback.","Duan He looked at the Class 3 water world dimensional rift that he had almost completely cleared out.","“I’ll be able to be at your store in ten minutes.”"]},{"number":597,"title":"Chapter 597 - Lin Yuan’s Thousand-Layer Scheme","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan hung up the call.","He had blurted out his intention to recruit Duan He because he wanted to use a kind of psychological tactic—a thousand-layer scheme.","He wanted to allow Duan He to have time to prepare and evaluate the circumstances.","If Duan He did not have any inclination to join Sky City, Lin Yuan would not be able to recruit him no matter what he offered.","However, if Duan He wanted to join Sky City, Lin Yuan would be able to build up his stakes layer by layer, which would exert pressure until it reached the amount that would convince Duan He to join Sky City.","This was the essence of the thousand-layer scheme.","Lin Yuan straightened his posture before logging onto Star Web and entering the Purchase With No Loss store to wait for Duan He.","Lin Yuan frowned as he waited for Duan He. He was deep in thought about what kind of stakes he should exhibit in order to be able to recruit Duan He.","Shortly after Lin Yuan sat down, Duan He’s figure appeared in the doorway.","When Lin Yuan saw Duan He, his lips curled into a smile.","Duan He’s arrival signaled that Lin Yuan’s thousand-layer scheme had already partially succeeded.","Duan He had come despite knowing Lin Yuan’s motive, indicating that he was interested.","Even if Duan He was opposed to the idea, it was not a strong opposition.","There was room for negotiation.","Duan He noticed that Lin Yuan looked the same as he was on the deserted island outside Indigo Azure City.","He was still wearing the strange mask with the majestic sky city engraving.","Only Lin Yuan and Duan He were present in the store. Duan He walked up to Lin Yuan and said, “Sir, my nephew Recluse Study was just spouting nonsense. I didn’t know that the brat had eavesdropped on the adults’ conversation.”","Lin Yuan shook his head and said generously, “I don’t mind such things. No one would believe him anywhere. Here you go. These are the ten wind-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with 98% purity. The price we agreed on was two source-type items for one elemental pearl.”","Duan He felt a sting from Lin Yuan’s words, but his limbs were numb. He hurriedly took out the 20 source-type items to trade with Lin Yuan.","Duan He had just retrieved three of the 20 source-type items from the Class 3 water world dimensional rift.","No matter how reluctant Duan He was, he had to admit that Lin Yuan was offering a much lower price than other pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters.","At the very least, he did not need to waste the immense amount of effort he would need to search for the extremely rare spiritual ingredients that the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters wanted.","Lin Yuan did not immediately receive the 20 source-type items that Duan He offered.","“Senior Duan He, if you’re willing to join Sky City, you don’t have to offer anything in return for these 10 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls,” said Lin Yuan earnestly.","When Duan He had first heard Lin Yuan’s offer, he instinctively rejected it. But afterward, he felt a slight ripple against his decision.","Duan He knew that Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple. He would undoubtedly gain closer access to the Moon Empress by joining Lin Yuan’s faction.","However, there were not only benefits to joining a faction but also a larger load of responsibilities to bear.","He would also gain many comrades whose lives would be codependent on his.","The feeling Duan He hated the most was seeing his comrades die in front of him.","This was the reason that Duan He had left the Spirit Guards after that one mission and decided to become a free spirit qi professional.","Thus, Duan He had decided that a deal was a deal.","Lin Yuan noticed that Duan He had not retracted his hand, meaning that his first layer of offering had not been accepted.","Hence, Lin Yuan threw out his second layer of offering.","“If you’re willing to join Sky City, Sky City will provide you with a compatible and valuable Bronze fey each time you comprehend a Willpower Rune.”","Duan He shook his head again.","He had comprehended a Willpower Rune, but he only needed a bit of time and effort to find a valuable Bronze fey on his own.","As an emperor-class expert, the challenge was not finding compatible Bronze feys but how to nurture the Bronze feys to Myth Breed.","Duan He only needed to request a Class 4 Creation Master to privately create a compatible Bronze fey.","After being rejected again, Lin Yuan waved his hand and summoned the Bronze/Legend Golden Curtain Peonies.","The moment that the brilliant Golden Curtain Peonies appeared, Duan He’s gaze changed.","Duan He had assumed that the Bronze feys Lin Yuan mentioned would be Bronze/Epic at most. He did not expect Lin Yuan to possess a Bronze/Legend.","Duan He could find suitable Bronze/Epic feys, but there was no way he would be able to obtain Bronze/Legend feys on his own.","Even when nurtured by a Class 4 Creation Master, there was only a small chance of a Bronze/Legend fey being produced.","It could be said that only Class 5 Creation Masters could nurture Bronze/Legend feys.","Duan He asked himself, The three great Class 5 Creation Masters are the Moon Empress, Bamboo Monarch, and Chef Supreme. I don’t have the right to approach any of them, much less ask them to help me create a fey that’s compatible with my Willpower Rune.","Duan He gulped as he considered the practical benefits of Lin Yuan’s offer.","Duan He no longer had any reason to reject him.","Lin Yuan observed Duan He’s demeanor and knew that he had hooked Duan He with his second layer of offering.","He now needed to seal the deal so that Duan He would immediately agree to join Sky City.","It was normal for a faction to give up an enormous amount of resources when they were trying to recruit an expert.","Even the unbelievably wealthy rising factions needed to pad the pockets of king-class experts when trying to recruit them.","That was the only way to convince the king-class experts to willingly join them.","Lin Yuan was now trying to recruit an emperor-class expert, so he was ready to shower Duan He with resources.","If Duan He was willing to join his faction, Duan He would also become stronger through Lin Yuan’s resources.","It was a win-win situation.","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment before throwing out the third layer of offering without another word to Duan He."]},{"number":598,"title":"Chapter 598 - Successful Recruitment","paragraphs":["“Senior Duan He, I heard that you’ve been running around collecting spiritual ingredients because you contracted a Sea Demon Snake. Is it the Suzerain/Myth I Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake? If so, all the resources you’ve been trying to accumulate will eventually be devoured by it. You should be able to evolve it to Myth II, but it will grow a new head and become a Seven-Headed Sea Demon Snake. The Seven-Headed Sea Demon Snake will need a lot of law power to evolve to Myth III. I wonder where you’re planning on going in order to procure enough law power to evolve the Seven-Headed Sea Demon Snake from Myth II to Myth III?”","Duan He was not surprised by how well Lin Yuan knew about his need for resources.","Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple. It was easy for Lin Yuan to uncover any secret in the entire Radiance Continent.","The legendary Hidden Moon Pavilion held even more secrets than the Spirit Guards’.","Duan He’s biggest issue at the moment was nurturing the Sea Demon Snake.","The Sea Demon Snake was already at the peak of Suzerain/Myth I, and Duan He had invested years of hard work into it.","All these years, Duan He had not even had the chance to rest at home. He spent every waking hour hard at work.","“If you’re able to obtain Law Crystals after joining Sky City, I can provide you with pure law power,” said Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan proclaimed his third layer of offering.","This was also the last layer of offering that Lin Yuan had prepared.","If Duan He rejected this as well, Lin Yuan would be at a loss.","If Duan He agreed, it would be great news to Lin Yuan.","Not only would Sky City gain a capable member that would increase its fighting ability, but the Law Crystals that Duan He would find would allow Lin Yuan to nurture his Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","Duan He was stunned by Lin Yuan’s words, mumbling in disbelief, “Are you telling the truth?”","Lin Yuan looked straight at Duan He and nodded solemnly.","“Of course I’m telling the truth.”","Duan He immediately retracted his hand that was holding the 20 source-type items.","He called Lin Yuan ‘Young Master’ in a loud and clear bark.","“Young Master, do I need to swear using a Willpower Rune in order to join Sky City?”","Duan He was elated.","Even if Class 4 Creation Masters could also nurture Bronze/Legend feys, only Class 5 Creation Masters were able to draw out the pure law power from Law Crystals.","The three great Class 5 Creation Masters were the Moon Empress, Bamboo Monarch, and Chef Supreme.","The drain of drawing out law power was completely internal.","This was why Class 5 Creation Masters had so much authority and received so much respect.","Even if an even stronger emperor-class expert went to join a top faction, they would not be able to obtain the pure power of laws.","They would need to deeply comprehend laws when their contracted Suzerain feys evolved to Suzerain/Myth II or absorb Law Crystals that were compatible with their contracted fey’s type.","Naturally, allowing the fey to absorb the energy inside Law Crystals could not compare to pure law power.","As long as Duan He wanted to advance as a combat-class spirit qi professional, there was no way he could reject Lin Yuan’s offer.","Upon hearing Duan He’s prompt agreement, Lin Yuan said, “All you need to do is make an oath by a Law Rune to become mine and Sky City’s Protector.”","Duan He breathed a sigh of relief.","If Lin Yuan wanted Duan He to become his servant, Duan He would not have agreed no matter how attracted he was by Lin Yuan’s offer.","As an emperor-class expert, pride was more important than benefits.","Although not all emperor-class experts subscribed to this, it was a principle that Duan He lived by.","This principle allowed Duan He to have a sense of discipline whenever he was faced with temptation.","Duan He contemplated for a full three seconds before looking at Lin Yuan and said,” I know how to be your Protector. But, how am I supposed to protect a faction?”","In Duan He’s eyes, Lin Yuan was the head of Sky City. As Lin Yuan’s Protector, he needed to listen to Lin Yuan’s orders.","The way Duan He saw it, becoming Lin Yuan’s Protector was the equivalent of becoming Sky City’s Protector as well.","“As Sky City’s Protector, you need to protect every plant and everything in Sky City, even if it costs you your life. Meanwhile, I will make you stronger.”","Lin Yuan spoke with immense austerity.","He was completely different from the friendly person he usually was. He now seemed like an elite that was full of attacking power.","Lin Yuan had not thrown out so many offers in his effort to recruit Duan He to gain a useless layabout.","Thus, he laid out the conditions first.","Lin Yuan had grown and learned more about the world and his own power in the past half a year.","Given Lin Yuan’s abilities as a Creation Master, his Sacred Sword Wielding Queen would be able to help evolve Duan He’s Suzerain/Myth I Six-Headed Demon as long as Duan He found enough Law Crystals.","If Duan He was confident that the Sea Demon Snake could survive the Trial of World Creation, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could even help the Sea Demon Snake evolve to the Creation Nine-Headed Sea Demon Snake.","Lin Yuan did not talk to Duan He as the disciple of the Moon Empress. Instead, he spoke with his usual humility.","Lin Yuan’s words left Duan He at ease. Since he was going to join a faction, it was natural that he would have the duty of protecting everything in the faction.","Duan He bent over and bowed to Lin Yuan.","“Young Master, I can’t make an oath by a Law Rune on Star Web. However, I have decided to join Sky City and become your Protector.”"]},{"number":599,"title":"Chapter 599 - Lin Yuan Gives Out Nectar","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan smiled brightly.","The sudden shift in Lin Yuan’s expression made Duan He feel that this masked youth was a cheerful youth even though he could not see his face clearly.","Duan He suddenly heard Lin Yuan say,” You’re not the only one who has to protect everything in the faction. I have to do it too!”","As he spoke, Lin Yuan thought back to how Liu Jie and Zhou Luo had bravely confronted their enemies in the evolving water world dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan pursed his lips and said softly, “I’ll do everything I can to protect everyone in Sky City.”","Lin Yuan’s voice had barely been a whisper, but Duan He could clearly sense the meaning and weight in Lin Yuan’s words.","Although Duan He was not familiar with Sky City, he could tell from the way its leader spoke that Sky City was a warm faction at the very least.","Lin Yuan did not expect himself to fall into such a trove of emotions.","The head of a faction definitely had heavier burdens to bear than the others.","Lin Yuan straightened his posture and said to Duan He, “Senior Duan He, come to the Royal Capital if you have time.”","Duan He extended his arm and awkwardly stroked his beard.","“Young Master, I want to make use of the dimensional rift’s active period to collect more resources. As of now, I only have half the spiritual ingredients needed to evolve both my Six-Headed Sea Demon Snake and Thunderwave Sky Chaos Snail to Myth II.”","Lin Yuan touched the Legend Gold Curtain Peonies’ flowers and replied with a smile, “Since you agreed to join Sky City, the faction will take care of all the spirit ingredients you need other than Law Crystals.”","It was not as easy to gain an emperor-class expert’s loyalty as it was to gain a king-class expert’s.","Any faction, including elite factions, would put their emperor-class expert members on a pedestal.","The faction was sure to provide their emperor-class experts with all their daily necessities.","Lin Yuan was not going to skimp on anything either.","Both the Zheng family and the Divine Wood Federation already had their bows drawn.","With another emperor-class expert in his ranks, Lin Yuan would be able to better handle matters on both ends.","Duan He blinked. He assumed he would only be receiving the benefits that Lin Yuan had mentioned.","Frankly, Duan He was already satisfied with being able to receive pure law power. He did not expect Lin Yuan would be willing to provide the resources he needed to evolve his feys.","He had been courted by veteran factions and elite factions before. However, not one of them had been willing to do the same as Lin Yuan.","Duan He knew that he required many times more the resources of other emperor-class experts. It was not easy for any faction to provide for him.","This blessing came too abruptly!","The thought of being freed from trudging around and being beaten by the elements allowed Duan He to feel a newfound sense of ease.","Duan He thought about how difficult it had been for him to nurture the Unmatchable Bird to the Sword Plume Sea Hawk, yet he had not used it much since.","Duan He felt that it was doable.","It looks like I’ll have to nurture the Sword Plume Sea Hawk as a group-control rather than group-attack type from now on.","Lin Yuan was not stressed by the increased burden of Duan He’s immense resource needs.","The strength of Duan He’s Sea Demon Snake outweighed the cons of the enormous amount of resources it devoured.","The number of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls in the Spirit Lock spatial zone were increasing every day.","This was a good way to use them up and raise Sky City’s combat power.","Once Lin Yuan settled things with Duan He, he left Star Web.","Duan He also started rushing toward the Royal Capital.","Given the Diamond X/Fantasy V Sword Plume Sea Hawk, Duan He would only need a day to reach the Royal Capital.","Duan He would be able to sign the contract with Lin Yuan when the latter announced Sky City’s roles on Star Web.","When Lin Yuan walked out of the room, the banquet had already been set up.","Besides the variety of dishes, there was also a jade square platter that was about a meter long in the middle of the table. Various cakes and deserts sat atop the platter.","Only a few of the deserts were exquisitely shaped like various feys. They were very lifelike.","It was obvious that Liu Jie had prepared them. The rest of the slipshod products had to have been made by the others.","After being steamed, the slipshod deserts all looked the same.","Chu Ci, the Mother of Bloodbath, and Endless Summer tried to pick out the desert that they had made.","However, they could not tell the difference no matter how hard they tried.","Lin Yuan saw that Wen Yu looked like a completely different person.","She must have already used the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar to completely cleanse herself .","Soon after, Listen and Zhou Luo returned and took a seat at the table.","Almost everyone was present at the Return from Faraway Mansion.","No one depicted on the feature wall was absent.","Lin Yuan thought for a moment before pulling out a large bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar that he had left in the fey storage box.","He also took out six empty bottles and filled each to the brim with nectar.","Lin Yuan placed a bottle in front of the Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, Liu Jie, Listen, Zhou Luo, and Hu Quan.","Lin Yuan had already given Chu Ci and Wen Yu Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, using it to cleanse their body of impurities.","No matter how much Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar he had, Lin Yuan was reluctant to drink it for sport.","One might be rich, but they should still use items to their best potential.","Chu Ci watched as Lin Yuan poured out the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar and immediately thought about what had happened to her after drinking it.","She was about to speak when she saw Hu Quan, who had been toiling over his crafts, and Zhou Luo, who was exhausted and hungry after returning, gulp down the entire bottle of nectar.","Once they were done drinking, Zhou Luo and Hu Quan could not help but give Lin Yuan a thumbs-up as they exclaimed, “This nectar is delicious! Where did you buy it from?”","Wen Yu’s eyelid twitched as she looked at both of them, thinking to herself, Unworthy people will never be able to touch the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar no matter how much they want to or how much they’re willing to spend. How can they ask where it was bought from?","If Leaning Moon Mountain was willing to sell the nectar, even elite factions would scramble and riot in order to obtain it.","Lin Yuan blinked. He did not expect Zhou Luo and Hu Quan to finish drinking the full bottles of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Lin Yuan hastily said, “Uncle Hu, Big Brother Zhou, the both of you should head to your bathrooms quickly.”"]},{"number":600,"title":"Chapter 600 - Evolve! Vajra Butterfly!","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan had not finished speaking before Zhou Luo, and Hu Quan dashed toward their respective rooms.","Liu Jie looked at the full bowl of amber fluid. He had already recognized the contents.","When the Insect Queen had been in danger, the Bamboo Monarch had given Liu Jie a drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Although the drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar had not cured the Insect Queen, it did grant it one more year of time.","Otherwise, it would have died before Liu Jie met Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie would also not be living the life he was living at the moment.","The Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar was especially beneficial to the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer, who were already Myth Breed feys.","In order for the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar to cleanse a body, it evolved the genetic model to perfection.","Feys had much more complicated genes than humans.","The Mother of Bloodbath, Endless Summer, and Liu Jie returned to their rooms as well after drinking the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Lin Yuan felt slightly awkward and felt that he should have taken out the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar after the meal.","Now, only he, Chu Ci, and Wen Yu were left seated at the table.","After the meal, Lin Yuan took out the two pots of Golden Curtain Peonies and placed them beside the water rhinoceros leather sofa. Hu Quan had already created a plant holder that had not been used.","The Glow-Winged Butterflies inside the red sandalwood longevity fish tank flew out after sensing the Golden Curtain Peonies’ aura.","They danced around the Bronze/Legend Golden Curtain Peonies.","The Glow-Winged Butterflies were diurnal and usually refused to fly at night.","However, they were now flitting around the Golden Curtain Peonies with as much vigor as they had in the daytime.","Lin Yuan knew that the Glow-Winged Butterflies were after the Golden Curtain Peonies’ pollen.","The two Golden Curtain Peonies were full of pollen. Even after evolving to Fantasy Breed, the Vajra Butterfly would not be able to use up all of the pollen.","Lin Yuan did not continue to stop the Glow-Winged Butterflies from consuming the pollen.","The longer that Lin Yuan looked at the dancing Glow-Winged Butterflies, the more he felt that something was wrong with one of them.","The other Glow-Winged Butterflies were trying to put as much space between them and this particular Glow-Winged Butterfly as possible while they were flying.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to check on this Glow-Winged Butterfly using True Data, Chu Ci said, “Lin Yuan, I’m done eating. I’ll wait for you in the training room.”","After hearing what Chu Ci said, Lin Yuan stopped caring about the Glow-Winged Butterflies and said, “Wait for me. Let’s go over together once I’m done eating. Before we go, I want to prepare all the metal and plant-type pollen that the Varja Butterfly will need in its evolution to Fantasy Breed.”","Lin Yuan took out a wooden box and gently patted the large peonies, sending a plume of pollen cascading into the wooden box.","The shining golden pollen shimmered as they filled the box’s interior.","Lin Yuan carried the box as he pulled Chu Ci to the training room.","Presently, all of Chu Ci’s feys had been built by Lin Yuan.","Thus, Lin Yuan was looking forward to seeing what kinds of exclusive skills the Vajra Butterfly would develop once it evolved to Fantasy Breed.","Lin Yuan was not expecting much of the Burning Sunflower because its original abilities were already enough to aid Chu Ci in battle.","Lin Yuan felt that any additional exclusive skills were all just icing on top of the cake.","When they arrived at the training room, Lin Yuan summoned the Bronze/Legend Vajra Butterfly.","The Vajra Butterfly had been by Lin Yuan’s side for some time. When it saw Chu Ci, it flew over to her and flitted around her lovingly.","It landed on Chu Ci’s finger, then on her nose. Chu Ci was tickled pink as she giggled.","Lin Yuan had also contracted a butterfly-species fey. It was a fey that could be considered one of the ten most beautiful feys in existence—the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly.","However, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was extremely aloof.","Although Lin Yuan could sense the deep affection that the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly felt for him, it did not interact with him on the regular.","Lin Yuan felt that the Jasmine Lily was the only one to which the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly could warm up.","Six months had passed since the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly had hatched, and Lin Yuan had nurtured it from the beginning.","Among all his feys, Lin Yuan was the most clueless about what Willpower Runes suited the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly best.","He thought about how Chu Ci had picked the most compatible Willpower Rune through observing the Vajra Butterfly. Hence, Lin Yuan decided that he would also find the right time to study the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to see if he could comprehend a compatible Willpower Rune.","After Chu Ci and the Vajra Butterfly played around for a while, she summoned the Willpower Rune that she had comprehended from the Vajra Butterfly.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan had seen this Willpower Rune of Chu Ci’s.","This Willpower Rune had an oddly thick feeling, as though it was a strong shield.","However, behind this heavy feeling was an exploding aura.","Lin Yuan had always felt that this Willpower Rune had a subtle aura of impulsivity.","Lin Yuan placed the wooden box of pollen on the table in the training room.","“Instruct the Vajra Butterfly to eat the pollen in the wooden box until you feel that it can’t eat anymore. Then, combine your Willpower Rune with the Vajra Butterfly and evolve the Vajra Butterfly to Fantasy Breed,” said Lin Yuan.","This was not Chu Ci’s first Fantasy Breed. However, Chu Ci was more nervous as compared to the previous time when she was still rather ignorant.","Ever since she started on the path of a spirit qi professional, Chu Ci, who was obsessed with real combat practice, understood exclusive skills and ability compatibility more than other people her age.","Although Chu Ci was nervous, she did not seem anxious as she instructed the Vajra Butterfly.","By the time the Vajra Butterfly had eaten half of the pollen in the wooden box, its abdomen had swelled.","A golden light shone from within its abdomen. It illuminated the Vajra Butterfly’s green metal body with a light golden sheen.","Chu Ci sensed the Vajra Butterfly’s condition. When the Vajra Butterfly’s entire body was gleaming golden, she immediately directed the Willpower Rune toward the Vajra Butterfly.","The Vajra Butterfly combined with the Willpower Rune and the golden light intensified in an instant.","Soon after, Lin Yuan watched as the intense golden light retreated.","Suddenly, a watery green light appeared in the center of the golden light.","The moment that the watery green light appeared, Lin Yuan became certain.","Judging from the Vajra Butterfly’s process of evolving to Fantasy Breed, everything seemed to be going smoothly."]}]);
